AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:08958 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:08959))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:08959 "initiating species")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:08959 "Species to which monomer adds or becomes inserted to start a chain polymerization.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:08959 "An initiating species may be formed from an initiator or be the initiator itself."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:08959 "In radical polymerization, initiating species formed directly from an initiator are called primary radicals."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:08959 doi:10.1515/pac-2020-1211)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:08959 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:08960))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:08960 "initiator efficiency")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:08960 "Number of growing chains initiated divided by the number of active-centers generated from initiator molecules.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:08960 "The number of growing chains initiated is the number of initiating radicals formed. The number of active centers generated is the number of active centers that could formed be in the absence of any cage effect."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:08960 "In a radical polymerization, the frequency of production of propagating radicals from an initiator that provides two similar radicals is \\(2k_{\\rm{d}} f_{\\rm{i}}\\), where \\(k_{\\rm{d}}\\) is the rate coefficient for initiator decomposition."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:08960 "In RDP the efficiency of conversion of a starting initiator into a macroinitiator may be called the initiator efficiency (see initialization efficiency)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:08960 "The initiator efficiency for radical generation from initiators such as dialkyl diazenes and organic peroxides (common symbol \\(f\\), recommended symbol \\(f_{\\rm{g}}\\) to distinguish from \\(f_{\\rm{i}}\\)) is defined as the fraction of radicals that escape the cage (see cage effect) and are potentially available for reaction with a substrate (e.g., monomer). The value of \\(f_{\\rm{i}}\\) will usually be less than \\(f_{\\rm{g}}\\) as depending on the monomer and the monomer concentration, initiator-derived radicals may react to form products other than initiating radicals."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:08960 goldbook:08958)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:08960 goldbook:08959)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:08960 goldbook:08963)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:08960 goldbook:08966)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:08960 doi:10.1515/pac-2020-1211)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:08960 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:08961))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:08961 "living polymer chain")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:08961 "Polymer chains that possess the potential for chain growth under the polymerization conditions.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:08961 "living macromolecule (in RDP)")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:08961 "Living polymer chains comprise all active and dormant polymer chains."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:08961 goldbook:08952)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:08961 doi:10.1515/pac-2020-1211)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:08961 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:08962))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:08962 "macro-chain-transfer agent")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:08962 "Macromolecule containing chain-transfer-agent functionality.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:08962 "macroCTA")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:08962 "macroRAFT agent (in RAFT polymerization)")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:08962 "The dormant species in RAFT polymerization is often referred to as a macroCTA or macroRAFT agent."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:08962 goldbook:08935)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:08962 goldbook:08947)
