AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:11094 "hypophysis")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:11094 "pituitary gland")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:11094 "The pituitary is structurally and functionally divided into anterior and posterior lobes. The anterior lobe secretes growth hormone (somatotropin), thyroid-stimulating hormone (TSH), adrenocortocotropic hormone (ACTH), prolactin (PRL), luteinizing hormone (LH), and follicle-stimulating hormone (FSH). The posterior lobe develops from the hypothalamus and secretes oxytocin and antidiuretic hormone (ADH) (also called arginine vasopressin (AVP)). An intermediate lobe (indistinct in humans) secretes melanocyte-stimulating hormone (MSH)."^^xsd:string)
