AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:11166 "If the exchange is equal (i.e., no genetic material is missing) it is called a balanced translocation, and may be without severe consequences for the developing embryo. If extra or missing genetic material results from the process, it is called an unbalanced translocation, and the consequences are often more harmful."^^xsd:string)
