AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:11830 "Reaction of the body to injury or to infectious, allergic, or chemical irritation; characterized by redness, swelling, heat, and pain resulting from dilation of the blood vessels accompanied by loss of plasma and leukocytes into the tissues.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:11830 "This process differs in the brain, where lymphocytic invasion requires compromise of the blood–brain barrier, although T-cells can enter the brain for surveillance."^^xsd:string)
