AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:11990 "paralytic shellfish poisoning")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:11990 "Illness that is a consequence of consumption of bivalve molluscs such as mussels, oysters, and clams that have ingested large quantities of microalgae containing saxitoxin or its derivatives.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:11990 "PSP")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:11990 "Initially there is tingling, numbness, and burning of the tongue and lips, which spreads to the face, neck, arms, fingertips, legs, and toes; this is followed by weakness of the upper and lower limbs, loss of motor coordination, and, in severe cases, paralysis."^^xsd:string)
