AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12184 doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0103)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12184 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12185))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12185 "zebrafish")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12185 "Tropical fish (Danio rerio) about \\(\\pu{4 cm}\\) long, commonly used as a model organism in developmental biology.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12185 "Danio rerio")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12185 "The zebrafish has been used in studies of neurodevelopment, neuronal networks and the blood–brain barrier."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12185 "The zebrafish is also used for alternative toxicity testing; multiple endpoints for developmental neurotoxicity are known."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12185 goldbook:11640)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12185 goldbook:11919)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12185 goldbook:11948)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12185 doi:10.1515/pac-2015-0103)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12185 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12186))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12186 "chain segment")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12186 "Group of contiguous skeletal atoms in a chain, including their side groups, if any, such that the chain itself can be represented as a chain of segments.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12186 "segment")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12186 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12186 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12187))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12187 "rotational isomeric state")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12187 "Rotamer defined by a relative rotation about a skeletal bond of a single-strand chain.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12187 "bond-conformational state (in polymer science)")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12187 "A rotational isomeric state is conventionally defined over a sequence of three contiguous skeletal bonds with reference to the dihedral (or torsion) angle (\\(\\phi\\)) between the planes defined by the first two bonds and the second two bonds. For example, for a chain composed of single \\(\\ce{C-C}\\) skeletal bonds, \\(\\phi \\approx 0^{\\circ}\\) can be used to define the (planar) trans (\\(t\\)) rotational isomeric state, and \\(\\phi \\approx \\pm 120^{\\circ}\\) to define the gauche\\(\\pm\\) (\\(g_{\\pm}\\)) rotational isomeric states."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12187 "Alternative notations exist. For example, \\(\\phi = 180°, \\pm 60^{\\circ}\\), respectively, can be used to denote the \\(t\\) and \\(g_{\\pm}\\) states, which can also be given the symbols \\(\\rm{T}\\), \\(\\rm{G}^{+}\\), and \\(\\rm{G}^{-}\\). The trans and gauche states or conformers are also known as the \"antiperiplanar conformers\" and \"synclinal conformers\". The notation used in Note 1 is that introduced by Flory and co-workers and is now the one most frequently used in polymer science."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12187 "The energies of rotational isomeric states are determined by short-range intramolecular interactions."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12187 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12187 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12188))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12188 "chain conformation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12188 "Conformation of a chain as defined by its sequence of bond-conformational states.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12188 "If no ambiguity results, the word \"chain\" can be omitted."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12188 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12188 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12189))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12189 "unperturbed conformational state")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12189 "Chain conformation corresponding to unperturbed dimensions.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12189 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12189 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12190))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12190 "unperturbed radius of gyration")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12190 "Radius of gyration of a macromolecule in an unperturbed conformational state.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12190 goldbook:12189)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12190 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12190 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12191))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12191 "root-mean-square radius of gyration")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12191 "For a flexible macromolecule composed of \\(n\\) mass elements, of masses \\(m_{i}\\), \\(i = 1, 2, \\ldots, n\\), located at statistical-mechanical mean-square distances \\(\\lt\\!s_{i}^{2}\\!\\gt\\) from the centre of mass, the root-mean-square radius of gyration is the square-root of the mass average of \\(\\lt\\!s_{i}^{2}\\!\\gt\\) over all mass elements, i.e., \\[\\lt\\!s^{2}\\!\\gt^{1/2}\\;= \\left(\\sum\\limits_{i=1}^{n} m_{i} \\lt\\!s_{i}^{2}\\!\\gt\\!/\\sum\\limits_{i=1}^{n} m_{i} \\right)^{1/2}\\]")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12191 "The mass elements are usually taken as the masses of the skeletal groups constituting the macromolecule, e.g., \\(\\ce{-CH2-}\\) in poly(methylene)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12191 "\\(\\lt\\!s_{i}^{2}\\!\\gt\\) is the statistical mechanical average of \\(s_{i}^{2}\\) over all chain conformations."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12191 "The radius of gyration is a parameter characterizing the size of a macromolecule as a time-averaged spherical domain in laboratory coordinates."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12191 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12191 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12192))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12192 "mean-square radius of gyration")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12192 "For a flexible macromolecule composed of \\(n\\) mass elements, of masses \\(m_{i}\\) , \\(i = 1, 2, \\ldots, n\\), located at statistical-mechanical mean-square distances \\(\\lt\\!s_{i}^{2}\\!\\gt\\) from the centre of mass, the mean-square radius of gyration is the mass average of \\(\\lt\\!s_{i}^{2}\\!\\gt\\) over all mass elements, i.e., \\[\\lt\\!s^{2}\\!\\gt = \\left(\\sum\\limits_{i=1}^{n} m_{i} \\lt\\!s_{i}^{2}\\!\\gt\\!/\\sum\\limits_{i=1}^{n} m_{i} \\right)\\]")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12192 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12192 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12193))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12193 "root-mean-square unperturbed radius of gyration")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12193 "Root-mean-square radius of gyration of a macromolecule having unperturbed dimensions.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12193 "The traditionally used symbol \\(\\lt\\!s^{2}\\!\\gt_{\\rm{o}}^{1/2}\\) is not recommended as it signifies the square root of the unperturbed average, namely, \\(\\lt \\; \\gt_{\\rm{o}}^{1/2}\\) of \\(s^{2}\\) rather than the root-mean-square, namely, \\(\\lt \\; \\gt^{1/2}\\) of the unperturbed squared radius, \\(s_{\\rm{o}}^{2}\\)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12193 goldbook:12191)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12193 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12193 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12194))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12194 "mean-square unperturbed radius of gyration")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12194 "Mean-square radius of gyration of a macromolecule having unperturbed dimensions.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12194 goldbook:12192)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12194 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12194 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12195))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12195 "unperturbed end-to-end vector")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12195 "Vector connecting the two ends of a linear chain in a particular conformation, with the chain having unperturbed dimensions.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12195 goldbook:12188)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12195 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12195 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12196))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12196 "unperturbed end-to-end distance")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12196 "Magnitude of the unperturbed end-to-end vector.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12196 goldbook:12195)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12196 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12196 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12197))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12197 "mean-square end-to-end distance")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12197 "Statistical-mechanical mean-square end-to-end distance of a linear chain averaged over all chain conformations.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12197 goldbook:12188)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12197 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12197 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12198))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12198 "root-mean-square unperturbed end-to-end distance")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12198 "Root-mean-square end-to-end distance of a chain having unperturbed dimensions.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12198 "If no ambiguity results, the term \"unperturbed end-to-end distance\" can be used."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12198 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12198 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12199))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12199 "mean-square unperturbed end-to-end distance")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12199 "Mean-square end-to-end distance of a chain having unperturbed dimensions.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12199 "\\(\\lt\\!r_{\\rm{o}}^{2}\\! \\gt\\) of a hypothetical, sufficiently long, linear chain of identical single skeletal bonds having rotational isomeric states that are independent of each other is given by the equation \\[\\lt\\!r_{\\rm{o}}^{2}\\!\\gt = nl^{2} \\frac{(1 + \\cos\\theta)}{(1 - \\cos \\theta)} {\\cdot} \\frac{(1 + \\lt\\!\\cos \\phi\\!\\gt )}{(1 - \\lt\\!\\cos \\phi\\!\\gt)}\\] where \\(n\\) is the number of skeletal bonds of length \\(l\\) and valence-angle supplement \\(\\theta\\), and \\(\\lt\\!\\cos \\phi\\!\\gt\\) is the average of the cosine of the dihedral angles \\(\\phi\\) defined over sequences of three contiguous skeletal bonds. This equation is useful for understanding the significance of characteristic ratio, steric factor, and effective bond-length."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12199 goldbook:12202)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12199 goldbook:12187)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12199 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12199 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12200))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12200 "root-mean-square end-to-end distance of a freely rotating chain")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12200 "Root-mean-square end-to-end distance of a linear freely rotating chain.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12200 "If no ambiguity results, the term \"freely rotating end-to-end distance\" can be used."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12200 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12200 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12201))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12201 "mean-square end-to-end distance of a freely rotating chain")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12201 "Mean-square end-to-end distance of a linear freely rotating chain.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12201 "\\(\\lt\\!r_{\\rm{o,f}}^2\\!\\gt\\) of a hypothetical, sufficiently long, linear freely rotating chain of identical single skeletal bonds is given by the equation \\[\\lt\\!r_{\\rm{o,f}}^{2}\\!\\gt = nl^{2}\\frac{(1 + \\cos \\theta)}{(1 - \\cos \\theta)}\\] where \\(n\\) is the number of skeletal bonds of length \\(l\\) and valence-angle supplement \\(\\theta\\)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12201 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12201 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12202))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12202 "effective bond length")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12202 "Square root of the ratio of the unperturbed mean-square end-to-end distance of a linear chain to its number of skeletal bonds, i.e., \\[b = (\\lt\\!r_{\\rm{o}}^{2}\\!\\gt\\!/n)^{1/2}\\]")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12202 "The effective bond length is a type of characteristic ratio relating to chain structure, cf., characteristic ratio."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12202 "\\(b^{2}\\) is the unperturbed mean-square end-to-end distance per skeletal bond. For a hypothetical, sufficiently long chain of identical single skeletal bonds having rotational isomeric states that are independent of each other, the equation in mean-square unperturbed end-to-end distance shows that the value of \\(b\\) depends on the values of \\(l\\), \\(\\cos \\theta\\) and \\(\\lt\\!\\cos \\phi\\!\\gt\\). In general, for actual chains, the value of \\(b\\) is still characteristic of the values of the lengths and valence angles of the skeletal bonds and of the dihedral bond-conformational angles, although it may be difficult to write an analytical expression for \\(b\\)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12202 goldbook:12187)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12202 goldbook:12199)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12202 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12202 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12203))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12203 "equivalent freely jointed chain")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12203 "Hypothetical freely jointed chain with the same mean-square end-to-end distance and contour length as an actual linear chain having unperturbed dimensions.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12203 "The number of links, \\(m\\), and their length, \\(l^{\\prime}\\), are evaluated from the mean-square end-to-end distance, \\(\\lt\\!r_{\\rm{o}}^{2}\\!\\gt\\), and contour length, \\(r_{\\rm{max}}\\), of the actual chain using the equations in freely jointed chain and contour length, with \\[m = \\frac{r_{\\max}^{2}}{\\lt\\!r_{\\rm{o}}^{2}\\!\\gt} \\quad {\\rm{and}} \\quad l^{\\prime} = \\frac{\\lt\\!r_{\\rm{o}}^{2}\\!\\gt}{r_{\\max}}\\] For example, for polymethylene at room temperature, one freely jointed link is equivalent to about 10 actual \\(\\ce{C-C}\\) skeletal bonds."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12203 goldbook:12197)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12203 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12203 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12204))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12204 "Kuhn segment")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12204 "Segment or link of an equivalent freely jointed chain.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12204 "equivalent freely jointed link")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12204 "statistical segment")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12204 goldbook:12186)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12204 goldbook:12203)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12204 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12204 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12205))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12205 "Kuhn segment length")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12205 "Length of a Kuhn segment.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12205 "freely jointed link length")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12205 "statistical segment length")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12205 goldbook:12204)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12205 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12205 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12206))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12206 "self-avoiding random-walk chain")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12206 "Freely jointed chain subject to the condition that the segments cannot intersect one another.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12206 "In the model of a self-avoiding chain, segments are considered to have a finite volume such that two or more cannot occupy the same volume simultaneously."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12206 "The self-avoiding random-walk chain model is used to represent a polymer chain with excluded volume."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12206 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12206 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12207))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12207 "macromolecular coil")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12207 "Depiction of a macromolecule in which its segments are distributed about some point in space.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12207 "The point in space is usually chosen as the molecular centre of mass or a chain end."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12207 goldbook:12186)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12207 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12207 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12209))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12209 "chain stiffness")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12209 "Parameter describing the end-to-end distance of a linear, single-strand macromolecular chain having unperturbed dimensions relative to that of a model macromolecular chain not subject to short-range interactions.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12209 "The steric factor, \\(\\sigma\\), Kuhn segment length, \\(l^{\\prime}\\), and persistence length, \\(a\\), are all measures of chain stiffness."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12209 goldbook:12205)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12209 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12209 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12212))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12212 "<i>g</i>-factor")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12212 "Ratio of the mean-square radius of gyration of a branched molecule, \\(\\lt\\!s_{\\rm{b}}^{2}\\!\\gt\\), to that of an otherwise identical linear molecule, \\(\\lt\\!s_{\\rm{l}}^{2}\\!\\gt\\), of the same relative molecular mass in the same solvent at the same temperature, i.e., \\(g = \\lt\\!s_{\\rm{b}}^{2}\\!\\gt\\!/\\!\\lt\\!s_{\\rm{l}}^{2}\\!\\gt\\).")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12212 "contraction factor")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12212 "geometric contraction factor")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12212 "radius of gyration contraction factor")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12212 "The \\(g\\mbox{-}\\rm{factor}\\) is a quantity characterizing the effects of long-chain branches on the size of a branched molecule."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12212 goldbook:12213)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12212 goldbook:12211)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12212 goldbook:12192)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12212 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12212 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12213))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12213 "<i>g</i>′-factor")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12213 "Ratio of the intrinsic viscosity of a branched molecule, \\([\\eta_{\\rm{b}}]\\), to that of an otherwise identical linear molecule, \\([\\eta_{\\rm{l}}]\\), of the same relative molecular mass in the same solvent at the same temperature, i.e., \\(g^{\\prime} = [\\eta_{\\rm{b}}]/[\\eta_{\\rm{l}}]\\).")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12213 "hydrodynamic contraction factor")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12213 "viscosity contraction factor")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12213 "The \\(g^{\\prime}\\mbox{-}\\rm{factor}\\) is a quantity characterizing the effects of long-chain branches on the size of a branched molecule."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12213 goldbook:12212)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12213 goldbook:12211)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12213 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12213 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12214))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12214 "molar mass")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12214 "Mass divided by amount of substance.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12214 "In the present context, \"amount of substance\" is the number of molecules divided by the Avogadro constant, \\(N_{\\rm{A}} [= \\pu{6.02214179(30)E23 mol-1}]\\)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12214 "If the unit \\(\\pu{g mol-1}\\) unit is used, the numerical values of molar mass, relative molecular mass and relative molar mass are equal."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12214 "The term \"molar\" may also be used for entities consisting of more than one molecule, such as complexes, aggregates, micelles, etc."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12214 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12214 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12215))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12215 "molar-mass average")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12215 "Any average of the molar mass, molecular weight, relative molar mass, or relative molecular mass for a non-uniform polymer, with the symbol \\(\\rm{k}\\) specifying the type of average.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12215 "The various symbols that \\(\\rm{k}\\) can be are given in the terms number-average molar mass, mass-average molar mass, z-average molar mass, (z+1)-average molar mass, and viscosity-average molar mass. For example, with \\(\\rm{k} \\equiv n\\), number-average quantities are defined."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12215 "An infinite number of molar-mass averages can in principle be defined, but only a few types of averages are directly accessible experimentally. The most important averages are defined in terms of simple moments of the distribution functions and are obtained by methods applied to systems in thermodynamic equilibrium, such as osmometry, static light scattering, and sedimentation equilibrium. Hydrodynamic methods, as a rule, yield more complex molar-mass averages."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12215 "Any molar-mass average can be defined in terms of mass fractions or mole fractions. In this document, the most important molar-mass averages are defined in terms of the mass fraction, \\(w_{\\rm{M}}\\), of the species of molar mass \\(M\\). These definitions are most closely related to experimental determinations of molar-mass averages."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12215 "Quantities molecular-weight average, relative-molar-mass average, and relative-molecular-mass average (\\(M_{\\rm{r,k}}\\)) are synonyms. These quantities are dimensionless (pure numbers) and are not associated with any units."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12215 goldbook:12219)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12215 goldbook:12217)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12215 goldbook:12214)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12215 goldbook:12216)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12215 goldbook:12220)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12215 goldbook:12218)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12215 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12215 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12216))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12216 "number-average molar mass")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12216 "The equation for number-average molar mass is \\[M_{\\rm{n}} = \\frac{1}{\\sum\\limits_{M} (w_{M}/M)}\\] The equation for number-average molecular weight  is \\[M_{\\rm{r,n}} = \\frac{1}{\\sum\\limits_{M_{\\rm{r}}}(w_{M_{\\rm{r}}}/M_{\\rm{r}})}\\]")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12216 "For definition of the symbols, see molar-mass average."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12216 "Quantities number-average molecular weight, number-average relative molar mass, and number-average relative molecular mass (\\(M_{\\rm{r,n}}\\)) are synonyms. These quantities are dimensionless (pure numbers) and are not associated with any units."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12216 goldbook:12215)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12216 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12216 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12217))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12217 "mass-average molar mass")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12217 "The equation for mass-average molar mass is \\[M_{\\rm{m}} \\equiv M_{\\rm{w}} = \\sum\\limits_{M} w_{M}M\\] The equation for mass-average molecular weight  is \\[M_{\\rm{r,m}} \\equiv {M_{\\rm{r,w}}} = \\sum\\limits_{M_{\\rm{r}}} w_{M_{\\rm{r}}} M_{\\rm{r}}\\]")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12217 "For definition of the symbols, see molar-mass average."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12217 "Quantities mass-average molecular weight, mass-average relative molar mass, and mass-average relative molecular mass (\\(M_{\\rm{r,m}}\\)) are synonyms. These quantities are dimensionless (pure numbers) and are not associated with any units."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12217 goldbook:12215)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12217 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12217 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12218))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12218 "z-average molar mass")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12218 "The equation for z-average molar mass is \\[M_{\\rm{z}} = \\frac{\\sum\\limits_{M} w_{M}M^{2}}{\\sum\\limits_{M} w_{M}M}\\] The equation for z-average molecular weight is \\[M_{\\rm{r,z}} = \\frac{\\sum\\limits_{M_{\\rm{r}}} w_{M_{\\rm{r}}}M_{\\rm{r}}^{2}}{\\sum\\limits_{M_{\\rm{r}}} w_{M_{\\rm{r}}}M_{\\rm{r}}}\\]")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12218 "For definition of the symbols, see molar-mass average."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12218 "Quantities z-average molecular weight, z-average relative molar mass, and z-average relative molecular mass, (\\(M_{\\rm{r,z}}\\)) are synonyms. These quantities are dimensionless (pure numbers) and are not associated with any units."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12218 goldbook:12215)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12218 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12218 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12219))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12219 "(z + 1)-average molar mass")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12219 "The equation for (z + 1)-average molar mass is \\[M_{\\rm{z+1}} = \\frac{\\sum\\limits_{M} w_{M}M^{3}}{\\sum\\limits_M w_{M}M^{2}}\\] The equation for (z + 1)-average molecular weight is \\[M_{\\rm{r,z+1}} = \\frac{\\sum\\limits_{M_{\\rm{r}}} w_{M_{\\rm{r}}}M^{3}}{\\sum\\limits_{M_{\\rm{r}}} w_{M_{\\rm{r}}}M^{2}}\\]")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12219 "For definition of the symbols, see molar-mass average."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12219 "Quantities (z + 1)-average molecular weight, (z + 1)-average relative molar mass, and (z + 1)-average relative molecular mass (\\(M_{\\rm{r,z+1}}\\)) are synonyms. These quantities are dimensionless (pure numbers) and are not associated with any units."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12219 goldbook:12215)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12219 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12219 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12220))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12220 "viscosity-average molar mass")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12220 "The equation for viscosity-average molar mass is \\[M_{\\rm{v}} = \\left[\\sum\\limits_{M} w_{M}M^{a} \\right]^{1/a}\\] The equation for viscosity-average molecular weight is \\[M_{\\rm{r,v}} = \\left[\\sum\\limits_{M_{\\rm{r}}} w_{M_{\\rm{r}}}M_{\\rm{r}}^{a} \\right]^{1/a}\\] where \\(a\\) is the exponent in the Mark–Houwink equation, \\([\\eta] = KM^{a}\\)")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12220 "For definition of the symbols, see molar-mass average."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12220 "Quantities viscosity-average molecular weight, viscosity-average relative molar mass, and viscosity-average relative molecular mass (\\(M_{\\rm{r,v}}\\)) are synonyms. These quantities are dimensionless (pure numbers) and are not associated with any units."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12220 "The exponent \\(a\\) is different from the adjustable parameter of some of the distribution functions and from the persistence length."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12220 goldbook:12215)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12220 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12220 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12221))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12221 "apparent molar mass")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12221 "Molar mass, molecular weight, relative molar mass, or relative molecular mass calculated from experimental data without the application of appropriate corrections.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12221 "Quantities apparent molecular weight, apparent relative molar mass, and apparent relative molecular mass (\\(M_{\\rm{r,app}}\\)) are synonyms. These quantities are dimensionless (pure numbers) and are not associated with any units."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12221 "Examples of corrections are those for finite polymer concentration, association, preferential sorption, compositional heterogeneity, constitutional heterogeneity, and also from experimental data obtained from an instrument (often an SEC instrument) calibrated using standard samples of known molar masses of a polymer constitutionally different from that being analysed."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12221 goldbook:12214)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12221 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12221 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12222))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12222 "cumulative number-distribution function")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12222 "Cumulative distribution function in which the relative amount of a portion of a substance with values of the random variable or variables less than or equal to a given value or given values is expressed in terms of mole fraction.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12222 "cumulative number distribution")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12222 "integral number distribution")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12222 "integral number-distribution function")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12222 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12222 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12223))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12223 "cumulative mass-distribution function")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12223 "Cumulative distribution function in which the relative amount of a portion of a substance with values of the random variable or variables less than or equal to a given value or given values is expressed in terms of mass fraction.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12223 "cumulative mass distribution")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12223 "integral mass distribution")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12223 "integral mass-distribution function")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12223 "It is the differential and cumulative mass-distribution functions that are usually determined experimentally."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12223 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12223 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12224))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12224 "molar-mass dispersity")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12224 "Ratio of the mass-average molar mass, \\(M_{\\rm{m}}\\), molecular weight, relative molar mass, or relative molecular mass, \\(M_{\\rm{r,m}}\\), to the number-average molar mass, \\(M_{\\rm{n}}\\), molecular weight, relative molar mass, or relative molecular mass, \\(M_{\\rm{r,n}}\\). \\[Ð\\!_{\\rm{M}} = M_{\\rm{m}}/M_{\\rm{n}} = M_{\\rm{r,m}}/M_{\\rm{r,n}}\\]")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12224 "molecular-weight dispersity")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12224 "relative-molar-mass dispersity")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12224 "relative-molecular-mass dispersity")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12224 "Use of the term \"polydispersity index\", or other terms involving the word \"polydispersity\", for \\(M_{\\rm{m}}/M_{\\rm{n}}\\), \\(M_{\\rm{r,m}}/M_{\\rm{r,n}}\\) is strongly discouraged."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12224 goldbook:12217)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12224 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12224 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12225))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12225 "degree-of-polymerisation dispersity")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12225 "Ratio of the mass-average degree of polymerisation, \\(X_{\\rm{m}}\\), to the number-average degree of polymerisation, \\(X_{\\rm{n}}\\). \\[Ð\\!_{\\rm{X}} = X_{\\rm{m}}/X_{\\rm{n}}\\]")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12225 "Use of the term \"polydispersity index\", or other terms involving the word \"polydispersity\", for \\(X_{\\rm{m}}/X_{\\rm{n}}\\) is strongly discouraged."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12225 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12225 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12226))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12226 "dispersity")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12226 "Ratio of \\(M_{\\rm{m}}\\) to \\(M_{\\rm{n}}\\), or the ratio of \\(X_{\\rm{m}}\\) to \\(X_{\\rm{n}}\\) for a homopolymer or an alternating copolymer of sufficiently large molar mass, such that the effects of the distinct structures of the end-groups of the constituent macromolecules can be neglected, giving \\(X_{\\rm{n}}\\) directly proportional to \\(M_{\\rm{n}}\\), \\(X_{\\rm{m}}\\) directly proportional to \\(M_{\\rm{m}}\\) and \\(Ð\\!_{\\rm{M}} = Ð\\!_{\\rm{X}} = Ð\\).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12226 "Dispersity is a measure of the dispersion (or spread) of a molar mass, molecular weight, relative molar mass, relative molecular mass, or degree-of-polymerisation distribution function. For a uniform polymer, \\(Ð = 1\\); for a polymer of sufficiently high \\(X_{\\rm{n}}\\) having a Poisson distribution of molar masses, molecular weights, relative-molar-masses, or relative-molecular-masses, \\(Ð \\cong 1\\); and for a polymer of sufficiently high \\(X_{\\rm{n}}\\) having a most probable distribution of molar masses, molecular weights, relative-molar-masses, or relative-molecular-masses, \\(Ð \\cong 2\\)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12226 "For a copolymer that is not an alternating copolymer \\(X_{\\rm{n}}\\) cannot be considered to be directly proportional to \\(M_{\\rm{n}}\\), nor \\(X_{\\rm{w}}\\) directly proportional to \\(M_{\\rm{w}}\\). It is then necessary to state whether \\(Ð\\!_{\\rm{M}}\\) or \\(Ð\\!_{\\rm{X}}\\) is being used."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12226 goldbook:12214)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12226 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12226 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12228))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12228 "semi-dilute solution")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12228 "Polymer solution in the concentration range at which the domains occupied by the dissolved macromolecules or entities start to overlap.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12228 "The semi-dilute solution behaviour sets in at concentrations larger than the overlap concentration, \\(c^{\\ast}\\)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12228 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12228 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12229))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12229 "concentrated solution")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12229 "Polymer solution in the concentration range at which the domains occupied by the dissolved macromolecules or entities overlap to such an extent that it is not possible to distinguish the individual domains from one another.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12229 "The limiting maximum mass concentration is the density of the bulk amorphous polymer."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12229 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12229 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12230))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12230 "entanglement")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12230 "Entanglement, involving one or more macromolecular chains, of duration at least equal to the period of observation.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12230 "A volume element, in which the chains of two or more macromolecules are entangled, acts as a temporary junction point of a transient polymer network, such as can occur in a semi-dilute solution or a concentrated solution."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12230 goldbook:12229)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12230 goldbook:12228)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12230 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12230 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12231))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12231 "mesh size")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12231 "Average distance between two adjacent entanglements on a given macromolecule in a semi-dilute solution, a concentrated solution, or bulk amorphous polymer.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12231 goldbook:12229)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12231 goldbook:12228)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12231 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12231 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12232))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12232 "blob")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12232 "Hypothetical spherical volume element occupied by a subchain of a macromolecule between two neighbouring entanglements on the same macromolecule.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12232 "The size of a blob is a scaling function of concentration and temperature."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12232 "It is assumed that the behaviours of portions of a macromolecule separated by more than the size of a blob are not correlated with each other."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12232 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12232 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12233))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12233 "scaling law")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12233 "Equation of the type \\(y = k x^{a}\\), relating two physical quantities, \\(x\\) and \\(y\\ (\\rm{g})\\), in which the value of the exponent \\(a\\) can be predicted by theory.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12233 "The constant \\(k\\) cannot be predicted from theory and must be determined experimentally."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12233 "It has been shown that scaling laws are particularly useful in the description of semi-dilute polymer solutions."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12233 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12233 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12234))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12234 "free volume")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12234 "Difference between specific volume of an amorphous polymer and that of its perfect crystalline form.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12234 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12234 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12235))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12235 "mean-field theory")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12235 "Theory reducing the difficult exact evaluation of interactions in a multi-body system to a simpler but approximate evaluation of an average effective interaction of one body with its surroundings.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12235 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12235 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12236))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12236 "co-nonsolvency")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12236 "Decrease in solubility of a polymer in a solvent comprising more than one component, each component of which by itself is a solvent for the polymer.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12236 "Poly(N-isopropylacrylamide) in water/methanol and poly(vinyl alcohol) in dimethylsulfoxide/water are examples of systems in which co-nonsolvency occurs."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12236 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12236 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12237))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12237 "osmometer")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12237 "Apparatus for measuring osmotic pressure.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12237 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12237 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12238))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12238 "osmometry")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12238 "Measurement of the osmotic pressure of a solution using an osmometer.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12238 "The osmometry of a dilute solution of polymer is an absolute method for determining the number-average molar mass of the polymer and the osmotic virial coefficients of the solution."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12238 goldbook:12227)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12238 goldbook:12216)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12238 goldbook:12237)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12238 goldbook:12239)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12238 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12238 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12239))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12239 "osmotic virial coefficient")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12239 "Coefficient in the expansion of the chemical potential of the solvent, \\(\\mu_{\\rm{s}}\\), in powers of the mass concentration, \\(c\\), of the solute, i.e., \\[\\mu_{\\rm{s}} - \\mu_{\\rm{s}}^{\\circ} = -\\mathit{\\Pi} V_{s}^{\\prime} = -RT V_{s}^{\\prime} (A_{1}c + A_{2}c^{2} + A_{3}c^{3} + \\ldots)\\] where \\(\\mu_{\\rm{s}}^{\\circ}\\) is the chemical potential of the solvent in the reference state at the temperature of the system and ambient pressure, \\(\\mathit{\\Pi}\\) is the osmotic pressure and \\(V_{s}^{\\prime}\\) is the partial molar volume of the solvent. In solvents comprising more than one component, the definition applies to any solvent component.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12239 "virial coefficient of the chemical potential")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12239 "The first osmotic virial coefficient is the reciprocal number-average molar mass, i.e., \\(A_{1} = 1/M_{\\rm{n}}\\). The values of the second and higher virial coefficients, \\(A_{2}, A_{3}, \\dots\\), respectively, are characteristic of polymer-solvent and polymer-polymer interactions."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12239 "The factor \\(RT\\) is sometimes included in the virial coefficients, to give \\[\\mu_{\\rm{s}} - \\mu_{\\rm{s}}^{\\circ} = -\\mathit{\\Pi}V_{s}^{\\prime} = -V_{s}^{\\prime}(A_{1}^{\\prime}c + A_{2}^{\\prime}c^{2} + A_{3}^{\\prime}c^{3} + \\dots),\\quad {\\rm{where}}\\ A_{i}^{\\prime} = RT A_{i}\\]"^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12239 "To evaluate \\(M_{\\rm{n}}\\) and \\(A_{2}\\), \\(\\mathit{\\Pi}/c\\) is often plotted versus \\(c\\), so that \\[\\frac{\\mathit{\\Pi}}{c} = \\left({\\frac{\\mathit{\\Pi}}{c}} \\right)_{\\circ}(1 + \\mathit{\\Gamma}_{2}c + \\mathit{\\Gamma}_{3}c^{2} + \\ldots),\\ {\\rm{where}}\\ \\left(\\frac{\\mathit{\\Pi}}{c} \\right)_{\\circ} = \\frac{RT}{M_{\\rm{n}}}\\ {\\rm{and,}}\\ \\mathit{\\Gamma}_{i} = M_{\\rm{n}}A_{i}\\]"^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12239 goldbook:12216)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12239 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12239 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12240))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12240 "binodal")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12240 "Curve in the isobaric temperature-composition plane for a mixture defining the region of composition and temperature across which a transition occurs from miscibility of the components to conditions where single-phase mixtures are metastable or unstable.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12240 "binodal curve")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12240 "coexistence curve")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12240 "Binodal compositions are defined by pairs of points on the curve defining the dependence of Gibbs energy of mixing on composition that have common tangents, corresponding to compositions of equal chemical potentials of each of the two components in two phases."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12240 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12240 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12241))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12241 "cloud point")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12241 "Point in the isobaric temperature-composition plane of a binary or multicomponent mixture at which a decrease in transparency is observed due to the turbidity caused by phase separation.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12241 "A cloud point is characterized by the first appearance of turbidity or cloudiness."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12241 "A cloud point can be induced by varying temperature or composition."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12241 "A cloud point induced by varying temperature is heating-rate or cooling-rate dependent."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12241 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12241 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12242))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12242 "cloud-point curve")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12242 "Curve of temperature vs. composition defined by the cloud points over range of compositions of two substances.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12242 goldbook:12241)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12242 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12242 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12243))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12243 "cloud-point temperature")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12243 "Temperature at a cloud point.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12243 goldbook:12241)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12243 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12243 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12244))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12244 "lower critical solution temperature")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12244 "Critical temperature below which a mixture is miscible at any composition.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12244 "LCST")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12244 "The LCST depends upon pressure and the molar-mass distribution functions of the constituent polymer(s)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12244 "For a mixture containing or consisting of polymeric components, these may be different polymers or species of different molar mass of the same polymer."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12244 "The LCST occurs near the minimum on the cloud point curve."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12244 "An LCST exists for mixtures in which solubility decreases with temperature."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12244 "The occurrence of an LSCT is less common than that of an upper critical solution temperature. It cannot be explained by simple polymer solution theories, such as the Flory–Huggins theory. However, it occurs for several polymer/solvent pairs and frequently for polymer blends."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12244 goldbook:12241)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12244 goldbook:12214)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12244 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12244 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12245))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12245 "translational diffusion")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12245 "Process by which the equilibrium statistical distribution of positions of molecules or entities in space is maintained or restored due to their translational Brownian motion.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12245 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12245 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12246))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12246 "translational frictional coefficient")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12246 "Frictional force, \\(F\\), per unit velocity, \\(u\\), experienced by an isolated spherical body moving unidirectionally in a viscous isotropic fluid, i.e., \\(F = fu\\).")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12246 "frictional coefficient (in polymer science)")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12246 "More generally, \\(\\boldsymbol{f}\\) is defined as the tensor that correlates the vectorial frictional force, \\(\\boldsymbol{F}\\), on a body in a viscous fluid and the vectorial velocity, \\(\\boldsymbol{u}\\) , with \\(\\boldsymbol{F} = \\boldsymbol{f}\\boldsymbol{u}\\). However, the more general definition is not needed in polymer science as experimental determinations of the translational frictional coefficient all employ situations in which \\(\\boldsymbol{F}\\) and \\(\\boldsymbol{u}\\) are collinear and \\(F = fu\\)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12246 "\\(f\\) is related to the translational diffusion coefficient, \\(D\\), of an isolated body by the Einstein equation \\(D = kT/f\\), where \\(k\\) is the Boltzmann constant and \\(T\\) the thermodynamic temperature."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12246 goldbook:12247)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12246 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12246 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12247))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12247 "translational diffusion coefficient")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12247 "Proportionality constant relating the flux per unit area, \\(J_{n}\\), in unidirectional flow of amount, \\(n\\), of entities \\(\\ce{B}\\) to their concentration gradient in the direction (\\(x\\)) of flow, \\({\\rm{d}}c_{\\ce{B}}/{\\rm{d}}x\\), i.e., \\(J_{n} = -D{\\rm{d}} c_{\\ce{B}}/{\\rm{d}}x\\).")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12247 "diffusion coefficient (in polymer science)")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12247 "More generally, \\(D\\) is defined using vectorial flow as the proportionality constant, relating the flux per unit area, \\(\\boldsymbol{J_{n}}\\) , of amount, \\(n\\), of entities \\(\\ce{B}\\) to their concentration gradient, \\(\\boldsymbol{\\nabla} c_{\\ce{B}}\\), i.e., \\(J_{n} = -D \\boldsymbol{\\nabla} c_{\\ce{B}}\\). However, the more general definition is not needed in polymer science as experimental determinations of the translational diffusion coefficient all employ unidirectional flow."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12247 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12247 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12248))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12248 "rotational frictional coefficient")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12248 "Torque, \\(T\\), per unit angular velocity, \\(\\omega\\), required for rotation of a body about a given axis in a viscous isotropic fluid, i.e., \\(T = \\zeta\\omega\\).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12248 "\\(\\zeta\\) is related to the rotational diffusion coefficient, \\(\\mathit{\\Theta}\\), of an isolated body in a viscous isotropic fluid by the equation \\(\\mathit{\\Theta} = kT/\\zeta\\), where \\(k\\) is the Boltzmann constant and \\(T\\) the absolute temperature."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12248 "A body whose shape is described by principal axes, \\(\\rm{a}\\), \\(\\rm{b}\\), and \\(\\rm{c}\\), of different lengths has three different rotational frictional coefficients denoted by \\(\\zeta_{\\rm{a}}\\), \\(\\zeta_{\\rm{b}}\\), and \\(\\zeta_{\\rm{c}}\\), relating to rotation about the axes \\(\\rm{a}\\), \\(\\rm{b}\\), and \\(\\rm{c}\\), respectively, and three different rotational diffusion coefficients, \\(\\mathit{\\Theta}_{\\rm{a}}\\), \\(\\mathit{\\Theta}_{\\rm{b}}\\), and \\(\\mathit{\\Theta}_{\\rm{c}}\\), where, for an isolated body in a viscous isotropic fluid, \\(\\mathit{\\Theta}_{\\rm{a}} = kT/\\zeta_{\\rm{a}}\\), \\(\\mathit{\\Theta}_{\\rm{b}} = kT/\\zeta_{\\rm{b}}\\), and \\(\\mathit{\\Theta}_{\\rm{c}} = kT/\\zeta_{\\rm{c}}\\)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12248 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12248 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12249))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12249 "equilibrium sedimentation method")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12249 "Experimental method by which the distribution of the concentration of the solute or dispersed component in a dilute solution or dispersion along the centrifuge cell is measured at sedimentation equilibrium, and the results are interpreted in terms of the molar masses of the solute species or their distribution functions, or both.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12249 "sedimentation-equilibrium method")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12249 goldbook:12227)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12249 goldbook:12214)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12249 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12249 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12250))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12250 "equilibrium sedimentation in a density gradient")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12250 "Equilibrium sedimentation method using a multicomponent solvent forming a density gradient in a centrifugal field.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12250 "sedimentation equilibrium in a density gradient")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12250 "Equilibrium sedimentation in a density gradient can be used to determine the compositional heterogeneity of copolymers."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12250 goldbook:12249)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12250 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12250 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12251))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12251 "Kraemer equation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12251 "Equation describing the dependence of the inherent viscosity, \\(\\eta_{\\rm{inh}}\\), of a dilute solution on the mass concentration of the solute, \\(c\\), with \\[\\eta_{\\rm{inh}} = (\\ln \\eta_{\\rm{r}})/c = [\\eta] + k_{\\rm{K}}[\\eta]^{2} c\\] where \\(k_{\\rm{K}}\\) is the Kraemer coefficient and \\([\\eta]\\) is the intrinsic viscosity.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12251 goldbook:12227)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12251 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12251 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12252))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12252 "Kraemer coefficient")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12252 "Parameter in the Kraemer equation.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12252 goldbook:12251)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12252 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12252 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12253))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12253 "hydrodynamic interaction")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12253 "In a solution or dispersion, the perturbation of the flow of the solvent continuum or dispersing medium continuum around a solute molecule, a segment of a dissolved macromolecule or dispersed entity caused by the presence of the other solute molecules, segments, or dispersed entities.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12253 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12253 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12254))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12254 "free-draining")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12254 "Adjective describing the undisturbed flow of solvent through the domain of a dissolved macromolecule.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12254 "freely draining")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12254 "Free-draining flow occurs in the limit of zero hydrodynamic interaction."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12254 goldbook:12253)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12254 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12254 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12255))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12255 "impermeable")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12255 "Adjective describing the flow behaviour of a macromolecule in solution or a dispersed entity when, due to hydrodynamic interaction, the solvent or dispersion medium within the domain of the macromolecule or dispersed entity is essentially immobilised and moves with the dissolved macromolecule or dispersed entity.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12255 "non-free-draining")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12255 goldbook:12253)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12255 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12255 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12256))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12256 "partial free-draining")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12256 "Adjective describing the flow behaviour of a macromolecule in solution or a dispersed entity when, due to hydrodynamic interaction, the solvent within the domain of the macromolecule or a dispersed entity becomes progressively more immobilised with respect to the macromolecule or a dispersed entity in the direction from its outer fringes inward.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12256 "partially draining")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12256 "Free-draining and impermeable behaviour are two extremes of the concept of partial free-draining behaviour."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12256 goldbook:12254)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12256 goldbook:12253)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12256 goldbook:12255)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12256 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12256 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12257))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12257 "equivalent hydrodynamic volume")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12257 "Volume of the hydrodynamically equivalent sphere.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12257 "The molar equivalent hydrodynamic volume determined using measurements of intrinsic viscosity, \\([\\eta]\\), is \\(V_{\\eta}\\), where \\(V_{\\eta} = [\\eta]M/N_{\\rm{A}}\\), with \\(M\\) the molar mass and \\(N_{\\rm{A}}\\) the Avogadro constant."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12257 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12257 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12258))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12258 "equivalent hydrodynamic radius")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12258 "Radius of the hydrodynamically equivalent sphere.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12258 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12258 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12259))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12259 "Stokes equation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12259 "For an isolated dissolved molecule or dispersed entity, an equation relating the translational frictional coefficient, \\(f\\), to the equivalent hydrodynamic radius in translational diffusive flow, \\(r_{D}\\), and to the viscosity of the solvent continuum or the dispersion medium continuum, \\(η_{0}\\), with \\[f = 6\\uppi \\eta_{0}r_{D}\\]")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12259 goldbook:12258)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12259 goldbook:12246)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12259 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12259 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12260))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12260 "Stokes–Einstein equation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12260 "For an isolated dissolved molecule or dispersed entity, an equation relating the translational diffusion coefficient, \\(D\\), to the equivalent hydrodynamic radius in translational diffusive flow, \\(r_{D}\\) , and to the viscosity of the solvent continuum or the dispersion medium continuum, \\(\\eta_{0}\\), with \\[D = kT/(6\\uppi \\eta_{0}r_{D})\\] where \\(k\\) is the Boltzmann constant, and \\(T\\) the thermodynamic temperature.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12260 "The Stokes–Einstein equation is derived by combining the Stokes equation with the Einstein equation \\(D = kT/f\\)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12260 goldbook:12258)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12260 goldbook:12247)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12260 goldbook:12246)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12260 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12260 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12261))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12261 "Perrin equation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12261 "For an isolated dissolved molecule or dispersed entity, an equation relating the rotational diffusion coefficient, \\(\\mathit{\\Theta}\\), to the equivalent hydrodynamic radius in rotational diffusive flow, \\(r_{\\mathit{\\Theta}}\\), and to the viscosity of the solvent continuum or the dispersion medium continuum, \\(\\eta_{0}\\), with \\[D = kT/(6\\pi \\eta_{\\rm{0}} r_{\\mathit{\\Theta}}^3)\\] where \\(k\\) is the Boltzmann constant and \\(T\\) the thermodynamic temperature.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12261 goldbook:12258)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12261 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12261 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12262))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12262 "pearl-necklace model")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12262 "Model describing the flow behaviour of a dissolved chain macromolecule in terms of a freely jointed sequence of beads, each of which offers hydrodynamic resistance to the flow of the surrounding solvent continuum and is connected to the next bead by a rigid rod that offers no hydrodynamic resistance.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12262 "bead-rod model")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12262 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12262 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12263))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12263 "Kirkwood–Riseman theory")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12263 "Theory, based on the pearl-necklace model, that describes the translational diffusive and viscous flows of an isolated linear macromolecule in solution in the theta state and accounts for the gradual change from free-draining behaviour at lower molecular weights to impermeable behaviour at higher molecular weights.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12263 "The Kirkwood–Riseman theory is usually applied in the impermeable limit when it essentially relates the equivalent hydrodynamic radius to the root-mean-square unperturbed radius of gyration, \\(\\lt\\!s_{\\circ}^{2}\\!\\gt\\), with \\[r_{D} = 0.675 \\lt\\!s_{\\circ}^{2}\\!\\gt^{1/2}\\] and \\[r_{\\eta} = 0.256 \\lt\\!s_{\\circ}^{2}\\!\\gt^{1/2}\\] where \\(r_{D}\\) and \\(r_{\\eta}\\) are the equivalent hydrodynamic radii in translational diffusive flow and viscous flow."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12263 goldbook:12258)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12263 goldbook:12254)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12263 goldbook:12255)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12263 goldbook:12262)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12263 goldbook:12193)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12263 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12263 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12264))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12264 "Flory–Fox assumption")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12264 "Assumption that the Kirkwood–Riseman theory can be applied to linear isolated macromolecules in solution, independent of whether they are in the theta state.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12264 "The Kirkwood–Riseman relationships between \\(r_{D}\\) and \\(r_{\\eta}\\) and the root-mean-square radius of gyration, \\(\\lt\\!s^{2}\\!\\gt\\), are then \\[r_{D} = 0.675 \\lt\\!s^{2}\\!\\gt^{1/2} = 0.675 \\lt\\!s_{\\circ}^{2}\\!\\gt^{1/2} \\alpha_{D}\\] and \\[r_{\\eta} = 0.256 \\lt\\!s^{2}\\!\\gt^{1/2} = 0.256 \\lt\\!s_{\\circ}^{2}\\!\\gt^{1/2} \\alpha_{\\eta}\\] where \\(r_{D}\\) and \\(r_{\\eta}\\) are the equivalent hydrodynamic radii in translational diffusive flow and viscous flow, and \\(\\alpha_{D}\\) and \\(\\alpha_{\\eta}\\) are the corresponding expansion factors."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12264 goldbook:12263)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12264 goldbook:12258)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12264 goldbook:12191)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12264 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12264 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12265))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12265 "Flory–Fox equation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12265 "Equation relating intrinsic viscosity, \\(\\eta\\), and molar mass, \\(M\\), to the mean-square radius of gyration, with \\[[\\eta]M = \\mathit{\\Phi}^{\\prime}\\!\\lt\\!s^{2}\\!\\gt^{3/2}\\] where \\(\\mathit{\\Phi}^{\\prime}\\) is a parameter the value of which depends on the molar-mass distribution, macromolecular constitution, and chain expansion.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12265 "\\([\\eta]M/N_{\\rm{A}}\\), where \\(N_{\\rm{A}}\\) is the Avogadro constant, is the equivalent hydrodynamic volume in viscous flow, \\(V_{\\eta}\\), with \\(V_{\\eta} = 4\\uppi r_{\\eta}^{3}/3\\), Hence, the Flory–Fox equation is consistent with the Kirkwood–Riseman theory and the Flory–Fox assumption. (See Notes to Kirkwood–Riseman theory and Flory–Fox assumption.)"^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12265 "For a solution in the theta state, \\(\\mathit{\\Phi}^{\\prime}\\) is denoted \\(\\mathit{\\Phi}_{\\uptheta}^{\\prime}\\) and its value is given by the Kirkwood–Riseman theory, with \\(\\mathit{\\Phi}_{\\uptheta}^{\\prime} = \\pu{4.22E22 mol-1}\\)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12265 "The Flory–Fox equation is sometimes written in terms of \\(\\lt\\!r^{2}\\!\\gt\\), the mean-square end-to-end distance, instead of \\(\\lt\\!s^{2}\\!\\gt\\), with \\[[\\eta]M = \\mathit{\\Phi} \\lt\\!r^{2}\\!\\gt^{3/2}\\] where \\(\\mathit{\\Phi} = \\mathit{\\Phi}^{\\prime}/6^{3/2}\\). The latter equality assumes that \\(\\lt\\!r^{2}\\!\\gt = 6\\!\\lt\\!s^{2}\\!\\gt\\), which is only exactly true in the theta state. In this case, \\[[\\eta]M = \\mathit{\\Phi}_{\\theta}\\!\\lt\\!r^{2}\\!\\gt^{3/2}\\] where \\(\\mathit{\\Phi}_{\\theta} = \\mathit{\\Phi}_{\\theta}/6^{3/2} = \\pu{2.87E21 mol-1}\\)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12265 "\\(\\mathit{\\Phi}\\) is known as the viscosity function or the Flory function."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12265 goldbook:12264)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12265 goldbook:12263)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12265 goldbook:12257)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12265 goldbook:12197)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12265 goldbook:12192)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12265 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12265 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12266))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12266 "Rouse theory")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12266 "Molecular theory for treating polymer chain dynamics based on the bead-spring model assuming the beads (segments) have zero excluded volume and there is no hydrodynamic interaction between the beads.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12266 goldbook:12253)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12266 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12266 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12267))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12267 "Rouse chain")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12267 "Hypothetical polymer chain satisfying the assumptions made in the Rouse theory.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12267 goldbook:12266)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12267 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12267 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12268))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12268 "reptation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12268 "Snake-like movement of a polymer chain in a semi-dilute or concentrated solution or bulk amorphous polymer through the hypothetical tube created by neighbouring chains.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12268 goldbook:12229)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12268 goldbook:12228)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12268 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12268 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12269))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12269 "tube model")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12269 "Model to describe the motion of a polymer chain confined in the hypothetical tube created by neighbouring chains.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12269 "In the tube model, the polymer chain moves along the hypothetical tube defined by the neighbouring polymer chains. The tube is continually undergoing tube renewal."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12269 "The tube model is an essential concept for reptation."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12269 goldbook:12268)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12269 goldbook:12270)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12269 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12269 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12270))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12270 "tube renewal")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12270 "Dynamic renewal of tubes by the disentanglement and re-entanglement of polymer chains.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12270 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12270 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12271))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12271 "primitive chain")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12271 "Polymer chain allowed to undergo reptation along the tube created by neighbouring chains.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12271 "The chain can be depicted as a connected sequence of blobs."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12271 goldbook:12232)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12271 goldbook:12268)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12271 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12271 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12272))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12272 "uniform dispersion")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12272 "Dispersion of particles of identical size, shape, and constitution.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12272 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12272 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12273))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12273 "non-uniform dispersion")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12273 "Dispersion of particles not identical with respect to size, shape, or constitution.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12273 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12273 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12274))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12274 "static light scattering")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12274 "Experimental method based on the measurement of the time-averaged intensity of light scattered from a polymer solutions or a dispersion of particles at various angles with respect to the incident beam.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12274 "SLS")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12274 "SLS is an absolute method, i.e., one not requiring calibration, for the determination of the molar mass of a macromolecular substance or dispersion of particles."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12274 "Measurement of the angular dependence of the time-averaged intensity of light scattered from a dilute solution of macromolecules or a dilute dispersion of particles that are not negligibly small with respect to the wavelength of the incident light can be used to evaluate an average radius of gyration of the solute macromolecules or dispersed particles."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12274 "Measurement of the concentration dependence of the intensity of light scattered from a dilute solution of macromolecules or a dilute dispersion of particles yields information on the thermodynamic interaction between the solute and solvent or dispersed particles and dispersion medium in terms of the second osmotic virial coefficient and, less frequently, higher virial coefficients."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12274 goldbook:12227)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12274 goldbook:12214)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12274 goldbook:12239)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12274 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12274 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12275))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12275 "dynamic light scattering")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12275 "Experimental method based on the measurement of the time autocorrelation function of the intensity of light scattered from a polymer solution or a dispersion of particles.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12275 "DLS")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12275 "photon-correlation spectroscopy (PCS)")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12275 "quasi-elastic light scattering (QELS)")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12275 "The basic information that can be obtained from the time autocorrelation function of a polymer solution or a dispersion is: (i) for a uniform polymer or a uniform dispersion, the diffusion coefficient of the macromolecules or the dispersed particles; (ii) for a non-uniform polymer or a non-uniform dispersion, the distribution function of diffusion coefficients of the macromolecules or the dispersed particles."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12275 goldbook:12273)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12275 goldbook:12272)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12275 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12275 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12276))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12276 "small molecule")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12276 "Molecule much smaller than the wavelength of the radiation in the solvent used.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12276 "For a molecule to be considered to be small, the lengths of all of its dimensions must be less than about one-twentieth of the wavelength employed."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12276 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12276 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12277))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12277 "large molecule")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12277 "Molecule of size similar to or larger than the wavelength of the radiation in the solvent used.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12277 "A molecule is treated as large if the length of its largest dimension exceeds about one-twentieth of the wavelength employed."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12277 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12277 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12278))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12278 "excess scattering")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12278 "Difference between the scattering intensity for a dilute solution or a dilute dispersion and that for the pure solvent or the dispersion medium at the same scattering angle.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12278 goldbook:12227)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12278 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12278 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12279))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12279 "static structure factor")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12279 "Function describing the dependence of relative scattering intensity on the magnitude of the scattering vector, \\(q\\), for a polymer solution or a dispersion.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12279 "The static structure factor accounts for interference of the scattered radiation within individual macromolecules or individual dispersed particles, described by the form factor, as well as interference of the scattered radiation from different macromolecules or dispersed particles, reflecting the ordering of the positions of the scattering entities."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12279 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12279 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12280))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12280 "dynamic structure factor")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12280 "Function describing the temporal dependence of relative scattering intensity on the magnitude of the scattering vector, \\(q\\).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12280 "The value of the dynamic structure factor is characteristic of the various modes of motions of the polymer molecules or the dispersed particles and their parts and is also characteristic of the time-dependent interference of scattering, reflecting ordering of the positions of the scattering entities in time. In dynamic light scattering, it can be derived from the time autocorrelation function."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12280 goldbook:12275)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12280 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12280 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12281))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12281 "elution time")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12281 "Time elapsed from the injection of the sample into a chromatography bed to the recording of a specified signal of the detector due to the sample having passed through the bed.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12281 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12281 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12282))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12282 "elution volume")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12282 "Volume of solvent that has passed through a chromatography bed from the injection of the sample to the recording of a specified signal of the detector due to the sample having passed through the bed.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12282 doi:10.1515/pac-2013-0201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12282 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12283))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12283 "transfer coefficient")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12283 "The anodic transfer coefficient \\(\\alpha_{\\rm{a}}\\) and the cathodic transfer coefficient \\(\\alpha_{\\rm{c}}\\) are defined by the following equations: \\[\\alpha_{\\rm{a}} = (RT/F)({\\rm{d}}\\ln\\! j_{\\rm{a}}/{\\rm{d}}E); \\quad \\alpha_{\\rm{c}} = -(RT/F)({\\rm{d}}\\ln\\!\\vert {j_{\\rm{c}}} \\vert /{\\rm{d}}E)\\] In these equations, \\(j_{\\rm{a}}\\) and \\(j_{\\rm{c}}\\) are the anodic and cathodic current densities, respectively, corrected for any changes in the reactant concentration at the electrode surface with respect to its bulk value; incidentally, the symbols \\(\\ln\\! j_{\\rm{a}}\\) and \\(\\ln\\!\\vert j_{\\rm{c}}\\vert\\) imply that the argument of the logarithm is of dimension one, obtained by division with the corresponding unit, e.g., \\(\\ln\\! j_{\\rm{a}}\\) meaning \\(\\ln(j_{\\rm{a}}/\\pu{A m^{-2}})\\), and similarly for the other quantities \\(\\vert j_{\\rm{c}}\\vert\\), \\(k_{\\rm{a}}\\) and \\(k_{\\rm{c}}\\). \\(E\\) is the applied electric potential, \\(R\\) is the gas constant, \\(T\\) is the thermodynamic temperature, and \\(F\\) is the Faraday constant. In practice, \\(\\alpha_{\\rm{a}}\\) and \\(\\alpha_{\\rm{c}}\\) are defined as the reciprocal of the corresponding Tafel slopes, \\({\\rm{d}}E/{\\rm{d}}\\ln\\! j_{\\rm{a}}\\) and \\(-{\\rm{d}}E/{\\rm{d}} \\ln\\! \\vert j_{\\rm{c}} \\vert\\), made dimensionless by the multiplying factor \\(RT/F\\). Both the transfer coefficient and the Tafel slope are determined at constant temperature and pressure.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12283 doi:10.1515/pac-2014-5025)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12283 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12284))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12284 "combined technique")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12284 "Application of two or more techniques to different samples at the same time. This can include thermal and nonthermal analytical techniques.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12284 goldbook:12306)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12284 doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12284 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12285))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12285 "controlled-rate thermal analysis")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12285 "Sample-controlled method where the feedback used to control the heating is the rate of transformation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12285 "CRTA")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12285 doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12285 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12286))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12286 "controlled temperature program")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12286 "Temperature history imposed on the sample during the course of the thermal analysis experiment.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12286 doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12286 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12287))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12287 "cooling curve")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12287 "Experimental result of measuring the temperature of the sample as a function of time during cooling. Heating curves are obtained for temperature-time experiments during heating.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12287 doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12287 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12288))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12288 "derivative technique")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12288 "Pertaining to the \\(1^{\\rm{st}}\\) derivative (mathematical) of any curve with respect to temperature or time.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12288 doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12288 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12289))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12289 "dielectric thermal analysis")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12289 "Technique where dielectric properties are measured.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12289 "DEA")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12289 doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12289 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12290))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12290 "differential technique")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12290 "Pertaining to a difference in measured or measurable quantities usually between a sample and a reference or standard material.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12290 doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12290 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12291))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12291 "heat-flow differential scanning calorimetry")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12291 "Technique where the difference between the heat-flow rates into a sample and a reference material is measured.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12291 "DSC")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12291 "heat-flow DSC")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12291 doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12291 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12292))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12292 "power compensation differential scanning calorimetry")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12292 "Technique where the difference between the electrical powers into a sample and a reference material is measured.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12292 "DSC")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12292 "power compensation DSC")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12292 doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12292 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12293))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12293 "dynamic technique")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12293 "Indicates, especially in the mechanical analysis of materials, that a parameter changes continuously during the experiment.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12293 goldbook:12307)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12293 doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12293 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12294))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12294 "dynamic mechanical analysis")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12294 "Technique where storage and loss viscoelastic moduli are determined with the help of a periodical stress.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12294 "DMA")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12294 doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12294 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12295))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12295 "gas flow")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12295 "Passage of gas from one part of the system to another. The gas may be either inert (carrier gas) or reactive, either introduced into the system or evolving from the sample.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12295 doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12295 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12296))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12296 "isothermal technique")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12296 "Applied to a technique to indicate that the temperature is maintained constant throughout the experiment.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12296 doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12296 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12297))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12297 "material")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12297 "The substance which is studied and from which the sample is taken.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12297 doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12297 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12298))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12298 "micro- technique")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12298 "Prefix used to denote that the technique measures small quantities, either with respect to the amount of sample studied, or with respect to the change in the properties measured.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12298 "This prefix has been applied to many thermal methods, and the equipment associated with them, for example, microbalance, microreactor, microcalorimeter and also to the technique itself: microthermal, microscopic, and the property studied: microstructural."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12298 "The opposite prefix, macro-, is also occasionally used."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12298 "Mathematically, micro = \\(\\upmu\\) = \\(\\pu{E-6}\\)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12298 doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12298 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12299))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12299 "modulated technique")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12299 "Indicates that a parameter changes in a periodic manner during the experiment.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12299 doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12299 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12300))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12300 "modulated temperature technique")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12300 "Applied to the technique name to indicate that a temperature modulation has been applied to the temperature program.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12300 "MT")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12300 "The prefix TM is occasionally used instead, but not recommended."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12300 doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12300 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12301))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12301 "photo- technique")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12301 "Indicates that the experiment involves the illumination of the sample or measures the amount of light emitted from a sample. Where possible, the wavelength range of the light should be specified.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12301 doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12301 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12302))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12302 "sample controlled technique")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12302 "Applied to the technique to indicate that a property of the sample is used either continuously or discontinuously to control the sample heating. Without this term, it is assumed that the experiment is following a controlled-temperature program.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12302 "The generic term for all TA techniques making use of such feedback is sample-controlled TA (SCTA), whereas specific names will be of the form sample-controlled TGA (SC-TGA), etc."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12302 doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12302 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12303))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12303 "scan")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12303 "A term used to describe the data produced from a thermal analysis experiment. More correct usage is a thermal analysis curve, or, for a specific technique thermogravimetric curve, etc.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12303 "thermal analysis curve")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12303 "This term is discouraged."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12303 doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12303 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12304))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12304 "scanning technique")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12304 "Indicates that a specified experimental parameter, if not temperature, is changed in a controlled manner.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12304 doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12304 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12305))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12305 "scanning calorimetry")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12305 "Techniques where heat is measured as a function of temperature.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12305 doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12305 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12306))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12306 "simultaneous technique")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12306 "Indicates the measurement of two or more properties of a single sample at the same time.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12306 "A hyphen is used to separate the abbreviations of the techniques; for example, simultaneous measurement of mass and heat flow rate (thermogravimetric analysis and differential scanning calorimetry) would be TGA-DSC."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12306 goldbook:12284)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12306 doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12306 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12307))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12307 "static technique")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12307 "Indicates, especially in the mechanical analysis of materials, a constant parameter during the experiment.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12307 goldbook:12293)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12307 doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12307 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12308))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12308 "stepwise technique")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12308 "Indicates discrete, discontinuous changes in an experimental parameter, e.g., force, temperature, etc.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12308 doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12308 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12309))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12309 "tan $\\delta$")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12309 "The dimensionless ratio of energy lost to energy returned during one cycle of a periodic process.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12309 goldbook:12294)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12309 doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12309 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12310))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12310 "temperature-programmed desorption")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12310 "EGA using an inert atmosphere or vacuum, in the absence of sample decomposition.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12310 "TPD")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12310 doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12310 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12311))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12311 "temperature-programmed oxidation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12311 "Experiment using an oxidising atmosphere, usually oxygen. Oxidation is monitored by any appropriate technique (EGA, TGA, gas sorption, etc.).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12311 "TPO")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12311 doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12311 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12312))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12312 "temperature-programmed reduction")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12312 "Experiment using a reducing atmosphere, usually hydrogen. Reduction is monitored by any appropriate technique (EGA, TGA, gas sorption, etc.).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12312 "TPR")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12312 doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12312 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12313))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12313 "thermal curve")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12313 "Any graph of any combination of property, time, temperature derived from a thermal analysis technique.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12313 "thermoanalytical curve")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12313 "Thermal curve is a loose abbreviation of the more correct term thermoanalytical curve."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12313 "This term is discouraged."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12313 doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12313 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12314))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12314 "thermally stimulated current")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12314 "Electrical current observed during heating and caused by the thermally initiated relaxation of the frozen-in electrical polarization of a sample.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12314 "TSC")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12314 "By extension, the same name and abbreviation (TSC) are given to the thermal analysis technique based on the measurement of this current."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12314 goldbook:12315)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12314 doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12314 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12315))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12315 "thermally stimulated depolarisation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12315 "Relaxation of frozen-in electrical polarization caused by a temperature increase.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12315 "The effect is measured through the thermally stimulated current."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12315 goldbook:12314)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12315 doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12315 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12316))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12316 "thermo- technique")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12316 "Indicating the use of changing temperature during the experiment, when in the name of a thermal analysis technique.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12316 doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12316 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12317))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12317 "thermoanalytical")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12317 "Of, or pertaining to, thermal analysis.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12317 doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12317 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12318))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12318 "thermodiffractometry")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12318 "A technique where the X-ray diffraction of the sample is measured.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12318 doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12318 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12319))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12319 "thermogravimetric analysis")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12319 "A technique where the mass of the sample is measured, also known as thermogravimetry.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12319 "TGA")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12319 "thermogravimetry (TG)")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12319 doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12319 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12320))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12320 "thermomanometry")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12320 "A technique where the gas pressure is measured.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12320 doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12320 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12321))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12321 "thermomechanical analysis")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12321 "A technique where the deformation of the sample is measured under constant load.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12321 "TMA")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12321 doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12321 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12322))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12322 "thermomicroscopy")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12322 "A technique where the optical properties of the sample are observed and measured through a microscope.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12322 doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12322 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12323))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12323 "thermospectrometry")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12323 "A group of techniques where a spectrum of the sample is measured.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12323 doi:10.1515/pac-2012-0609)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12323 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12324))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12324 "absolute quantitation of proteins")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12324 "Method for absolute quantitation of proteins via measurements on constituent proteolytic peptides using chemically synthesized isotope-labeled peptides as surrogate internal standards for mass spectrometry.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003012) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12324 "AQUA")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12324 goldbook:12589)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12324 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12324 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12325))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12325 "accelerating potential")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12325 "Electrical potential difference used to impart translational energy to ions.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12325 "Accelerating voltage is often used as a synonym, but the terms are equivalent only in the case of a static accelerating potential."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12325 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12325 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12326))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12326 "accurate mass")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12326 "Experimentally determined mass of an ion of known charge.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12326 "Can be used to determine elemental composition to within limits defined by both the accuracy and precision of the measurement."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12326 "Accurate mass and exact mass are not synonymous. Accurate mass refers to a measured mass, and exact mass refers to a calculated mass."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12326 goldbook:12407)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12326 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12326 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12327))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12327 "accurate mass tag")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12327 "Value of the mass of a peptide from a protein that has been chemically or enzymatically cleaved into fragments. The mass is recorded with sufficiently high accuracy and precision that it can be used in identification of the protein.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12327 goldbook:12522)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12327 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12327 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12328))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12328 "a-ion")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12328 "Fragment ion containing the peptide \\(\\ce{N}\\)-terminus formed upon dissociation of a peptide ion at the peptide backbone \\(\\ce{C-C}\\) bond.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12328 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12328 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12329))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12329 "alkyl cation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12329 "Even-electron positively charged saturated hydrocarbon ion containing no aromatic groups, a special case of carbenium ions.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12329 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12329 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12330))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12330 "all-glass heated inlet system")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12330 "All-glass inlet system for ion sources operating under vacuum that can be heated to about \\(\\pu{500^{\\circ}C}\\) and allows low vapor pressure materials to be introduced into the mass spectrometer without breaking vacuum.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003012) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12330 "AGHIS")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12330 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12330 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12331))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12331 "allyl cation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12331 "Even-electron ion formulated as \\(\\ce{R^{1}R^{2}C=CR^{3}C+R^{4}R^{5}}\\) and its resonance forms.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12331 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12331 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12332))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12332 "ambient ionization")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12332 "Desorption of molecules and formation of ions outside the mass spectrometer directly from samples in their native environment with no or minimal sample preparation.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12332 "\"Direct analysis in real time\" is a proprietary term indicating the formation of ions from a solid or liquid sample at atmospheric pressure through the interaction of a gas stream containing internally excited atoms or molecules with the surface. The excited-state species are typically formed in a glow discharge in helium or nitrogen. The term should only be used to describe the commercial product."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12332 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12332 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12333))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12333 "ambient mass spectrometry")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12333 "Mass spectrometry analysis performed using an ambient ionization technique.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12333 goldbook:12332)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12333 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12333 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12334))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12334 "angle resolved mass spectrometry")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12334 "Technique used to investigate details of the collisional excitation process by studying trends relating scattering angle of the precursor ion, internal energy transferred, and the masses of the ion and its collision partner.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12334 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12334 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12335))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12335 "anionized molecule")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12335 "Ion formed by the association of an anion with a molecule, \\(\\ce{M}\\).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12335 "The terms quasi-molecular ion and pseudo-molecular ion are deprecated and should not be used in place of anionized molecule."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12335 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12335 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12336))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12336 "atmospheric pressure chemical ionization")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12336 "Chemical ionization of a sample that is a gas or nebulized liquid, using an atmospheric pressure corona discharge or beta emitter such as \\(\\ce{^{63}Ni}\\).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12336 "APCI")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12336 goldbook:12373)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12336 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12336 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12337))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12337 "atmospheric pressure matrix-assisted laser desorption/ionization")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12337 "Matrix-assisted laser desorption/ionization in which the sample target is at atmospheric pressure.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12337 "AP MALDI")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12337 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12337 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12338))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12338 "atmospheric pressure photoionization")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12338 "Direct ionization of molecules at atmospheric pressure by electron detachment induced by photons forming \\(\\ce{M^{+.}}\\), or atmospheric pressure chemical ionization in which the reactant ions are generated by photoionization of suitable dopant species and subsequent ion/molecule reactions of their molecular ions.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12338 "APPI")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12338 goldbook:12336)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12338 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12338 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12339))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12339 "autodetachment")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12339 "Process whereby a negative ion in a discrete state with energy greater than the detachment threshold loses an electron spontaneously without further interaction with an energy source.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12339 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12339 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12340))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12340 "auxiliary gas")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12340 "Gas used in a spray ion source in addition to the nebulizing gas to aid in solvent removal.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12340 goldbook:12365)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12340 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12340 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12341))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12341 "average mass")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12341 "Mass of an ion or molecule weighted for its isotopic composition.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12341 goldbook:12495)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12341 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12341 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12342))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12342 "axial ejection")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12342 "Ejection of an ion from an ion trap in a direction parallel to the longitudinal axis of the trap.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12342 goldbook:12447)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12342 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12342 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12343))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12343 "axialization")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12343 "Technique used in Fourier-transform ion cyclotron resonance mass spectrometers to limit the translational motion of the trapped ions so that they occupy a small volume near the trap center, thus optimizing performance criteria including resolving power.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12343 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12343 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12344))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12344 "base peak chromatogram")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12344 "Chromatogram obtained by plotting the signal of the ions represented by the base peak detected in each of a series of mass spectra recorded as a function of retention time.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12344 "BPC")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12344 "base peak ion chromatogram")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12344 "This term should be used for samples introduced following a chromatographic separation."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12344 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12344 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12345))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12345 "beam mass spectrometer")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12345 "Mass spectrometer in which an ion beam accelerated from the ion source is transmitted through a m/z analyzer, or analyzers, to the detector.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12345 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12345 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12346))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12346 "benzyl ion")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12346 "Even-electron ion \\(\\ce{C7H7^{+}}\\) with the same carbon skeleton as toluene that has lost a hydrogen atom from the methyl side-chain that carries the positive charge.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12346 goldbook:12597)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12346 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12346 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12347))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12347 "b-ion")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12347 "Fragment ion containing the peptide \\(\\ce{N}\\)-terminus formed upon dissociation of a peptide ion at the peptide backbone \\(\\ce{C-N}\\) bond.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12347 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12347 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12348))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12348 "blackbody infrared radiative dissociation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12348 "Special case of infrared multiphoton dissociation wherein excitation of the reactant ion is caused by absorption of infrared photons radiating from heated blackbody surroundings, which are usually the walls of a vacuum chamber.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003012) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12348 "BIRD")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12348 goldbook:12433)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12348 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12348 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12349))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12349 "Brubaker lens")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12349 "Additional set of four short, cylindrical electrodes, mounted co-linearly with a transmission quadrupole mass spectrometer that is excited with some fraction of the AC potential but not the DC potential applied to the main quadrupole. The Brubaker lens thus acts as a high-pass filter for ion m/z, but the resulting delay in application of the DC potential component also results in a reduction in defocusing by fringe fields and thus significantly improves overall ion transmission efficiency at a given mass resolution.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12349 "Brubaker pre-filter")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12349 goldbook:12420)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12349 goldbook:12601)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12349 goldbook:12602)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12349 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12349 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12350))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12350 "buffer gas")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12350 "Inert gas used for collisional reduction of the internal or translational energy of ions, such as in ion traps.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12350 "bath gas")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12350 goldbook:12362)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12350 goldbook:12447)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12350 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12350 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12351))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12351 "centroid acquisition")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12351 "Procedure of recording mass spectra in which an automated computer-based system detects peaks, calculates the centroid based on the average m/z value weighted by the intensity, and assigns m/z values based on a calibration file. Only the centroid m/z value and the peak magnitude are stored.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12351 goldbook:12536)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12351 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12351 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12352))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12352 "charged residue model")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12352 "Theoretical model for production of highly charged macromolecules by electrospray ionization in which the excess charges on electrosprayed droplets are transferred to and remain on molecules enclosed within the droplets after solvent evaporation.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12352 goldbook:12438)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12352 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12352 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12353))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12353 "charge inversion reaction")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12353 "Reaction of an ion with a neutral, surface, or ion of opposite polarity, in which the charge on the product ion is reversed in sign with respect to the reactant ion.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12353 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12353 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12354))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12354 "charge-mediated fragmentation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12354 "Fragmentation of an ion in which the cleavage of one of its bonds is induced by the charge site. The cleaved bond is adjacent to the apparent charge site, and its cleavage involves movement of the electron pair forming that bond to the original charge site and thus migration of the charge to the released fragment.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12354 "heterolytic fragmentation; inductive cleavage")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12354 goldbook:12355)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12354 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12354 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12355))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12355 "charge remote fragmentation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12355 "Fragmentation of an ion in which the cleaved bond is isolated from the apparent charge site by a distance of several bond lengths.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12355 "CRF")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12355 goldbook:12354)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12355 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12355 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12356))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12356 "charge site derivatization")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12356 "Chemical derivatization of molecules to introduce a fixed charge site, thus improving ionization efficiency by electrospray ionization or matrix-assisted laser desorption/ionization and directing subsequent ion fragmentation in a manner that facilitates structure identification.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12356 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12356 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12357))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12357 "c-ion")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12357 "Fragment ion containing the peptide \\(\\ce{N}\\)-terminus formed upon dissociation of a peptide ion at the peptide backbone \\(\\ce{N-C}\\) bond.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12357 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12357 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12358))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12358 "coaxial reflectron")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12358 "Reflectron that is arranged such that its main axis is coaxial with the ion source and first stage of the time-of-flight analyzer.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12358 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12358 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12359))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12359 "collector slit")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12359 "Slit installed in a magnetic sector mass spectrometer to allow only those m/z separated ions with a specific m/z into the detector system.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12359 goldbook:12473)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12359 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12359 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12360))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12360 "collisional focusing")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12360 "Effect where collisions with a buffer gas in a radio-frequency ion trap or transmission quadrupole causes ions to lose translational energy and concentrate at the center of the trap or axis of the linear quadrupole. The effect increases with gas pressure up to a point where ion scattering becomes the dominant process.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12360 goldbook:12350)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12360 goldbook:12447)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12360 goldbook:12602)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12360 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12360 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12361))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12361 "collision cell")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12361 "Chamber in the ion path between m/z separation elements, or between ion source acceleration region and the first analyzer, in tandem mass spectrometry in space configurations.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12361 goldbook:12364)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12361 goldbook:12591)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12361 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12361 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12362))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12362 "collision gas")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12362 "Inert gas used for collisional excitation or a reactive gas used for ion/molecule reactions.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12362 goldbook:12350)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12362 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12362 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12363))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12363 "collision quadrupole")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12363 "Transmission quadrupole to which an oscillating radio frequency potential is applied so as to focus a beam of ions through a collision gas or buffer gas with no m/z separation other than low m/z cut-off.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12363 "Higher-order multipoles can also be used in this manner."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12363 goldbook:12560)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12363 goldbook:12602)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12363 goldbook:12350)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12363 goldbook:12362)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12363 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12363 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12364))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12364 "collision reaction cell")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12364 "Collision cell for removal of interfering ions by ion/neutral reactions in inductively coupled plasma mass spectrometry.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12364 "CRC")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12364 goldbook:12361)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12364 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12364 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12365))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12365 "concentric nebulizer")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12365 "Pneumatic nebulizer in which the liquid flows through a central capillary and dispersion gas flows through a surrounding outer tube.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12365 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12365 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12366))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12366 "consecutive reaction monitoring")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12366 "Multiple-stage mass spectrometry experiment with three or more stages of m/z separation in which products of sequential fragmentation or bimolecular reactions are selected for detection.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12366 "CRM")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12366 goldbook:12501)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12366 goldbook:12500)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12366 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12366 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12367))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12367 "constant neutral mass gain spectrum")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12367 "Spectrum formed of all precursor ions that have undergone a selected m/z increase corresponding to the mass of a particular neutral species divided by the charge number of the precursor. The ions detected are the product ions produced by gain of a preselected neutral species mass following ion/molecule reactions of the precursor ions with a reactant gas in a collision cell.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12367 "fixed neutral gain spectrum")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12367 "fixed neutral mass gain spectrum")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12367 goldbook:12361)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12367 goldbook:12368)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12367 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12367 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12368))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12368 "constant neutral mass loss spectrum")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12368 "Spectrum of all precursor ions that have undergone a selected m/z decrement corresponding to the mass of a particular neutral divided by the charge number of the precursor. The ions detected are the product ions produced by loss of a preselected neutral mass following collision-induced dissociation of the precursor ions in a collision cell.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12368 "fixed neutral loss spectrum")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12368 "fixed neutral mass loss spectrum")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12368 goldbook:12361)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12368 goldbook:12367)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12368 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12368 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12369))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12369 "continuous dynode particle multiplier")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12369 "Ion-to-electron detector in which the ion strikes the inner surface of a continuous tube device and induces the production of secondary electrons that, in turn, impinge on the inner surfaces of the device to produce more secondary electrons. This avalanche effect produces an increase in the final measured current pulse.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12369 "channel electron multiplier")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12369 goldbook:12395)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12369 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12369 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12370))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12370 "continuous-flow fast atom bombardment")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12370 "Variant of fast atom bombardment in which the mixture of analyte and liquid matrix is continuously supplied to the sample probe tip.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12370 "CF-FAB")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12370 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12370 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12371))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12371 "continuous-flow matrix-assisted laser desorption/ionization")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12371 "Variant of matrix-assisted laser desorption/ionization in which the analyte is dissolved in a liquid matrix that is continuously supplied to the sample probe tip.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12371 "CF-MALDI")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12371 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12371 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12372))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12372 "conversion dynode")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12372 "Surface that is held at high potential so that ions striking the surface produce secondary charged particles that are subsequently detected.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12372 "For positive ions, the potential is negative and the secondary particles are electrons and negative ions. For negative ions, the potential is positive and the secondary particles are positive ions."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12372 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12372 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12373))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12373 "corona discharge")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12373 "Electric discharge generated in a gas, usually at atmospheric pressure, surrounding a conductor carrying a sufficiently high potential that the electric field around it ionizes the gas so as to form a plasma in the immediate vicinity of the conductor without causing complete electric breakdown or arcing.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12373 "A corona discharge can also be sustained in a liquid."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12373 goldbook:12422)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12373 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12373 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12374))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12374 "corona discharge ionization")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12374 "Formation of ions in a corona discharge.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12374 goldbook:12373)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12374 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12374 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12375))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12375 "counter-current gas")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12375 "Stream of inert gas, often heated, that is used in an electrospray or other spray ionization source to aid in the evaporation of solvent from the sprayed particles. The flow of the gas is in the direction opposite to that of the spray.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12375 "Curtain gas is a proprietary term used to indicate a flow of counter-current gas emanating from between two closely spaced plates each with a central orifice along the axis of a spray ionization source. The term should only be used to describe the commercial device."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12375 goldbook:12398)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12375 goldbook:12579)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12375 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12375 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12376))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12376 "counter electrode")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12376 "Counter electrode in an electrospray ionization ion source is one of two electrodes between which the high electric potential is applied, the other electrode being the electrospray needle.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12376 goldbook:12404)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12376 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12376 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12377))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12377 "cross-flow nebulizer")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12377 "Pneumatic nebulizer in which the dispersion gas flows at an angle, usually \\(\\pu{90\\!^{\\circ}}\\), with respect to the column of liquid emerging from a capillary.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12377 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12377 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12378))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12378 "curved field reflectron")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12378 "Reflectron designed to provide a decelerating field strength that varies with depth of ion penetration and thus with ion translational energy, permitting energy focusing of ions with a range of translational energies such as those formed as product ions from post-source decay of metastable ions.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12378 goldbook:12530)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12378 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12378 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12379))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12379 "cyclotron motion")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12379 "Circular motion of a charged particle moving perpendicularly to the direction of a magnetic field that results from the Lorentz force.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12379 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12379 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12380))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12380 "Daly detector")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12380 "Detector consisting of an off-axis conversion dynode, scintillator, and photomultiplier. The dynode at high potential emits secondary electrons when ions impinge on the surface. The secondary electrons are accelerated onto the scintillator that produces light that is then detected by the photomultiplier detector, which can be outside the vacuum system.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12380 goldbook:12372)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12380 goldbook:12446)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12380 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12380 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12381))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12381 "data-dependent acquisition")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12381 "Mode of data collection in tandem mass spectrometry in which a fixed number of precursor ions whose m/z values were recorded in a survey scan are selected using predetermined rules and are subjected to a second stage of mass selection in an MS/MS analysis.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12381 goldbook:12485)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12381 goldbook:12591)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12381 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12381 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12382))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12382 "deconvoluted mass spectrum")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12382 "Mass spectrum processed with an algorithm designed to extract a desired signal or signals from raw experimental data in which the desired signals have been complicated (convolved) by some interferences or in some other way.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12382 "Examples of deconvoluted mass spectra include mass spectra corrected for instrumental mass bias, or extraction of spectra for pure components from the spectrum of a mixture, or a mass (not m/z) spectrum of a biopolymer from an electrospray ionization spectrum containing peaks corresponding to several charge states."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12382 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12382 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12383))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12383 "delayed extraction")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12383 "Application of the accelerating voltage pulse after a time delay in desorption ionization from a surface.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12383 "DE")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12383 "The extraction delay can produce energy focusing in a time-of-flight mass spectrometer."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12383 goldbook:12325)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12383 goldbook:12386)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12383 goldbook:12596)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12383 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12383 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12384))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12384 "deprotonated molecule")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12384 "Ion formed by the removal of a proton from a molecule \\(\\ce{M}\\) to produce an anion represented as \\(\\ce{[M - H]^{-}}\\).")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12384 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12384 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12385))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12385 "desorption chemical ionization")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12385 "Formation of gas-phase ions by chemical ionization of gaseous molecules produced by the rapid heating and desorption of a solid or low vapour pressure liquid.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12385 "DCI")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12385 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12385 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12386))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12386 "desorption ionization")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12386 "Formation of gas phase ions from a solid or liquid sample surface upon activation by heat, strong electric field, particles, droplets, or photon bombardment.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12386 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12386 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12387))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12387 "desorption ionization on silicon")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12387 "Soft ionization alternative to matrix-assisted desorption/ionization involving laser desorption ionization of a sample deposited on a porous silicon surface.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003012) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12387 "DIOS")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12387 goldbook:12575)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12387 goldbook:12463)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12387 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12387 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12388))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12388 "diagnostic ion")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12388 "Product ion whose formation reveals structural or compositional information about its precursor ion.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12388 "For example, the phenyl cation in an electron ionization mass spectrum is a diagnostic ion for benzene and derivatives."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12388 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12388 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12389))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12389 "dielectric barrier discharge ionization")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12389 "Atmospheric pressure chemical ionization in which the low-temperature plasma is not generated by a corona discharge but by a device consisting of two electrodes with at least one dielectric layer that separates the electrode from the plasma.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12389 goldbook:12336)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12389 goldbook:12373)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12389 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12389 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12390))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12390 "d-ion")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12390 "High-energy fragment ion of a protonated peptide, formally equivalent to a fragment ion formed by homolytic cleavage of a peptide \\(\\ce{C-N}\\) bond together with the part of the \\(\\ce{C}\\)-terminal side-chain starting at the \\(\\ce{\\upgamma\\mbox{-}carbon}\\) (if any).")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12390 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12390 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12391))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12391 "direct exposure probe")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12391 "Device based on a modification of a direct insertion probe for exposing an involatile sample directly to the electron beam (in an electron ionization source) or to a chemical ionization plasma as in desorption chemical ionization.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003012) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12391 "DEP")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12391 "The sample can be deposited on an inert surface or on a heater filament for rapid heating."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12391 goldbook:12385)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12391 goldbook:12393)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12391 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12391 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12392))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12392 "direct infusion")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12392 "Method of liquid sample introduction in which the sample is continuously flowed into a mass spectrometer ion source.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12392 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12392 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12393))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12393 "direct insertion probe")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12393 "Device for introducing a single sample of a solid or liquid, usually contained in a quartz or other nonreactive sample holder, into a mass spectrometer ion source.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003012) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12393 "DIP")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12393 goldbook:12391)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12393 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12393 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12394))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12394 "direct liquid introduction")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12394 "Direct delivery of a liquid sample at a low solvent flow rate into the chemical ionization ion source of a mass spectrometer. The solvent vapour can act as the reagent gas.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12394 "DLI")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12394 goldbook:12546)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12394 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12394 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12395))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12395 "discrete dynode particle multiplier")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12395 "Ion-to-electron detector in which the ion strikes the surface of an electrode and induces the production of secondary electrons. In turn, these impinge in sequence on dynodes at a more positive electric potential to produce more secondary electrons. This avalanche effect produces an amplification of several orders of magnitude in the final measured current pulse.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12395 goldbook:12369)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12395 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12395 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12396))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12396 "dissociative electron capture")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12396 "Ionization mechanism in which capture of a low-energy electron by a molecule leads directly to a dissociative state of the nascent anion, an example of dissociative ionization.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12396 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12396 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12397))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12397 "drift tube")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12397 "Cylindrical chamber containing a buffer gas. Ions introduced at one end are caused to move to the other end by either a flow of the buffer gas or by a uniform longitudinal electric field.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12397 goldbook:12350)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12397 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12397 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12398))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12398 "drying gas")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12398 "Inert gas that is used to promote the removal of solvent from aerosol particles in spray ionization.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12398 goldbook:12375)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12398 goldbook:12579)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12398 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12398 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12399))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12399 "dynamic exclusion")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12399 "Software method used to minimize repeat selections of identical precursor ions for collision-induced dissociation in replicate chromatography-tandem mass spectrometry analyses of complex mixtures.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12399 goldbook:12381)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12399 goldbook:12591)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12399 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12399 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12400))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12400 "einzel lens")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12400 "Three-element charged particle lens in which the first and third elements are maintained at the same electric potential. Such a lens produces focusing without changing the translational energy of the particle.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12400 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12400 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12401))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12401 "electrohydrodynamic ionization")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12401 "Ionization process that produces charged droplets and gas-phase ions from a liquid under vacuum with the application of an electric field.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12401 "The process is formally equivalent to sub-ambient pressure electrospray ionization."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12401 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12401 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12402))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12402 "electron capture dissociation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12402 "Process in which multiply protonated molecules interact with low-energy electrons followed by fragmentation. The capture of an electron by the even-electron cation \\(\\ce{[M + nH]^{n+}}\\) liberates energy and reduces its charge state, thus producing the corresponding \\(\\ce{[M + nH]^{(n - 1)+.}}\\) odd-electron ion, which readily fragments.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12402 "ECD")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12402 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12402 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12403))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12403 "electron capture ionization")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12403 "Ionization of a gas-phase atom or molecule by attachment of a free electron to form molecular ions of the \\(\\ce{M^{-.}}\\) type.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12403 "ECI")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12403 "electron capture negative ionization")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12403 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12403 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12404))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12404 "electrospray needle")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12404 "Narrow bore tube from which highly charged droplets are emitted in electrospray ionization.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12404 "electrospray emitter")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12404 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12404 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12405))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12405 "electrostatic energy analyser")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12405 "Device consisting of pairs of parallel conducting plates, concentric cylinders, or concentric spheres that separate charged particles according to their ratio of translational energy to charge by means of a potential difference applied between the pair.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12405 "ESA")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12405 "electric sector")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12405 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12405 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12406))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12406 "even-electron rule")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12406 "Rule that states that even-electron ions tend to form even-electron fragment ions whereas odd-electron ions tend to dissociate to form either odd- or even-electron ions.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12406 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12406 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12407))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12407 "exact mass")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12407 "Calculated mass of an ion or molecule with specified isotopic composition.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12407 goldbook:12326)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12407 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12407 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12408))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12408 "extracted ion chromatogram")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12408 "Chromatogram created by plotting the intensity of the signal observed at a chosen m/z value or set of values in a series of mass spectra recorded as a function of retention time.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12408 "mass chromatogram")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12408 "reconstructed ion chromatogram")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12408 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12408 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12409))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12409 "extracted ion electropherogram")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12409 "Electropherogram created by plotting the intensity of the signal observed at a chosen m/z value or set of values in a series of mass spectra recorded as a function of electrophoresis time.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12409 "extracted ion electrophorogram")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12409 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12409 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12410))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12410 "extracted ion profile")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12410 "Any plot of signal intensity observed at a chosen m/z value or set of values in a series of mass spectra recorded as a function of time, including extracted ion chromatogram, extracted ion electropherogram, or from flow injection analysis or any other time-dependent sampling.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12410 goldbook:12408)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12410 goldbook:12409)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12410 goldbook:12600)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12410 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12410 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12411))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12411 "fast ion bombardment")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12411 "Ionization of any species by the interaction of a focused beam of ions, with a translational energy of several thousand \\(\\pu{eV}\\), with a solid or liquid sample.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003012) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12411 "FIB")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12411 "For a liquid sample, fast ion bombardment is the same as liquid secondary ionization."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12411 goldbook:12469)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12411 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12411 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12412))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12412 "field-free region")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12412 "Section of a mass spectrometer in which there are no electric or magnetic fields.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12412 "FFR")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12412 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12412 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12413))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12413 "first stability region")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12413 "Stability region of a Mathieu stability diagram closest to the origin.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12413 "Ions within this region can traverse the full length of a transmission quadrupole or can be trapped in a Paul ion trap."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12413 goldbook:12486)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12413 goldbook:12516)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12413 goldbook:12602)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12413 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12413 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12414))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12414 "fixed precursor ion spectrum")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12414 "Spectrum obtained when data are acquired that determine the m/z values of product ions produced by the reaction of a selected precursor ion with a user-specified m/z value.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12414 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12414 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12415))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12415 "flow injection mass spectrometry")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12415 "Method of flow injection analysis in which an aliquot of sample is injected, without chromatographic separation, into a liquid carrier stream for on-line mass spectrometry.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12415 "flow injection analysis mass spectrometry")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12415 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12415 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12416))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12416 "focal plane detector")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12416 "Detector for m/z spatially dispersed ion beams in which all ions simultaneously impinge on the detector plane to produce spatially defined signals.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12416 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12416 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12417))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12417 "forward geometry")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12417 "Double-focusing mass spectrometer configuration in which the ion beam traverses the electric sector before the magnetic sector.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12417 "normal geometry")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12417 goldbook:12405)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12417 goldbook:12473)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12417 goldbook:12558)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12417 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12417 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12418))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12418 "forward library search")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12418 "Procedure of comparing a mass spectrum of an unknown compound with a mass spectral library so that the unknown spectrum is compared in turn with the library spectra, considering only the m/z peaks that have intensities greater than a specific threshold in the unknown.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12418 "In a forward library search, a higher similarity index indicates the extent to which the library spectrum resembles the unknown spectrum."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12418 goldbook:12484)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12418 goldbook:12559)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12418 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12418 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12419))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12419 "Fourier-transform mass spectrometry")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12419 "Mass spectrometry technique in which m/z values are represented by frequencies of ion motion and mass spectra are generated by Fourier transform mathematical operations from time domain transients produced by image current detection.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12419 "Fourier transform mass spectrometry is typically carried out using Fourier transform-ion cyclotron resonance-mass spectrometers or Kingdon traps."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12419 goldbook:12460)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12419 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12419 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12420))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12420 "fringe field")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12420 "Electric or magnetic field that extends from the edge of an electric sector, magnetic sector, lens, or other ion optics element.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12420 goldbook:12405)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12420 goldbook:12444)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12420 goldbook:12473)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12420 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12420 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12421))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12421 "gas chromatography-mass spectrometry")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12421 "Technique by which a mixture is separated into individual components by gas chromatography, followed by detection with a mass spectrometer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12421 "GC-MS")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12421 "gas chromatography/mass spectrometry (GC/MS)")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12421 "Either a hyphen or slash can be used to indicate combined instruments."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12421 "The mass spectrum is typically obtained on a time scale that allows resolution of the component in a single chromatographic peak."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12421 goldbook:12466)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12421 goldbook:12585)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12421 goldbook:12595)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12421 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12421 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12422))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12422 "glow discharge ionization")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12422 "Formation of ions from gaseous atoms or molecules or from the vapor of a solid sample at the cathode by applying a potential difference between two electrodes immersed in a low-pressure inert gas environment.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12422 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12422 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12423))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12423 "gridless reflectron")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12423 "Reflectron design in which the decelerating/accelerating field is produced without the use of wire-mesh grids.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12423 "This design improves ion transmission but at the cost of a less homogeneous field and thus reduced resolution."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12423 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12423 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12424))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12424 "hard ionization")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12424 "Formation of gas-phase ions accompanied by extensive fragmentation.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12424 goldbook:12575)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12424 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12424 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12425))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12425 "high-field asymmetric waveform ion mobility spectrometry")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12425 "Separation of ions at atmospheric pressure between two electrodes due to simultaneous application of a high potential asymmetric waveform, whereby ions migrate towards one of the two electrodes depending on the ratio of the high- to low-field mobility of the ion. A variable compensating DC potential is used to selectively transmit ions of interest.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003012) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12425 "FAIMS")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12425 "RF-DC ion mobility spectrometry")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12425 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12425 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12426))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12426 "hybrid mass spectrometer")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12426 "Mass spectrometer that combines m/z analyzers of different types to perform tandem mass spectrometry or higher-order \\({\\rm{MS}}^{n}\\) experiment.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12426 goldbook:12591)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12426 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12426 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12427))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12427 "hydrogen/deuterium exchange")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12427 "Exchange of hydrogen atoms with deuterium atoms in a chemical species in solution prior to introduction into a mass spectrometer, or by ion/molecule reaction with a neutral gas inside a mass spectrometer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12427 "HDX")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12427 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12427 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12428))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12428 "hydrogen shifts")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12428 "Sigmatropic reactions of ions in which the \\(\\ce{\\upsigma\\mbox{-}bonds}\\) broken and formed involve hydrogen atoms, and are subject to the Woodward–Hofmann rules resulting from orbital symmetry considerations.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12428 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12428 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12429))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12429 "hyphenated mass spectrometry technique")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12429 "Analytical technique in which mass spectrometry is interfaced with a pretreatment step, most often chromatographic separation but many other combinations are possible.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12429 "Despite the use of the term \"hyphenated\" in the name of the general category, a slash separator as in gas chromatography/mass spectrometry may also be used."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12429 goldbook:12421)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12429 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12429 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12430))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12430 "image current detection")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12430 "Method of ion detection by measuring the current that results from the image charge induced by a coherent motion of ions passing near a conductor.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12430 "In Fourier transform mass spectrometers or Kingdon traps, the coherent orbital motion of ions between a pair of electrodes induces a radio frequency image charge in the electrodes and an alternating image current in the detection circuit connecting to the electrodes."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12430 goldbook:12419)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12430 goldbook:12460)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12430 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12430 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12431))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12431 "imaging mass spectrometry")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12431 "Procedure used to form chemically selective images of an object based on the mass spectrometric detection of ions desorbed from its surface.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12431 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12431 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12432))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12432 "iminium ion")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12432 "Cation with the structure \\(\\ce{R2C=N^{+}R2}\\).")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12432 "alkylideneaminylium ion")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12432 "The terms imonium ion and immonium ion are irregularly formed and should not be used."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12432 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12432 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12433))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12433 "infrared multiphoton dissociation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12433 "Dissociation of a reactant ion as a result of the absorption of multiple infrared photons.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12433 "IRMPD")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12433 goldbook:12348)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12433 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12433 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12434))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12434 "in-source collision-induced dissociation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12434 "Dissociation of an ion as a result of collisional excitation during ion transfer from an atmospheric pressure ion source to the vacuum chamber of the mass spectrometer.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12434 "in-source collisionally activated dissociation")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12434 "This process is similar to ion desolvation but uses higher collision energy."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12434 "Terms such as cone voltage dissociation and capillary exit fragmentation are design specific versions of this term, and are deprecated."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12434 goldbook:12436)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12434 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12434 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12435))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12435 "internal fragment")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12435 "Fragment ion of a peptide ion precursor formed by a double backbone cleavage that contains neither the original \\(\\ce{C}\\)- or \\(\\ce{N}\\)-terminal residues. Typically a combination of b- and y-type cleavages or occasionally an a- and y-type combination.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12435 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12435 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12436))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12436 "ion desolvation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12436 "Removal of solvent molecules clustered around a gas-phase ion by means of heating and/or collisions with gas molecules.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12436 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12436 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12437))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12437 "ion enhancement")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12437 "Phenomenon in which the ionization efficiency of a compound is increased by the presence of another compound.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12437 "ionization enhancement")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12437 "The effect is most significant in electrospray ionization but is also observed in atmospheric pressure chemical ionization and to a lesser extent in other ionization methods."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12437 goldbook:12336)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12437 goldbook:12445)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12437 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12437 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12438))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12438 "ion evaporation model")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12438 "Mechanism for production of gas-phase ions from highly charged fine liquid droplets as in electrospray ionization that involves direct ejection of the ions from the droplet surface.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12438 "This mechanism is thought to be dominant for smaller molecules."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12438 goldbook:12352)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12438 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12438 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12439))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12439 "ion funnel")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12439 "Series of stacked ring electrodes with progressively decreasing inner diameter to which a combined radio frequency and fixed potential is applied. The resulting field focuses ions travelling along the central axis.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12439 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12439 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12440))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12440 "ion gate")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12440 "Set of plates or grid of wires in an ion mobility spectrometer, time-of-flight mass spectrometer, or other mass spectrometer that is used to apply a pulsed electric field with the purpose of selectively deflecting charged particles.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12440 goldbook:12442)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12440 goldbook:12480)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12440 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12440 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12441))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12441 "ion/ion reaction")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12441 "Reaction between two ions, generally of opposite polarity.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12441 "ion-ion reaction")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12441 "The hyphenated term ion-ion reaction is superseded."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12441 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12441 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12442))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12442 "ion mobility spectrometry")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12442 "Separation of ions according to their velocity through a buffer gas under the influence of an electric field.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12442 "IMS")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12442 goldbook:12350)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12442 goldbook:12425)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12442 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12442 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12443))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12443 "ion/neutral complex")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12443 "Weakly bound species formed from an ion and neutral.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12443 "In the context of some unimolecular ion dissociations, these complexes are particular types of transition states or local energy minima that lie between precursor ions and product ions on the reaction coordinate."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12443 "The hyphenated formulation of this term, ion-neutral complex, is deprecated; the hyphen suggests a reaction of a species that is both an ion and a molecule and is not the intended meaning."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12443 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12443 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12444))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12444 "ion optics")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12444 "Devices designed to control the formation, focusing, and deflection of charged particle beams in a vacuum under the influence of electric and magnetic fields.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12444 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12444 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12445))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12445 "ion suppression")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12445 "Phenomenon in which the ionization efficiency of a species is lowered by the presence of a different species.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12445 "ionization suppression")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12445 "The effect is most significant in electrospray ionization but is also observed in atmospheric pressure chemical ionization and to a lesser extent in other ionization methods."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12445 goldbook:12336)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12445 goldbook:12437)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12445 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12445 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12446))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12446 "ion-to-photon detector")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12446 "Detector in which ions strike a conversion dynode to produce electrons that in turn strike a phosphor and the resulting photons are detected by a photomultiplier.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12446 goldbook:12380)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12446 goldbook:12372)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12446 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12446 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12447))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12447 "ion trap")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12447 "Device for spatially confining ions using electric and magnetic fields alone or in combination.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12447 "IT")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12447 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12447 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12448))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12448 "isobaric tag for relative and absolute quantitation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12448 "Chemical labeling reagents used for relative or absolute quantitation in proteomics, based on covalent labeling of the \\(\\ce{N}\\)-terminus and side-chain amines of peptides from protein digestions with tags of varying mass.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003012) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12448 "iTRAQ")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12448 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12448 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12449))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12449 "isotope cluster")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12449 "Group of peaks representing ions of the same elemental composition, but different isotopic compositions.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12449 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12449 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12450))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12450 "isotope coded affinity tag")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12450 "Chemical labeling reagents used for relative quantitation in proteomics, consisting of a reactive group capable of labeling a defined amino acid side-chain, an isotopically coded linker, and a tag for the affinity isolation of labeled proteins and peptides.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003012) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12450 "ICAT")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12450 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12450 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12451))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12451 "isotope dilution mass spectrometry")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12451 "Quantitative mass spectrometry technique in which an isotopically enriched compound is used as a surrogate internal standard.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12451 "IDMS")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12451 goldbook:12589)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12451 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12451 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12452))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12452 "isotope ratio")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12452 "Ratio of the number of atoms of one isotope to the number of atoms of another isotope of the same chemical element in the same system.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12452 "isotope–number ratio")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12452 "Usually the minor, less abundant isotope to the major, most abundant isotope, for example, \\(\\ce{^{13}C}/\\ce{^{12}C}\\)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12452 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12452 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12453))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12453 "isotope ratio mass spectrometry")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12453 "Measurement and study of the relative abundances of the different isotopes of an element in a material using a mass spectrometer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12453 "IRMS")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12453 "stable isotope mass spectrometry")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12453 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12453 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12454))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12454 "isotopolog ions")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12454 "Ions that differ only in the isotopic composition of one or more of the constituent atoms.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12454 "isotopic homolog ions")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12454 "Isotopolog is an abbreviation of isotopic homolog."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12454 goldbook:12449)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12454 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12454 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12455))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12455 "isotopomeric ion")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12455 "Isomeric ions having the same numbers of each isotopic atom but differing in their positions within the ion.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12455 "Isotopomeric ions can be either configurational isomers in which two atomic isotopes exchange positions or isotopic stereoisomers."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12455 "Isotopomer is an abbreviation of isotopic isomer."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12455 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12455 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12456))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12456 "jet separator")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12456 "Gas chromatograph-to-mass spectrometer interface where the gas chromatography effluent expands into a lower-pressure region and then through a downstream orifice. The low mass carrier gas molecules diffuse from the jet axis, leaving the sample stream enriched in the heavier analyte molecules.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12456 goldbook:12493)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12456 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12456 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12457))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12457 "kinetic energy release")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12457 "Translational energy of fragments resulting from dissociation of a metastable ion measured relative to the center-of-mass.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003012) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12457 "KER")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12457 "In this context, kinetic energy is interpreted as translational, rather than vibrational or rotational, kinetic energy."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12457 goldbook:12458)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12457 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12457 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12458))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12458 "kinetic energy release distribution")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12458 "Distribution of values of translational energies in the center-of-mass reference for an ensemble of metastable ions undergoing a specific dissociation reaction.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003012) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12458 "KERD")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12458 "In this context, kinetic energy is interpreted as translational, rather than vibrational or rotational, kinetic energy."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12458 goldbook:12476)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12458 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12458 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12459))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12459 "kinetic shift")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12459 "Excess energy above the thermochemical threshold required to observe dissociation of a precursor ion within the timeframe of a particular mass spectrometry experiment.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12459 "Kinetic shifts are important when thermochemical quantities are deduced from appearance energy measurements."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12459 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12459 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12460))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12460 "Kingdon trap")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12460 "Ion trapping device that consists of an outer barrel-like electrode and a coaxial inner spindle-like electrode that form an electrostatic field with a quadro-logarithmic potential distribution.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12460 "The frequency of harmonic oscillations of the orbitally trapped ions along the axis of the electrostatic field is independent of the ion velocity and is inversely proportional to the square root of m/z so that the trap can be operated as a mass analyzer using image current detection and Fourier transformation of the time domain signal."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12460 "The trademarked term \"Orbitrap\" has been used to describe a Kingdon trap used as a mass spectrometer."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12460 goldbook:12430)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12460 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12460 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12461))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12461 "label-free quantitation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12461 "Method for determining the concentration of proteins through a combination of protein digestion and liquid chromatography-mass spectrometry (LC-MS) without relying on stable isotope labeling. Protein quantification is achieved by measuring the signal intensity of peptide ions corresponding to a protein or by counting and comparing the number of fragment mass spectra identifying peptides of a given protein.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12461 goldbook:12466)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12461 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12461 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12462))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12462 "laser desorption")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12462 "Formation of gas-phase species from a solid or liquid sample surface upon activation using a short pulse of photons from a laser.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12462 "LD")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12462 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12462 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12463))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12463 "laser desorption ionization")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12463 "Formation of gas-phase ions by the interaction of a laser with a solid or liquid material.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12463 "LDI")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12463 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12463 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12464))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12464 "laser microprobe mass spectrometry")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12464 "Laser desorption ionization mass spectrometry, particularly emphasizing spatially resolved composition information.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12464 "LMMS")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12464 goldbook:12463)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12464 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12464 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12465))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12465 "linear ion trap")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12465 "Two-dimensional Paul ion trap in which ions are confined in the axial dimension by means of a static electric potential.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003012) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12465 "LIT")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12465 goldbook:12516)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12465 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12465 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12466))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12466 "liquid chromatography-mass spectrometry")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12466 "Technique by which a mixture of analytes is separated into individual components by liquid chromatography (typically high-performance liquid chromatography), followed by detection with a mass spectrometer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12466 "LC-MS")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12466 "liquid chromatography/mass spectrometry (LC/MS)")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12466 "Either a hyphen or slash can be used to indicate combined instruments."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12466 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12466 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12467))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12467 "liquid ion evaporation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12467 "Spray ionization interface in which droplets are dispersed from a pneumatic nebulizer toward a high potential electrode that produces a static charge on the droplets leading to ion formation after solvent evaporation.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12467 goldbook:12579)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12467 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12467 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12468))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12468 "liquid junction interface")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12468 "Means of coupling capillary electrophoresis to a mass spectrometer in which a liquid reservoir surrounds the separation capillary and transfer capillary to the mass spectrometer and provides electric contact for the capillary electrophoresis.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12468 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12468 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12469))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12469 "liquid secondary ionization")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12469 "Ionization of any species by the interaction of a focused beam of ions or atoms with a sample that is dissolved in a solvent matrix.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12469 "LSI")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12469 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12469 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12470))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12470 "liquid sheath")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12470 "Flow of make-up liquid in a sheath flow interface.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12470 goldbook:12570)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12470 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12470 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12471))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12471 "lock mass")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12471 "Mass of an ion of known m/z value, derived from a suitable standard compound introduced into an ion source together with the sample to be analyzed, which permits real-time recalibration by correction of m/z shifts arising from instrumental drift.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12471 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12471 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12472))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12472 "low-energy collision-induced dissociation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12472 "Collision-induced dissociation process wherein the precursor ion has laboratory-frame translational energy lower than a given value, often taken to be \\(\\pu{1 keV}\\).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12472 "This process can be carried out under single collision conditions but typically requires multiple collisions and the collisional excitation is cumulative."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12472 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12472 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12473))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12473 "magnetic sector")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12473 "Device that produces a magnetic field perpendicular to a charged particle beam that deflects the beam to an extent that is proportional to the ratio of particle momentum and charge.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12473 "For a mono-energetic beam, the deflection is proportional to m/z."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12473 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12473 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12474))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12474 "magnetron motion")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12474 "Slow rotation of the center of cyclotron motion around the central axis of a Penning ion trap that results from a drift of the cyclotron centre along the electric equipotential lines perpendicular to the magnetic field direction.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12474 "The characteristic frequency of this motion is called the magnetron frequency."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12474 goldbook:12521)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12474 goldbook:12379)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12474 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12474 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12475))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12475 "make-up liquid")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12475 "Solvent that is mixed with the sample flow in a liquid introduction mass spectrometry interface in order to adjust the flow rate or solvent characteristics of the system, for example, to promote ionization efficiency.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12475 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12475 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12476))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12476 "mass-analyzed ion kinetic energy spectrometry")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12476 "Procedure by which translational energy spectra are obtained from a sector mass spectrometer that incorporates at least one magnetic sector plus one electric sector in reverse geometry (a magnetic sector followed by an electric sector).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003012) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12476 "MIKES")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12476 "In this context, kinetic energy is interpreted as translational rather than vibrational or rotational kinetic energy."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12476 "The accelerating potential, \\(V\\), and the magnetic flux density, \\(B\\), are set at fixed values to m/z select the precursor ions, which are then allowed to dissociate or to react in a field-free region between the two sectors. The translational energy-to-charge ratios of the various product ions are analyzed by scanning the electric sector field \\(E\\). The width of a product ion spectral peak is related to the kinetic energy release distribution for the dissociation process."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12476 goldbook:12325)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12476 goldbook:12405)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12476 goldbook:12412)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12476 goldbook:12458)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12476 goldbook:12473)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12476 goldbook:12558)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12476 goldbook:12566)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12476 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12476 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12477))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12477 "mass calibration")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12477 "Means of determining m/z values of ions from experimentally detected signals using a theoretical or empirical relational equation.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12477 "Most commonly this is accomplished using a computer-based data system and a calibration file obtained from a mass spectrum of a compound that produces ions of known m/z values."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12477 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12477 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12478))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12478 "mass defect")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12478 "Difference between the nominal mass and the monoisotopic mass of an atom, molecule, or ion.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12478 "Mass defect can be a positive or negative value dependent upon the elemental composition."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12478 goldbook:12495)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12478 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12478 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12479))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12479 "mass discrimination")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12479 "Differences in overall detection sensitivities for ions of different m/z values in a mass spectrum, caused by variations in ionization efficiency, transmission efficiency through the interface between the ion source and the analyzer vacuum system, analyzer, and detector response.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12479 goldbook:12601)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12479 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12479 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12480))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12480 "mass gate")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12480 "Ion gate used to transmit ions in a given m/z range.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12480 goldbook:12440)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12480 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12480 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12481))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12481 "mass limit")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12481 "Value of m/z above or below which ions cannot be detected in a mass spectrometer.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12481 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12481 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12482))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12482 "mass selective axial ejection")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12482 "Use of mass selective instability to eject ions of selected m/z values from an ion trap along the trap axis.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12482 goldbook:12447)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12482 goldbook:12483)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12482 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12482 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12483))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12483 "mass selective instability")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12483 "Unstable trajectories in an ion trap for ions within a particular range of m/z values caused by an appropriate combination of oscillating electric fields.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12483 "MSI")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12483 goldbook:12482)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12483 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12483 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12484))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12484 "mass spectral library")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12484 "Collection of mass spectra of different compounds, usually represented as arrays of signal intensity vs. the m/z values.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12484 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12484 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12485))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12485 "mass spectrometry/mass spectrometry")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12485 "Acquisition and study of the spectra of the product ions or precursor ions of m/z selected ions, or of precursor ions of a selected neutral mass loss.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12485 "MS/MS")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12485 "tandem mass spectrometry")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12485 "MS/MS can be accomplished using instruments incorporating more than one analyzer (tandem mass spectrometry in space) or in trap instruments (tandem mass spectrometry in time)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12485 goldbook:12591)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12485 goldbook:12592)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12485 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12485 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12486))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12486 "Mathieu stability diagram")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12486 "Graphical representation expressed in terms of dimensionless reduced coordinates that describes the stability or instability of charged particle motion in a transmission quadrupole mass spectrometer or Paul ion trap, based on an appropriate form of the Mathieu differential equation.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12486 "stability diagram")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12486 goldbook:12516)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12486 goldbook:12602)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12486 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12486 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12487))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12487 "membrane introduction mass spectrometry")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12487 "Mass spectrometry measurement that uses a semi-permeable membrane separator that permits the passage of analytes directly from solutions or ambient air to the mass spectrometer ion source.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003012) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12487 "MIMS")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12487 "membrane inlet mass spectrometry")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12487 "membrane interface mass spectrometry")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12487 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12487 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12488))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12488 "membrane separator")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12488 "GC-MS interface with a polymer membrane that selectively passes analyte molecules in preference to the carrier gas thereby enriching the analyte in the gas stream.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12488 goldbook:12421)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12488 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12488 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12489))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12489 "microchannel plate")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12489 "Thin plate that contains a closely spaced array of channels each of which acts as a continuous dynode particle multiplier. A fast charged or neutral particle, or a photon, that strikes the plate causes a cascade of secondary electrons that ultimately exits the opposite side of the plate.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12489 "MCP")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12489 "channel electron multiplier array")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12489 goldbook:12369)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12489 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12489 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12490))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12490 "microelectrospray")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12490 "Electrospray ionization at a low solvent flow rate, typically several microliters per minute (\\(\\pu{\\upmu L min-1}\\)) or lower, where a pump is used to provide the sample flow.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12490 goldbook:12502)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12490 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12490 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12491))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12491 "molecular beam mass spectrometry")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12491 "Mass spectrometry measurement in which the sample is introduced into the ion source of the mass spectrometer as a collimated beam of molecules with a narrow velocity distribution.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12491 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12491 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12492))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12492 "molecular effusion separator")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12492 "GC-MS interface that subjects the GC effluent to effusive flow through a porous glass tube. The lighter carrier gas passes out of the tube, leaving the gas within the tube enriched in analyte.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12492 goldbook:12421)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12492 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12492 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12493))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12493 "momentum separator")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12493 "Mass spectrometer interface to inlets including chromatography and spray-based ion sources that enriches the sample by selecting the central part of the effluent or spray using an orifice or skimmer. Particles with a higher forward momentum diverge less from the spray axis for a given radial momentum.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12493 goldbook:12456)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12493 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12493 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12494))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12494 "monodisperse aerosol generating interface for chromatography")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12494 "Particle beam interface that incorporates a monodisperse aerosol generator.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003012) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12494 "MAGIC")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12494 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12494 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12495))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12495 "monoisotopic mass")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12495 "Exact mass of an ion or molecule calculated using the mass of the most abundant isotope of each element.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12495 goldbook:12407)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12495 goldbook:12326)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12495 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12495 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12496))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12496 "moving belt interface")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12496 "Liquid sample mass spectrometer interface that uses two or more pulleys and a continuous loop of material. Samples are sprayed or deposited from solution onto the belt where they are transported into the vacuum system for vaporization or desorption and ionization.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12496 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12496 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12497))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12497 "MS/MS spectrum")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12497 "Mass spectrum obtained using tandem mass spectrometry.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12497 goldbook:12591)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12497 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12497 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12498))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12498 "MS<sup><i>n</i></sup>")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12498 "Symbol for multiple-stage mass spectrometry experiments designed to record product ion spectra where \\(n\\) is the number of product ion stages (nth-generation product ions).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12498 goldbook:12501)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12498 goldbook:12511)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12498 goldbook:12535)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12498 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12498 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12499))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12499 "multicollector mass spectrometer")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12499 "Mass spectrograph based on a double-focusing magnetic analyzer that spatially disperses ions of different m/z values on to an array of Faraday cup detectors, generally used with inductively coupled plasma ion sources for isotopic composition measurements.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12499 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12499 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12500))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12500 "multiple reaction monitoring")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12500 "Application of selected reaction monitoring to multiple product ions from one or more precursor ions.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12500 "MRM")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12500 "This term should not be confused with consecutive reaction monitoring, which involves the serial application of three or more stages of selected reaction monitoring."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12500 goldbook:12366)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12500 goldbook:12568)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12500 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12500 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12501))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12501 "multiple-stage mass spectrometry")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12501 "Multiple stages of precursor ion m/z selection followed by product ion detection for successive nth-generation product ions.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12501 goldbook:12498)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12501 goldbook:12511)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12501 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12501 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12502))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12502 "nanoelectrospray")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12502 "Electrospray ionization at a very low solvent flow rate, typically hundreds of nanoliters per minute of sample solution or lower, often without the use of an external solvent delivery system.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12502 "Nanospray should only be used to describe the commercial product."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12502 goldbook:12490)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12502 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12502 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12503))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12503 "negative ion chemical ionization")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12503 "Chemical ionization that results in the formation of negative ions.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003012) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12503 "NICI")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12503 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12503 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12504))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12504 "neutralization-reionization mass spectrometry")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12504 "Procedure by which neutral species are formed from m/z selected ions by charge transfer to a collision gas or by dissociation. The neutral species are separated from the remaining ions and ionized through collisions with a second gas.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12504 "NRMS")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12504 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12504 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12505))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12505 "neutral loss")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12505 "Loss of an uncharged species from an ion during dissociation.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12505 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12505 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12506))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12506 "neutral loss scan")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12506 "Scan used to generate a constant neutral loss spectrum.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12506 goldbook:12368)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12506 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12506 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12507))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12507 "nitrogen rule")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12507 "Rule stating that a neutral organic molecule containing one or more atoms of the elements \\(\\ce{C}\\), \\(\\ce{H}\\), \\(\\ce{O}\\), \\(\\ce{N}\\), \\(\\ce{S}\\), \\(\\ce{P}\\), or any halogen has an odd nominal mass if it contains an odd number of nitrogen atoms.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12507 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12507 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12508))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12508 "nozzle-skimmer dissociation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12508 "Collisionally activated dissociation that is caused by collisions in the region between the nozzle and skimmer of an atmospheric pressure ionization source such as electrospray or atmospheric pressure chemical ionization.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12508 "in-source collision-induced dissociation")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12508 "The process can be induced by a higher than typical nozzle-skimmer voltage."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12508 goldbook:12336)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12508 goldbook:12509)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12508 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12508 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12509))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12509 "nozzle-skimmer voltage")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12509 "Electric potential difference applied between the electrospray needle and the skimmer, which is typically held at the same potential as the counter electrode.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12509 "needle voltage")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12509 goldbook:12376)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12509 goldbook:12404)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12509 goldbook:12574)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12509 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12509 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12510))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12510 "<i>n</i><sup>th</sup>-generation product ion")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12510 "Serial product ions from dissociation or bimolecular reaction of selected precursor ions where \\(n\\) refers to the number of stages of dissociation or bimolecular reaction in a series of consecutive reactions that involve successive product ions.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12510 "Given the sequential fragmentation scheme: \\[\\ce{M1^{+} -> M2^{+} -> M3^{+} -> M4^{+} -> M5^{+}}\\] \\(\\ce{M4^{+}}\\) is the precursor ion of \\(\\ce{M5^{+}}\\), a 1st-generation product ion of \\(\\ce{M3^{+}}\\), a 2nd-generation product ion of \\(\\ce{M2^{+}}\\), and a 3rd-generation product ion of \\(\\ce{M1^{+}}\\)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12510 goldbook:12511)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12510 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12510 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12511))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12511 "<i>n</i><sup>th</sup>-generation product ion spectrum")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12511 "Mass spectrum recorded from any mass spectrometer in which the appropriate scan function can be set to record the appropriate generation product ion or ions of m/z selected precursor ions.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12511 goldbook:12510)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12511 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12511 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12512))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12512 "orthogonal electrospray")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12512 "Configuration for electrospray ionization in which the axis of the spray is at a right angle to the axis of the sampling cone.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12512 goldbook:12563)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12512 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12512 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12513))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12513 "orthogonal extraction")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12513 "Pulsed acceleration of ions perpendicular to their original direction of travel into a mass spectrometer, typically time-of-flight.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12513 "orthogonal acceleration")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12513 "Ions may be extracted from a directional ion source, drift tube, or m/z separation stage."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12513 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12513 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12514))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12514 "partial isotopic scrambling")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12514 "Partial random mixing of isotopes among specified atom positions in an ion or neutral species.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12514 "In mass spectrometry, this term usually refers to the partial random mixing of isotopes in isolated ions that were formed with a fixed isotopic composition."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12514 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12514 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12515))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12515 "particle beam interface")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12515 "Method for coupling liquid chromatography to mass spectrometry in which the effluent is passed through a heated capillary to form an expanding jet of vapour and aerosol particles. After passing through a skimmer that acts as a momentum separator, the beam impinges on a heated surface to form ions through chemical ionization at the surface or ionization of the resulting vapour in a chemical ionization or electron ionization source.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12515 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12515 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12516))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12516 "Paul ion trap")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12516 "Ion trapping device that depends on the application of radio frequency potentials between a ring electrode and two end-cap electrodes to confine the ion motion to a cyclic path described by an appropriate form of the Mathieu equation. The choice of these potentials determines the m/z value below which ions are not trapped.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12516 "quadrupole ion storage trap")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12516 "quadrupole ion trap")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12516 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12516 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12517))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12517 "peak matching")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12517 "Procedure for measuring the accurate mass of an ion using scanning mass spectrometers, in which the peak corresponding to the unknown ion and that for a reference ion of known m/z are displayed alternately and caused to overlap by adjusting appropriate electric fields.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12517 goldbook:12326)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12517 goldbook:12550)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12517 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12517 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12518))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12518 "peak parking")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12518 "Method used to extend the amount of time available for mass spectrometric analysis of the components in a narrow chromatographic peak. The eluent flow rate is reduced to an ultra-low level at the leading edge of the peak and held at this low flow rate for the duration of compound elution, thus enabling collection of sufficient data for reliable statistical analysis.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12518 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12518 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12519))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12519 "peak stripping")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12519 "Data analysis technique used in elemental mass spectrometry to correct the intensity of an unresolved multiplet peak monitored for a specific element for contributions from a multi-isotopic contaminant. The correction is calculated from the measured intensity of a different isotopic peak of the contaminant and the known natural isotopic abundance ratio.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12519 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12519 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12520))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12520 "Penning ionization")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12520 "Ionization via electron removal that occurs through the energy transfer from a neutral species \\(\\ce{N}\\) internally excited to a metastable state (such as a high Rydberg state) to a neutral species \\(\\ce{M}\\) with lower ionization energy, as represented by the following reaction: \\(\\ce{N^{\\ast} + M -> N + M^{+.} + \\textit{e}^{-}}\\).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12520 "Penning ionization differs from chemi-ionization in that no chemical change is involved."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12520 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12520 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12521))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12521 "Penning ion trap")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12521 "Ion trapping device using a static magnetic field and a static electric potential well. The magnetic field confines the ion motion to circular orbits around the magnetic force line direction, which aligns with the direction of the trap axis, whereas the electric potential well confines the ion motion axially.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12521 "This device is used for the mass analyzer of Fourier transform-ion cyclotron resonance-mass spectrometers."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12521 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12521 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12522))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12522 "peptide mass fingerprinting")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12522 "Method for protein analysis where an unknown protein is chemically or enzymatically cleaved into peptide fragments whose masses are determined by mass spectrometry. The peptide masses are compared to peptide masses calculated for known proteins in a database and analyzed statistically to determine the best match.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12522 "PMF")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12522 "mass mapping")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12522 goldbook:12327)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12522 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12522 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12523))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12523 "peptide sequence tag")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12523 "Sequence of peptide ion fragment masses that can be used to aid in the identification of the amino acid sequence.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12523 "Sequence tags are often obtained in tandem mass spectrometry analysis of peptides from an unknown protein that has been chemically or enzymatically cleaved into peptide fragments."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12523 goldbook:12591)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12523 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12523 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12524))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12524 "photodissociation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12524 "Process wherein the reactant ion or molecule is dissociated as a result of absorption of one or more photons.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12524 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12524 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12525))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12525 "photographic plate recording")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12525 "Recording of ion currents by allowing them to strike a photographic plate, which is subsequently developed.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12525 "This technique is typically associated with ion-beams that have been spatially separated by m/z and focused across a focal plane as in a Mattauch–Herzog geometry magnetic sector instrument."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12525 goldbook:12473)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12525 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12525 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12526))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12526 "$\\boldsymbol{\\pi}$/n rad magnetic sector")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12526 "Arrangement in which an ion beam is deflected magnetically through \\(\\pi/n\\ \\rm{rad}\\), where \\(n \\gt 1\\).")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12526 "180º/<em>n</em> magnetic sector")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12526 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12526 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12527))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12527 "pneumatically assisted electrospray ionization")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12527 "Electrospray ionization in which the nebulization of the liquid stream is assisted by a concentric stream of gas.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12527 "Ionspray should only be used to describe the commercial product."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12527 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12527 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12528))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12528 "point detector")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12528 "Detector in which the ion beam is focused onto a small area, for example, defined by a collector slit, rather than dispersed by m/z spatially across a focal plane.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12528 goldbook:12359)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12528 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12528 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12529))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12529 "post-acceleration detector")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12529 "Detector in which a high potential is applied after m/z separation to accelerate the ions and produce an improved signal.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003012) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12529 "PAD")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12529 goldbook:12372)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12529 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12529 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12530))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12530 "post-source decay")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12530 "Technique specific to reflectron time-of-flight mass spectrometers where product ions of metastable transitions or collision-induced dissociations generated in the flight tube prior to entering the reflectron are separated according to m/z to yield product ion spectra.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12530 "PSD")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12530 goldbook:12535)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12530 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12530 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12531))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12531 "precursor ion spectrum")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12531 "Mass spectrum in which the appropriate m/z separation function records the precursor ions of selected product ions or specified neutral loss.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12531 "The ion current recorded by the detector is that from the product ion but the m/z values corresponding to the peaks in the resulting spectrum are those of precursor ions that fragmented in the fashion specified by the m/z separation function of the tandem mass spectrometer."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12531 goldbook:12535)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12531 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12531 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12532))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12532 "pre-ionization state")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12532 "Electronic state capable of undergoing autoionization.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12532 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12532 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12533))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12533 "probability-based matching")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12533 "Automated system for computer examination of the mass spectrum of an unknown mixture for the presence of a specific compound for which a standard spectrum is available in a library. The probability that the compound is present is given by a confidence index \\(K\\) such that \\(2^{K}\\) is the average number of randomly selected compounds whose mass spectra would have to be examined to find data which match the target spectrum to the same degree as does the unknown.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12533 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12533 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12534))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12534 "product ion analysis")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12534 "Process whereby a precursor ion of a particular m/z is selected by m/z, fragmentation is induced, and the mass spectrum of the resulting product ions is recorded.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12534 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12534 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12535))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12535 "product ion spectrum")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12535 "Mass spectrum in which the appropriate m/z separation analysis function is set to record the product ions of a selected precursor ion selected by m/z.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12535 goldbook:12531)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12535 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12535 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12536))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12536 "profile mode")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12536 "Method for acquiring a mass spectrum where each peak is displayed as a curve, with the data points defining the curve corresponding to the signal intensities at each particular m/z value.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12536 goldbook:12351)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12536 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12536 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12537))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12537 "proton-bound dimer")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12537 "Dimeric ion consisting of two similar or dissimilar molecules bound together by hydrogen bonding with a shared proton.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12537 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12537 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12538))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12538 "pyrolysis mass spectrometry")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12538 "Mass spectrometry technique in which the sample is heated to the point of decomposition and the gas-phase decomposition products are characterized by mass spectrometry.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003012) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12538 "PYMS")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12538 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12538 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12539))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12539 "quadratic field reflectron")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12539 "Reflectron in which the electric field varies with the square of the distance from the entrance and compensates for kinetic energy spread to all orders.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12539 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12539 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12540))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12540 "quadrupolar axialization")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12540 "Technique for axialization in Fourier transform-ion cyclotron resonance-mass spectrometers in which magnetron motion is converted into cyclotron motion by subjecting the trapped ions to a quadrupolar excitation field while they undergo collisions.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12540 goldbook:12343)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12540 goldbook:12379)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12540 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12540 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12541))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12541 "quadrupole time-of-flight")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12541 "Hybrid mass spectrometer consisting of a transmission quadrupole mass spectrometer coupled to an orthogonal acceleration time-of-flight mass spectrometer. A collision quadrupole is typically inserted between the two mass spectrometers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003012) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12541 "QTOF")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12541 goldbook:12426)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12541 goldbook:12363)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12541 goldbook:12513)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12541 goldbook:12602)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12541 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12541 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12542))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12542 "quantitation by concatenated tryptic peptides")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12542 "Method for absolute quantitation of a protein or proteins in a multiplexed fashion using isotope-labeled peptides as surrogate internal standards. The labeled peptides are produced by synthesizing a gene coding for all desired peptides, expressing this gene in E. coli culture containing appropriately labeled substrate, and digesting with trypsin the expressed protein composed of the desired concatenated peptides.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003012) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12542 "QCAT")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12542 goldbook:12589)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12542 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12542 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12543))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12543 "quasi-equilibrium theory")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12543 "Statistical theory of unimolecular reaction rates (isomerization or fragmentation) of molecular species that assumes that reaction occurs from the ground electronic state of the reactant regardless of its mode of formation, at a rate determined by the free statistical redistribution of internal energy into those vibrational and rotational modes that must be activated sufficiently to reach the appropriate transition state for the specified reaction to occur.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12543 "QET")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12543 "The QET applies to isolated molecular species in the absence of collisions, as for ion fragmentations in a mass spectrometer. Early formulations assumed the reactant contained \\(s\\) identical harmonic oscillators of frequency \\(\\nu\\), with a transition state corresponding to just one critical oscillator containing at least \\(m\\) quanta corresponding to the critical energy for reaction \\(\\varepsilon^{\\ast} = m\\nu\\). A further assumption that \\(m \\gg s\\) leads to an ultra-simple expression for the unimolecular rate constant at total internal energy \\(\\varepsilon\\): \\(k(\\varepsilon) = \\nu[(\\varepsilon - \\varepsilon^{\\ast})/\\varepsilon]^{(s-1)}\\). Elimination of most of these simplifying assumptions followed development of the Rice–Ramsperger–Kassel–Marcus (RRKM) theory."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12543 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12543 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12544))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12544 "radial ejection")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12544 "Ejection of an ion from an ion trap in a direction perpendicular to the longitudinal axis of the trap.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12544 goldbook:12447)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12544 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12544 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12545))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12545 "Rayleigh limit")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12545 "Limiting droplet size at which self-fragmentation will occur for charged droplets generated in electrospray or other ionization processes. Self-fragmentation occurs when the electrostatic repulsion force generated by the excess charge exceeds the surface tension that maintains the integrity of the droplet.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12545 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12545 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12546))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12546 "reagent gas")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12546 "Gas that reacts with ions to produce product ions through ion/molecule reactions; for example, a gas such as methane, ammonia, or isobutane used in chemical ionization to create reagent ions or a gas used in ion traps or collision cells to perform gas-phase ion/molecule reactions.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12546 goldbook:12361)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12546 goldbook:12447)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12546 goldbook:12547)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12546 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12546 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12547))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12547 "reagent ion")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12547 "Ion that reacts with a neutral to produce an ionized form of such species through an ion/molecule reaction, for example, as in chemical ionization.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12547 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12547 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12548))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12548 "recombination energy")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12548 "Energy released when an electron is added to an ionized molecule or atom.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12548 "This is the energy required for the reverse process of vertical ionization."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12548 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12548 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12549))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12549 "rectilinear ion trap")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12549 "Quadrupole ion trap whose electrodes form a rectilinear polygon, the simplest form of which consists of two pairs of rectangular electrodes supplied with radio frequency (RF) potentials and a pair of electrodes to which a DC potential is applied. Slits or apertures in the electrodes allow injection and ejection of charged particles.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12549 goldbook:12516)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12549 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12549 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12550))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12550 "reference ion")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12550 "Stable ion whose structure or elemental formula is known with certainty. These ions are formed by direct ionization of a molecule of known structure or elemental formula, and are used to verify by comparison the structure or thermochemistry of an unknown ion or to calibrate the m/z scale of the mass spectrometer.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12550 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12550 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12551))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12551 "relative isotope-ratio difference")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12551 "Measure of an isotope ratio in a sample of interest relative to a reference defined by the relation \\[\\delta = (R_{\\rm{sample}} - R_{\\rm{standard}})/R_{\\rm{standard}}\\] where \\(R\\) is the isotope ratio of the element.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12551 "delta notation")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12551 "isotope delta")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12551 "relative difference of isotope ratios")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12551 "The reference is often an international measurement standard."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12551 "The same relative differences are used to calculate delta values from the abundance of isotopomers and isotopologs, ion currents, frequencies, or optical extinctions."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12551 "Relative isotope ratio differences are usually small and are therefore often expressed in units of parts per mil with symbol ‰."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12551 "Units of parts per thousand (\\(\\pu{ppt}\\), \\(\\pu{E-3}\\)) or parts per million (\\(\\pu{ppm}\\), \\(\\pu{E-6}\\)) are deprecated."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12551 goldbook:12452)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12551 goldbook:12454)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12551 goldbook:12455)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12551 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12551 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12552))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12552 "residual gas analyser")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12552 "Mass spectrometer used to measure the composition and pressure of gases in an evacuated chamber and to test for leaks in pressurized systems.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12552 "RGA")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12552 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12552 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12553))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12553 "resolution: 10 per cent valley definition")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12553 "Value of \\((m/z)/\\Delta(m/z)\\) measured for two peaks of equal height in a mass spectrum at m/z and \\(m/z \\pm \\Delta(m/z)\\) that are separated by a valley which at its lowest point is \\(\\pu{10\\%}\\) of the height of either peak. For peaks of similar height separated by a valley, let the height of the valley at its lowest point be \\(\\pu{10\\%}\\) of the lower peak. Then the resolution (\\(\\pu{10\\%}\\) valley definition) is \\((m/z)/\\Delta(m/z)\\) and should be given for a number of values of m/z.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12553 goldbook:12554)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12553 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12553 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12554))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12554 "resolution: peak width definition")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12554 "For a single peak corresponding to singly charged ions at mass \\(m\\) in a mass spectrum, the resolution may be expressed as \\((m/z)/\\Delta(m/z)\\), where \\(\\Delta(m/z)\\) is the width of the peak at a height which is a specified fraction of the maximum peak height. It is recommended that one of three values 50, 5, or \\(\\pu{0.5\\%}\\) should always be used.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12554 "For an isolated symmetrical peak recorded with a system which is linear in the range between \\(\\pu{5\\%}\\) and \\(\\pu{10\\%}\\) levels of the peak, the \\(\\pu{5\\%}\\) peak width definition is equivalent to the \\(\\pu{10\\%}\\) valley definition. A common standard is the definition of resolution based upon \\(\\Delta m\\) being full width of the peak at half its maximum (FWHM) height."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12554 goldbook:12553)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12554 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12554 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12555))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12555 "resonance-enhanced multiphoton ionization")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12555 "Multiphoton ionization in which the ionization cross section is significantly enhanced because the energy of the incident photons is resonant with an intermediate excited state of the neutral.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003012) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12555 "REMPI")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12555 "resonance ionization")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12555 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12555 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12556))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12556 "resonance ion ejection")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12556 "Mode of ion ejection in an ion trap that relies on an auxiliary radio frequency potential that is applied to the end-cap or trapping electrodes. The potential is tuned to the classical oscillation frequency of a particular ion to eject it.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12556 goldbook:12447)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12556 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12556 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12557))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12557 "retro Diels–Alder reaction")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12557 "Ion fragmentation mechanism in which the molecular ion \\(\\ce{M^{+.}}\\) of a cyclic alkene fragments to form a neutral diene and an alkene radical cation or a diene radical cation and an alkene. The reaction is the reverse of the Diels–Alder reaction of organic synthesis.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12557 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12557 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12558))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12558 "reverse geometry")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12558 "Double-focusing mass spectrometer configuration in which the ion beam traverses the magnetic sector prior to the electric sector.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12558 goldbook:12405)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12558 goldbook:12417)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12558 goldbook:12473)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12558 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12558 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12559))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12559 "reverse library search")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12559 "Process of comparing a subset of the peaks in the mass spectrum of an unknown compound with peaks present in the library mass spectrum. Any peaks in the mass spectrum of the unknown compound that are not in the library spectrum are disregarded.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12559 "A reverse library search measures the extent to which the peaks in a reference spectrum are present in the unknown spectrum and is more effective than a forward library search when peaks arising from two or more components are present in the unknown spectrum"^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12559 goldbook:12418)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12559 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12559 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12560))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12560 "RF-only quadrupole")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12560 "Transmission quadrupole device in which a sinusoidal radio frequency (RF) potential is applied between the connected pairs of opposite rod electrodes in a linear quadrupole, providing a transmission device for all ions with m/z values above a cut-off value.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12560 "Higher-order multipoles can also be used in this manner."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12560 goldbook:12602)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12560 goldbook:12363)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12560 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12560 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12561))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12561 "ring and double bond equivalent")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12561 "Conventional measure of the degree of unsaturation of an organic molecule given by \\(X - Y/2 + Z/2 + 1\\) where \\(X\\) is the number of carbon atoms, \\(Y\\) is the number of hydrogen or halogen atoms and \\(Z\\) is the number of nitrogen and phosphorus atoms.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12561 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12561 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12562))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12562 "saddle field gun")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12562 "Compact ion and fast atom sources for use when small size and high beam intensity are required, as in fast atom bombardment mass spectrometry. The discharge is produced by electrons oscillating between two cold cathodes in an electric field that possesses a single saddle point. To produce and intensify the plasma the electrons must have long path lengths, achieved by allowing the electrons to have an oscillatory motion in the saddle-shaped electric field between the cathodes separated by the anode.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12562 goldbook:12411)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12562 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12562 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12563))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12563 "sampling cone")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12563 "Component of a spray ionization interface that consists of a cone with a small orifice through which the spray passes into a differentially pumped chamber")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12563 "In interfaces that have both a sampling cone and skimmer, the spray passes first through the sampling cone and then through the skimmer."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12563 "A capillary can also be used in place of a cone."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12563 goldbook:12574)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12563 goldbook:12579)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12563 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12563 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12564))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12564 "scan cycle time")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12564 "Time required to obtain a mass spectrum (or other mass spectrometric data quantity) such as in a separation coupled to mass spectrometry.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12564 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12564 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12565))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12565 "secondary neutral mass spectrometry")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12565 "Mass spectrometry technique in which neutral species ejected from a sample surface as a result of bombardment by a primary beam of atoms or ions are ionized, most often by photoionization, prior to analysis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12565 "SNMS")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12565 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12565 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12566))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12566 "sector mass spectrometer")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12566 "Mass spectrometer consisting of one or more magnetic sectors for recording a mass spectrum of a monoenergetic beam of ions. Such instruments may also have one or more electric sectors for energy dispersion that can be arranged for velocity-focusing by compensating for dispersion by the magnetic sector if the beam is not truly monoenergetic. Such a combination provides double focusing of ions of the same m/z, i.e., focusing with respect to both direction and speed.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12566 goldbook:12405)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12566 goldbook:12473)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12566 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12566 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12567))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12567 "selected ion flow tube")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12567 "Device in which m/z selected ions are entrained in an inert carrier gas and subsequently undergo ion/molecule reactions with molecules introduced into the gas flow.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003012) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12567 "SIFT")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12567 goldbook:12397)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12567 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12567 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12568))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12568 "selected reaction monitoring")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12568 "Data acquired from one or more specific product ions corresponding to m/z selected precursor ions recorded via two or more stages of mass spectrometry.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12568 "SRM")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12568 "Selected reaction monitoring in multiple-stage mass spectrometry is known as consecutive reaction monitoring."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12568 "Selected reaction monitoring applied to multiple product ions from one or more precursor ions is known as multiple reaction monitoring."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12568 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12568 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12569))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12569 "self-chemical ionization")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12569 "Chemical ionization of an analyte where the reagent ion is an ionized form of the analyte or one of its product ions.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003012) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12569 "self-CI")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12569 goldbook:12547)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12569 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12569 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12570))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12570 "sheath flow interface")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12570 "Capillary electrophoresis to electrospray ionization interface that uses a coaxial flow of make-up liquid that is introduced through a tube that is concentric with the separation capillary.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12570 goldbook:12475)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12570 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12570 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12571))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12571 "sheath gas")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12571 "Gas introduced through a tube that is coaxial with the electrospray emitter to pneumatically assist the formation of the sprayed droplets.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12571 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12571 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12572))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12572 "sheath liquid")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12572 "Make-up liquid in a sheath flow interface")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12572 goldbook:12475)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12572 goldbook:12570)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12572 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12572 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12573))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12573 "shotgun proteomics")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12573 "Protein identification using a combination of high-performance liquid chromatography and mass spectrometry in which the proteins in a mixture are digested, usually by a specific enzyme, and the resulting peptides are separated by liquid chromatography and identified by tandem mass spectrometry.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12573 goldbook:12591)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12573 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12573 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12574))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12574 "skimmer")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12574 "Cone with a central orifice that intercepts the center of a spray or jet expansion to sample the central portion of the expansion, for example, as in a momentum separator.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12574 goldbook:12493)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12574 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12574 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12575))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12575 "soft ionization")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12575 "Formation of gas-phase ions without extensive fragmentation.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12575 goldbook:12424)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12575 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12575 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12576))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12576 "sonic spray ionization")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12576 "Process in which both anions and cations are produced at atmospheric pressure from an ionic solution due to a statistically unbalanced charge distribution in the minute droplets formed by the action of a sonic atomizer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12576 "SSI")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12576 goldbook:12579)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12576 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12576 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12577))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12577 "space charge effect")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12577 "Result of mutual repulsion of particles of like charge (ions, electrons, etc.) that can limit the current in a charged-particle beam and can also cause some motion of ions in a beam or packet in addition to that caused by external fields.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12577 "Space charge effects on ion trajectories are most noticeable in ion trap instruments that confine large numbers of ions in a small volume."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12577 goldbook:12447)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12577 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12577 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12578))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12578 "spectral skewing")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12578 "Deviation of the peak intensities in a mass spectrum from their expected values that occurs when the relative concentration of the various analytes change during acquisition of the mass spectrum.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12578 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12578 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12579))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12579 "spray ionization")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12579 "General term used to describe a range of ionization techniques for analytes in solution that involve dispersing the liquid into fine droplets as a component step.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12579 "Most of these techniques are examples of atmospheric pressure ionization."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12579 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12579 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12580))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12580 "stable isotope ratio analysis of amino acids in cell culture")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12580 "Proteomics technique that detects differences in protein abundance between cultured cell samples using stable isotopic labeling achieved with labeled amino acids in one cell culture and unlabeled ones in a separate culture.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003012) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12580 "SILAC")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12580 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12580 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12581))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12581 "stable isotope standards and capture by anti-peptide antibodies")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12581 "Method for absolute quantitation of a protein or proteins in a multiplexed fashion using isotope-labeled peptides as surrogate internal standards. The labeled peptides are produced by synthesizing a gene coding for each desired peptide, cell-free transcription, and translation of this gene in a medium containing \\(\\ce{^{13}C6}\\)-labeled lysine, and digesting with trypsin the expressed protein composed of the desired concatenated peptides. For low-abundance proteins the sensitivity is increased by selective enrichment of the target peptides by antibody capture.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003012) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12581 "SISCAPA")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12581 goldbook:12589)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12581 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12581 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12582))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12582 "static field")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12582 "Electric or magnetic field that does not change in time.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12582 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12582 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12583))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12583 "Stevenson’s rule")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12583 "Rule stating that in competing fragmentations the product ion formed from its neutral species counterpart with the lower ionization energy will usually be the more abundant.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12583 "The original version of this rule referred to reliability of determination of thermochemical data obtained for an ion produced by fragmentation of a single \\(\\ce{\\upsigma\\mbox{-}bond}\\) in an odd-electron ion \\(\\ce{X{-}Y^{+.}}\\), but was later extended to the version in more common use since then."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12583 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12583 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12584))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12584 "stored waveform inverse fourier transform")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12584 "Technique to create excitation waveforms for ions in Fourier transform-ion cyclotron resonance-mass spectrometers or Paul ion traps. An excitation waveform in the time-domain is generated by taking the inverse Fourier transform of an appropriate frequency-domain programmed excitation spectrum, in which the resonance frequencies of ions to be excited are included.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003012) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12584 "SWIFT")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12584 "This procedure may be used for selection of precursor ions in MSn experiments."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12584 goldbook:12498)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12584 goldbook:12516)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12584 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12584 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12585))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12585 "supercritical fluid chromatography-mass spectrometry")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12585 "Combined technique in which a mixture of analytes is separated into solutions of individual components by chromatography that uses a supercritical fluid as mobile phase, followed by the ionization of the separation effluent in the ion source of a mass spectrometer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12585 "SFC-MS")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12585 "supercritical fluid chromatography/mass spectrometry (SFC/MS)")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12585 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12585 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12586))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12586 "surface-enhanced laser desorption/ionization")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12586 "Variant of matrix-assisted laser desorption/ionization (MALDI) in which the matrix is replaced by a surface coating of a chromatographic stationary phase designed to selectively retain different subsets of proteins or peptides from a mixture depending on their physico-chemical properties or biochemical affinity characteristics.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003012) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12586 "SELDI")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12586 "Originally this technique was named surface-enhanced affinity capture (SEAC) to distinguish it from surface-enhanced neat desorption (SEND) where the surface coating is designed to increase the efficiency of laser desorption."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12586 goldbook:12462)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12586 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12586 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12587))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12587 "surface-induced dissociation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12587 "Fragmentation that results from the collision of an ion with a surface.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003012) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12587 "SID")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12587 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12587 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12588))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12588 "surface-induced reaction")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12588 "Process wherein a reactant ion interacts with a surface to produce either chemically different species or a change in the internal energy of the reactant ion.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003012) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12588 "SIR")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12588 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12588 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12589))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12589 "surrogate internal standard")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12589 "Compound added in accurately known amounts to a sample to be analyzed for a specified analyte. The surrogate internal standard is chemically similar to the analyte so that losses in the analytical procedure are the same for both and thus the analyte concentration can be determined relative to that of the standard.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12589 "internal standard")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12589 "In quantitative mass spectrometry the preferred type is an isotope-labeled version of the analyte."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12589 "The abbreviated term \"internal standard\" is often used."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12589 goldbook:12608)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12589 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12589 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12590))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12590 "sustained off-resonance irradiation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12590 "Procedure associated with Fourier transform-ion cyclotron resonance-mass spectrometers to facilitate ion/neutral reactions such as low-energy collision-induced dissociation in which a radio-frequency electric field, slightly off-resonance with respect to the cyclotron frequency of the reactant ion, cyclically accelerates and decelerates the reactant ion that is confined in the Penning ion trap. As a consequence, the orbit does not exceed the dimensions of the ion trap but maintains a high average translational energy for an extended time that activates an ion/neutral process.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003012) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12590 "SORI")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12590 goldbook:12521)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12590 goldbook:12472)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12590 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12590 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12591))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12591 "tandem mass spectrometry in space")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12591 "Tandem mass spectrometry procedure in which product ion spectra are recorded for ion beams in m/z analyzers separated in space. Specific m/z separation functions are designed so that in one section of the instrument ions are selected, dissociated in an intermediate region, and the product ions are then transmitted to another analyzer for m/z separation and data acquisition.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12591 goldbook:12535)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12591 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12591 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12592))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12592 "tandem mass spectrometry in time")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12592 "Tandem mass spectrometry procedure in which product ion spectra are recorded in a single m/z analyzer (such as a Paul ion trap, linear ion trap, or Fourier transform-ion cyclotron resonance-mass spectrometer) in discrete steps over time. Ions in a specific m/z range are selected, dissociated, and the product ions analyzed sequentially in time.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12592 "Mass spectrometers that can perform tandem mass spectrometry in time can also perform MSn."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12592 goldbook:12498)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12592 goldbook:12516)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12592 goldbook:12465)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12592 goldbook:12535)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12592 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12592 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12593))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12593 "Taylor cone")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12593 "Conical shape of the liquid emanating from a capillary under high potential, as in electrospray or other electrohydrodynamic spray processes.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12593 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12593 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12594))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12594 "thermospray ionization")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12594 "Spray ionization in which a liquid is flowed through a heated capillary to produce a spray of droplets and solvent vapor. Ions are formed due to the statistical imbalance of charges in the droplets or by a heated filament.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12594 goldbook:12579)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12594 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12594 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12595))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12595 "thin layer chromatography-mass spectrometry")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12595 "Technique by which a mixture of analytes is separated into individual components by liquid chromatography, followed by the ionization of the separated species by an ion source of a mass spectrometer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12595 "TLC-MS")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12595 "thin layer chromatography/mass spectrometry (TLC/MS)")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12595 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12595 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12596))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12596 "time-lag focusing")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12596 "Energy focusing of ions formed in the gas phase in a time-of-flight mass spectrometer that is accomplished by introducing a time delay between the formation of the ions and the application of the accelerating potential pulse.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12596 "TLF")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12596 goldbook:12325)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12596 goldbook:12383)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12596 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12596 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12597))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12597 "tolyl ion")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12597 "Even-electron \\(\\ce{C7H7^{+}}\\) ion with the same carbon skeleton as toluene that has lost a hydrogen atom from one of the ring carbons that carries the positive charge.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12597 goldbook:12346)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12597 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12597 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12598))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12598 "toroidal ion trap")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12598 "Ion trapping device based on the three-dimensional structure formed by rotating the cross-section of a quadrupole ion trap about the edge perpendicular to the plane of the ring electrode. The resulting trapping region is toroidal.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12598 goldbook:12516)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12598 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12598 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12599))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12599 "total ion current electropherogram")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12599 "Plot of the total ion current in each of a series of mass spectra that are recorded as a function of electrophoresis time.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12599 "total ion current electrophorogram")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12599 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12599 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12600))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12600 "total ion current profile")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12600 "Any plot of total ion current in a series of mass spectra recorded as a function of time, including total ion current chromatogram, total ion current electropherogram, flow injection mass spectrometry, or any other time dependent sampling.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12600 goldbook:12410)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12600 goldbook:12415)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12600 goldbook:12599)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12600 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12600 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12601))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12601 "transmission efficiency")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12601 "Ratio of the number of ions leaving a region of a mass spectrometer to the number entering that region.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12601 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12601 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12602))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12602 "transmission quadrupole mass spectrometer")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12602 "Mass spectrometer that consists of an array of four parallel rod electrodes whose centers form the corners of a square and whose opposing electrode pairs are connected. The electric potential applied between the connected pairs of rods is a superposition of a static potential and a sinusoidal radio frequency potential. The motion of an ion in the \\(x\\mbox{-}y\\) plane perpendicular to the length direction of the rod electrodes is described by the Mathieu equation whose solutions show that ions in a particular m/z range can be transmitted along the \\(z\\mbox{-}\\rm{axis}\\).")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12602 "quadrupole mass analyzer")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12602 "quadrupole mass filter")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12602 "quadrupole mass spectrometer")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12602 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12602 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12603))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12603 "transport region")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12603 "Region in a mass spectrometer in which an ion beam is transported from the ion source to the ion optics or from one ion optical element to the next.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12603 goldbook:12444)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12603 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12603 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12604))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12604 "triple quadrupole mass spectrometer")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12604 "Tandem mass spectrometer comprising two transmission quadrupole mass spectrometers in series, with a (non-selecting) RF-only quadrupole (or other multipole) between them to act as a collision cell.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12604 goldbook:12560)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12604 goldbook:12361)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12604 goldbook:12602)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12604 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12604 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12605))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12605 "unimolecular dissociation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12605 "Fragmentation reaction in which the molecularity of the reaction system is unity. The dissociation may arise from the extra energy acquired by a metastable ion produced in the ion source or that provided by collisional excitation of a stable ion.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12605 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12605 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12606))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12606 "unit mass resolution")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12606 "Mass resolution such that it is possible to clearly distinguish a peak corresponding to a singly charged ion from its neighbors \\(\\pu{1 u}\\) away, usually with no more than \\(\\pu{5\\!-\\! 10\\%}\\) overlap.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12606 "This term is most frequently used to describe resolution obtained using a Paul ion trap or a transmission quadrupole mass spectrometer."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12606 goldbook:12516)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12606 goldbook:12602)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12606 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12606 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12607))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12607 "v-ion")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12607 "High-energy product ion of a protonated peptide formally equivalent to a y-ion with the ionizing proton on the \\(\\ce{N}\\)-terminus, but with elimination of \\(\\ce{HR}\\) from the \\(\\ce{N}\\)-terminus where \\(\\ce{R}\\) is the side-chain on the \\(\\ce{C}\\)-atom of the \\(\\ce{N}\\)-terminal residue, to give a (\\(\\ce{H2N^{+}=CH-CO\\bond{-}}\\)) structure.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12607 goldbook:12613)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12607 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12607 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12608))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12608 "volumetric internal standard")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12608 "Compound added in a fixed reproducible amount to a solution to be analyzed by gas chromatography to permit corrections for uncontrolled variations in injected volumes.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12608 goldbook:12589)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12608 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12608 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12609))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12609 "Wahrhaftig diagram")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12609 "Diagram illustrating the relative contributions in unimolecular dissociation of an ion, for example, by homolytic cleavage of a single bond, and fragmentation following rearrangement. The diagram is in two parts with a common horizontal axis representing the internal energy of the ion. The vertical axis in one part of the diagram shows the two types of rate constant on a logarithmic scale, and that for the other portion of the diagram indicates the distribution function for internal energy of the ion.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12609 goldbook:12605)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12609 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12609 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12610))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12610 "Wien filter")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12610 "Mass spectrometer in which m/z separation is achieved using crossed electric and magnetic fields.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12610 "It can also be operated as a charged particle energy analyzer or monochromator."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12610 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12610 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12611))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12611 "w-ion")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12611 "High-energy product ion of a protonated peptide formally equivalent to a z-ion that has lost the part of the \\(\\ce{N}\\)-terminal side-chain starting at the \\(\\ce{\\upgamma\\mbox{-}carbon}\\) (if any).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12611 goldbook:12614)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12611 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12611 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12612))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12612 "x-ion")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12612 "Fragment ion containing the peptide \\(\\ce{C}\\)-terminus formed upon dissociation of a peptide ion at the peptide backbone \\(\\ce{C-C}\\) bond.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12612 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12612 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12613))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12613 "y-ion")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12613 "Fragment ion containing the peptide \\(\\ce{C}\\)-terminus formed upon dissociation of a peptide ion at the peptide backbone \\(\\ce{C-N}\\) bond.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12613 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12613 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12614))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12614 "z-ion")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12614 "Fragment ion containing the peptide \\(\\ce{C}\\)-terminus formed upon dissociation of a peptide ion at the peptide backbone \\(\\ce{N-C}\\) bond.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12614 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-06-04-06)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12614 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12615))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12615 "ADMET")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12615 "Acronym referring to the absorption, distribution, metabolism, excretion, and toxicity profile or processes for a xenobiotic upon its administration in vivo.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12615 "ADME is also used to delineate these selected parameters within the context of a xenobiotic’s pharmacokinetic profile. Because any of the five characteristics may become hurdles during drug development, ADMET behaviour is typically studied and optimized among efficacious analogues during the early drug discovery stage by using in vitro models that attempt to predict such behaviours in clinical studies."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12615 goldbook:12646)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12615 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12615 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12616))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12616 "allosteric antagonist")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12616 "Compound that binds to a receptor at a site separate from, but actively coupled to, that of the endogenous agonist to reduce actively receptor signals.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12616 "The terms \"allosteric antagonist\" and \"noncompetitive antagonist\" are often synonymous but not necessarily so."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12616 goldbook:12694)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12616 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12616 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12617))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12617 "alpha-helix")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12617 "Secondary 3D structure of a protein or peptide containing a right-handed coiled or spiral conformation, in which every backbone \\(\\ce{N-H}\\) group donates a hydrogen bond to the backbone \\(\\ce{C=O}\\) group of the amino acid four residues earlier.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12617 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12617 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12618))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12618 "analogue")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12618 "Chemical compound having structural similarity to a reference compound.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12618 "analog")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12618 "Despite the structural similarity, an analogue may display different chemical and/or biological properties, as is often intentionally the case during design and synthesis to optimize either efficacy or ADMET properties within a given series."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12618 goldbook:12615)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12618 goldbook:12619)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12618 goldbook:12658)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12618 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12618 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12619))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12619 "analogue-based drug discovery")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12619 "Strategy for drug discovery and/or optimization in which structural modification of an existing drug provides a new drug with improved chemical and/or biological properties.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12619 "analog-based drug discovery")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12619 "Within the context of analogue-based drug discovery, three categories of drug analogues are recognized: Compounds possessing structural, chemical, and pharmacological similarities, termed \"direct analogues\" and sometimes referred to as \"me-too\" drugs; compounds possessing structural and often chemical but not pharmacological similarities, termed \"structural analogues\"; and structurally different compounds displaying similar pharmacological properties, termed \"pharmacological analogues\"."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12619 goldbook:12681)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12619 goldbook:12679)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12619 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12619 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12620))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12620 "ATP binding cassette protein")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12620 "Large gene family of transporter proteins that bind ATP and use the energy to transport substrates (e.g., sugars, amino acids, metal ions, peptides, proteins, and a large number of hydrophobic compounds and metabolites) across lipid membranes.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12620 "ABC protein")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12620 "These proteins have an important role in limiting oral absorption and brain penetration of xenobiotics."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12620 goldbook:12704)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12620 goldbook:12653)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12620 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12620 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12621))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12621 "attrition rate")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12621 "Rate of loss of drug candidates during progression through the optimisation and developmental stages while on route to the marketplace.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12621 "It has been estimated that for every \\(\\pu{10000}\\) compounds examined during the early stages of biological testing just one reaches the market."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12621 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12621 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12622))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12622 "autoinduction")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12622 "Capacity of a drug to induce enzymes that mediate its own metabolism.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12622 "This often results in lower, often sub-therapeutic, drug exposure on prolonged or multiple dosing."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12622 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12622 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12623))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12623 "back-up compound")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12623 "Molecule selected as a replacement for the lead drug candidate should this subsequently fail during further preclinical evaluation or in clinical studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12623 "Ideally, a back-up should be pharmacologically equivalent to the lead drug but have significant structural differences. Possession of a distinct core scaffold is optimal."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12623 goldbook:12724)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12623 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12623 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12624))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12624 "best-in-class")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12624 "Drug acting on a specific molecular target that provides the best balance between efficacy and adverse effects.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12624 goldbook:12684)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12624 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12624 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12625))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12625 "beta-barrel")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12625 "Secondary 3D protein structure containing a large beta-sheet that twists and coils to form a closed structure in which the first-strand hydrogen bonds to the last.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12625 goldbook:12626)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12625 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12625 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12626))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12626 "beta-sheet")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12626 "Secondary 3D structure of a protein that takes on a flat, pleated appearance.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12626 "Other common protein structural motifs are the alpha-helix and beta-barrel."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12626 goldbook:12617)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12626 goldbook:12625)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12626 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12626 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12627))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12627 "beta-sheet breaker")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12627 "Compound that on binding to a protein disrupts beta-sheet formation.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12627 goldbook:12626)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12627 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12627 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12628))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12628 "biological agent")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12628 "Biopolymer-based pharmaceutical, such as a protein, applicable to the prevention, treatment, or cure of diseases or injuries to man.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12628 "Biological agents may be any virus, therapeutic serum, toxin, antitoxin, vaccine, blood component or derivative, allergenic product, or analogous products."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12628 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12628 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12629))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12629 "blockbuster drug")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12629 "Drug that generates annual sales of USD 1 billion (\\(\\$\\pu{E9}\\)) or more.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12629 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12629 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12630))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12630 "carcinogen")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12630 "Agent (chemical, physical, or biological) that is capable of increasing the incidence of malignant neoplasms, thus causing cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12630 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12630 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12631))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12631 "chemical biology")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12631 "Application of chemistry to the study of molecular events in biological systems, often using tool compounds.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12631 "Distinguished from medicinal chemistry, which is focused on the design and optimisation of compounds for specific molecular targets."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12631 goldbook:12684)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12631 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12631 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12632))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12632 "chemical database")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12632 "Specific electronic repository for storage and retrieval of chemical information.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12632 "Chemical structural information is sometimes stored in string notation such as the InChI or SMILES notations."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12632 "Such databases can be searched to retrieve structural information and data on specific or related molecules."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12632 "A free database of chemical structures of small organic molecules and information on their biological activities is available from PubChem."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12632 goldbook:12671)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12632 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12632 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12633))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12633 "chemical library")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12633 "Collection of samples (e.g., chemical compounds, natural products, over-expression library of a microbe) available for biological screening. Set of compounds produced through combinatorial chemistry or other means that expands around a single core structure or scaffold.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12633 "compound collection")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12633 "compound library")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12633 goldbook:12724)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12633 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12633 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12634))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12634 "chemical space")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12634 "Set of all possible stable molecules based on a specific chemical entity that interacts at one or more specific molecular targets.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12634 goldbook:12684)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12634 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12634 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12635))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12635 "chemogenomics")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12635 "Systematic screening of chemical libraries of congeneric compounds against members of a target family of proteins.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12635 "chemical genomics")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12635 goldbook:12633)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12635 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12635 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12636))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12636 "chemokine")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12636 "Member of a superfamily of proteins with the primary function to control leukocyte activity and trafficking through tissues.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12636 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12636 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12637))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12637 "co-drug")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12637 "Two chemically linked synergistic drugs designed to improve the drug delivery properties of one or both drugs.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12637 "mutual prodrug [1]")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12637 "The constituent drugs are indicated for the same disease, but may exert different therapeutic effects via disparate mechanisms of action."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12637 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12637 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12638))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12638 "constitutive activity")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12638 "Receptor or enzymatic function displayed in the absence of an agonist or activator.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12638 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12638 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12639))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12639 "contract research organisation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12639 "Commercial organisation that can be engaged to undertake specifically defined chemical, biological, safety, or clinical studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12639 "CRO")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12639 "Typically, such studies are subject to confidentially agreements."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12639 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12639 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12640))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12640 "covalent drug")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12640 "Ligand that binds irreversibly to its molecular target through the formation of a new chemical bond.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12640 goldbook:12684)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12640 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12640 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12641))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12641 "designed multiple ligands")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12641 "Compounds conceived and synthesised to act on two or more molecular targets.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12641 goldbook:12684)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12641 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12641 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12642))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12642 "diversity")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12642 "Unrelatedness of a set of molecules (e.g., building blocks or members of a compound library), as measured by properties such as atom connectivity, physical properties, or computationally generated descriptors.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12642 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12642 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12643))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12643 "diversity-oriented synthesis")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12643 "Efficient production of a range of structures and templates with skeletal and stereochemical diversity as opposed to the synthesis of a specific target molecule.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12643 "DOS")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12643 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12643 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12644))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12644 "drug cocktail")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12644 "­(in drug therapy) Administration of two or more distinct pharmacological agents to achieve a combination of their individual effects. Note 1: The combined effect may be additive, synergistic, or designed to reduce side-effects. Note 2: This term is often used synonymously with that of 'drug combination' but is preferred in order to avoid confusion with medications in which different drugs are included in a single formulation. (in drug testing) Administration of two or more distinct compounds to test simultaneously their individual behaviours (e.g., pharmacological effects in high-throughput screens or drug metabolism).")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12644 "drug combination")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12644 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12644 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12645))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12645 "drug delivery")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12645 "Process by which a drug is administered to its intended recipient.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12645 goldbook:12646)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12645 goldbook:12732)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12645 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12645 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12646))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12646 "drug distribution")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12646 "Measured amounts of an administered compound in various parts of the organism to which it is given.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12646 goldbook:12645)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12646 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12646 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12647))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12647 "druggability")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12647 "Capacity of a molecular target to be modulated in a favourable manner by a small-molecule drug.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12647 "It is estimated that only around \\(\\pu{10\\%}\\) of the human genome affords druggable targets."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12647 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12647 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12648))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12648 "drug repurposing")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12648 "Strategy that seeks to discover new applications for an existing drug that were not previously referenced and not currently prescribed or investigated.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12648 "drug repositioning")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12648 "drug reprofiling")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12648 "Various additional synonymous terms have been used to describe the process of drug repurposing. All appear to be used interchangeably."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12648 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12648 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12649))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12649 "drug safety")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12649 "Assessment of the nontolerable biological effects of a drug.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12649 "Because the nontolerable effects of a drug are directly related to its concentration or dose, safety is generally ranked relative to the dose required to obtain the desirable effect."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12649 goldbook:12735)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12649 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12649 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12650))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12650 "dual binding site")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12650 "Presence of two distinct ligand binding sites on the same molecular target.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12650 goldbook:12684)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12650 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12650 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12651))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12651 "effective concentration")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12651 "Concentration of a substance that produces a defined magnitude of response in a given system.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12651 "EC")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12651 "EC50 is the median dose that causes \\(\\pu{50\\%}\\) of the maximal response."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12651 "The term usually refers to an agonist in a receptor system effect and could represent either an increase or a decrease in a biological function."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12651 goldbook:12669)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12651 goldbook:12652)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12651 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12651 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12652))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12652 "effective dose")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12652 "Dose of a substance that causes a defined magnitude of response in a given system.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12652 "ED")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12652 "ED50 is the median dose that causes \\(\\pu{50\\%}\\) of the maximal response."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12652 goldbook:12669)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12652 goldbook:12651)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12652 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12652 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12653))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12653 "efflux pump")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12653 "Transporter protein located in the membrane of cells that utilizes active transport to move a compound from the internal to the external environment.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12653 goldbook:12620)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12653 goldbook:12704)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12653 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12653 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12654))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12654 "equilibrium solubility")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12654 "Analytical composition of a mixture or solution that is saturated with one of the components in the designated mixture or solution.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12654 "Solubility may be expressed in any units corresponding to quantities that denote relative composition, such as mass, amount concentration, molality, etc."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12654 "The mixture or solution may involve any physical state: solid, liquid, gas, vapour, supercritical fluid."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12654 "The term \"solubility\" is also often used in a more general sense to refer to processes and phenomena related to dissolution."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12654 goldbook:12672)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12654 goldbook:12676)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12654 goldbook:12730)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12654 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12654 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12655))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12655 "fast follower")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12655 "Compound selected as a rapid successor to a lead drug candidate.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12655 "Fast followers usually possess a marked increase in one or more pharmacological/pharmaceutical characteristics such as potency, efficacy, therapeutic index, or physicochemical parameters (e.g., solubility)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12655 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12655 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12656))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12656 "fingerprint")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12656 "Representation of a compound or chemical library by attributes (descriptors) such as atom connectivities, 3D structure, or physical properties.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12656 goldbook:12633)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12656 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12656 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12657))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12657 "first-in-class")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12657 "First drug acting on a hitherto unaddressed molecular target to reach the market.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12657 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12657 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12658))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12658 "follow-on drug")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12658 "Drug having a similar mechanism of action to an existing drug.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12658 "Compounds may be of the same or different chemical class. A therapeutic advantage over first-in-class drugs must be demonstrated for regulatory approval."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12658 goldbook:12618)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12658 goldbook:12619)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12658 goldbook:12657)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12658 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12658 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12659))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12659 "fragment")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12659 "Low-molar-mass ligand (typically smaller than \\(\\pu{200 Da}\\)) that binds to a target with low affinity but high ligand efficiency.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12659 "Typically fragments have affinities in a concentration interval from \\(\\pu{0.1 mm}\\) to \\(\\pu{1.0 mM}\\)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12659 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12659 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12660))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12660 "fragment-based lead discovery")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12660 "Screening libraries of low-molar-mass compounds (typically \\(\\pu{120\\!{-}\\! 250 Da}\\)) using sensitive biophysical techniques capable of detecting weakly binding lead compounds.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12660 "X-ray structures are frequently used to drive the optimisation of fragment hits to leads."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12660 goldbook:12659)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12660 goldbook:12664)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12660 goldbook:12677)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12660 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12660 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12661))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12661 "frequent hitter")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12661 "Structural feature that regularly results in a positive response in a variety of high-throughput or primary screens.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12661 "Such compounds often exert their actions through nonspecific mechanisms and are therefore unreliable leads."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12661 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12661 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12662))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12662 "G protein")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12662 "Member of a family of membrane-associated proteins which on activation by cellular receptors lead to signal transduction.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12662 "guanine binding protein")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12662 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12662 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12663))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12663 "green chemistry")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12663 "Invention, design, and application of chemical products and processes to reduce or eliminate the use and generation of hazardous substances.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12663 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12663 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12664))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12664 "hit")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12664 "Molecule that produces reproducible activity above a defined threshold in a biological assay and whose structural identity has been established.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12664 "Hits typically derive from high-throughput screening initiatives or other relatively extensive primary assays and do not become true hits until fully validated."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12664 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12664 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12665))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12665 "hit expansion")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12665 "Generation of additional compound sets that contain chemical motifs and scaffolds that have activity in the primary screen.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12665 "This methodology permits the identification of additional hits and new scaffolds and develops structure-activity relationships around existing hits."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12665 goldbook:12664)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12665 goldbook:12724)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12665 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12665 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12666))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12666 "hit-to-lead chemistry")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12666 "Process by which a proven molecule or series derived from high-throughput screening or primary screens is chemically optimised to a viable lead or series.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12666 goldbook:12677)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12666 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12666 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12667))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12667 "homology model")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12667 "Computational representation of a protein built from the 3D structure of a similar protein or proteins using alignment techniques and homology arguments.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12667 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12667 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12668))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12668 "hydrophobic fragmental constant")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12668 "Representation of the lipophilicity contribution of a constituent part of a structure to the total lipophilicity.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12668 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12668 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12669))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12669 "inhibitory concentration at 50%")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12669 "The concentration of an enzyme inhibitor or receptor antagonist that reduces the enzyme activity or agonist response by \\(\\pu{50\\%}\\).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12669 "\\(\\rm{IC}_{50}\\) values are influenced by experimental conditions (e.g., substrate or agonist concentration, which should be specified)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12669 goldbook:12670)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12669 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12669 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12670))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12670 "inhibition constant")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12670 "Equilibrium dissociation constant of an enzyme-inhibitor complex: \\(K_{\\rm{i}} = [\\ce{E}][\\ce{I}]/[\\ce{EI}]\\). The equilibrium dissociation constant of a receptor-ligand complex.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12670 "This value is usually obtained through competition binding experiments, where the \\(K_{\\rm{i}}\\) is determined after the IC50 obtained in a competition assay performed in the presence of a known concentration of labeled reference ligand."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12670 goldbook:12669)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12670 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12670 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12672))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12672 "intrinsic solubility")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12672 "Equilibrium solubility of the uncharged form of an ionisable compound at a pH where it is fully unionised. \\[\\ce{HA(s)  HA(aq)} \\quad (1)\\] \\[\\ce{HA(aq)  H^{+}(aq) + A^{-}(aq)} \\quad (2)\\]")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12672 "The intrinsic solubility can be determined from the analytical composition at a \\(\\pu{pH}\\) where \\([\\ce{HA}]\\) is very much greater than \\([\\ce{A^{-}}]\\)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12672 goldbook:12654)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12672 goldbook:12676)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12672 goldbook:12730)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12672 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12672 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12673))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12673 "investigational new drug")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12673 "Drug not yet approved for general use by the national authority, such as the Food and Drug Administration of the United States of America, but undergoing clinical investigation to assess its safety and efficacy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12673 "IND")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12673 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12673 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12674))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12674 "ionotropic receptor")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12674 "Transmembrane ion channel that opens or closes in response to the binding of a ligand.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12674 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12674 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12675))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12675 "kinase")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12675 "Enzyme that transfers a phosphate group from high-energy donor molecules, such as ATP, to specific target molecules.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12675 "phosphotransferase")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12675 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12675 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12676))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12676 "kinetic solubility")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12676 "Composition of a solution with respect to a compound when its induced precipitate first appears.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12676 "turbidimetric solubility")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12676 goldbook:12654)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12676 goldbook:12672)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12676 goldbook:12730)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12676 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12676 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12677))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12677 "lead")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12677 "Compound (or compound series) that satisfies predefined minimum criteria for further structure and activity optimization.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12677 "Typically, a lead will demonstrate appropriate activity, selectivity, tractable structure-activity relationship and have confirmed activity in a relevant cell-based assay."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12677 goldbook:12678)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12677 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12677 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12678))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12678 "lead validation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12678 "Process by which a lead compound is authenticated by the confirmation of its expected pharmacological properties.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12678 "Usually, a cluster of structurally similar compounds showing discernable structure-activity relationships will support the validation process."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12678 goldbook:12677)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12678 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12678 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12679))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12679 "ligand-based drug design")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12679 "Method of drug discovery and/or optimization in which the pursuit of new structures and/or structural modifications is based upon one or more ligands known to interact with the molecular target of interest.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12679 "This approach is applicable even when no structural detail of the target is known. In such cases a series of analogues is usually prepared and tested to produce structure-activity relationship data that can be extrapolated to indirectly derive a topographical map of the biological surface."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12679 goldbook:12619)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12679 goldbook:12618)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12679 goldbook:12684)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12679 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12679 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12680))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12680 "metabotropic receptor")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12680 "Receptor that modulates electric potential-gated channels via G-proteins.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12680 "The interaction can occur entirely within the membrane or by the generation of diffusible second messengers. The involvement of G-proteins causes the activation of these receptors to last tens of seconds to minutes, in contrast with the brief effect of ionotropic receptors."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12680 goldbook:12662)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12680 goldbook:12674)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12680 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12680 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12681))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12681 "me-too drug")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12681 "Term applied to drug analogues that offer no significant advantage over the prototype compound.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12681 "Continued use of this term is not recommended."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12681 goldbook:12618)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12681 goldbook:12658)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12681 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12681 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12682))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12682 "microRNA")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12682 "Small single-stranded RNA molecules that play a significant role in the post-transcriptional regulation of gene expression.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12682 "miRNA")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12682 "MicroRNA usually comprises approximately 22 nucleotides."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12682 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12682 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12683))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12683 "molecular descriptor")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12683 "Parameter that characterizes a specific structural or physicochemical aspect of a molecule.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12683 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12683 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12684))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12684 "molecular target")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12684 "Protein (e.g., receptor, enzyme, or ion channel), RNA, or DNA that is implicated in a clinical disorder or the propagation of any untoward event.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12684 "Usually, biochemical, pharmacological, or genomic information supporting the role of such a target in disease will be available."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12684 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12684 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12685))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12685 "multidrug resistance")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12685 "Characteristic of cells that confers resistance to the effects of several different classes of drugs.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12685 "MDR")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12685 "There are several forms of drug resistance. Each is determined by genes that govern how cells will respond to chemical agents. One type of multidrug resistance involves the ability to eject several drugs out of cells (e.g., efflux pumps such as P-glycoprotein)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12685 goldbook:12704)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12685 goldbook:12653)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12685 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12685 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12686))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12686 "multiparameter optimisation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12686 "Drug-likeness penetrability algorithm derived from CLOGP, clogD, molar mass, topological polar surface area, number of hydrogen-bond donors, and \\(\\pu{p}K_{\\rm{a}}\\).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12686 "MPO")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12686 "The MPO desirability score is larger or equal to 4 on a scale of 0 to 6."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12686 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12686 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12687))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12687 "multitarget-directed ligand")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12687 "Ligand acting on more than one distinct molecular target. Targets may be of the same or different mechanistic classes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12687 "MTDL")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12687 "multitarget drug")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12687 goldbook:12684)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12687 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12687 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12688))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12688 "multitarget drug discovery")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12688 "Deliberate design of compounds that act on more than one molecular target.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12688 "MTDD")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12688 goldbook:12684)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12688 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12688 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12689))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12689 "Murcko assembly")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12689 "Core scaffold of a molecule that remains after all chain substituents that do not terminate in a ring are removed. Single atoms connected by a double bond are typically also retained.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12689 goldbook:12724)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12689 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12689 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12690))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12690 "neglected disease")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12690 "Term used to emphasise an imbalance between therapeutic needs and resource allocation.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12690 "Different groups define neglected diseases differently, but typically they include diseases such as schistosomiasis, Chagas disease, tuberculosis, and malaria, as well as other parasitic and vector-borne diseases."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12690 "The terms \"tropical disease\" and \"neglected disease\" are sometimes indistinguishable or used interchangeably."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12690 goldbook:12698)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12690 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12690 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12691))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12691 "neutral antagonist")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12691 "Ligand that blocks the responses of a receptor to both agonists and inverse agonists with the same intensity. It binds to the receptor without evoking any change of conformation or change to the ratio of activated to inactivated conformations.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12691 "Perfect neutral antagonism is difficult to achieve."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12691 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12691 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12692))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12692 "new chemical entity")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12692 "Drug that contains no active moiety previously approved for use by the national authority, such as the U.S. Food and Drug Administration.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12692 goldbook:12693)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12692 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12692 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12693))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12693 "new molecular entity")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12693 "Active ingredient that has never before been approved in any form by the national authority, such as the U.S. Food and Drug Administration.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12693 goldbook:12692)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12693 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12693 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12694))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12694 "noncompetitive antagonist")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12694 "Functional antagonist that either binds irreversibly to a receptor or to a site distinct from that of the natural agonist.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12694 goldbook:12616)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12694 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12694 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12695))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12695 "nuclear hormone receptor")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12695 "Ligand-activated transcription factor that regulates gene expression by interacting with specific DNA sequences upstream of its target gene(s).")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12695 "nuclear receptor")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12695 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12695 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12696))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12696 "obviousness")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12696 "Term associated with intellectual property wherein the latter’s patentability is assessed relative to the combination of more than one item of 'prior art'.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12696 "To be patentable within the context of medicinal chemistry, a given compound must be: (i) novel, in that its specific arrangement of atoms has never been previously disclosed; (ii) non-obvious, in that its specific arrangement of atoms is not readily suggested to be of benefit by a person having ordinary skill in the art upon considering two or more other, previously disclosed structures; and, (iii) useful, in that it should have some benefit, the disclosure of the latter encompassing a valid \"reduction to practice\"."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12696 goldbook:12702)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12696 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12696 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12697))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12697 "off-target effect")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12697 "Pharmacological action induced by any molecule at molecular/biological sites distinct from that for which it was designed.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12697 "Such effects are dose-dependent and may be beneficial, adverse, or neutral."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12697 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12697 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12698))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12698 "orphan disease")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12698 "Disease for which drug research, development, and marketing is economically unfavourable.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12698 "The poor commercial environment could be due to a lack of economic incentives or a lack of understanding of the diseases or a combination of both."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12698 "Sometimes the term \"rare disease\" is used synonymously with orphan disease, although there is a slight difference. For example, a rare disease is so uncommon that there is no drug development effort."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12698 "Which diseases are classified as orphan depends strongly on the country that classifies it. In the United States, for example, any disease affecting less than \\(\\pu{200000}\\) people is considered an orphan or rare disease. Europe and countries such as Japan, Australia, and Singapore have a different definition."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12698 goldbook:12690)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12698 goldbook:12699)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12698 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12698 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12699))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12699 "orphan drug")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12699 "Pharmaceutical agent that has been approved specifically to treat a rare and commercially unfavourable medical condition.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12699 goldbook:12698)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12699 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12699 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12700))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12700 "orphan receptor")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12700 "Receptor for which an endogenous ligand has yet to be identified.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12700 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12700 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12701))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12701 "parallel synthesis")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12701 "Simultaneous preparation of sets of discrete compounds in arrays of physically separate reaction vessels or microcompartments without interchange of intermediates during the assembly process.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12701 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12701 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12702))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12702 "patentability")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12702 "Set of criteria that must be satisfied in order to achieve commercial exclusivity for an invention.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12702 "These criteria are essentially the same in all major countries and include: suitability, novelty, inventiveness, utility, and the provision of an adequate description."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12702 goldbook:12696)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12702 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12702 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12703))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12703 "peptoid")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12703 "Peptide-like oligomer consisting of repeating \\(N\\)-substituted glycine units  where \\(\\ce{R1}\\) to \\(\\ce{R4}\\) are typically alkyl or aryl and may be the same or different.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12703 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12703 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12704))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12704 "P-glycoprotein")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12704 "ATP-binding cassette transporter responsible for the efflux of small molecules from cells.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12704 "Pgp")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12704 "P-glycoproteins can play a major role in limiting brain penetration and restricting the intestinal absorption of drugs. Their over-expression in cancer cells becomes a common mechanism of multidrug resistance."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12704 goldbook:12620)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12704 goldbook:12653)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12704 goldbook:12685)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12704 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12704 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12705))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12705 "pharmacogenetics")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12705 "Study of inherited differences (variation) in drug metabolism and response.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12705 goldbook:12706)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12705 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12705 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12706))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12706 "pharmacogenomics")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12706 "General study of all of the many different genes that determine drug behaviour.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12706 "The distinction between the terms pharmacogenetics and pharmacogenomics has blurred with time. and they are now frequently used interchangeably."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12706 goldbook:12705)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12706 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12706 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12707))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12707 "phase 0 clinical studies")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12707 "Exploratory first-in-human trials that involve microdosing of drug to allow the assessment of pharmacokinetic parameters with limited drug exposure.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12707 "exploratory investigational new drug")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12707 "These trials have no therapeutic or diagnostic intent but are designed to assist decision making by providing bioavailability, metabolism, and other limited data from a small number of patients."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12707 goldbook:12708)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12707 goldbook:12709)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12707 goldbook:12710)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12707 goldbook:12711)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12707 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12707 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12708))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12708 "phase I clinical studies")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12708 "Initial introduction of an investigational new drug into humans.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12708 "These studies are designed to determine the metabolic and pharmacologic actions of the drug in humans, the side-effects associated with increasing doses, and, if possible, to gain early evidence on effectiveness."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12708 goldbook:12673)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12708 goldbook:12709)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12708 goldbook:12710)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12708 goldbook:12711)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12708 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12708 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12709))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12709 "phase II clinical studies")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12709 "Controlled clinical studies conducted in a limited number of individuals to obtain some preliminary data on the effectiveness of an investigational new drug for a particular indication or indications in patients with the disease or condition.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12709 "Phase II clinical trials have two subclasses, IIa and IIb. Phase IIa trials are essentially pilot clinical trials designed to evaluate efficacy (and safety) in selected populations of patients with the disease or condition to be treated, diagnosed, or prevented. Phase IIb trials extend those of Phase IIa to well-controlled trials that evaluate the same parameters in similar patient populations."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12709 goldbook:12673)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12709 goldbook:12707)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12709 goldbook:12708)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12709 goldbook:12710)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12709 goldbook:12711)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12709 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12709 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12710))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12710 "phase III clinical studies")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12710 "Expanded controlled and uncontrolled trials in humans.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12710 "These trials are performed after preliminary evidence suggesting effectiveness of the drug has been obtained in phase II, and are intended to gather the additional information about effectiveness and safety that is needed to evaluate the overall benefit/risk relationship of the drug."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12710 goldbook:12707)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12710 goldbook:12708)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12710 goldbook:12709)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12710 goldbook:12711)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12710 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12710 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12711))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12711 "phase IV clinical studies")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12711 "Extended post-marketing studies in humans.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12711 "These trials are designed to broaden information concerning treatment risks, benefits, and optimal drug use."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12711 goldbook:12707)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12711 goldbook:12708)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12711 goldbook:12709)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12711 goldbook:12710)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12711 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12711 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12712))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12712 "phenotypic screening")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12712 "Evaluation of compounds (small molecules, peptides, siRNA, etc.) in cells, tissues, or organisms for their ability to modify the system in a measurable manner.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12712 "Phenotypic screening differs from target-based screens in that it assesses the overall response of the compound under investigation rather than its specific response on a purified molecular target. Advances in molecular biology resulted in a marked shift away from phenotypic screening, although the latter is now regaining popularity."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12712 goldbook:12727)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12712 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12712 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12713))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12713 "pipeline")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12713 "Discovery and development compound portfolio of a pharmaceutical company or research organization.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12713 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12713 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12714))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12714 "pivotal study")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12714 "Experiment that provides strong support for or against the drug or molecular target under investigation.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12714 goldbook:12684)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12714 goldbook:12718)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12714 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12714 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12715))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12715 "potential genotoxic impurity")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12715 "Confirmed or suspected presence of one or more known genotoxic materials in an active pharmaceutical ingredient.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12715 "Typically, such impurities arise from reactive intermediates involved in the synthetic pathway and have the potential to adversely affect subsequent genotoxicity tests."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12715 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12715 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12716))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12716 "preclinical candidate")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12716 "Optimised lead compound successfully passing key screening, selectivity, and physicochemical criteria sufficient to warrant further detailed pharmacological and pharmacokinetic evaluation in animal models.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12716 "PCC")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12716 "safety assessment candidate")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12716 "Critical studies usually include bioavailability, therapeutic efficacy in an appropriate disease model, and side-effect profiling."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12716 goldbook:12677)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12716 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12716 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12717))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12717 "privileged structure")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12717 "Substructural feature that confers desirable (often drug-like) properties on compounds containing that feature. They often consist of a semi-rigid scaffold that presents multiple hydrophobic residues without undergoing hydrophobic collapse.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12717 "For example, diazepam (below) in which the diphenylmethane moiety prevents association of the aromatic rings. "^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12717 "Such structures are commonly found to confer activity against different targets belonging to the same receptor family."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12717 goldbook:12724)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12717 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12717 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12718))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12718 "proof of concept")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12718 "Procedure by which a specific therapeutic mechanism or treatment/diagnostic paradigm is shown to be beneficial.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12718 "Similar to, and often simultaneously associated with, that for a new drug candidate. This process usually involves an early supporting step prior to clinical testing and final validation within human studies."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12718 goldbook:12678)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12718 goldbook:12714)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12718 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12718 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12719))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12719 "proteinase")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12719 "Enzyme that catalyses the hydrolysis of proteins.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12719 "protease")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12719 "Usually, several proteolytic enzymes are necessary for the complete breakdown of polypeptides to their amino acids."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12719 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12719 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12720))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12720 "prototype drug")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12720 "Early compound that has biological properties suitable for target validation but may not necessarily be adequate for clinical studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12720 goldbook:12684)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12720 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12720 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12721))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12721 "QTc interval")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12721 "Time between the start of the Q wave and the end of the T wave in the heart’s electrical cycle. When corrected for individual heart rate it becomes known as the corrected QT, or QTc interval.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12721 "Significant prolongation of the QTc interval by pharmaceutical agents can induce life-threatening ventricular arrhythmia (Torsades de Pointes), typically by interacting with the hERG channel."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12721 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12721 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12722))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12722 "retrosynthesis")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12722 "Process of conceptually deconstructing complex molecules into simpler fragments capable of chemical manipulation to reform the parent compound.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12722 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12722 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12723))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12723 "rule of three")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12723 "Set of molecular descriptors used to assess the quality of hit or lead molecules.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12723 "Most commonly applied to fragments that ideally are characterized by a mass of less than \\(\\pu{300 Da}\\) less than or equal to three hydrogen bond donors, less than or equal to three hydrogen bond acceptors, and a CLOGP of less than or equal to three. In addition, the number of rotatable bonds should average or be less than three and the polar surface area about \\(\\pu{0.6 nm2}\\)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12723 "Often used to distinguish \"lead-like\" from \"drug-like\" molecules."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12723 goldbook:12660)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12723 goldbook:12659)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12723 goldbook:12664)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12723 goldbook:12677)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12723 goldbook:12683)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12723 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12723 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12724))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12724 "scaffold")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12724 "Core portion of a molecule common to all members of a chemical library or compound series.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12724 "template")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12724 goldbook:12633)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12724 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12724 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12725))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12725 "scaffold hopping")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12725 "Exchange of one scaffold for another while maintaining molecular features that are important for biological properties.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12725 goldbook:12724)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12725 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12725 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12726))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12726 "site-directed mutagenesis")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12726 "Molecular biology technique in which mutations are created at one or more defined sites in a DNA molecule.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12726 "Typically used in molecular target validation and to determine whether specific amino acids are involved at ligand or substrate interaction sites."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12726 goldbook:12684)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12726 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12726 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12727))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12727 "small inhibitory double-stranded RNA")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12727 "Small RNA fragments that can combine with specific genes to silence their expression.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12727 "siRNA")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12727 "small interfering double-stranded RNA")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12727 "siRNAs are powerful tools that are often used for manipulating gene expression during molecular target validation."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12727 goldbook:12684)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12727 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12727 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12728))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12728 "spare receptor")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12728 "Residual binding site still available to an endogenous ligand after sufficient sites have already been filled to elicit the maximal response possible for that particular biological system.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12728 "receptor reserve")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12728 "Xenobiotics such as drugs may similarly interact with such receptors, but by definition, their identification and quantification occurs via use of the natural ligand."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12728 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12728 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12729))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12729 "structural alert")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12729 "Chemical features present in a hit or lead molecule indicative of potential toxicity.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12729 "Typically, such features include chemically reactive functionality and components known to metabolise to chemically reactive entities."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12729 goldbook:12664)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12729 goldbook:12677)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12729 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12729 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12730))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12730 "supersaturated solution")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12730 "Solution that has a greater composition of a solute than one that is in equilibrium with undissolved solute at specified values of temperature and pressure.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12730 goldbook:12654)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12730 goldbook:12672)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12730 goldbook:12676)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12730 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12730 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12731))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12731 "systems biology")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12731 "Integration of high-throughput biology measurements with computational models that study the projection of the mechanistic characteristics of metabolic and signalling pathways onto physiological and pathological phenotypes.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12731 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12731 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12732))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12732 "targeted drug delivery")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12732 "Approach to target a drug to a specific tissue or molecular target using a prodrug or antibody recognition systems.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12732 goldbook:12684)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12732 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12732 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12733))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12733 "target validation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12733 "Process by which a protein, RNA, or DNA is implicated in a biological pathway thought to be of relevance to a disease or adverse pathology.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12733 "Typically, validation will involve location of the molecular target in relevant cells, organs, or tissues, evidence for its up-regulation/activation in the disorder, and the ability to attenuate adverse responses by agents known to interfere with the target."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12733 goldbook:12684)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12733 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12733 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12734))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12734 "tautomer")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12734 "Structural isomer that can readily convert to another form that differs only by the attachment position of a hydrogen atom and the location of double bond(s).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12734 "In most cases, these isomers are formed by a proton shift to or from heteroatoms such as \\(\\ce{O}\\), \\(\\ce{N}\\), or \\(\\ce{S}\\) as typified by the enol and keto forms of carbonyl compounds. Tautomers rapidly interconvert by proton transfer and are usually in equilibrium with one another."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12734 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12734 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12735))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12735 "therapeutic index")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12735 "Ratio of the exposure/concentration of a therapeutic agent that causes beneficial effects to that which causes the first observed adverse effect.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12735 "therapeutic ratio")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12735 "A commonly used measure of therapeutic index is the toxic dose of a drug for \\(\\pu{50\\%}\\) of a population divided by the minimum effective dose for \\(\\pu{50\\%}\\) of a population."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12735 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12735 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12736))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12736 "unmet medical need")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12736 "Term used for diseases or other disorders for which no optimal therapeutic options exist.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12736 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12736 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12737))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12737 "virtual chemical library")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12737 "Collection of chemical structures constructed solely in electronic form or on paper.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12737 "The building blocks required for such a library may not exist, and the chemical steps for such a library may not have been tested. These libraries are used in the design and evaluation of possible libraries."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12737 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12737 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12738))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12738 "volume of distribution")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12738 "Apparent (hypothetical) volume of fluid required to contain the total amount of a substance in the body at the same concentration as that present in the plasma assuming equilibrium has been attained.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12738 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12738 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12739))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12739 "wild-type receptor")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12739 "Receptor that occurs naturally in human and other species.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12739 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-23)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12739 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12740))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12740 "alpha relaxation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12740 "Highest-temperature or lowest-frequency relaxation in the loss curve of a polymer.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12740 "α-relaxation")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12740 "The \\(\\upalpha\\)-relaxation is commonly related to cooperative conformational changes in macromolecules. These changes typically involve \\(\\pu{10\\!-\\! 20}\\) main-chain atoms. For a polymer in a glassy state, the \\(\\upalpha\\)-relaxation is characteristic of the glass transition."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12740 "For some partially crystalline polymers, for example, polyethylene or polyoxymethylene, the \\(\\upalpha\\)-relaxation originates from motions within the crystalline regions (the so-called \"crystalline relaxation\"). In such cases, the β-relaxation usually corresponds to the glass transition."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12740 goldbook:12774)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12740 goldbook:12781)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12740 goldbook:12744)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12740 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12740 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12741))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12741 "alpha relaxation peak")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12741 "Highest-temperature peak or lowest-frequency peak in the loss curve of a polymer.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12741 "α-loss peak")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12741 "α-relaxation peak")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12741 "alpha loss peak")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12741 "Secondary relaxation peaks occurring successively at lower temperatures or higher frequencies are termed the beta (β-), gamma (γ-), relaxation or loss peaks."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12741 goldbook:12800)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12741 goldbook:12745)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12741 goldbook:12772)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12741 goldbook:12781)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12741 goldbook:12799)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12741 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12741 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12742))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12742 "amorphous polymer")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12742 "Polymer in the amorphous state.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12742 goldbook:12743)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12742 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12742 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12743))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12743 "amorphous state")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12743 "State of matter characterised by the absence of long-range molecular order.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12743 "Some degree of local order about \\(\\pu{1 nm}\\) in length may exist in the amorphous state."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12743 "In the absence of stress, the structure and properties of the amorphous state are generally isotropic at a large-enough scale, as in liquids."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12743 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12743 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12744))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12744 "beta relaxation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12744 "Second-highest-temperature or second-lowest-frequency relaxation in the loss curve of a polymer.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12744 "β-relaxation")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12744 "For an amorphous polymer, the \\(\\upbeta\\)-relaxation is generally related to localised motions involving only a few atoms of a polymer chain or is due to side-group motion."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12744 "In some partially crystalline polymers, the \\(\\upbeta\\)-relaxation corresponds to the glass-transition temperature (see Note 2 of definition alpha relaxation)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12744 goldbook:12740)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12744 goldbook:12742)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12744 goldbook:12781)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12744 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12744 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12745))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12745 "beta relaxation peak")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12745 "Second-highest-temperature or second-lowest-frequency peak in the loss curve of a polymer.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12745 "β-loss peak")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12745 "β-relaxation peak")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12745 "beta loss peak")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12745 goldbook:12781)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12745 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12745 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12746))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12746 "characteristic temperatures")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12746 "Temperatures obtained from a differential scanning calorimeter (DSC) experiment or a differential thermal analysis (DTA) experiment that characterise the physical processes occurring.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12746 "The physical processes frequently studied in polymer science are crystallisation, melting, and the glass transition. See the figures below, which illustrate the corresponding characteristic temperatures. The ordinate used in the figures is specific heat capacity \\(c_{p}/\\pu{J K-1 g-1}\\). When using DSC, the quantity measured is the specific heat flow rate/\\(\\pu{W g-1}\\), and when using DTA, the quantity measured is the temperature difference between sample and reference. Both quantities can be converted to \\(c_{p}\\) by calibration. Figure 1: Characteristic temperatures found from a DSC or DTA cooling experiment involving crystallisation. In a heating experiment, the subscripts for \"initial\" and \"final\" are interchanged. Cold crystallisation can sometimes be observed in a heating experiment.
\\(T_{\\rm{i,cr}}\\) = initial (onset) crystallisation temperature (at which crystallisation starts).
\\(T_{\\rm{ei,cr}}\\) = extrapolated initial (onset) crystallisation temperature.
\\(T_{\\rm{p,cr}}\\) = peak crystallisation temperature (at which the maximum rate of crystallisation occurs).
\\(T_{\\rm{ef,cr}}\\) = extrapolated final (end) crystallisation temperature.
\\(T_{\\rm{f,cr}}\\) = final (end) crystallisation temperature (at which crystallisation stops).
\\(\\Delta_{\\rm{cr}} h\\) = specific enthalpy of crystallisation, unit: \\(\\pu{J g-1}\\).
\\(c_{p}\\) = specific heat capacity, unit: \\(\\pu{J K-1 g-1}\\). Figure 2: Characteristic temperatures found from a DSC or DTA heating experiment involving melting (fusion).
_028101_ = initial (onset) melting temperature (at which melting starts).
_028102_ = extrapolated initial (onset) melting temperature.
_028103_ = peak melting temperature (at which the maximum rate of melting occurs).
_028104_ = extrapolated final (end) melting temperature.
_028105_ = final (end) melting temperature (at which melting stops).
_028106_ = specific enthalpy of fusion, unit: \\(\\pu{J g-1}\\).
\\(c_{p}\\) = specific heat capacity, unit: \\(\\pu{J K-1 g-1}\\). Figure 3: Characteristic temperatures found from a DSC or DTA experiment involving a glass transition. The experiment is often carried out by cooling the polymer melt rather than heating the polymer glass because of the small variation of the transition temperature with the cooling rate in contrast to the more complex situation in a heating experiment; see enthalpy relaxation.
_028107_ = initial (onset) temperature of the glass transition.
_028108_ = extrapolated initial (onset) temperature of the glass transition.
_014497_ = mid-point temperature, equated to the glass-transition temperature.
_028109_ = extrapolated final (end) temperature of the glass transition.
_028110_ = final (end) temperature of the glass transition.
\\(c_{p}\\) = specific heat capacity, unit: \\(\\pu{J K-1 g-1}\\).
_028111_ = change in specific heat capacity, unit: \\(\\pu{J K-1 g-1}\\)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12746 "The glass transition is usually near the point of inflection of the function \\(c_{p}(T)\\)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12746 "In a symmetrical curve, the point of inflection is at \\(½\\) of the height of the step of the curve (the mid-point temperature)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12746 "Alternative methods for evaluating the glass-transition temperature, \\(T_{\\rm{g}}\\), from DSC or DTA curves exist, for example, evaluation of the temperature of equal specific enthalpy of the glass and the melt."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12746 goldbook:12748)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12746 goldbook:12758)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12746 goldbook:12765)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12746 goldbook:12788)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12746 goldbook:12793)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12746 goldbook:12794)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12746 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12746 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12747))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12747 "clearing temperature")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12747 "Temperature at which the transition between the mesophase with the highest temperature range and the isotropic phase occurs.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12747 "clearing point")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12747 "The clearing temperature of a mesophase is a special case of the more general isotropisation temperature."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12747 goldbook:12776)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12747 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12747 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12748))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12748 "cold crystallisation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12748 "Polymer crystallisation brought about from a glass, from a liquid-crystalline state, or a state displaying a low degree of crystallinity at temperatures a little above the glass-transition temperature.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12748 "Cold crystallisation is frequently observed if crystallisation was not completed before sample vitrification."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12748 goldbook:12773)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12748 goldbook:12818)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12748 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12748 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12749))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12749 "conformational enthalpy")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12749 "Enthalpy change associated with conformational changes.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12749 "In polymers, conformational changes can be associated with conformational melting."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12749 goldbook:12751)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12749 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12749 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12750))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12750 "conformational entropy")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12750 "Entropy change associated with conformational changes.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12750 "In polymers, conformational changes can be associated with conformational melting."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12750 goldbook:12751)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12750 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12750 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12751))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12751 "conformational melting")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12751 "Step-like increase in the conformational entropy of macromolecules, or parts of macromolecules.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12751 "This melting can be caused by a temperature change or by interaction with a solvent."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12751 "Conformational melting normally occurs along with crystalline melting in a partially crystalline polymer."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12751 goldbook:12750)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12751 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12751 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12752))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12752 "conformational transition")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12752 "Transition between two conformational states.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12752 "Conformational melting is a type of conformational transition."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12752 "Conformational transitions are relevant in biopolymers, for example, nucleic acids and proteins or complex systems like lipid membranes, where a number of neighbouring local minima in the profile of the Gibbs energy are possible. A conformational transition can result in important biological action."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12752 goldbook:12751)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12752 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12752 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12753))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12753 "constant oscillation-amplitude method")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12753 "Forced-resonance method to determine the viscoelastic properties of a material.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12753 "Indirect measurement of the energy that has to be added to a material sample to compensate the damping of the oscillation by determination of the change of the resonance frequency of a material sample."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12753 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12753 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12754))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12754 "crystalline state")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12754 "State of matter ideally characterised by three-dimensional, long-range order on an atomic scale.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12754 "One- or two-dimensional order leads to a mesophase structure."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12754 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12754 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12755))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12755 "crystallisable polymer")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12755 "Polymer that is able to partially crystallise.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12755 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12755 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12756))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12756 "damping curve")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12756 "Decrease in the deformation amplitude of a material specimen plotted vs. time when the specimen is subjected to a free oscillation.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12756 "loss curve")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12756 goldbook:12770)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12756 goldbook:12780)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12756 goldbook:12814)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12756 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12756 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12757))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12757 "devitrification")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12757 "Formation of a polymer melt from a polymer glass.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12757 "Devitrification is usually brought about by heating or exposure to a solvent as liquid or vapour."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12757 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12757 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12758))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12758 "differential scanning calorimeter")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12758 "Apparatus for conducting a differential scanning calorimetry (DSC) experiment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12758 "DSC")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12758 "It is common to use the same abbreviation (DSC) for both differential scanning calorimetry and the apparatus."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12758 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12758 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12759))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12759 "differential thermal analyser")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12759 "Apparatus for conducting a differential thermal analysis experiment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12759 "DTA")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12759 "It is common to use the same abbreviation (DTA) for both differential thermal analysis and the apparatus."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12759 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12759 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12760))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12760 "dilatometer")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12760 "Apparatus for conducting a dilatometry experiment.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12760 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12760 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12761))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12761 "dilatometry")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12761 "The measurement of changes with time in the volume, length, width, or thickness of a material sample caused by temperature changes under negligible load or by chemical reaction.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12761 "One-dimensional changes are often measured using mechanical displacement detection. Volume changes are often determined using an inert confining liquid, for example, mercury."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12761 "Measurement of an applied hydrostatic pressure allows the determination of pressure–volume–temperature (\\(p,V,T\\)) diagrams."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12761 "A polymerisation reaction is an example of a chemical reaction that can be studied using a dilatometer."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12761 goldbook:12760)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12761 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12761 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12762))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12762 "dynamic-load thermomechanical analysis")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12762 "Thermomechanical analysis carried out using a sinusoidal stress.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12762 "DLTMA")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12762 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12762 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12763))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12763 "dynamic mechanical analyser")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12763 "Apparatus for conducting a dynamic mechanical analysis experiment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12763 "DMA")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12763 "It is common to use the same abbreviation (DMA) for both dynamic mechanical analysis and the apparatus."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12763 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12763 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12764))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12764 "dynamic viscometer")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12764 "Apparatus that uses a forced, non-resonance method to determine the viscoelastic properties of a material sample.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12764 "A sinusoidal displacement is applied to one end of a strip-like sample, and the response of the material is measured at the opposite end, allowing the angle between the stress and the strain, the phase angle, \\(\\delta\\), to be obtained directly."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12764 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12764 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12765))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12765 "enthalpy relaxation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12765 "Enthalpy change observed near the glass transition when a sample is heated at a rate different from that at which it was cooled down, or observed after annealing in the glassy state below the glass-transition temperature.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12765 "Enthalpy relaxation is caused by the transformation of a glassy material to a more stable glass."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12765 "Enthalpy relaxation can be described by the Kohlrausch–Williams–Watts equation."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12765 "Moduli, stress–strain behaviour, and molecular motions are affected by enthalpy relaxation."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12765 "Enthalpy relaxation reflects physical aging."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12765 goldbook:12778)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12765 goldbook:12774)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12765 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12765 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12766))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12766 "equilibrium melting temperature")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12766 "Temperature at which perfect polymer crystals of infinite thickness melt under equilibrium conditions.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12766 "The equilibrium melting temperature can be determined, for example, from a Hoffman–Weeks plot."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12766 "The transition occurring at the equilibrium melting temperature is a first-order phase transition."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12766 goldbook:12775)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12766 goldbook:12788)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12766 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12766 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12767))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12767 "forced sinusoidal oscillation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12767 "Deformation of a material by the application of a small sinusoidal strain (\\(\\gamma\\)) such that \\[\\gamma = \\gamma_{0} \\cos \\omega t\\] where \\(\\gamma_{0}\\) and \\(\\omega\\) are positive constants.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12767 "forced oscillation")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12767 "sinusoidal oscillation")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12767 "\\(\\gamma\\) may be in simple shear or uniaxial deformation."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12767 "\\(\\gamma_{0}\\) is the strain amplitude."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12767 "\\(\\omega\\) is the angular velocity of the circular motion equivalent to a sinusoidal frequency \\(v\\) with \\(\\omega = 2\\uppi \\nu\\). The unit of \\(\\omega\\) is \\(\\pu{rad s-1}\\)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12767 "For linear viscoelastic behaviour, a sinusoidal stress (\\(\\sigma\\)) results from the sinusoidal strain with \\(\\sigma = \\sigma_{0} \\cos (\\omega t + \\delta) = \\sigma_{0} \\cos \\delta \\cos \\omega t - \\sigma_{0} \\sin \\delta \\sin \\omega t\\)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12767 goldbook:12770)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12767 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12767 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12768))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12768 "fragile glass")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12768 "Glass characterised by a large value of the fragility index (m).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12768 "A very fragile glass has \\(m \\approx 250\\)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12768 "A fragile glass has a markedly non-Arrhenius-type temperature dependence of the viscosity and relaxation time."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12768 "The Vogel–Fulcher–Tammann equation can be used to describe the relaxation-time behaviour of a fragile glass."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12768 goldbook:12773)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12768 goldbook:12819)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12768 goldbook:12769)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12768 goldbook:12804)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12768 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12768 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12769))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12769 "fragility index")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12769 "Quantity characterising the fragility or the strength of a glass at a given temperature \\[m = \\left (\\frac{\\rm{d} \\log_{10} \\tau}{{\\rm{d}} (T_{\\rm{g}}/T)} \\right)_{T = T_{\\rm{g}}}\\] \\(\\tau\\) = relaxation time [\\(\\pu{s}\\)]; \\(T_{\\rm{g}}\\) = glass-transition temperature [\\(\\pu{K}\\)]; \\(T\\) = temperature [\\(\\pu{K}\\)].")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12769 "The value of the fragility index depends on the thermal history of the glass."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12769 "The values of \\(m\\) range from \\(m \\approx 16\\) for a very strong glass to \\(m \\approx 250\\) for a very fragile glass."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12769 goldbook:12768)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12769 goldbook:12773)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12769 goldbook:12804)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12769 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12769 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12770))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12770 "free oscillation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12770 "Oscillatory deformation of a material specimen with the motion generated without the continuous application of an external force.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12770 "free sinusoidal oscillation")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12770 "For any real sample of material, the resulting oscillatory deformation is one of decaying amplitudes."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12770 goldbook:12767)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12770 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12770 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12771))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12771 "gamma relaxation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12771 "Third-highest-temperature or third-lowest-frequency relaxation in the loss curve of a polymer.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12771 "γ-relaxation")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12771 goldbook:12781)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12771 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12771 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12772))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12772 "gamma relaxation peak")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12772 "Third-highest-temperature or third-lowest-frequency peak in the loss curve of a polymer.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12772 "γ-loss peak")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12772 "γ-relaxation peak")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12772 "gamma loss peak")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12772 "The \\(\\gamma\\)-peak is typically related to localised motions involving side groups or a few atoms of a polymer chain."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12772 goldbook:12781)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12772 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12772 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12773))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12773 "glass")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12773 "Amorphous matter in the glassy state, i.e., below its glass-transition temperature.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12773 "A glass is usually described as a solid, as most physical properties vary in a manner similar to those in the crystalline state. However, considering the ongoing debate about the nature of the glass transition, and the ability of some glasses to flow, some authors prefer to consider glasses in the context of the liquid state."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12773 "The creep compliance of a glass is less than \\(\\pu{E-9 N-1 m2}\\), and the dynamic viscosity larger than \\(\\pu{E4 Pa s}\\)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12773 goldbook:12754)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12773 goldbook:12774)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12773 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12773 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12774))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12774 "glassy state")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12774 "State of amorphous matter below its glass-transition temperature.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12774 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12774 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12775))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12775 "Hoffman–Weeks plot")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12775 "Plot of melting temperature, \\(T_{\\rm{m}}\\), vs. crystallisation temperature, \\(T_{\\rm{cr}}\\).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12775 "A Hoffman–Weeks plot is used to determine the equilibrium melting temperature, \\(T_{\\rm{m}}^{0}\\)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12775 "\\(T_{\\rm{m}}^{0}\\) is determined as the intersection of the straight line that describes \\(T_{\\rm{cr}} = T_{\\rm{m}}\\) with the extrapolated curve that is drawn through the experimental data points (\\(T_{\\rm{cr}}\\), \\(T_{\\rm{m}}\\))."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12775 goldbook:12766)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12775 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12775 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12776))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12776 "isotropisation temperature")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12776 "Temperature at which a transition from any anisotropic state to an isotropic liquid occurs.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12776 "In mesomorphic systems, the isotropisation temperature is usually called clearing temperature."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12776 goldbook:12747)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12776 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12776 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12777))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12777 "Kauzmann temperature")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12777 "Temperature at which the extrapolation of the entropy of a super-cooled liquid is equal to the entropy of its crystalline state.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12777 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12777 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12778))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12778 "Kohlrausch–Williams–Watts equation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12778 "Equation describing the enthalpy relaxation, \\(\\Delta H\\) which is observed during the annealing of polymers in the glassy state at a temperature, \\(T_{\\rm{a}}\\), lower than \\(T_{\\rm{g}}\\) \\[\\Delta H(t_{\\rm{a}}) = \\Delta c_{p}(T_{\\rm{g}} - T_{\\rm{a}}) \\exp\\!\\left[- \\left (\\frac{t_{\\rm{a}}}{\\tau} \\right)^{\\beta} \\right]\\] \\(\\Delta H\\) = difference of the enthalpy in the initial, glassy state, and the enthalpy of the glassy state after annealing; \\(t_{\\rm{a}}\\) = time of annealing; \\(\\Delta c_{p}\\) = difference in heat capacity at the glass-transition temperature, \\(T_{\\rm{g}}\\), and the starting temperature of the annealing process, \\(T_{\\rm{a}}\\); \\(\\tau\\) = relaxation time at \\(T_{\\rm{a}}\\); \\(\\beta\\) = exponential factor.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12778 "KWW Equation")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12778 "The exponential factor \\(\\beta\\) has a value between 0 and 1, and characterises the asymmetry of the distribution of relaxation times."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12778 "Moduli, stress-strain behaviour, and molecular motions are affected by enthalpy relaxation, which reflects physical aging."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12778 goldbook:12765)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12778 goldbook:12774)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12778 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12778 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12779))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12779 "linear thermodilatometry")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12779 "Technique in which one dimension of a substance under negligible load is measured as a function of temperature while the substance is subjected to a controlled temperature program.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12779 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12779 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12780))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12780 "logarithmic decrement")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12780 "Natural logarithm of the ratio of the displacement of a damping curve separated by one period of the displacement.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12780 "If equals the \\(n^{th}\\) displacement of the damping curve and equals the \\((n + 1)^{th}\\) displacement (\\(n = 1, 2, 3, \\dots\\)), then \\(\\mathit{\\Lambda} = \\ln(A_{n}/A_{n + 1})\\)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12780 goldbook:12756)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12780 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12780 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12781))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12781 "loss curve")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12781 "Plot of loss tangent (\\(\\tan \\delta\\)) vs. the temperature or the frequency of the forced sinusoidal oscillation.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12781 goldbook:12767)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12781 goldbook:12783)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12781 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12781 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12782))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12782 "loss modulus")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12782 "Ratio of the amplitude of the stress \\(\\pu{90\\!^{\\circ}}\\) out of phase with the strain (\\(\\sigma_{0} \\sin \\delta\\)) to the amplitude of the strain (\\(\\gamma_{0}\\)) in the forced sinusoidal oscillation of a material. \\[M^{\\prime\\prime} = \\frac{\\sigma_{0} \\sin \\delta}{\\gamma_{0}}\\]")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12782 "For the definitions of the symbols used, see forced sinusoidal oscillation."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12782 "In a linear viscoelastic material, the strain \\(\\gamma = \\gamma_{0} \\cos \\omega t\\) produces a stress \\(\\sigma = \\sigma_{0} \\cos (\\omega t + \\delta) = \\sigma_{0} \\cos \\delta \\cos \\omega t - \\sigma_{0} \\sin \\delta \\sin \\omega t\\)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12782 "The loss modulus characterises the viscous response of a material."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12782 goldbook:12767)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12782 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12782 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12783))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12783 "loss tangent")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12783 "Tangent of the phase angle (\\(\\delta\\)) between stress and strain during a forced sinusoidal oscillation.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12783 "loss factor")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12783 "\\(\\tan \\delta\\) is also equal to the ratio of loss modulus to storage modulus."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12783 goldbook:12767)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12783 goldbook:12782)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12783 goldbook:12802)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12783 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12783 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12784))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12784 "master curve")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12784 "Viscoelastic spectrum of a polymer or polymer material constructed using the time–temperature superposition (TTS) principle, so that the spectrum covers a wide range of lengths of time or frequencies of measurement.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12784 "A master curve is usually constructed by superimposing a sequence of isothermal measurements of a viscoelastic property vs. time."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12784 goldbook:12817)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12784 goldbook:12821)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12784 goldbook:12813)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12784 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12784 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12785))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12785 "mechanical melting")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12785 "Mechanically induced transition of matter in the crystalline or glassy state to its melt.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12785 goldbook:12754)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12785 goldbook:12774)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12785 goldbook:12786)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12785 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12785 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12786))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12786 "melt")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12786 "Matter in the amorphous state above its glass-transition temperature.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12786 "A melt has the physical properties of a liquid."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12786 goldbook:12794)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12786 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12786 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12787))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12787 "melt flow index")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12787 "Mass of a polymer in grams that flows through a calibrated orifice at constant temperature under a specified load over a \\(\\pu{10\\!{-}min}\\) period.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12787 "MFI")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12787 "melt flow rate")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12787 "MFR")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12787 "melt mass flow rate")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12787 "melt volume flow")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12787 "There is no suitable SI unit for MFI."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12787 "Specified loads are mandated for specific polymers."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12787 "The values of MFI as a function of load can give information on the molar mass distribution."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12787 "Standard procedures for determining MFI are available from ISO and ASTM."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12787 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12787 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12788))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12788 "melting temperature")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12788 "Temperature at which the last trace of crystallinity disappears upon heating.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12788 "melting point")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12788 "This temperature usually refers to the highest temperature of the melting range, i.e., when the last and therefore the most perfectly ordered crystals or the largest crystals melt."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12788 "An experimentally determined melting temperature is not necessarily identical with the equilibrium melting temperature. See equilibrium melting temperature and Hoffman–Weeks plot."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12788 "Experimentally determined values of the melting temperature may depend on the method and the experimental conditions, for example, sample mass, heating rate, etc."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12788 "If \\(T_{\\rm{m}}\\) is determined using DSC or DTA, then the characteristic temperature (Figure 2) used should be stated."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12788 goldbook:12775)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12788 goldbook:12746)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12788 goldbook:12766)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12788 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12788 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12789))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12789 "modulated heat flow")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12789 "Heat flow in a modulated-temperature DSC experiment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12789 "MHF")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12789 goldbook:12790)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12789 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12789 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12790))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12790 "modulated-temperature DSC")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12790 "DSC experiment in which a small sinusoidal modulation overlays the change in temperature with time.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12790 "MTDSC")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12790 "The resulting DSC data can be separated, by Fourier analysis, into components in-phase with the modulation (reversing heat flow) and out-of-phase with the modulation (nonreversing heat flow). \\[\\underbrace {{\\left({\\frac{{\\partial H}}{{\\partial t}}} \\right)}_{p}}_{\\rm{total\\ heat\\ flow}} = \\frac{{\\rm{d}}Q}{{\\rm{d}}t} = \\underbrace {C_{p}\\frac{{\\rm{d}}T}{{\\rm{d}}t}}_{\\rm{reversing\\ heat\\ flow}} + \\underbrace {f\\left({T,t}\\right)}_{\\rm{non\\mbox{-}reversing\\ heat\\ flow}}\\] The total heat flow is the average value calculated from the measured signals during the modulated heat flow (MHF). \\(C_{p}\\) is the heat capacity of the sample, \\(\\frac{{\\rm{d}}T}{{\\rm{d}}t}\\) is the heating rate."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12790 "Use of the terms \"oscillating DSC (ODSC)\" and \"modulated DSC (MDSC)\" is discouraged."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12790 goldbook:12789)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12790 goldbook:12792)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12790 goldbook:12797)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12790 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12790 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12791))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12791 "multiplexing")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12791 "Technique used in dynamic mechanical analysis in which a specimen is subjected to the superposition of a number of forced sinusoidal oscillations of different frequencies.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12791 "In one experiment, this technique delivers the frequency dependence of the mechanical properties at all the frequencies covered by the forced sinusoidal oscillations."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12791 goldbook:12767)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12791 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12791 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12792))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12792 "non-reversing heat flow")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12792 "In modulated-temperature DSC, the component of the total heat flow that is out-of-phase with the temperature modulation.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12792 "The out-of-phase component of the total heat flow relates to kinetic processes like crystallisation, melting, evaporation, or condensation."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12792 "The term \"non-reversing\" must not be confused with \"irreversible\"."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12792 goldbook:12790)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12792 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12792 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12793))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12793 "polymer glass")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12793 "Amorphous polymer at temperatures below its glass-transition temperature.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12793 "glassy polymer")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12793 goldbook:12742)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12793 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12793 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12794))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12794 "polymer melt")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12794 "Polymer in the amorphous state above its glass-transition temperature.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12794 "A polymer melt has the physical properties of a viscoelastic liquid."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12794 "The term applies both to crystallisable polymers and to polymers that are unable to crystallise. In the latter case, no specifications are needed. In the former case, in the range between the glass-transition temperature and the equilibrium melting temperature, the polymer melt is metastable, and, as long as crystallisation does not occur (see Note 3), the term supercooled polymer melt can be used to define more accurately the thermodynamic state of the system."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12794 "When a crystallisable polymer undergoes crystallisation, the remaining amorphous component cannot be considered a polymer melt. Flow is inhibited by polymer crystallites, which physically cross-link the amorphous component or constrain it at the surface of polymer crystals."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12794 goldbook:12755)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12794 goldbook:12766)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12794 goldbook:12805)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12794 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12794 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12795))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12795 "relaxation map")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12795 "Plot of the logarithm of the relaxation time vs. the reciprocal temperature.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12795 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12795 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12796))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12796 "relaxation spectrum")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12796 "Range of relaxation times describing stress relaxation in a polymer.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12796 "spectrum of relaxation times")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12796 goldbook:12803)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12796 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12796 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12797))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12797 "reversing heat flow")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12797 "In modulated-temperature DSC the heat-capacity component of the total heat flow that is in-phase with the temperature modulation.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12797 "The reversing-heat-flow component contains the changes in the heat capacity, \\(C_{p}\\), of the specimen, in particular during the glass transition."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12797 "The term \"reversing\" must not be confused with \"reversible\"."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12797 goldbook:12790)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12797 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12797 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12798))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12798 "secondary relaxation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12798 "Second-, third-, fourth-, … highest-temperature or second-, third-, fourth-, … lowest-frequency relaxation in the loss curve of a polymer.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12798 goldbook:12744)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12798 goldbook:12771)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12798 goldbook:12781)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12798 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12798 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12799))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12799 "secondary relaxation peak")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12799 "Any peak in a loss curve either at a lower temperature than the temperature of the alpha relaxation peak or at a higher frequency than the frequency of the alpha relaxation peak.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12799 "secondary loss peak")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12799 "The use of the term \"secondary relaxation transition peak\" is discouraged."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12799 goldbook:12741)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12799 goldbook:12745)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12799 goldbook:12772)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12799 goldbook:12781)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12799 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12799 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12800))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12800 "secondary relaxation temperature")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12800 "Temperature characterising a secondary relaxation peak identified as the temperature at which the loss modulus (or loss tangent), measured by DMA or DETA, exhibits a maximum at the measurement frequency, due to the occurrence of localised motions involving only short segments of the polymer chains, or side groups of the polymer chains.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12800 goldbook:12782)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12800 goldbook:12783)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12800 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12800 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12801))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12801 "shift factor")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12801 "Multiplier used to change the interval of time or the range frequencies of measurement of a viscoelastic property at a given temperature, \\(T_{1}\\), so that the values of the property superimpose on the values measured at a reference temperature, \\(T_{0}\\).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12801 "The shift factor is temperature dependent but independent of the time or frequency."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12801 goldbook:12821)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12801 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12801 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12802))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12802 "storage modulus")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12802 "Ratio of the amplitude of the stress in phase with the strain (\\(\\sigma_{0} \\cos \\delta\\)) to the amplitude of the strain (\\(\\gamma_{0}\\)) in the forced sinusoidal oscillation of a material. \\[M^{\\prime} = \\frac{\\sigma_{0} \\cos \\delta}{\\gamma_{0}}\\]")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12802 "Definition taken, with \"forced sinusoidal oscillation\" replacing \"forced oscillation\"."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12802 "For the definitions of the symbols used, see forced sinusoidal oscillation. In a linear viscoelastic material, the strain \\(\\gamma = \\gamma_{0} \\cos \\omega t\\) produces a stress. \\[\\sigma = \\sigma_{0} \\cos (\\omega t + \\delta) = \\sigma_{0} \\cos \\delta \\cos \\omega t - \\sigma_{0} \\sin \\delta \\sin \\omega t\\]"^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12802 "The storage modulus characterises the elastic response of a material."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12802 goldbook:12767)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12802 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12802 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12803))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12803 "stress relaxation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12803 "Change in stress with time after the instantaneous application of a constant strain.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12803 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12803 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12804))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12804 "strong glass")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12804 "Glass characterised by a small value of the fragility index (\\(m\\)).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12804 "A very strong glass has \\(m \\approx 16\\)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12804 "A strong glass has an approximately Arrhenius-type temperature dependence of the viscosity and relaxation time."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12804 goldbook:12773)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12804 goldbook:12768)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12804 goldbook:12769)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12804 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12804 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12805))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12805 "supercooled polymer melt")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12805 "Metastable melt of a crystallisable polymer at temperatures below its equilibrium melting temperature.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12805 goldbook:12766)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12805 goldbook:12786)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12805 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12805 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12806))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12806 "Tammann’s 2/3rd rule")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12806 "Empirical rule that states that in a partially crystalline polymer the glass-transition temperature can be reasonably approximated by a value equal to two-thirds of the melting temperature, \\(T_{\\rm{m}}\\)/\\(\\pu{K}\\).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12806 goldbook:12788)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12806 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12806 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12807))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12807 "thermal history")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12807 "Thermal treatment a polymer material has experienced before its characterisation or measurement of its properties.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12807 "Thermal history affects many physical properties. Its influence can be modified or removed by annealing."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12807 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12807 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12808))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12808 "thermal lag")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12808 "Delay of the response of a system to a change in temperature.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12808 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12808 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12809))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12809 "thermogravimetric analyser")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12809 "Apparatus for conducting thermogravimetric analysis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12809 "TGA")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12809 "thermobalance")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12809 "It is common to use the same abbreviation (TGA) for both thermogravimetric analysis and the apparatus."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12809 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12809 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12810))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12810 "thermoluminescence analysis")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12810 "Technique that monitors the light that is emitted from a sample against time or temperature while the temperature of the sample, in a specified atmosphere, is heated in a controlled manner.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12810 "TLA")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12810 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12810 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12811))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12811 "thermomechanical analyser")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12811 "Apparatus for conducting thermomechanical analysis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12811 "TMA")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12811 "It is common to use the same abbreviation (TMA) for both thermomechanical analysis and the apparatus."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12811 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12811 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12812))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12812 "thermomechanical properties")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12812 "The temperature dependence of deformability or mechanical properties of a polymer sample.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12812 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12812 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12813))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12813 "time–temperature superposition principle")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12813 "Principle stating that the value of a viscoelastic property measured at a given temperature, after a given length of time or at a given frequency, is equal to the value of the property at a different temperature after a length of time or at a frequency equal to the given length of time or given frequency multiplied by a shift factor, \\(a_{T}\\) , with the value of the shift factor being independent of length of the time or frequency.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12813 "TTS Principle")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12813 "The Williams–Landel–Ferry (WLF) equation provides a semi-empirical relation between the shift factor \\(a_{T}\\) and the temperature, at temperatures near the glass-transition temperature, \\(T_{\\rm{g}}\\)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12813 goldbook:12821)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12813 goldbook:12801)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12813 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12813 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12814))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12814 "torsion pendulum")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12814 "Device consisting of a disc or other body of large moment of inertia mounted on one end of a torsionally flexible elastic rod or wire, the other end of which is fixed.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12814 "When the disc is displaced by a (small) angle around its primary rotational axis it will undergo a simple harmonic oscillation after it is released as long as the torque of the rod or the wire is proportional to the torsion angle."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12814 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12814 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12815))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12815 "torsional pendulum analysis")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12815 "Dynamic mechanical analysis performed using a torsion pendulum.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12815 "A strip-shaped polymer sample is mounted on a torsion pendulum and subjected to a small torque. The decay in the amplitude of the free sinusoidal oscillation is observed over a range of temperatures."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12815 "Storage (shear) modulus G', loss (shear) modulus G'', and the loss-tangent can be calculated from the logarithmic decrement, \\(\\mathit{\\Lambda}\\)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12815 goldbook:12802)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12815 goldbook:12770)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12815 goldbook:12780)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12815 goldbook:12782)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12815 goldbook:12783)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12815 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12815 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12816))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12816 "Vicat softening temperature")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12816 "Temperature at which a thermoplastic polymer reaches a specific degree of softness as measured by a standard test.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12816 "softening point")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12816 "Vicat hardness")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12816 "Vicat softening point")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12816 "Usually this temperature is determined using standardised methods, such as indentation tests, or the ring-ball method that characterise the dimensional stability of a polymer to heating. These standardised methods are often polymer specific."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12816 "For an amorphous polymer, the softening temperature is close to the glass-transition temperature, and for a crystalline polymer the softening temperature is close to but lower than the melting temperature."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12816 goldbook:12788)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12816 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12816 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12817))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12817 "viscoelastic spectrum")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12817 "Double logarithmic plot of a viscoelastic property vs. frequency of measurement or interval of time of measurement at constant temperature.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12817 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12817 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12818))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12818 "vitrification")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12818 "Formation of a polymer glass from a polymer melt.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12818 "Vitrification is usually brought about by cooling."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12818 goldbook:12793)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12818 goldbook:12794)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12818 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12818 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12819))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12819 "Vogel–Fulcher–Tammann equation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12819 "Equation describing the time-dependence of a relaxation time that deviates from an Arrhenius-type temperature dependence. \\[\\tau = \\tau_{0} \\exp\\!\\left({\\frac{B}{T - T_{0}}}\\right)\\] \\(\\tau\\)/\\(\\pu{s}\\) = relaxation time; \\(\\tau_{0}\\)/\\(\\pu{s}\\) = relaxation time at the Kauzmann temperature, \\(B\\)/\\(\\pu{K}\\) = constant; \\(T\\)/\\(\\pu{K}\\) = temperature; \\(T_{0}\\)/\\(\\pu{K}\\) = Kauzmann temperature.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12819 "VFT Equation")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12819 goldbook:12777)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12819 goldbook:12768)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12819 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12819 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12820))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12820 "volume thermodilatometry")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12820 "Technique in which the volume of a substance under negligible load is measured as a function of temperature while the substance is heated or cooled in a controlled programme.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12820 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12820 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12821))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12821 "Williams–Landel–Ferry equation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12821 "Equation describing the temperature dependence of the shift factor, \\(a_{T}\\), for time–temperature superposition \\[\\log_{10}a_{\\rm{T}} = \\frac{-C_{1}(T_{1} - T_{0})}{C_{2} + (T_{1} - T_{0})}\\] \\(C_{1}\\) and \\(C_{2}\\) are empirical constants, \\(T\\) is the temperature of measurement, and \\(T_{0}\\) is the reference temperature.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12821 "WLF Equation")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12821 "The WLF equation is usually applied with the reference temperature, \\(T_{0}\\), equal to the glass-transition temperature, \\(T_{\\rm{g}}\\). The values of the constants \\(C_{1}\\) and \\(C_{2}\\) depend on the type of polymer and are valid over a limited range of temperature, from \\(T_{\\rm{g}}\\) to about \\(T_{\\rm{g}}\\) + \\(\\pu{50 K}\\)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12821 goldbook:12801)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12821 goldbook:12813)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12821 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-03-02)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12821 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12822))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12822 "coordination polymer")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12822 "A coordination compound with repeating coordination entities extending in 1, 2, or 3 dimensions.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12822 "Coordination polymers do not need to be crystalline; therefore, the more appropriate terms (for crystalline states) 1-periodic, 2-periodic, and 3-periodic cannot be used throughout. These compounds may in some cases, such as those being composed of mainly carboxylates, even be regarded as salts. The prefix 1D-, 2D-, or 3D- is acceptable for the indicating the degree of extension of the coordination polymer."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12822 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-20)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12822 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12823))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12823 "coordination network")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12823 "A coordination compound extending, through repeating coordination entities, in one dimension, but with cross-links between two or more individual chains, loops, or spiro-links, or a coordination compound extending through repeating coordination entities in two or three dimensions.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12823 "The preferred and most widely understood term will likely be: \"coordination polymer\". However, IUPAC endorses also the use of the term \"coordination network\", even though it should be clear that these two terms are not synonymous and that coordination network is in fact a subset of coordination polymer."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12823 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-20)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12823 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12824))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12824 "metal-organic framework")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12824 "A metal-organic framework, abbreviated to MOF, is a coordination network with organic ligands containing potential voids.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12824 "MOF")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12824 "This wording accounts for the fact that many systems are dynamic, and changes in structure and thus corresponding changes in potential porosity or solvent and/or guest filled voids may occur depending on temperature, pressure, or other external stimuli. For these reasons it is also not required that an MOF be crystalline. Arguments based on both theory and experiment can be used, suggesting that some of these coordination polymers (i.e., those that can be described as salts) with direct anion-cation binding are more prone to form structures with open frameworks exhibiting permanent porosity than those forming positively charged networks. However, the grey zone between these extremes is large and increasing so that a definition based on such a charge distinction would be too restrictive."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12824 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-12-11-20)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12824 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12825))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12825 "α:β T-cell receptor")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12825 "T-cell receptor (TCR) consisting of a heterodimer of two different glycoprotein chains, designated \\(\\upalpha\\) and \\(\\upbeta\\), assembled into an \\(\\upalpha{:}\\upbeta\\) heterodimer.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12825 goldbook:13714)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12825 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12825 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12826))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12826 "α:β T cell")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12826 "Lymphocyte whose T-cell receptor (TCR) is a heterodimer of an \\(\\upalpha\\) chain and a \\(\\upbeta\\) chain.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12826 "\\(\\upalpha{:}\\upbeta\\) T cells represent the majority of thymocytes in the thymus and T cells in the periphery."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12826 goldbook:13399)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12826 goldbook:13724)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12826 goldbook:13714)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12826 goldbook:13598)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12826 goldbook:12825)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12826 goldbook:13161)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12826 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12826 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12827))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12827 "ABL oncogene")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12827 "Gene resulting from a chromosomal translocation (9;22) that fuses sequences from the BCR (breakpoint cluster region) gene with the ABL gene.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12827 "BCR-ABL")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12827 "This translocation creates the Philadelphia chromosome, found in most human patients with chronic myelogenous leukemia (CML)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12827 "The fusion protein encoded by BCR-ABL possesses unregulated tyrosine kinase activity."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12827 "The term ABL derives from the Abelson murine leukemia virus, from which the gene was first isolated."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12827 goldbook:13565)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12827 goldbook:13008)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12827 goldbook:13766)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12827 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12827 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12828))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12828 "ABO blood group system")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12828 "System of antigens expressed on erythrocytes and used for typing human blood for transfusion.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12828 "Individuals who do not express A or B antigens on their erythrocytes naturally form antibodies against them."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12828 goldbook:13127)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12828 goldbook:13753)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12828 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12828 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12829))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12829 "abzyme")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12829 "Antibody or antibody construct with catalytic activity.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12829 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12829 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12830))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12830 "accessory cell")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12830 "Cell that assists in the adaptive immune response but does not directly mediate specific antigen recognition.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12830 "Such cells include phagocytes, mast cells, dendritic cells, and NK cells."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12830 "The term is often used to describe antigen-presenting cells (APCs)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12830 goldbook:13499)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12830 goldbook:12843)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12830 goldbook:12888)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12830 goldbook:13087)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12830 goldbook:13442)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12830 goldbook:13560)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12830 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12830 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12831))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12831 "accessory molecule")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12831 "Molecule other than immunoglobulin (Ig), T-cell receptor (TCR), or major histocompatibility complex (MHC) molecule that participates in T lymphocyte recognition and response to antigen.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12831 goldbook:13724)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12831 goldbook:13714)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12831 goldbook:13434)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12831 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12831 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12832))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12832 "acquired immunity")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12832 "State of protection against pathogen-induced injury, with rapid immune elimination of pathogenic invaders owing to previous immunization or vaccination.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12832 goldbook:13260)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12832 goldbook:13771)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12832 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12832 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12833))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12833 "acquired immunodeficiency syndrome")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12833 "Disease caused by infection with the human immunodeficiency virus (HIV), assuming clinical relevance when an infected patient has lost most of his/her CD4+ T cells, so that infections with opportunistic pathogens occur.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003012) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12833 "AIDS")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12833 goldbook:12974)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12833 goldbook:13228)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12833 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12833 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12834))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12834 "activation-induced cell death")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12834 "Process by which immune responses end in the death of most of the responding lymphocytes, leaving only a small number of resting memory cells.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12834 goldbook:13399)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12834 goldbook:13452)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12834 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12834 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12835))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12835 "active immunization")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12835 "Immunization with antigen, as distinct from the transfer of antibody to an unimmunized individual, which is called passive immunization.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12835 goldbook:13540)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12835 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12835 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12836))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12836 "active systemic anaphylaxis test")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12836 "Test for determining whether a drug can cause anaphylactic reactions in an animal following immunization with the drug.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12836 "ASA")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12836 "ASA test")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12836 goldbook:12871)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12836 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12836 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12837))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12837 "acute lymphoblastic leukemia")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12837 "Highly aggressive, undifferentiated form of lymphoid malignancy derived from a progenitor cell that is thought to be able to give rise to both T- and B-cell lineages.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003012) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12837 "ALL")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12837 "Acute Lymphocytic Leukemia")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12837 "Most of these leukemias show partial differentiation toward the B-cell lineage (so-called B-ALL) whereas a minority show features of T cells (T-ALL)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12837 goldbook:12937)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12837 goldbook:13724)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12837 goldbook:13378)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12837 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12837 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12838))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12838 "acute myelogenous leukemia")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12838 "Cancer characterized by rapid growth of abnormal granulocytes that accumulate in the bone marrow.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12838 "AML")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12838 goldbook:12959)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12838 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12838 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12839))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12839 "acute-phase protein")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12839 "Serum protein, mostly produced in the liver, which rapidly changes in concentration (some acute-phase proteins increase, some decrease) during the initiation of an inflammatory response.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12839 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12839 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12840))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12840 "acute-phase response")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12840 "Physiological response stimulated by cytokines including interleukin-1, interleukin-6, interferons, and tumor necrosis factor (TNF), characterized by increased vascular permeability, fever, and increased levels of proteins (thus called acute-phase proteins) such as C-reactive protein (CRP), occurring within a few hours of initiation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12840 "APR")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12840 "Infection, inflammation, tissue injury, and occasionally neoplasms may trigger the APR."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12840 goldbook:12982)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12840 goldbook:12839)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12840 goldbook:13065)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12840 goldbook:13338)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12840 goldbook:13762)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12840 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12840 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12841))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12841 "acute rejection")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12841 "Rejection of a tissue or organ graft from a genetically unrelated donor, typically occurring within 10 to 13 days of transplantation.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12841 goldbook:13645)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12841 goldbook:13754)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12841 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12841 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12842))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12842 "acute respiratory distress syndrome")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12842 "Acute lung failure characterized by alveolar and interstitial edema, perivascular pulmonary edema, and hyaline membrane formation, resulting from a variety of underlying diseases that result in increased pulmonary vascular permeability.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12842 "ARDS")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12842 "adult respiratory distress syndrome")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12842 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12842 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12843))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12843 "adaptive immune response")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12843 "Immune response based on the principle of clonal recognition, such that upon first exposure to an antigen, primed lymphocytes either differentiate into immune effector cells or form an expanded pool of memory cells that respond to secondary exposure to the same antigen by mounting an amplified and more rapid response.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12843 "The response may be classified as cellular (T cell-mediated) or humoral (antibody-dependent)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12843 goldbook:13724)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12843 goldbook:13234)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12843 goldbook:13399)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12843 goldbook:13452)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12843 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12843 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12844))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12844 "adaptive immune system")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12844 "Part of the immune system responsible for the adaptive immune response.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12844 goldbook:12843)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12844 goldbook:13271)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12844 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12844 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12845))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12845 "Addison disease")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12845 "Adrenocortical hypofunction characterized by hypotension, weight loss, anorexia, and weakness. The most common form is idiopathic Addison disease, mediated by autoimmune mechanisms. Autoantibodies specific to the adrenal cortex are specific diagnostic markers of this form.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12845 "Addison autoimmune disease")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12845 "Addison's autoimmune disease")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12845 "Addison's disease")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12845 "21-Hydroxylase, a cytochrome P450 steroidogenic enzyme, is one of the major targets of adrenal autoantibodies in idiopathic Addison disease as well as in Addison disease in the context of autoimmune polyglandular syndromes (polyendocrinopathies, autoimmune). Hypofunction or failure of the adrenal gland may also be a manifestation of antiphospholipid syndrome due to thrombosis of the blood vessels of the adrenal glands."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12845 goldbook:12913)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12845 goldbook:12899)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12845 goldbook:12918)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12845 goldbook:13249)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12845 goldbook:13587)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12845 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12845 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12846))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12846 "addressin")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12846 "Extracellular protein of the venular endothelium serving as a ligand to a homing receptor for lymphocytes.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12846 "Addressins are glycoproteins recognized by L-selectin."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12846 goldbook:13369)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12846 goldbook:10661)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12846 goldbook:13222)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12846 goldbook:13399)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12846 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12846 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12847))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12847 "adenosine deaminase deficiency")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12847 "Lack of the enzyme adenosine deaminase (ADA), which catalyzes the deamination of adenosine and deoxyadenosine to produce inosine and deoxyinosine, respectively. Affected individuals have a form of severe combined immunodeficiency (SCID).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12847 "ADA")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12847 "ADA Deficiency")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12847 goldbook:13674)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12847 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12847 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12848))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12848 "adhesion molecule")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12848 "Molecule belonging mainly to the immunoglobulins, integrin superfamily (e.g., LFA-1, ICAM-1) or selectins, expressed on the cell membrane of various cells including those of the immune system. Interaction of adhesion molecules with each other as receptor and corresponding ligand facilitates cooperation (cross-talk) of cells, signal transduction, and information transfer between cells.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12848 goldbook:13271)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12848 goldbook:13667)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12848 goldbook:13700)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12848 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12848 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12849))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12849 "adjuvant arthritis")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12849 "Experimental model of immunopathology with features of rheumatoid arthritis (RA), induced in rats by injection with bacterial products, which may be used to study anti-inflammatory therapies.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12849 goldbook:13306)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12849 goldbook:13651)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12849 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12849 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12850))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12850 "adoptive transfer")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12850 "Transfer, by transplantation of immunocompetent cells, of the capacity to mount an immune response.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12850 goldbook:13277)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12850 goldbook:13754)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12850 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12850 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12851))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12851 "adverse drug reaction")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12851 "Appreciably harmful or unpleasant reaction resulting from an intervention related to the administration of a pharmaceutical product.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12851 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12851 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12852))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12852 "adverse immunostimulation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12852 "Antigen-non-specific, inappropriate, or unintended activation of a component of the immune system.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12852 "The distinction from pseudoallergy is subtle."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12852 goldbook:13271)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12852 goldbook:13621)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12852 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12852 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12853))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12853 "aeroallergen")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12853 "Any airborne particle, such as a pollen grain or spore, that triggers an allergic reaction in sensitive individuals.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12853 goldbook:12858)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12853 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12853 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12854))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12854 "affinity maturation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12854 "Increase in antibody affinity for an antigen observed as the humoral immune response progresses.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12854 goldbook:13235)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12854 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12854 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12855))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12855 "agranulocytosis")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12855 "Failure of the bone marrow to make sufficient granulocytes, especially neutrophils.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12855 "This is normally identified by a neutrophil count less than \\(\\pu{0.5E9}\\) per litre of blood."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12855 goldbook:12959)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12855 goldbook:13510)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12855 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12855 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12856))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12856 "allelic exclusion")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12856 "Phenomenon whereby, following successful rearrangement of one allele of an antigen receptor gene, rearrangement of the other parental allele is suppressed, thereby ensuring each lymphocyte expresses only a single specificity of antigen receptor.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12856 "This does not occur for \\(\\upalpha\\) chains in T lymphocytes."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12856 goldbook:13724)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12856 goldbook:12891)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12856 goldbook:13399)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12856 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12856 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12857))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12857 "allergen")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12857 "Immunostimulant antigenic substance that may or may not cause a clinically significant effect but which is capable of producing an immune reaction, often immediate-type hypersensitivity.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12857 goldbook:13318)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12857 goldbook:12885)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12857 goldbook:13040)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12857 goldbook:13255)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12857 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12857 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12858))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12858 "allergic")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12858 "Immunologically hypersensitive.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12858 goldbook:13241)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12858 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12858 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12859))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12859 "allergy")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12859 "Symptoms or signs occurring in sensitized individuals following exposure to a previously encountered substance (allergen) that would otherwise not cause such symptoms or signs in non-sensitized individuals. The most common forms of allergy are rhinitis, urticaria, asthma, and contact dermatitis.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12859 "Except in the case of contact allergens, it is often an immunoglobulin E (IgE)-mediated hypersensitivity, e.g., asthma, eczema, hay fever, or food allergy."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12859 goldbook:12857)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12859 goldbook:12905)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12859 goldbook:13040)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12859 goldbook:13041)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12859 goldbook:13107)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12859 goldbook:13196)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12859 goldbook:13291)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12859 goldbook:13653)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12859 goldbook:13219)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12859 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12859 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12860))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12860 "alloantibody")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12860 "Antibody produced against an antigen from another member of the same species.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12860 goldbook:12861)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12860 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12860 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12861))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12861 "alloantigen")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12861 "Antigen, present in some but not all individuals of a particular species, that arises from polymorphisms at the major histocompatibility complex (MHC) loci and stimulates intense reactions to allograft tissues from other individuals of the same species that do not produce it.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12861 "isoantigen")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12861 "The human ABO blood group system antigens and Rhesus (Rh) factor are important examples of alloantigens."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12861 goldbook:12828)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12861 goldbook:13649)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12861 goldbook:12863)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12861 goldbook:13430)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12861 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12861 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12862))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12862 "allogeneic")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12862 "Genetically different, referring to individuals of the same species.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12862 "allogenic")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12862 "In immunotoxicology this generally refers to the use of genetically dissimilar cells to elicit a cell-mediated immune response in in vitro assays."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12862 goldbook:12994)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12862 goldbook:13325)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12862 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12862 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12863))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12863 "allograft")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12863 "Tissue or organ graft between allogeneic individuals.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12863 goldbook:12862)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12863 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12863 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12864))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12864 "allotype")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12864 "Allelic variant of an antigen that, because it is not present in all individuals, may be immunogenic in members of the same species that have a different version of the allele.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12864 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12864 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12865))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12865 "alloreactivity")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12865 "Reactivity of an antibody with an alloantigen.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12865 goldbook:12861)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12865 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12865 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12866))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12866 "alternative pathway")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12866 "Activation pathway involving complement components C3, Factor B, Factor D, and properdin that, in the presence of a stabilizing activator surface such as microbial polysaccharide, generates the alternative pathway C3 convertase C3bBb.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12866 goldbook:13011)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12866 goldbook:13612)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12866 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12866 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12867))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12867 "alveolar macrophage")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12867 "Macrophage found in the lung alveoli; it may remove and sometimes retain inhaled particulate matter.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12867 goldbook:13424)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12867 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12867 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12868))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12868 "alveolitis")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12868 "1) Inflammation of alveoli. 2) Inflammation of a tooth socket.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12868 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12868 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12869))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12869 "amyloid")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12869 "Fibrous protein secreted into the extracellular space where it forms amorphous deposits in multiple organs in some pathological states.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12869 "Amyloid beta (\\({\\rm{A}}\\upbeta\\)) is found in neuronal plaques in the brain in Alzheimer disease."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12869 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12869 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12870))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12870 "anamnestic")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12870 "Describing immunological memory that gives rise to a rapid increase in immunological response after reexposure to antigen.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12870 "Literally, \"does not forget\"."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12870 goldbook:13300)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12870 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12870 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12871))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12871 "anaphylactic shock")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12871 "Immediate overreaction of the immune system to a drug or other agent in an individual who has previously encountered the agent and has produced antibodies to that agent.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12871 "The major manifestation of anaphylactic shock is angioedema, which leads to hypovalemia, obstruction of the airway, and bronchospasm; these in turn may lead to coma or death."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12871 goldbook:12874)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12871 goldbook:12876)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12871 goldbook:13271)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12871 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12871 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12872))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12872 "anaphylactoid")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12872 "Of or resembling anaphylaxis.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12872 goldbook:12874)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12872 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12872 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12873))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12873 "anaphylatoxin")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12873 "Complement-derived protein fragment (e.g., C3a, C4a, or C5a) capable of directly triggering mast cell degranulation, chemotaxis, smooth muscle contraction, and inflammation.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12873 goldbook:13000)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12873 goldbook:13084)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12873 goldbook:13442)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12873 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12873 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12874))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12874 "anaphylaxis")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12874 "Life-threatening type I hypersensitivity allergic reaction occurring in a person or animal exposed to an antigen or hapten to which they have previously been sensitized.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12874 "Consequences of the reaction may include angioedema, vascular collapse, shock, and respiratory distress."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12874 goldbook:12859)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12874 goldbook:12876)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12874 goldbook:12871)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12874 goldbook:13255)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12874 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12874 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12875))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12875 "anergy")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12875 "Lack of an immune response, usually taken as lack of response to common recall antigens.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12875 "The failure of B or T cells to proliferate in response to defined autoantigens (clonal anergy) is a primary mechanism of self-tolerance."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12875 goldbook:12932)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12875 goldbook:13724)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12875 goldbook:12914)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12875 goldbook:13012)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12875 goldbook:13636)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12875 goldbook:13669)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:12875 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:12875 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:12876))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:12876 "angioedema")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12876 "Swelling that occurs in the tissue just below the surface of the skin, most often around the lips and eyes, the mucous membranes and occasionally the viscera.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:12876 "angioneurotic edema")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12876 "It may be genetic, when it is referred to as hereditary angioedema (HAE), but is more usually caused by an allergic reaction to either food or medication, and is then called acquired angioedema (AAE)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12876 "Angioedema may take from minutes to hours to develop. Severe angioedema can compromise the airway, and can be life-threatening."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12876 "Angioedema is often associated with dermatographism, urticaria, erythema, and purpura. It may sometimes be a sign of a condition such as leukemia or Hodgkin disease."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:12876 "Angioedema is similar to hives, but hives involve itchy red welts on the surface of the skin, whereas angioedema is a deeper swelling under the skin."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12876 goldbook:13220)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12876 goldbook:12858)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:12876 goldbook:13125)
