AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:12965 "Any of several autoimmune diseases characterized by intraepidermal or subepidermal blisters (e.g., pemphigus vulgaris, bullous pemphigoid) and highly specific autoantibodies against components of the desmosome or hemidesmosome (e.g., desmoglein 3, BP180).")
