AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13046 "Independent evolution of similarity between molecules or between species.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13046 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13046 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13047))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13047 "convertase")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13047 "Enzyme activity that converts complement protein into its reactive form by cleaving it.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13047 "Generation of the C3/C5 convertase is the pivotal event in complement activation."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13047 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13047 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13048))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13048 "Coombs test")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13048 "Diagnostic test using anti-immunoglobulin (Ig) to agglutinate antibody-coated erythrocytes.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13048 "direct antiglobulin test (DAT)")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13048 "direct Coombs test")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13048 "indirect antiglobulin test (IAT)")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13048 "indirect Coombs test")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13048 "The direct Coombs test, or direct antiglobulin test (DAT) refers to agglutination of a blood sample due to antibodies present on the erythrocyte surface. In the indirect Coombs test, or indirect antiglobulin test (IAT) antibodies free in the subject’s serum are tested for their availability to agglutinate erythrocytes of known antigenicity."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13048 goldbook:12886)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13048 goldbook:13127)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13048 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13048 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13049))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13049 "coreceptor")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13049 "Cell surface protein receptor that recognizes a substance bound to a primary receptor, and binds to a signaling molecule that thereby enhances the activity of another receptor.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13049 "Optimal T cell activation in an immune response depends on the involvement of relevant coreceptors occurring in a cluster with the T-cell receptors (TCRs). The coreceptors are CD4 or CD8 proteins, which lie alongside the T-cell receptor in the plasma membrane. Only when both coreceptor and receptor bind the major histocompatibility complex (MHC) molecule-antigen complex simultaneously is the full set of intracellular effector molecules recruited and the signal pathway inside the cell maximally activated."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13049 "B-cell receptors (BCRs) require the contributions of several coreceptors, notably CD19, CD21, and CD81 proteins, for full activation of intracellular signaling pathways."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13049 goldbook:12936)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13049 goldbook:12973)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13049 goldbook:12976)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13049 goldbook:13724)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13049 goldbook:13714)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13049 goldbook:13434)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13049 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13049 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13050))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13050 "corticosteroid")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13050 "Any of the family of steroid molecules that are produced in the adrenal cortex, or their synthetic analogs.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13050 "Corticosteroids can induce apoptotic cell death in lymphocytes, especially developing thymocytes. Therefore, they are useful anti-inflammatory, anti-lymphoid tumor, and immunosuppressive agents."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13050 goldbook:13320)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13050 goldbook:13399)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13050 goldbook:13598)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13050 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13050 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13051))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13051 "co-stimulation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13051 "Delivery of a second signal, in addition to that of antigen binding or antigen presentation, that is required for lymphocyte proliferation.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13051 "Co-stimulatory signals are delivered to T cells by the co-stimulatory molecules, B7.1 and B7.2, related molecules (see B7 molecule) that are expressed on the surface of the antigen-presenting cell (APC), and which bind the T-cell surface molecule CD28."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13051 "B cells may receive co-stimulatory signals from common pathogen components such as lipopolysaccharide (LPS), from complement fragments, or from CD40 ligand (CD40L) expressed on the surface of an activated antigen-specific helper T lymphocyte (Th)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13051 goldbook:12937)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13051 goldbook:12933)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13051 goldbook:12981)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13051 goldbook:13724)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13051 goldbook:12887)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13051 goldbook:12888)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13051 goldbook:13199)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13051 goldbook:13399)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13051 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13051 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13052))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13052 "counter-regulation hypothesis")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13052 "Hypothesis that all types of infection early in childhood may protect against the development of atopy by driving the production of cytokines such as interleukin-10 (IL-10) and transforming growth factor $\\ce{\\upbeta\\!}$ ($\\ce{TGF\\mbox{-}\\upbeta\\!}$), which downregulate both Th1 and Th2 responses.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13052 goldbook:13718)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13052 goldbook:13719)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13052 goldbook:12910)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13052 goldbook:13065)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13052 goldbook:13338)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13052 goldbook:13752)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13052 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13052 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13053))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13053 "Crohn disease")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13053 "Chronic inflammatory bowel disease (IBD) thought to result from an abnormal overresponsiveness to commensal gut flora.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13053 "Crohn's disease")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13053 goldbook:13334)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13053 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13053 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13054))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13054 "cross-matching")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13054 "1) Test for determining the compatibility between the blood of a donor and that of a recipient before transfusion; the clumping of erythrocytes indicates incompatibility. 2) Test for determining tissue compatibility between a transplant donor and the recipient before transplantation, in which the recipient’s serum is tested for antibodies that may react with the lymphocytes or other cells of the donor. 3) Process of performing one of these tests.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13054 goldbook:13127)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13054 goldbook:13399)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13054 goldbook:13753)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13054 goldbook:13754)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13054 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13054 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13055))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13055 "cross-presentation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13055 "Activation of CD8+ lymphocytes by the presentation of exogenous antigens in association with major histocompatibility complex (MHC) class I molecules.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13055 "cross-priming")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13055 "This is in contrast to normal activation of these lymphocytes (direct-priming) that results from presentation of endogenous antigens."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13055 "The cells that cross-present antigens are the bone marrow-derived antigen-presenting cells (APCs). The form of antigen they monitor from tissues is predominantly cellular protein, acquired though phagocytosis and macropinocytosis and presented through two distinct pathways. In one pathway, antigen is transferred into the cytosol where it is degraded by proteasomes, and in the other, the antigen is hydrolyzed in the endocytic compartment"^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13055 "Cross-presentation can lead to different outcomes, tolerance or immunity."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13055 goldbook:13401)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13055 goldbook:12976)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13055 goldbook:12888)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13055 goldbook:13272)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13055 goldbook:13399)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13055 goldbook:13428)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13055 goldbook:13431)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13055 goldbook:13562)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13055 goldbook:13607)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13055 goldbook:13613)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13055 goldbook:13302)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13055 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13055 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13056))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13056 "cross-reacting antibody")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13056 "Antibody that is able to react with an antigen that did not specifically stimulate its production.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13056 "Cross-reactions are usually weaker than the reaction of the antibody with the antigen that caused its production."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13056 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13056 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13057))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13057 "cross-reacting antigen")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13057 "Antigen that is able to react with an antibody induced by a different antigen. Note: The two antigens may share the same antigenic determinants or carry determinants that are sufficiently alike stereochemically to enable the antibody to react with both. Antigen that has an identical structure in two strains of microorganism, so that antibody raised against one strain will react with the other strain.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13057 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13057 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13058))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13058 "cross sensitivity")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13058 "State of immunological hypersensitivity to one substance that predisposes an individual to sensitivity to other substances that are related in chemical structure (cross-reacting antigens).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13058 goldbook:13057)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13058 goldbook:13241)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13058 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13058 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13059))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13059 "cross-tolerance")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13059 "State of immunological tolerance to one substance produced by priming an animal with another substance that bears a cross-reacting antigen.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13059 goldbook:13057)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13059 goldbook:13607)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13059 goldbook:13302)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13059 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13059 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13060))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13060 "cryoglobulin")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13060 "Immunoglobulin (Ig) that forms insoluble aggregates at temperatures below body temperature.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13060 "Many cryoglobulins function as autoantibodies (e.g., rheumatoid factor). Cryoglobulins are found in lymphoproliferative (see lymphoproliferation) diseases, a number of autoimmune diseases, as well as chronic infections. They can cause vasculitic and secondary thrombotic manifestations (cryoglobulinemic vasculitis, glomerulonephritis)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13060 goldbook:12913)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13060 goldbook:12919)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13060 goldbook:13061)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13060 goldbook:13174)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13060 goldbook:13419)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13060 goldbook:13652)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13060 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13060 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13061))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13061 "cryoglobulinemic vasculitis")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13061 "Cutaneous or systemic vasculitis caused by cold-labile proteins (cryoglobulins, cryofibrinogen) that leads to increased viscosity, protein precipitation or gelatinification, complement activation, and endothelial cell damage, especially in the cold.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13061 "Frequently associated with chronic hepatitis C or B infection, but can also be induced by other infections and malignancies."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13061 goldbook:13060)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13061 goldbook:13708)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13061 goldbook:13776)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13061 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13061 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13062))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13062 "cryptic epitope")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13062 "Epitope that cannot be recognized by a lymphocyte receptor until the antigen has been broken down and processed or modified by hapten binding.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13062 goldbook:13399)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13062 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13062 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13063))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13063 "cutaneous lymphocyte antigen")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13063 "Cell-surface molecule that is involved in lymphocyte homing to the skin in humans.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13063 "CLA")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13063 goldbook:13403)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13063 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13063 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13064))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13064 "cutaneous T-cell lymphoma")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13064 "Malignant growth of T cells that home to the skin.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13064 "mycosis fungoides")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13064 goldbook:13724)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13064 goldbook:13221)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13064 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13064 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13065))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13065 "cytokine")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13065 "Any of a group of soluble small proteins released from a variety of cells, typically of the immune system, that affect cell behavior in an autocrine or paracrine fashion.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13065 "Cytokines produced by lymphocytes are known as lymphokines; those produced by monocytes are called monokines. Other types of cytokines include chemokines, growth factors, colony-stimulating factors (CSFs), transforming growth factors, interferons, interleukins, and tumor necrosis factors."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13065 goldbook:12916)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13065 goldbook:13024)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13065 goldbook:13271)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13065 goldbook:13399)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13065 goldbook:13415)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13065 goldbook:13467)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13065 goldbook:13468)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13065 goldbook:13752)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13065 goldbook:13762)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13065 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13065 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13066))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13066 "cytokine capture assay")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13066 "Method to detect cytokine release by injecting an animal with a neutralizing biotinylated antibody to the cytokine, which inhibits its utilization and allows its accumulation in the blood. Recovered cytokineantibody complexes are then measured in an enzyme-linked immunosorbent assay (ELISA) with an antibody to a second epitope on the cytokine.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13066 "<i>in vivo</i> cytokine capture assay (IVCCA)")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13066 goldbook:13065)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13066 goldbook:13115)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13066 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13066 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13067))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13067 "cytokine profile")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13067 "Characteristic pattern of cytokine production associated with a defined immunological state.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13067 goldbook:13065)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13067 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13067 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13068))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13068 "cytokine release assay")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13068 "Method of quantifying cytokines released by viable cells, using cytokine-specific antibodies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13068 "CRA")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13068 goldbook:13065)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13068 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13068 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13069))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13069 "immune cytolysis")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13069 "1) Cell lysis caused by a lesion produced by the action of complement proteins on the antibody-coated plasma membrane of a cell. 2) Cell lysis following plasma membrane reaction with perforins released by natural killer (NK) cells.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13069 "immune cytolysis")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13069 goldbook:13499)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13069 goldbook:13549)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13069 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13069 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13070))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13070 "cytopenia")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13070 "Decrease in the number of one or more types of blood cells.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13070 goldbook:13532)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13070 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13070 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13071))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13071 "cytotoxic")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13071 "Causing damage to cell structure or function.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13071 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13071 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13072))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13072 "cytotoxic T lymphocyte")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13072 "Any of a subset of T lymphocytes bearing the CD8 surface marker and able to kill target cells [infected somatic or tumor cells, recognized by the antigen receptor complex (TCR/CD3)] after induction of a specific immune response to the antigens bound to major histocompatibility complex (MHC) class I molecules.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13072 "CD8+ T cell")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13072 "cytolytic T cell")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13072 "cytotoxic T cell")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13072 "killer T cell")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13072 "CD4+ T cells may also become cytotoxic."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13072 goldbook:12976)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13072 goldbook:13724)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13072 goldbook:12972)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13072 goldbook:12891)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13072 goldbook:13431)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13072 goldbook:13727)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13072 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13072 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13073))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13073 "cytotoxic T lymphocyte antigen 4")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13073 "High affinity receptor for B7 molecules expressed on T cells, binding of which inhibits T cell activation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13073 "CTLA-4")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13073 "CD152")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13073 "Mutations in the gene encoding CTLA-4 have been associated with various autoimmune diseases."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13073 goldbook:12933)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13073 goldbook:13724)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13073 goldbook:13401)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13073 goldbook:12919)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13073 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13073 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13074))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13074 "cytotoxic T lymphocyte assay")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13074 "Assay based on quantitation of cell death caused by sensitized lymphocytes or splenocytes cultured with a fixed number of tumor or other target cells that have been prelabeled with \\(\\ce{^{51}Cr}\\). The \\(\\ce{^{51}Cr}\\) is taken up and reversibly binds to cytosolic proteins. When these target cells are incubated with sensitized lymphocytes, the target cells are killed and the \\(\\ce{^{51}Cr}\\) is released.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13074 "CTL")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13074 goldbook:13399)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13074 goldbook:13727)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13074 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13074 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13075))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13075 "cytotoxin")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13075 "Substance with a specific toxic effect on certain cells.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13075 "Major cytotoxins made by cytotoxic T lymphocytes (CTL, Tc) and natural killer (NK) cells that participate in the destruction of target cells include perforins, granzymes, and granulolysins."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13075 goldbook:13072)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13075 goldbook:13186)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13075 goldbook:13499)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13075 goldbook:13549)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13075 goldbook:13727)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13075 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13075 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13076))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13076 "DEC-205")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13076 "Surface antigen characteristic of dendritic cells.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13076 "CD205")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13076 goldbook:13087)
