AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13221 "Movement of leukocytes to specific locations in the body.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13221 goldbook:13379)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13221 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13221 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13222))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13222 "homing receptor")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13222 "Cell surface molecule that directs leukocytes to specific locations in the body.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13222 goldbook:13379)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13222 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13222 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13223))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13223 "homocytotropic antibody")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13223 "Antibody that binds preferentially to cells from the same species rather than to cells from other species.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13223 goldbook:12928)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13223 goldbook:13206)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13223 goldbook:13209)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13223 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13223 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13224))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13224 "homozygous")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13224 "Possessing the same allele at a given locus on the two homologous chromosomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13224 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13224 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13225))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13225 "horror autotoxicus")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13225 "Term (Latin: dread of self-poisoning) to describe the body’s innate aversion to immunological self destruction.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13225 "Introduced by Paul Ehrlich (1902)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13225 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13225 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13226))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13226 "host defense")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13226 "Ability of an individual to resist invasion by opportunistic agents and production of disease associated with exposure to microorganisms, foreign tissue, and particulates, as well as certain types of neoplasia. Host defense may be either nonspecific (innate or natural immunity) or specific (adaptive or acquired immunity) in nature.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13226 "Immunological defense may involve chemotaxis, phagocytosis, reaction with immunoglobulins (Ig) and/or with complement, and T-cell cytotoxicity."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13226 goldbook:13724)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13226 goldbook:12832)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13226 goldbook:12843)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13226 goldbook:13000)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13226 goldbook:12993)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13226 goldbook:13335)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13226 goldbook:13498)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13226 goldbook:13562)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13226 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13226 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13227))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13227 "host-resistance assay")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13227 "Evaluation of host resistance in rodents to in vivo challenge with an infectious organism under normal conditions and after pharmacological and nutritional alterations of the immune system.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13227 goldbook:12997)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13227 goldbook:13271)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13227 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13227 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13228))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13228 "human immunodeficiency virus")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13228 "Causative agent of acquired immune deficiency syndrome (AIDS).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13228 "HIV")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13228 "HIV is a retrovirus of the lentivirus family that selectively infects macrophages and CD4+ T cells, leading to their slow depletion, eventually resulting in immunodeficiency."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13228 "There are two major strains of the virus, HIV-1 and HIV-2, of which HIV-1 causes most disease worldwide. HIV-2 is endemic to West Africa but is spreading."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13228 goldbook:12974)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13228 goldbook:13724)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13228 goldbook:12833)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13228 goldbook:13281)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13228 goldbook:13424)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13228 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13228 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13229))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13229 "humanized antibody")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13229 "Genetically engineered monoclonal antibody of non-human origin in which all but the antigen-binding complementarity-determining region (CDR) sequences have been replaced with sequences derived from human antibodies.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13229 "This procedure is carried out to minimize the immunogenicity of therapeutic, monoclonal antibodies."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13229 goldbook:13029)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13229 goldbook:12878)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13229 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13229 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13230))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13230 "human leukocyte antigen")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13230 "Antigen coded by genes of the human major histocompatibility complex (MHC).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13230 "HLA")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13230 "Human HLA-A, -B and -C (resembling mouse H-2K, D and L) are MHC class I molecules, whereas HLA-DP, -DQ and -DR (resembling mouse I-A and I-E) are MHC class II molecules."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13230 "The genes for HLAs are situated on chromosome 6."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13230 goldbook:13431)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13230 goldbook:13432)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13230 goldbook:13430)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13230 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13230 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13231))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13231 "human leukocyte antigen polymorphism")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13231 "Discontinuous genetic variation in the major histocompatibility complex (MHC) that results in the occurrence of several different forms of MHC molecules among people.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13231 "HLA Polymorphism")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13231 "Specific HLA polymorphisms are associated with a number of diseases, e.g., HLA-B27 is associated with ankylosing spondylitis, psoriatic arthritis, rheumatoid arthritis (RA), etc., and some chemical sensitivities."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13231 goldbook:13430)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13231 goldbook:13651)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13231 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13231 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13232))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13232 "human leukocyte antigen type I")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13232 "Molecules that enable the body to recognize infected cells and tumor cells and destroy them with cytotoxic T lymphocytes (CTLs).")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13232 "HLA Type I")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13232 "HLA type I molecules are made by all nucleated cells in the body, possess a deep groove (see peptide-binding groove) that can bind peptide epitopes, typically 8-11 amino acids long, from endogenous antigens; and present HLA type I/peptide complexes to CD8+ lymphocytes that have a complementary shaped T-cell receptor (TCR)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13232 goldbook:12977)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13232 goldbook:13714)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13232 goldbook:13072)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13232 goldbook:13399)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13232 goldbook:13548)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13232 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13232 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13233))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13233 "human leukocyte antigen type II")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13233 "Molecules that enable CD4+ lymphocytes to recognize epitopes of exogenous antigens and discriminate self from non-self.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13233 "HLA Type II")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13233 "HLA type II molecules are made by antigen-presenting cells (APCs), such as dendritic cells, macrophages, and B lymphocytes, possess a deep groove (see peptide-binding groove) that can bind peptide epitopes, typically 10–30 amino acids long but with an optimum length of 12–16 amino acids, from exogenous antigens; and present HLA type II/peptide complexes to CD4+ lymphocytes that have a complementary shaped T-cell receptor (TCR)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13233 goldbook:12937)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13233 goldbook:12973)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13233 goldbook:13714)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13233 goldbook:12888)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13233 goldbook:13087)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13233 goldbook:13399)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13233 goldbook:13424)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13233 goldbook:13516)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13233 goldbook:13548)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13233 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13233 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13234))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13234 "humoral")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13234 "Pertaining to extracellular fluid such as plasma and lymph.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13234 "The term humoral immunity is used to denote antibody-mediated immune responses such as phagocytosis and activation of the complement system."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13234 goldbook:13033)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13234 goldbook:13236)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13234 goldbook:13562)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13234 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13234 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13235))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13235 "humoral immune response")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13235 "Immune response in which specific antibodies induce the effector functions (such as phagocytosis and activation of the complement system).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13235 goldbook:13033)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13235 goldbook:13562)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13235 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13235 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13236))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13236 "humoral immunity")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13236 "Specific immune response that is mediated primarily by humoral factors circulating in solution in the blood plasma and lymph (i.e., antibodies and complement).")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13236 "humorally mediated immunity (HMI)")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13236 "The induction of the humoral immune response generally requires the cooperation of cellular immune mechanisms."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13236 goldbook:13235)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13236 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13236 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13237))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13237 "hypergammaglobulinemia")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13237 "Increase of gammaglobulins in the blood by paraproteinemia or increased production of immunoglobulins (Ig).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13237 goldbook:13165)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13237 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13237 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13238))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13238 "hyperimmunoglobulin E syndrome")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13238 "Rare primary immunodeficiency syndrome characterized by recurrent severe staphylococcal skin abscesses (hence Job syndrome), lung infections, and markedly elevated serum immunoglobulin E (IgE) levels.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13238 "Job syndrome")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13238 goldbook:13288)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13238 goldbook:13281)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13238 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13238 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13239))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13239 "hyperimmunoglobulin M syndrome")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13239 "Primary T cell defect due to mutations in the CD40 ligand (CD40L), characterized by recurrent (opportunistic) infections and very low levels of immunoglobulin G (IgG) and immunoglobulin A (IgA).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13239 "HIGM")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13239 "Autoimmune manifestations (e.g., cytopenia, arthritis, sclerosing cholangitis) are often seen."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13239 goldbook:12918)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13239 goldbook:12981)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13239 goldbook:13724)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13239 goldbook:12903)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13239 goldbook:13070)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13239 goldbook:13286)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13239 goldbook:13292)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13239 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13239 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13240))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13240 "hyperreactivity")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13240 "Abnormally increased response to a stimulus.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13240 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13240 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13241))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13241 "hypersensitivity")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13241 "State in which an individual reacts with allergic effects following exposure to a certain substance (allergen) after having been exposed previously to the same substance. It is sometimes used loosely for any increased response.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13241 "Four types of hypersensitivity are recognized. Most common chemically induced allergies are type I [immunoglobulin E- (IgE-) mediated] and type IV (cell-mediated) hypersensitivity."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13241 goldbook:13167)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13241 goldbook:12857)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13241 goldbook:12858)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13241 goldbook:12859)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13241 goldbook:13288)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13241 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13241 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13242))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13242 "hypersensitivity pneumonitis")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13242 "Immune-mediated inflammatory disease of the lung parenchyma caused by exposure to an inhaled chemical allergen or organic dust.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13242 "HPS")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13242 "extrinsic allergic alveolitis")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13242 goldbook:12857)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13242 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13242 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13243))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13243 "hypersensitization")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13243 "Development of excessive immune reactivity to an antigen.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13243 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13243 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13244))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13244 "hypersusceptibility")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13244 "Adverse immunological effects in an individual occurring under conditions of exposure to an allergen that result in no effects in the great majority of the population, or an individual exhibiting exaggerated effects in comparison with the great majority of those showing some adverse effects.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13244 goldbook:12857)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13244 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13244 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13245))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13245 "hypervariable region")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13245 "Amino acid sequence within the immunoglobulin (Ig) and T-cell receptor (TCR) variable (V) regions that shows the greatest variability and contributes most to the antigen or peptide-major histocompatibility complex (MHC) molecule binding site.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13245 goldbook:13714)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13245 goldbook:13434)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13245 goldbook:13773)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13245 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13245 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13246))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13246 "hypogammaglobulinemia")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13246 "Immunodeficiency state marked by abnormally low levels of all classes of immunoglobulins (Ig), associated with increased susceptibility to infectious diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13246 "It may be primary (inherited), or secondary (acquired), or it may occur physiologically in normal neonates."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13246 goldbook:13281)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13246 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13246 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13247))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13247 "hyposensitization therapy")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13247 "Dermal application of a selected allergen to an allergic person in stepwise increasing dosage, with the aim of reducing the immune system’s tendency for the corresponding allergic reaction.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13247 goldbook:12857)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13247 goldbook:12858)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13247 goldbook:12851)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13247 goldbook:13271)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13247 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13247 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13248))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13248 "Ia antigen")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13248 "Isoantigen encoded by the Ia region of the mouse major histocompatibility complex (H-2 complex).")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13248 "I region-associated antigen")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13248 "immune response-associated antigen")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13248 "Ia antigens are defined by serological methods and are found predominantly on B lymphocytes and macrophages."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13248 "This term is also used as a generic term for any major histocompatibility complex (MHC) class II antigen."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13248 goldbook:12937)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13248 goldbook:12861)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13248 goldbook:13268)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13248 goldbook:13424)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13248 goldbook:13191)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13248 goldbook:13432)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13248 goldbook:13672)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13248 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13248 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13249))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13249 "idiopathic")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13249 "Term that describes a 'primary' symptom or disease in which no underlying cause or associated disorder can be found.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13249 "immune thrombocytopenic purpura")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13249 "In many cases, autoimmune processes are involved in the pathogenesis [e.g., idiopathic Addison disease, idiopathic thrombocytopenic purpura (ITP)]."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13249 goldbook:12845)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13249 goldbook:12918)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13249 goldbook:13250)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13249 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13249 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13250))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13250 "idiopathic thrombocytopenic purpura")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13250 "Thrombocytopenia of unknown cause, probably related to the production of anti-platelet antibodies, and leading to bruising (purpura).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13250 "ITP")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13250 "immune thrombocytopenic purpura")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13250 goldbook:13580)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13250 goldbook:13625)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13250 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13250 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13251))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13251 "idiosyncratic drug reaction")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13251 "Rare and unpredictable adverse drug reaction occurring only in susceptible individuals.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13251 "IDR")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13251 "A dose–response relationship may not be apparent within the dose range used clinically."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13251 goldbook:12851)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13251 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13251 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13252))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13252 "idiotype")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13252 "The combined antigenic determinants (idiotopes) expressed in the variable (V) region of immunoglobulins (Ig) of an individual that determine antibody specificity to a particular antigen.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13252 goldbook:12893)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13252 goldbook:13773)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13252 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13252 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13253))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13253 "idiotype network")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13253 "Regulatory network based on interactions of anti-idiotypic antibodies and idiotypes present on antibodies and T-cell receptors (TCRs), resulting in feedback inhibition of ongoing B cell or T cell responses.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13253 "idiotypic network")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13253 goldbook:12937)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13253 goldbook:13724)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13253 goldbook:13714)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13253 goldbook:12893)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13253 goldbook:13252)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13253 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13253 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13254))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13254 "immature")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13254 "Describing cells that are not fully developed and unable to participate immediately in an immune response.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13254 "Immature B cells and T cells migrate from their primary lymphoid sites (bone marrow and thymus) through the vascular and lymphatic systems to secondary lymphoid sites. These sites include the spleen, lymph nodes, tonsils, and Peyer’s patches in the intestine and appendix. The immature B cells and T cells mature only after they encounter an antigen."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13254 goldbook:12937)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13254 goldbook:13559)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13254 goldbook:13724)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13254 goldbook:12959)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13254 goldbook:13397)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13254 goldbook:13395)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13254 goldbook:13604)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13254 goldbook:13663)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13254 goldbook:13690)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13254 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13254 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13255))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13255 "immediate-type hypersensitivity")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13255 "Reaction provoked by re-exposure to an antigen (allergen) that causes plasma cells to secrete immunoglobulin E (IgE) which binds to Fc receptors on the surface of tissue mast cells and blood basophils, sensitizing them, so that later exposure to the same allergen cross-links the bound IgE, leading to degranulation and the secretion of pharmacologically active mediators such as histamine, leukotriene, and prostaglandin that act immediately on the surrounding tissues.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13255 "immediate-type allergy")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13255 "type I hypersensitivity")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13255 "The principal effects of these products are vasodilation and smooth-muscle contraction. The reaction may be either local or systemic. Symptoms vary from mild irritation to sudden death from anaphylactic shock."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13255 goldbook:13138)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13255 goldbook:12857)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13255 goldbook:12871)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13255 goldbook:12943)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13255 goldbook:13084)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13255 goldbook:13288)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13255 goldbook:13384)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13255 goldbook:13442)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13255 goldbook:13576)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13255 goldbook:13708)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13255 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13255 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13256))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13256 "immune adherence")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13256 "Attachment of particulate antigen coated with C3b (see complement) to cells expressing C3b receptors, which results in enhanced phagocytosis of bacteria by macrophages.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13256 goldbook:13424)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13256 goldbook:13562)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13256 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13256 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13257))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13257 "immune complex")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13257 "Product of an antigen–antibody reaction, which may also contain components of the complement system.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13257 goldbook:13033)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13257 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13257 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13258))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13258 "immune complex disease")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13258 "Illness resulting from deposition of antigen–antibody complexes in tissues.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13258 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13258 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13259))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13259 "immune deviation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13259 "Regulatory mechanism of the preferential activation of one aspect (cellular or humoral) of the adaptive immune system at the expense of the other.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13259 "Although not a form of true tolerance, this regulatory mechanism may be involved in the induction and maintenance of self-tolerance."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13259 goldbook:12844)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13259 goldbook:13669)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13259 goldbook:13302)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13259 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13259 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13260))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13260 "immune elimination")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13260 "Removal of pathogens or tumor cells by the immune system; the first step of immunoediting of tumors.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13260 goldbook:13284)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13260 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13260 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13261))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13261 "immune enhancement")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13261 "Therapeutic stimulation of the immune response, especially in tumor therapy.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13261 "enhancement (in immunology)")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13261 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13261 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13262))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13262 "immune equilibrium")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13262 "State in carcinogenesis where there is an equilibrium between elimination of tumor cells by the immune system and growth of non-immunogenic tumor cells; the second step in immunoediting.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13262 goldbook:13271)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13262 goldbook:13284)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13262 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13262 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13263))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13263 "immune escape")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13263 "Biological feature of an infectious agent or of a tumor cell that prevents its elimination by the immune system. Such a feature can be acquired by a selection process. Immune escape is the third step in immunoediting of tumors.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13263 goldbook:13271)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13263 goldbook:13284)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13263 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13263 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13264))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13264 "immune evasion")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13264 "Property of a pathogen that results in avoidance of attack by the immune system, e.g., because of reduced phagocytosis, lack of recognition by the innate immune system, or suppression of the immune response.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13264 goldbook:13271)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13264 goldbook:13335)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13264 goldbook:13562)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13264 goldbook:13701)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13264 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13264 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13265))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13265 "immune modulation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13265 "Alteration of the immune response to alleviate harmful effects of the immune system or to promote its activity by changes in regulatory factors; often part of deliberate therapeutic intervention.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13265 "immunomodulation")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13265 goldbook:13271)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13265 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13265 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13266))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13266 "immune regulation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13266 "Capacity of the immune system to regulate itself so that an immune response does not become excessive and cause tissue damage, autoimmune reactions, or allergic reactions.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13266 "immunoregulation")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13266 goldbook:12851)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13266 goldbook:12918)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13266 goldbook:13271)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13266 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13266 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13267))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13267 "immune reserve hypothesis")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13267 "Hypothesis that the immune response involves multiple redundancies that are capable of compensating for acute reductions in certain immune functions.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13267 "Such a reserve might prevent a serious reduction in host resistance after temporary immunosuppression of selected parameters [e.g., natural killer (NK) cell function]."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13267 goldbook:13499)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13267 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13267 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13268))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13268 "immune response-associated protein")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13268 "Protein found in antigen-presenting cells (APCs) and B lymphocytes in mice.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13268 "Ia protein")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13268 goldbook:12937)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13268 goldbook:13248)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13268 goldbook:12888)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13268 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13268 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13269))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13269 "immune response genes")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13269 "Genes, including those within the major histocompatibility complex (MHC), that together determine the overall level of immune response to a given antigen.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13269 "ir genes")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13269 goldbook:13430)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13269 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13269 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13270))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13270 "immune surveillance")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13270 "Recognition, and in some cases elimination, of tumor cells by the immune system before they become clinically detectable.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13270 "immunosurveillance")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13270 goldbook:13271)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13270 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13270 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13271))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13271 "immune system")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13271 "Integrated network of organs, glands, and tissues that has evolved to protect the body from foreign substances, including bacteria, viruses, and other infection-causing parasites and pathogens.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13271 "The immune system may produce hypersensitivity reactions that, in the extreme, can be fatal. If the immune system misidentifies normal body components as foreign, this leads to autoimmune disorders, such as systemic lupus erythematosus (SLE), in which the body destroys its own constituents."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13271 goldbook:12918)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13271 goldbook:13241)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13271 goldbook:13710)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13271 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13271 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13272))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13272 "immunity")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13272 "Inherited, acquired, or induced resistance to infection by a specific pathogen.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13272 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13272 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13273))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13273 "immunoactivation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13273 "Activation of the immune system as a whole to react more rapidly to antigens.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13273 goldbook:13271)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13273 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13273 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13274))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13274 "immunoactivator")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13274 "Substance that activates the immune system as a whole to react more rapidly to antigens.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13274 goldbook:13271)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13274 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13274 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13275))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13275 "immunoadsorption")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13275 "Method for removal of antibody or antigen by allowing it to bind to a corresponding antigen or antibody immobilized in the solid phase.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13275 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13275 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13276))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13276 "immunoblot")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13276 "Supporting substrate [often a nitrocellulose, nylon, or poly(vinylidene fluoride) membrane] onto which proteins that have been separated by gel electrophoresis are transferred and then identified by the binding of specific antibodies.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13276 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13276 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13277))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13277 "immunocompetence")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13277 "Having the ability to exhibit an immune response.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13277 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13277 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13278))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13278 "immunocompromised")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13278 "Unable to mount a full or effective immune response.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13278 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13278 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13279))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13279 "immunoconjugate")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13279 "Antibody or antibody fragment to which a functional molecule, such as a drug, has been chemically linked.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13279 "antibody conjugate")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13279 goldbook:13280)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13279 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13279 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13280))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13280 "immunocytokine")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13280 "Antibody or antibody fragment to which a cytokine has been chemically linked.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13280 "Such a construct may be used to direct a cytokine to its target cell."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13280 goldbook:13065)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13280 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13280 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13281))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13281 "immunodeficiency")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13281 "Inability to produce a normal repertoire of antibodies or immunologically sensitized T lymphocytes, especially in response to specific antigens.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13281 "Defects in one or more components of the immune system result in the inability to eliminate or neutralize antigens."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13281 "Congenital or primary immunodeficiencies are genetic or due to developmental disorders, such as congenital thymic aplasia (see also thymic atrophy)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13281 "Acquired or secondary immunodeficiencies develop as a consequence of malnutrition, malignancies, immunosuppressive compounds, radiation or infection of immunocompetent T lymphocytes with human immunodeficiency virus (HIV)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13281 "Defects in natural immunity may also result in immunodeficiency."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13281 goldbook:13724)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13281 goldbook:13228)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13281 goldbook:13271)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13281 goldbook:13277)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13281 goldbook:13320)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13281 goldbook:13498)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13281 goldbook:13734)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13281 goldbook:13735)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13281 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13281 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13282))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13282 "immunodominant epitope")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13282 "Epitope in an antigen that is preferentially recognized by T cells, which then come to dominate the immune response.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13282 goldbook:13724)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13282 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13282 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13283))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13283 "immunodysregulation–polyendocrinopathy–enteropathy, X-linked")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13283 "X-linked syndrome characterized by immunodysregulation, polyendocrinopathy (diabetes mellitus type 1, thyroiditis), hemolytic anemia, thrombocytopenia, dermatitis, and enteropathy, caused by mutations in the gene encoding Foxp3.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13283 "IPEX syndrome")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13283 goldbook:13141)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13283 goldbook:13089)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13283 goldbook:13092)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13283 goldbook:13202)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13283 goldbook:13741)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13283 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13283 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13284))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13284 "immunoediting")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13284 "Process of continuing immunosuppression of immunogenic tumor cells, which may finally result in the selection of non-immunogenic tumor cells. It consists of the steps immune elimination, immune equilibrium, and immune escape.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13284 goldbook:13260)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13284 goldbook:13262)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13284 goldbook:13263)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13284 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13284 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13285))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13285 "immunofluorescence")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13285 "Technique for detection of cell- or tissue-associated antigens by the use of a fluorescently tagged ligand, e.g., an anti-immunoglobulin (Ig) conjugated to fluorescein isothiocyanate (FITC).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13285 goldbook:13153)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13285 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13285 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13286))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13286 "immunoglobulin A")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13286 "Class of immunoglobulin (Ig) characterized by $\\ce{\\upalpha\\!}$ heavy chains.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13286 "IgA")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13286 "IgA antibodies are secreted mainly by mucosal lymphoid tissues, and in the dimeric form are present in mucosal secretions. IgA in the monomeric form is present in blood."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13286 goldbook:13198)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13286 goldbook:13473)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13286 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13286 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13287))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13287 "immunoglobulin D")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13287 "Class of immunoglobulin (Ig) characterized by $\\updelta\\!$ heavy chains.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13287 "IgD")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13287 "It appears as a surface immunoglobulin on mature naïve B cells (see naïve lymphocyte) but its function is unknown."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13287 goldbook:12937)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13287 goldbook:13198)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13287 goldbook:13496)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13287 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13287 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13288))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13288 "immunoglobulin E")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13288 "Class of immunoglobulin (Ig) characterized by $\\upvarepsilon\\!$ heavy chains.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13288 "IgE")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13288 "It is involved in the defense against parasite infections and in allergic reactions."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13288 goldbook:12851)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13288 goldbook:13198)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13288 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13288 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13289))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13289 "immunoglobulin Y")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13289 "Immunoglobulin (Ig) found in chickens.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13289 "IgY")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13289 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13289 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13290))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13290 "immunoglobulin E-binding Fc receptors")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13290 "High-affinity IgE-binding ${\\rm{Fc\\mbox{-}}}\\upvarepsilon\\!{\\rm{\\mbox{-}R}}$ type I receptors are expressed on mast cells and basophils and interact with IgE antibodies with high affinity.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13290 "IgE-binding FC receptors")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13290 "The cross-linking of these receptors results in release of mediators such as histamine."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13290 "The receptors are composed of \\(\\upalpha\\), \\(\\upbeta\\), and \\(\\upgamma\\) chains; the α chain contains the IgE binding site, while the \\(\\ce{\\upgamma\\ chain}\\) is responsible for signal transduction."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13290 "The low-affinity IgE binding Fc receptor (CD23) is expressed on B cells, and its soluble (truncated) form is generated by proteolytic cleavage and regulates IgE production by B cells."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13290 goldbook:12937)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13290 goldbook:12979)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13290 goldbook:13138)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13290 goldbook:12943)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13290 goldbook:13442)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13290 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13290 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13291))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13291 "immunoglobulin E-mediated hypersensitivity")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13291 "State in which an individual reacts with allergic effects caused fundamentally by the reaction of antigen-specific immunoglobulin E (IgE) following exposure to a certain substance (allergen) after having been exposed previously to the same substance.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13291 "IgE-Mediated Hypersensitivity")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13291 goldbook:12857)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13291 goldbook:12858)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13291 goldbook:13288)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13291 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13291 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13292))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13292 "immunoglobulin G")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13292 "Class of immunoglobulin (Ig) characterized by \\(\\upgamma\\) heavy chains.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13292 "IgG")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13292 "It is the most abundant class of immunoglobulin found in the plasma."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13292 goldbook:13198)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13292 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13292 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13293))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13293 "immunoglobulin M")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13293 "Class of immunoglobulin (Ig) characterized by \\(\\upmu\\) heavy chains.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13293 "IgM")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13293 "It is the first immunoglobulin to appear on the surface of B cells and the first to be secreted."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13293 "Unlike other immunoglobulins that exist in the monomeric (IgA, IgD, IgE, and IgG) or dimeric (IgA) state, IgM is found in the blood as a pentamer."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13293 goldbook:12937)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13293 goldbook:13286)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13293 goldbook:13287)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13293 goldbook:13288)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13293 goldbook:13292)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13293 goldbook:13198)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13293 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13293 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13294))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13294 "immunoglobulin gene superfamily")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13294 "Genes encoding proteins containing one or more immunoglobulin (Ig) domains (homology units) that are homologous to either Ig variable (V) region or constant (C) region domains. Cell surface and soluble molecules mediating recognition, adhesion, or binding functions in and outside the immune system, derived from the same precursor, belong to this family of molecules (e.g., immunoglobulin, T-cell receptor (TCR), major histocompatibility complex (MHC) class I and class II molecules, CD4, CD8, and $\\ce{Fc\\upgamma\\!R}$).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13294 goldbook:12973)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13294 goldbook:12976)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13294 goldbook:13714)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13294 goldbook:13432)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13294 goldbook:13039)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13294 goldbook:13099)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13294 goldbook:13271)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13294 goldbook:13431)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13294 goldbook:13773)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13294 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13294 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13295))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13295 "immunoglobulin superfamily")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13295 "Large family of proteins characterized by possession of 'immunoglobulin-type' domains of approximately 110 amino acids folded into two \\(\\ce{\\upbeta\\mbox{-}pleated sheets}\\). Members include immunoglobulins \\(A\\), \\(E\\), \\(G\\), \\(M\\) (IgA, IgE, IgG, and IgM), T-cell receptors (TCRs), and human leukocyte antigen (HLA) major histocompatibility complex (MHC) molecules.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13295 goldbook:13286)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13295 goldbook:13288)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13295 goldbook:13292)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13295 goldbook:13293)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13295 goldbook:13714)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13295 goldbook:13230)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13295 goldbook:13434)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13295 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13295 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13296))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13296 "immunohistochemistry")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13296 "Detection of cell-associated molecules in the light microscope with antibodies labeled with enzymes that change a substrate into a colored precipitate.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13296 "immunocytochemistry")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13296 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13296 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13297))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13297 "immunological ignorance")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13297 "Absence of a pathogenic autoimmune response in spite of the concomitant presence in the host of the autoantigen and T cells bearing the specific autoreactive T-cell receptor (TCR).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13297 goldbook:13724)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13297 goldbook:13714)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13297 goldbook:12914)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13297 goldbook:12918)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13297 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13297 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13298))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13298 "immunological incompetence")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13298 "Inability of the immune system to function in a normal fashion.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13298 goldbook:13271)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13298 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13298 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13299))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13299 "immunologically privileged site")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13299 "Any of various sites in the body where foreign tissue grafts do not induce an immune reaction.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13299 "privileged site")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13299 "Such sites include the eye, brain, testis, and unborn fetus. Although antigens do migrate from these privileged sites, they either induce immunological tolerance or a nondestructive response."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13299 goldbook:13302)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13299 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13299 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13300))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13300 "immunological memory")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13300 "Ability of the immune system to respond faster and more effectively to subsequent exposures to an antigen following a primary immune response to the same antigen.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13300 "immunological anamnesis")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13300 "Typically, memory T cells appear five days following initial immunization, whereas memory B cells may take about a month to reach maximum levels. Populations of such cells may persist for the lifetime of the individual."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13300 goldbook:13271)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13300 goldbook:13451)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13300 goldbook:13452)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13300 goldbook:13601)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13300 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13300 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13301))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13301 "immunological synapse")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13301 "Contact point between the T cell and antigen-presenting cell (APC) that is generated by reorganization and clustering of cell surface molecules in lipid rafts. The synapse facilitates interactions between T-cell receptor (TCR) and major histocompatibility complex (MHC) molecules, and between adhesion molecules, thereby potentiating a TCR-mediated activation signal.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13301 goldbook:13724)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13301 goldbook:13714)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13301 goldbook:12848)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13301 goldbook:12888)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13301 goldbook:13390)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13301 goldbook:13434)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13301 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13301 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13302))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13302 "immunological tolerance")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13302 "Persistent specific immunological unresponsiveness toward a substance that would normally be expected to elicit an immune response, resulting from previous non-sensitizing exposure to an antigen.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13302 "tolerance")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13302 "Tolerance to specific foreign antigens can be induced by the exposure to the foreign antigens during embryonic or neonatal life (depending upon species). In adults, tolerance (usually of shorter duration) can be induced by using particular routes of administration for the antigens or administration of agents that are particularly effective against cells proliferating in response to antigen. Mechanisms may include deletion of potentially reactive lymphocytes or their \"inactivation\" by immunological suppression."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13302 goldbook:13399)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13302 goldbook:13701)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13302 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13302 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13303))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13303 "immunology")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13303 "Science that deals with the immune system including cell-mediated immunity (CMI) and humoral aspects of immunity and immune responses.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13303 goldbook:12995)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13303 goldbook:13234)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13303 goldbook:13271)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13303 goldbook:13272)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13303 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13303 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13304))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13304 "immunomagnetic separation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13304 "Method of separating specific cell types or macromolecules with the aid of cell-specific antibodies coupled to paramagnetic beads.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13304 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13304 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13305))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13305 "immunomodulation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13305 "Modification of the functioning of the immune system by the action of a substance that increases or reduces the ability to produce an immune response.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13305 goldbook:13271)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13305 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13305 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13306))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13306 "immunopathology")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13306 "1) Study of diseases of the immune system. 2) The occurrence of such diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13306 goldbook:13271)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13306 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13306 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13307))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13307 "immunopathy")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13307 "Disease of the immune system.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13307 goldbook:13271)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13307 goldbook:13306)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13307 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13307 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13308))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13308 "immunopharmacology")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13308 "1) Study of the immune system using drugs as diagnostic tools. 2) Use of pharmaceutical molecules to support and stimulate the immune system in patients with immunodeficiency, or to suppress or specifically influence the reactivity of the immune system in order to control a pathological immune reaction or disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13308 goldbook:13271)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13308 goldbook:13281)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13308 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13308 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13309))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13309 "immunophenotyping")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13309 "Use of a panel of antibodies to determine a subset of proteins expressed on the surface of a cell or heterogeneous group of cells, often for diagnostic purposes, e.g., identifying the presence of leukemia cells in a population of lymphocytes.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13309 goldbook:13378)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13309 goldbook:13399)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13309 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13309 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13310))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13310 "immunophilin")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13310 "Any of a group of cytoplasmic proteins in T cells that are targets of the immunosuppressant drugs cyclosporin A, tacrolimus (fujimycin), rapamycin, and related compounds.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13310 goldbook:13724)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13310 goldbook:13319)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13310 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13310 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13311))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13311 "immunopotentiation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13311 "Enhancement of the capacity of the immune system to produce an effective response.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13311 goldbook:13271)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13311 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13311 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13312))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13312 "immunoprecipitate")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13312 "Precipitate formed in an antigen–antibody reaction.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13312 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13312 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13313))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13313 "immunoreceptor tyrosine-based activation motif")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13313 "Consensus sequence for src-family tyrosine kinases, found in the cytoplasmic domains of several signaling molecules including the signal transduction units of lymphocyte antigen receptors and of Fc receptors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13313 "ITAM")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13313 goldbook:13138)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13313 goldbook:12891)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13313 goldbook:13399)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13313 goldbook:13766)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13313 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13313 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13314))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13314 "immunoreceptor tyrosine-based inhibitory motif")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13314 "Consensus sequence present in the cytoplasmic domains of certain cell surface molecules [e.g., Fc \\(\\upgamma\\) RIIB, inhibitory natural killer (NK) cell receptors] and which mediates inhibitory signals.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13314 "ITIM")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13314 goldbook:13499)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13314 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13314 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13315))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13315 "immunosensitivity")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13315 "Reactivity to antigens.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13315 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13315 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13316))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13316 "immunosensitizer")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13316 "Substance that makes the immune system more reactive to antigens.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13316 goldbook:13271)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13316 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13316 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13317))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13317 "immunostimulating complex")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13317 "Immunological adjuvant composed of saponin, cholesterol, phospholipid, and an immunogen, usually protein.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13317 "ISCOM")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13317 "The adjuvant was originally designed to form a vaccine delivery system that combined certain aspects of virus particles such as their size and orientation of surface proteins, with the powerful immunostimulatory activity of saponins."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13317 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13317 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13318))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13318 "immunostimulation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13318 "Increase in immune function, e.g., by use of bacille Calmette–Guérin (BCG) vaccine or drugs.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13318 "Immunostimulation may be beneficial (e.g., restoration of a depressed immune response) or detrimental (e.g., induction by drugs of allergy, hypersensitivity, or autoimmunity)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13318 goldbook:12859)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13318 goldbook:12925)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13318 goldbook:12940)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13318 goldbook:13241)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13318 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13318 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13319))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13319 "immunosuppressant")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13319 "Substance that depresses the function of the immune system.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13319 goldbook:13271)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13319 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13319 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13320))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13320 "immunosuppressive")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13320 "Causing depression of the normal function of the immune system.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13320 goldbook:13271)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13320 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13320 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13321))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13321 "immunosurveillance")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13321 "Mechanisms by which the immune system is able to recognize and destroy malignant cells before the formation of an overt tumor.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13321 goldbook:13271)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13321 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13321 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13322))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13322 "immunotherapy")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13322 "Treatment or prevention of a disease using agents that can modify the immune response.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13322 "Immunotherapy is largely an experimental approach, applied most widely in the treatment of leukemias, melanoma, and hypernephroma."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13322 "Immunotherapy may involve active or passive immunization, immunopotentiation or immunosuppression, hyposensitization, bone marrow transplantation, or thymus implantation."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13322 goldbook:12835)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13322 goldbook:12960)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13322 goldbook:13247)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13322 goldbook:13311)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13322 goldbook:13378)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13322 goldbook:13540)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13322 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13322 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13323))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13323 "immunotoxic")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13323 "Harmful to the immune system.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13323 goldbook:13271)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13323 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13323 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13324))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13324 "immunotoxicant")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13324 "Substance that is harmful to the immune system.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13324 goldbook:13271)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13324 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13324 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13325))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13325 "immunotoxicology")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13325 "Discipline applying cardinal principals of both immunology and toxicology to study the ability of certain substances to alter the immune response.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13325 goldbook:13303)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13325 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13325 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13326))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13326 "immunotoxin")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13326 "Biochemical conjugate, or recombinant fusion protein, consisting of an immune targeting molecule such as an antibody or antibody fragment together with a cytotoxic molecule.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13326 goldbook:13071)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13326 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13326 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13327))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13327 "inactivated vaccine")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13327 "Vaccine formulated from the whole microorganism that has been rendered unable to reproduce or cause disease, often by mutation or heat denaturation.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13327 goldbook:12911)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13327 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13327 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13328))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13328 "indirect immunofluorescence")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13328 "Method of visualizing an antigen in which an unlabeled antibody against the antigen is reacted with it first, and then is detected by staining with a second fluorescently tagged immunoglobulin G (IgG) directed against the first antibody.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13328 goldbook:13292)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13328 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13328 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13329))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13329 "indolamine-2,3-dioxygenase")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13329 "Enzyme catalyzing the initial rate-limiting step of tryptophan degradation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13329 "IDO")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13329 "Tryptophan is required for T-cell proliferation. Local degradation of tryptophan thus modulates T-cell activity."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13329 goldbook:13724)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13329 goldbook:13756)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13329 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13329 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13330))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13330 "inducible co-stimulatory protein")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13330 "Highly specific receptor for the protein B7H/B7RP-1 that is expressed on the surface of B cells and macrophages, and also appears on the surface of T cells during the process of T-cell activation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13330 "ICOS")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13330 "Stimulation of the B cell and subsequent antibody production takes place after the ICOS receptor attaches to its partner B7RP-1 molecule. Thus, the co-stimulatory molecules, ICOS and B7H/B7RP-1, provide specificity for the immune system activation process."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13330 goldbook:12937)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13330 goldbook:13724)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13330 goldbook:13401)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13330 goldbook:13271)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13330 goldbook:13424)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13330 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13330 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13331))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13331 "infectious tolerance")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13331 "Continuing state of tolerance that can be transferred by T lymphocytes from a tolerant animal.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13331 "Maintenance of transplantation tolerance involves the induction of antigen-specific CD4+ regulatory T cells (Treg)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13331 goldbook:12974)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13331 goldbook:13724)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13331 goldbook:13644)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13331 goldbook:13302)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13331 goldbook:13754)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13331 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13331 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13332))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13332 "autoimmune infertility")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13332 "Infertility caused by sperm antibodies, autoimmune ovarian inflammation (oophoritis), or autoimmune orchitis.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13332 "autoimmune infertility")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13332 "This disease may be part of a polyendocrinopathy."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13332 goldbook:12918)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13332 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13332 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13333))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13333 "inflammasome")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13333 "High-molecular-weight complex that activates inflammatory caspases and the cytokines interleukin-1$\\ce{\\upbeta\\!}$ ($\\ce{IL\\mbox{-}1\\upbeta\\!}$) and IL-18.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13333 "There appear to be at least three types of inflammasomes. Those identified initially were the NALP1 inflammasome, the NALP3 (cryopyrin) inflammasome, and the interleukin-(IL-)1β converting enzyme (ICE) protease-activating factor (IPAF) inflammasome."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13333 goldbook:12990)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13333 goldbook:13492)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13333 goldbook:13065)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13333 goldbook:13338)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13333 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13333 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13334))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13334 "inflammatory bowel disease")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13334 "Group of chronic inflammatory conditions resulting in the inappropriate and persistent activation of the mucosal immune system of the bowel.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13334 "IBD")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13334 "Idiopathic IBD is a set of chronic conditions probably driven by the presence of normal intestinal flora."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13334 "Autoantibodies against proteins of neutrophil granulocytes, pancreatic acinus, intestinal goblet, and colonic epithelial cells are detectable."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13334 "Crohn disease and ulcerative colitis are two variants of IBD with overlapping clinical manifestations and probable autoimmune origins. Crohn disease is immunologically characterized by antibody to Saccharomyces cerevisiae and Th1 cell-dominated responses."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13334 goldbook:12913)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13334 goldbook:13053)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13334 goldbook:13249)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13334 goldbook:13718)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13334 goldbook:12918)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13334 goldbook:13271)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13334 goldbook:13473)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13334 goldbook:13510)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13334 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13334 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13335))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13335 "innate immunity")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13335 "Immunity that is not intrinsically affected by prior contact with antigen, i.e., all aspects of immunity not directly mediated by lymphocytes.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13335 goldbook:13272)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13335 goldbook:13399)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13335 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13335 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13336))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13336 "intercellular adhesion molecule")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13336 "Member of the immunoglobulin superfamily that interacts with integrins and is found on the surface of several cell types, including antigen-presenting cells (APCs) and T cells.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13336 "ICAM")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13336 goldbook:13724)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13336 goldbook:12888)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13336 goldbook:13295)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13336 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13336 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13337))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13337 "interclonal competition")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13337 "Process which favors survival of foreign-specific lymphocytes at the expense of self-specific lymphocytes and is a secondary mechanism involved in the induction and maintenance of self-tolerance.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13337 goldbook:13399)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13337 goldbook:13669)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13337 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13337 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13338))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13338 "interleukin")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13338 "Member of a group of immunoregulatory glycoproteins, also called lymphokines, monokines, or cytokines.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13338 "IL")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13338 "General features are low molecular mass (about \\(\\pu{80 kDa}\\)) and frequent glycosylation; regulation of immune cell function and inflammation by binding to specific cell surface receptors; transient and local production; action in paracrine, autocrine, or endocrine manner, with stimulatory or blocking effect on growth/differentiation; very potent, function at picomolar concentrations."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13338 "Interleukins represent an extensive series of mediators with a wide range of overlapping functions. Other mediators in this series are c-kit ligand, interferons (IFNs), tumor necrosis factor (TNF), transforming growth factor β (TGF-β), and a family of low relative molecular mass mediators, called chemokines."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13338 goldbook:12916)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13338 goldbook:13065)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13338 goldbook:13415)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13338 goldbook:13468)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13338 goldbook:13752)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13338 goldbook:13762)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13338 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13338 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13339))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13339 "internal image")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13339 "Epitope on an anti-idiotype that binds in a way that structurally and functionally mimics the antigen.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13339 goldbook:13252)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13339 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13339 "current"^^xsd:string)
