AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13591 "It is the predominating leukocyte in the blood and is found in the tissues during acute inflammatory processes and in the superficial surface aspects of a lesion during subacute or chronic inflammation."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13591 "There are three major types: neutrophils, eosinophils, and basophils."^^xsd:string)
