AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13710 "systemic lupus erythematosus")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13710 "Chronic autoimmune disease that is potentially debilitating and sometimes fatal as the immune system attacks the body’s cells and tissues, with inflammation and tissue damage.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13710 "SLE")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13710 "lupus")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13710 "lupus erythematosus")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13710 "SLE can affect any part of the body, but most often harms the heart, joints, skin, lungs, blood vessels, liver, kidneys, and nervous system. The course of the disease is unpredictable, with periods of illness (called flares) alternating with remission. SLE can occur at any age, and is most common in women, particularly of non-European descent."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13710 "The disease is very heterogeneous in clinical expression and serological factors. Autoantibodies directed against nuclear components [antinuclear antibodies (ANA)] are typically detected. Anti-dsDNA, anti-Sm, and antiphospholipid antibodies are used as classification criteria."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13710 goldbook:12913)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13710 goldbook:12898)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13710 goldbook:12919)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13710 goldbook:13271)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13710 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13710 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13711))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13711 "systemic sclerosis")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13711 "Fibrosing disease of unclear etiology that affects multiple organ systems.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13711 "SSc")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13711 "The skin (\"scleroderma\") and blood vessels (arteries, small vessels) are most commonly affected, but involvement of the lungs and gastrointestinal tract (esophagus) may also be observed."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13711 "Anticentromere antibodies (ACA) as well as autoantibodies against DNA topoisomerase I (scl-70) and various nucleolar antigens are diagnostic and prognostic markers and are often detectable years before disease manifestation. They are also detectable in quartz dust-exposed individuals."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13711 goldbook:12913)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13711 goldbook:13660)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13711 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13711 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13712))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13712 "drug-specific T cell")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13712 "T-memory cell that is specific for a drug allergen.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13712 "drug-specific T cell")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13712 goldbook:12857)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13712 goldbook:13452)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13712 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13712 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13713))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13713 "T-cell-dependent antibody response")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13713 "Immunotoxicity test that evaluates the ability of animals to produce antibodies to a T-dependent antigen [e.g., sheep red blood cells (SRBCs) or keyhole limpet hemocyanin (KLH)].")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13713 "TDAR")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13713 goldbook:13323)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13713 goldbook:13715)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13713 goldbook:13675)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13713 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13713 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13714))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13714 "T-cell receptor")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13714 "Antigen-specific receptor on T cells composed of one set of heterodimeric chains. Two types of TCR heterodimers are known (\\(\\upalpha/\\upbeta\\) and \\(\\upgamma/\\updelta\\)).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13714 "TCR")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13714 "Functional binding for TCR requires a complex of major histocompatibility complex (MHC) molecule, antigenic peptide, and TCR."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13714 goldbook:13724)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13714 goldbook:12885)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13714 goldbook:13434)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13714 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13714 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13715))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13715 "T-dependent antigen")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13715 "Antigen that requires helper T lymphocytes (Th) in order to elicit an antibody response.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13715 goldbook:13199)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13715 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13715 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13716))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13716 "TdT-dependent dUTP-biotin nick end labeling assay")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13716 "Method for detecting apoptotic cells in situ based on characteristic DNA fragmentation. It is based on the ability of terminal deoxynucleotidyl transferase (TdT) to transfer a labeled deoxyuridine triphosphate to the terminal ends arising from DNA cleavage.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003012) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13716 "TUNEL")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13716 "TUNEL assay")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13716 goldbook:13728)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13716 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13716 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13717))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13717 "Th0 cell")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13717 "Helper T lymphocyte (Th) with a less restricted cytokine profile than Th1 and Th2 cells.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13717 "Th0-like responses are observed in patients with rheumatoid arthritis (RA), Sjögren syndrome, and Graves disease."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13717 goldbook:13187)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13717 goldbook:13199)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13717 goldbook:13680)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13717 goldbook:13718)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13717 goldbook:13719)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13717 goldbook:13065)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13717 goldbook:13651)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13717 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13717 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13718))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13718 "Th1 cell")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13718 "Helper T lymphocyte (Th) producing mainly interleukin-2 (IL-2), interferon (IFN-$\\ce{\\upgamma\\!}$), and tumor necrosis factor $\\ce{\\upbeta\\!}$ ($\\ce{TNF\\mbox{-}\\upbeta\\!}$), and thereby responsible for phagocyte-dependent host responses.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13718 "Th1-dominated responses are seen in autoimmune diseases in which cytotoxic T cells and macrophages play a major role, e.g., multiple sclerosis, diabetes mellitus type 1, Hashimoto thyroiditis, and Crohn disease. Switching from Th1 to Th2 response can prevent Th1-mediated tissue destruction in animal models."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13718 goldbook:13053)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13718 goldbook:13195)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13718 goldbook:13199)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13718 goldbook:13719)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13718 goldbook:12919)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13718 goldbook:13072)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13718 goldbook:13092)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13718 goldbook:13336)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13718 goldbook:13338)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13718 goldbook:13424)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13718 goldbook:13560)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13718 goldbook:13421)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13718 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13718 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13719))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13719 "Th2 cell")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13719 "Helper T lymphocyte (Th) in mice producing interleukins IL-4, IL-5, IL-6, IL-9, IL-10, and IL-13.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13719 "Besides other effects, they provide optimal help for antibody responses. Th2 responses should also be regarded as an important downregulatory mechanism for exaggerated Th1 responses. Predominant Th2 cytokine profile is observed in patients with atopic disorders and graft-versus-host disease (GVHD)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13719 goldbook:13199)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13719 goldbook:13718)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13719 goldbook:12910)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13719 goldbook:13065)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13719 goldbook:13180)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13719 goldbook:13338)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13719 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13719 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13720))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13720 "Th3 cell")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13720 "Helper T lymphocyte (Th) producing and responding to transforming growth factor $\\ce{\\upbeta\\!}$ ($\\ce{TGF\\mbox{-}\\upbeta\\!}$) and helping immunoglobulin A (IgA) antibody responses.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13720 goldbook:13199)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13720 goldbook:13286)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13720 goldbook:13752)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13720 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13720 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13721))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13721 "Th9 cell")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13721 "Helper T lymphocyte (Th) producing interleukin IL-9, which stimulates mast cells.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13721 goldbook:13199)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13721 goldbook:13338)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13721 goldbook:13442)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13721 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13721 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13722))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13722 "Th17 cell")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13722 "Helper T lymphocyte (Th), distinct from Th1 and Th2 cells, that secretes the interleukin IL-17.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13722 "T17")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13722 "T17 lymphocytes are thought to play an important role in autoimmune disease."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13722 goldbook:13199)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13722 goldbook:13718)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13722 goldbook:13719)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13722 goldbook:12919)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13722 goldbook:13338)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13722 goldbook:13399)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13722 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13722 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13723))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13723 "T-independent antigen")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13723 "Antigen that is able to elicit an antibody response in the absence of T cells.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13723 goldbook:13724)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13723 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13723 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13724))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13724 "T lymphocyte")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13724 "Lymphocyte that matures in the thymus and has the ability to recognize specific peptide antigens through the receptors on its cell surface.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:13724 "T cell")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13724 "T-cell receptor (TCR) molecules are specific for complexes comprising short peptides bound to and presented by major histocompatibility complex (MHC) molecules."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13724 goldbook:13399)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13724 goldbook:13714)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13724 goldbook:13434)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:13724 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-11-06-03)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:13724 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:13725))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:13725 "Tr1 cell")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:13725 "T lymphocyte that regulates Th1 cell responses. It resembles the regulatory T cell (Treg) and is possibly related to the Th3 cell.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:13725 "It is abundant in the intestine and may be involved in tolerance to dietary antigens."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13725 goldbook:13724)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13725 goldbook:13718)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:13725 goldbook:13720)
