AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14927 "point source")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14927 "Single emission source in a defined location.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14927 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14927 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14928))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14928 "pollutant")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14928 "Any undesirable solid, liquid, or gaseous matter occurring, as a result of human activities, in a solid, liquid, or gaseous environmental medium and causing adverse effects.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:14928 "\"Undesirability\", like toxicity, is concentration-dependent, low concentrations of most substances being tolerable or even essential in many cases."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:14928 "A primary pollutant is one emitted into the atmosphere, water, sediments, or soil from an identifiable source."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:14928 "A secondary pollutant is a pollutant formed by chemical reaction in the atmosphere, water, sediments, or soil."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:14928 "Pollutant should be distinguished from contaminant; the latter implies presence above background due to human activities; the former implies that the substance also is causing adverse effects."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:14928 goldbook:14549)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:14928 goldbook:15036)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14928 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14928 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14929))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14929 "pollution-induced community tolerance")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14929 "Increase in tolerance to pollution resulting from species composition shifts in the community, acclimatization of individuals, and genetic changes in populations in the community.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:14929 "PICT")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:14929 goldbook:14418)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:14929 goldbook:14531)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:14929 goldbook:14932)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14929 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14929 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14930))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14930 "pollution tolerance index")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14930 "Means of measuring environmental quality, usually water quality, by determining the presence of indicator species, classified into three groups—sensitive, facultative, and tolerant. Each group is assigned an index value 1, 2, and 3, with the sensitive group having the highest index value. The number of species present from the list included in each group is identified in a representative environmental sample and the group index multiplied by the number of species in the group. The scores for each group are finally added to give the PTI for the environmental medium under consideration. The environmental quality is directly proportional to the value of the index.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:14930 "PTI")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14930 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14930 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14931))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14931 "polygenic control")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14931 "Control of a phenotypic trait by several genes.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14931 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14931 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14932))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14932 "population")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14932 "In ecology, any group of interacting and interbreeding organisms of the same species occupying a given area at the same time.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14932 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14932 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14933))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14933 "population biomass")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14933 "Total mass or weight of organisms in a population, given by the sum of the masses (or weights) of all the individual members of the population.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:14933 goldbook:14932)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14933 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14933 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14934))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14934 "population cycle")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14934 "Changes in the numbers of individuals in a population that repeatedly oscillate between periods of high and low density.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:14934 goldbook:14932)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14934 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14934 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14935))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14935 "population density")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14935 "Number of individuals divided by area (\\(\\pu{m-2}\\)) or volume (\\(\\pu{m-3}\\)).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:14935 "PD")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14935 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14935 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14936))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14936 "population dynamics")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14936 "Variations in time and space in the sizes and densities of populations.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:14936 goldbook:14932)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14936 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14936 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14937))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14937 "population ecology")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14937 "Study of the variations in time and space in the sizes and densities of populations, and of the factors causing these variations.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:14937 goldbook:14932)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14937 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14937 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14938))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14938 "population fluctuation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14938 "Variations over time in the size of a population.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:14938 goldbook:14932)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14938 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14938 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14939))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14939 "population growth rate")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14939 "Change in population size \\(\\Delta N\\) during a specified time period \\(\\Delta t\\) \\[\\Delta N/\\Delta t = (b - d)N\\] where \\(N\\) is population size, \\(b\\) is per capita birth rate, and \\(d\\) is per capita death rate.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:14939 goldbook:14904)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:14939 goldbook:14905)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:14939 goldbook:14906)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:14939 goldbook:14932)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14939 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14939 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14940))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14940 "population pyramid")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14940 "Diagrammatic illustration of the age structure of a population by depicting the youngest age class at the base and stacking successive age classes above it.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:14940 goldbook:14932)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14940 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14940 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14941))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14941 "population size")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14941 "Total number of organisms in a population.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:14941 goldbook:14932)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14941 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14941 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14942))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14942 "porous pot test")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14942 "Biodegradation test that simulates the continuous activated sludge (sewage treatment) system.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14942 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14942 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14943))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14943 "precautionary principle")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14943 "Approach to risk management that can be applied in circumstances of scientific uncertainty, reflecting a perceived need to take action in the face of a potentially serious risk without waiting for definitive results of scientific research.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14943 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14943 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14944))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14944 "predicted environmental concentration")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14944 "Concentration of a substance likely to be found in an environmental compartment calculated from estimates of quantities released, discharge patterns, and inherent disposition of the substance (fate and distribution) as well as the nature of the specific receiving ecosystems.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:14944 "PEC")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:14944 "estimated environmental concentration (EEC)")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:14944 "expected environmental concentration (EEC)")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:14944 "EEC models for pesticides assume a maximum number of applications per growing season at the maximum rate of application according to the application methods stated on the product label."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:14944 goldbook:14537)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:14944 goldbook:14619)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14944 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14944 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14945))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14945 "predicted no-effect concentration")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14945 "Concentration that is expected to cause no adverse effect to any naturally occurring population in an environment at risk from exposure to a given substance.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:14945 "PNEC")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:14945 goldbook:14932)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14945 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14945 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14946))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14946 "predictive risk assessment")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14946 "Risk assessment performed for a proposed future action, such as the use of a new chemical or the release of a new effluent.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:14946 "prospective risk assessment")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14946 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14946 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14947))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14947 "prevalence")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14947 "Number of instances of existing cases of a given disease or other condition in a given population at a designated time; sometimes used to mean prevalence rate.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:14947 "When used without qualification, refers usually to the situation at a specified time (point prevalence)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:14947 goldbook:14932)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:14947 goldbook:14948)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14947 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14947 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14948))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14948 "prevalence rate")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14948 "Total number of individuals who have an attribute or disease at a particular time (or during a particular period) divided by the population at risk of having the attribute or disease at this point in time or midway through the period.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:14948 "prevalence ratio")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:14948 goldbook:14932)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14948 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14948 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14949))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14949 "primary lamellae")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14949 "Gill structures extending outward at right angles from the branchial arches.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:14949 "filaments")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14949 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14949 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14950))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14950 "primary producer")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14950 "Organism capable of using the energy derived from light or a chemical substance in order to manufacture energy-rich organic compounds.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14950 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14950 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14951))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14951 "primary succession")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14951 "Sequential colonization by species which begin to colonize the bare ground and modify the environmental conditions after a region is completely denuded; e.g., behind a retreating glacier, early colonizing organisms provide the soils needed by succeeding organisms.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:14951 goldbook:15036)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:14951 goldbook:15077)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14951 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14951 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14952))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14952 "principle of allocation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14952 "Concept that there exists a cost or trade-off to every allocation of energy resources. Energy spent by an individual organism on one function, process, or structure cannot be spent on another. Optimal allocation of resources enhances Darwinian fitness.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:14952 "concept of strategy")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14952 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14952 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14953))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14953 "probit")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14953 "Probability unit obtained by adding 5 to the normal deviates of a standardized normal distribution of results from a dose-response study.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:14953 "Addition of 5 removes the complication of handling negative values."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:14953 "A plot of probit against the logarithm of dose or concentration gives a linear plot if the response follows a logarithmic normal distribution. Estimates of the \\(\\pu{LD_{50}}\\) and \\(\\pu{ED_{50}}\\)) (or \\(\\pu{LC_{50}}\\) and \\(\\pu{EC_{50}}\\)) can be obtained from this plot."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:14953 goldbook:14954)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14953 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14953 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14954))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14954 "probit log transform")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14954 "Probability unit obtained from the standardized normal distribution plotted against the logarithm of the concentration or dose of a substance when a quantal or graded response has been measured. A linear plot provides evidence that the distribution is log-normal. Estimates of the \\(\\pu{L(E)C_{50}}\\) and \\(\\pu{L(E)D_{50}}\\), as well as the standard deviation for the distribution, can then be made.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:14954 goldbook:14722)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:14954 goldbook:14965)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14954 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14954 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14955))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14955 "problem formulation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14955 "Planning and scoping phase that establishes the framework around which the risk assessment is done.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14955 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14955 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14956))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14956 "product-limit method")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14956 "Nonparametric method for analyzing time-to-death or survival-time data that does not require a specific model for the survival curve.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:14956 "Kaplan–Meier method")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14956 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14956 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14957))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14957 "proliferation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14957 "Multiplication, i.e., an increase by frequent and repeated reproduction or growth by cell division.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14957 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14957 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14958))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14958 "propagule")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14958 "Portion of a plant, fungus, etc., that is capable, when detached, of giving rise to a new individual by asexual reproduction (e.g., a cutting, leaf bud, bulbil, seed, or spore). Less commonly, any of the products of asexual reproduction in certain invertebrates.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14958 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14958 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14959))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14959 "propagule rain")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14959 "Relative to metapopulation dynamics, the presence of a seed bank or dormant stage for a species that continually introduces individuals to the patch regardless of the density of occupancy in the surrounding patches. This propagule rain increases the likelihood of population reappearance and decreases the likelihood of patch extinction.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:14959 goldbook:14850)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:14959 goldbook:14932)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14959 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14959 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14960))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14960 "Ptolemaic incongruity")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14960 "False assertion that any particular level of biological organization holds a more central or important role than any other in the science of ecotoxicology.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14960 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14960 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14961))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14961 "pyrogenic")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14961 "Describing anything that causes fire. Describing products of fire; e.g., organic compounds produced by the high-temperature combustion of complex organic substances are pyrogenic compounds.Examples: Polycyclic aromatic hydrocarbons (PAHs) are examples of pyrogenic compounds. Describing a substance that produces fever.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14961 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14961 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14962))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14962 "quality criteria")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14962 "Quality guidelines based on the evaluation of scientific data.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:14962 goldbook:14963)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14962 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14962 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14963))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14963 "quality guidelines")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14963 "Numerical limits or text statements established to support and maintain designated uses of the environment or to protect human health.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14963 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14963 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14964))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14964 "quality standards")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14964 "Fixed upper limits for exposure to certain chemicals recognized under law by one or more levels of government. Well-known examples include the air, water, and soil quality standards, as well as threshold limit values for air pollutants in the workplace.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:14964 goldbook:14928)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:14964 goldbook:15036)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14964 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14964 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14965))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14965 "quantal effect")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14965 "Condition that can be expressed only as 'occurring' or 'not occurring', such as death or occurrence of a tumor.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:14965 "all-or-none effect")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:14965 goldbook:14722)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14965 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14965 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14966))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14966 "quantitative structure–metabolism relationship")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14966 "Quantitative association between the physicochemical and (or) the structural properties of a substance and its metabolic behavior.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:14966 "QSMR")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14966 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14966 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14967))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14967 "quotient method")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14967 "Calculation of the quotient of the measured or predicted environmental concentration (PEC) of a contaminant and the predicted no-effect level (PNEC), used as an expression of hazard or risk. Higher quotients constitute greater evidence of a hazard or a greater risk.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:14967 goldbook:14549)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:14967 goldbook:14737)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:14967 goldbook:14944)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:14967 goldbook:14945)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14967 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14967 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14968))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14968 "rain-out")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14968 "Removal of pollutants from air by incorporation into developing rain droplets of rain clouds.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:14968 goldbook:14928)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14968 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14968 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14969))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14969 "rarefaction estimate of richness")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14969 "Estimate of species richness (\\(S\\)) expressed relative to that of a sample having a standard number of individuals.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:14969 goldbook:15051)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14969 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14969 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14970))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14970 "rate constant-based model")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14970 "Compartment model that employs rate constants to quantify the rate of change in concentration or amount of toxicant.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:14970 goldbook:14537)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14970 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14970 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14971))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14971 "rate-of-living theory of aging")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14971 "Theory that the total metabolic expenditure of a genotype is generally fixed, and longevity depends on the rate of energy expenditure.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14971 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14971 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14972))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14972 "rate ratio")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14972 "Value obtained by dividing the rate in an exposed population by the rate in an unexposed population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:14972 "RR")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:14972 goldbook:14932)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14972 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14972 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14973))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14973 "realised niche")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14973 "Portion of a species’ fundamental niche that it actually occupies.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:14973 "The realized niche is narrower than the fundamental niche due to pressure from, and interactions with, other organisms (e.g., superior competitors)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:14973 goldbook:14747)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:14973 goldbook:14877)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14973 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14973 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14974))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14974 "reasonable worst case")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14974 "Semiquantitative term referring to the lower portion of the high end of the exposure, dose, or risk distribution.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14974 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14974 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14975))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14975 "reasonable maximum exposure")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14975 "Highest exposure that is reasonably expected to occur.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:14975 "RME")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:14975 "Typically, the \\(\\pu{95\\%}\\) upper confidence limit of the toxicant distribution is used: if only a few data points (\\(\\pu{6\\!{-}\\! 10}\\)) are available, the maximum detected concentration is used."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14975 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14975 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14976))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14976 "receiving water")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14976 "Surface water (e.g., in a stream, river, or lake) that has received, or is about to receive, a discharged waste (i.e., the surface water immediately around the discharge point).")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14976 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14976 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14977))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14977 "recommended limit")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14977 "Maximum concentration of a potentially toxic substance that is expected to be safe.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:14977 "Such limits are rarely defined as legal limits to be enforced. They are analogous to guidelines, which have only advisory status."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14977 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14977 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14978))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14978 "reconstituted water")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14978 "De-ionized or glass-distilled water to which reagent-grade chemicals have been added. The resultant synthetic freshwater is expected to be free from contaminants and have the desired \\(\\rm{pH}\\) and hardness characteristics.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:14978 goldbook:14549)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14978 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14978 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14979))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14979 "redundancy hypothesis")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14979 "Hypothesis that many species are redundant, and their loss will not influence the community function as long as crucial (e.g., keystone and dominant) species populations are maintained.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:14979 goldbook:14531)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:14979 goldbook:14932)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14979 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14979 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14980))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14980 "reference environment")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14980 "Generalized description of the environment into which contaminants will be released and in which organisms will be exposed. Reference environments are used when there is no specific site at risk.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:14980 goldbook:14549)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14980 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14980 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14981))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14981 "reference sediment")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14981 "Whole sediment near an area of concern used to assess sediment conditions in the absence of substances of concern.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:14981 "Such sediment is collected near a site of concern and should represent the background conditions."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14981 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14981 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14982))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14982 "reference site")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14982 "Relatively unpolluted site used for comparison with polluted sites in environmental monitoring studies, often incorrectly referred to as a control site.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14982 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14982 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14983))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14983 "reference toxicant")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14983 "Chemical used in an aquatic toxicity test as a positive control in contrast to the negative control provided by exposure water without the test chemical. Information collected is used to determine the general health and viability of the test organisms and assess consistency in testing protocol implementation.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:14983 "In this definition, the term \"positive control\" is used to describe a procedure that is very similar to the actual experimental test and that is known from previous experience to give a positive result."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14983 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14983 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14984))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14984 "reference toxicity test")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14984 "Test conducted in conjunction with sediment tests to determine possible changes in condition of the test species.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:14984 "Deviations from an established normal range indicate a change in the condition of the test organism population. Reference toxicant tests are most often acute lethality tests performed in the absence of sediment."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:14984 "Sediment spiked with a toxicant might also be included as a positive control for the sediment toxicity test."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:14984 goldbook:14932)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14984 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14984 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14985))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14985 "region")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14985 "Area of the Earth’s surface differentiated by its specific characteristics.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14985 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14985 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14986))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14986 "relative risk")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14986 "Ratio of the risk of disease or death among the exposed to the risk among the unexposed. Ratio of the cumulative incidence rate in the exposed to the cumulative incidence rate in the unexposed.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:14986 "RR")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:14986 "risk ratio")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14986 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14986 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14987))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14987 "remedial investigation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14987 "Study that has three parts: characterization or the type and degree of the contamination, human risk assessment, and ecological risk assessment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:14987 "RI")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14987 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14987 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14988))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14988 "remedial investigation and feasibility study")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14988 "For an EPA Superfund site, a study that has as its goal the implementation of 'remedies that reduce, control, or eliminate risks to human health and the environment' or, more specifically, the accumulation of 'information sufficient to support an informed risk management decision regarding which remedy appears to be most appropriate for a given site'.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:14988 "RI/FS")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14988 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14988 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14989))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14989 "remediation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14989 "Giving a remedy. Removal of pollution or contaminants from environmental media such as soil, groundwater, sediment, or surface water for the general protection of human health and the environment.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:14989 goldbook:14549)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:14989 goldbook:15036)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14989 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14989 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14990))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14990 "remote sensing")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14990 "Technologies that allow the acquisition and analysis of data without requiring physical contact with the land or water surface being studied. Most determine qualities or characteristics of areas of interest based on measurements of visible light, infrared radiation, or radio energy coming from them.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14990 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14990 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14991))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14991 "reproductive value")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14991 "Expected contribution of offspring during the life of an individual of an age class \\(x\\) in a life table.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:14991 goldbook:14798)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14991 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14991 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14992))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14992 "rescue effect")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14992 "Increased probability of a vacated-patch reoccupation in a metapopulation as the number of nearby, occupied patches increases.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:14992 goldbook:14850)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14992 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14992 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14993))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14993 "resilience")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14993 "Ability of a community to maintain its structure and function in the face of disturbance, and to reorganize following disturbance-driven change.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:14993 goldbook:14531)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14993 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14993 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14994))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14994 "retention effect")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14994 "Observed effect of the properties of persistent organic pollutants (POPs) with high lipophilicity which causes them to be bound more firmly than less lipophilic POPs in solid phases such as soil and vegetation; consequently, they spend less time in the atmosphere and are less available for transport in that medium.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:14994 goldbook:14909)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:14994 goldbook:15036)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14994 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14994 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14995))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14995 "retrospective risk assessment")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14995 "Risk assessment dealing with an existing condition.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:14995 "retroactive risk assessment")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14995 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14995 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14996))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14996 "ring test")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14996 "Part of an external quality assurance program for assessment of an analytical method or test. A reference institute sends identical samples, which have to be analyzed or tested for specified parameters, to a number of different laboratories. The laboratory has a deadline before which to provide results. Statistical evaluation and interpretation of the results permits assessment of the reliability of the methods used and a comparison of the laboratories’ proficiency.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:14996 "round-robin test")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:14996 "For accreditation of laboratories, regular participation in ring tests is obligatory, but accreditation is not essential for participation in the tests."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14996 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14996 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14997))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14997 "riparian")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14997 "Interface between land and a flowing body of surface water.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:14997 "Plant communities along river margins are called riparian vegetation."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14997 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14997 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14998))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14998 "risk analysis")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14998 "Process for controlling situations where an organism, system, or subpopulation could be exposed to a hazard.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:14998 "The risk analysis process consists of three components: risk assessment, risk management, and risk communication."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:14998 "The term is misleading since \"analysis\" has the fundamental meaning \"resolution or breaking up of anything complex into its various simple elements, the opposite process to synthesis; the exact determination of the elements or components of anything complex (with or without their physical separation)\". The usage defined here originates with the WHO Joint Expert Committee on Food Additives and has been accepted in this context in spite of objections from terminologists."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:14998 goldbook:14932)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14998 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14998 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:14999))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:14999 "risk characterisation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:14999 "Outcome of hazard identification and risk estimation applied to a specific use of a substance or occurrence of an environmental health hazard.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:14999 "Risk characterization requires quantitative data on the exposure of organisms or people at risk in the specific situation. The end product is a quantitative statement about the proportion of organisms or people affected in a target population."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:14999 goldbook:14735)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:14999 goldbook:14932)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:14999 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:14999 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15000))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15000 "risk hypotheses")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15000 "Clear statements of postulated or predicted adverse effects of a toxicant on an assessment endpoint.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15000 goldbook:14451)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15000 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15000 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15001))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15001 "risk source")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15001 "Agent, medium, process, procedure, or site with the potential to cause an adverse effect or effects.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15001 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15001 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15002))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15002 "risk quotient")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15002 "Ratio of predicted exposure concentration (PEC) to predicted no-effect concentration (PNEC).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15002 "The higher this value is above one, the greater the risk. If the value is below one, there should be no risk as a result of the predicted exposure."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15002 goldbook:14944)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15002 goldbook:14945)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15002 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15002 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15003))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15003 "risk reduction")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15003 "Taking measures to protect humans or the environment against identified risks.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15003 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15003 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15004))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15004 "rivet popper hypothesis")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15004 "Hypothesis that each species in a community contributes to its proper functioning.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15004 "Derived from the metaphor that the species can be compared to rivets that hold an airplane together, and the loss of each rivet weakens the structure."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15004 goldbook:14531)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15004 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15004 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15005))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15005 "r-strategy")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15005 "Opportunistic strategy favoring species that establish themselves quickly, grow quickly to exploit as many resources as possible, and produce many offspring.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15005 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15005 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15006))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15006 "rules of practical causal inference")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15006 "Fox’s rules of practical causal inference that are used in ecotoxicology (environmental epidemiology) to infer causality for toxicant exposure/effect scenarios.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15006 "The rules apply the following criteria for objectively evaluating the relationship between a suspect cause and a chronic effect: (1) probability, (2) time order, (3) strength of association, (4) specificity, (5) consistency on replication, (6) predictive performance, and (7) coherence."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15006 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15006 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15007))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15007 "run-off")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15007 "Portion of the wet precipitation on the land that ultimately reaches streams and, eventually, the sea.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15007 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15007 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15008))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15008 "safe concentration")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15008 "Concentration of a substance to which prolonged exposure will cause no adverse effect.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15008 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15008 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15009))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15009 "salinity")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15009 "Mass of dissolved salts in seawater, brackish water, brine, or other saline solution divided by the mass of the solution.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15009 "In practice, this quantity cannot be measured directly in seawater or other natural waters because of the difficulty of drying the salts from these waters. Salinity is usually calculated from another property (e.g., chlorinity, electrical conductivity) whose relationship to salinity is well known."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15009 "In oceanography, where precise and reproducible determination of seawater density is of interest, practical salinity, \\(S\\), is defined in terms of the ratio \\(k_{15}\\) of the electrical conductivity of the seawater sample at \\(\\pu{15^{\\circ}C}\\) and \\(\\pu{1 atm}\\) (\\(\\pu{1.01325 kPa}\\)) to that of a potassium chloride (\\(\\ce{KCl}\\)) solution, in which the mass fraction of \\(\\ce{KCl}\\) is \\(\\pu{32.4536E-3}\\) at the same temperature and pressure."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15009 "Before 1978, the usual unit for \\(S\\) expressed as a mass fraction was permil (no longer recommended), now usually in units \\(\\pu{g kg-1}\\) or expressed as \\(\\pu{g kg-1}\\) without the units given explicitly."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15009 goldbook:14522)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15009 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15009 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15010))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15010 "salt tolerance index")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15010 "Quotient calculated as total plant (shoot + root) dry mass at different salt concentrations compared to the total plant dry mass obtained for the controls, as indicated below: \\[S_{\\rm{T}} = m_{\\rm{d}}({\\rm{x}})/m_{\\rm{d}}({\\rm{i}})\\] where \\(m_{\\rm{d}}\\) is the total dry mass, and \\(x\\), \\(i\\) refer to a control treatment and a defined salt treatment, respectively.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15010 "STI")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15010 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15010 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15011))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15011 "saprobic")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15011 "Living in or being an environment rich in organic matter but lacking oxygen.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15011 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15011 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15012))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15012 "saprobic index")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15012 "Means of classifying the saprobic state of running waters, covering the full range from unpolluted to extremely polluted waters.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15012 goldbook:15011)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15012 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15012 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15013))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15013 "saprobic water classification")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15013 "Biological classification of water quality according to five categories: oligosaprobic: clear, with no or only slight pollution and high dissolved oxygen (DO) content; p-mesosaprobic: moderately polluted with still high DO content; x-mesosaprobic: polluted with not very high DO content; polysaprobic: strongly polluted, with negligible DO content; and antisaprobic: so polluted that no living organism is capable of living in the water.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15013 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15013 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15014))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15014 "saprobien spectrum")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15014 "Characteristic change in community composition at different distances below the discharge of putrescible organic waste to a river or stream.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15014 goldbook:14531)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15014 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15014 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15015))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15015 "satellite groups")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15015 "Organisms or groups of organisms treated in a similar fashion to those in standard toxicity tests for the purpose of special additional studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15015 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15015 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15016))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15016 "scope for growth")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15016 "Index (\\(P\\) = production) calculated as the amount of energy taken into the organism in its food (\\(A\\)) minus the energy used for respiration (\\(R\\)) and excretion (\\(U\\)): \\[P = A - R - U\\]")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15016 "It is an indicator of the amount of energy available for growth or production of offspring."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15016 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15016 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15017))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15017 "scope of activity")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15017 "Difference between the rates of oxygen consumption of an organism under maximal and minimal activity levels.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15017 "It reflects the respiratory capacity available for the diverse demands on and activities of an organism."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15017 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15017 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15018))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15018 "screening level")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15018 "Decision limit or cut-off point at which a screening test is regarded as positive.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15018 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15018 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15019))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15019 "screening test")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15019 "Test conducted to estimate the concentrations to be used for a definitive test. Acute test used early in a testing program to evaluate the potential of a substance to produce a given adverse effect (e.g., mortality).")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15019 "preliminary test")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15019 "range-finding test")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15019 goldbook:14865)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15019 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15019 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15020))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15020 "secondary lamellae")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15020 "Parallel rows of projections on the dorsal and ventral sides of each primary lamella of the fish gill. They are the primary sites of gas exchange of the gills.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15020 "respiratory lamellae")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15020 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15020 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15021))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15021 "secondary poisoning")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15021 "Poisoning of a predator as a result of eating prey that has accumulated a toxicant as a result of biomagnification through its food chain.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15021 goldbook:14484)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15021 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15021 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15022))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15022 "secondary substrate metabolism")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15022 "Microbial growth on a nutrient substrate while transforming another substrate without gaining energetic benefit.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15022 "Although it must occur, secondary substance metabolism is very difficult to demonstrate in nature, but it can be demonstrated in pure cultures."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15022 goldbook:14530)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15022 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15022 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15023))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15023 "secondary succession")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15023 "Sequential appearance of species following major changes to an established ecosystem.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15023 "Catastrophic weather events, fire, or human activities all disturb the environment. After such an event on land, well-developed soil remains, giving pioneer species an easy foothold; similar changes occur in abandoned agricultural areas."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15023 goldbook:14619)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15023 goldbook:15036)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15023 goldbook:15077)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15023 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15023 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15024))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15024 "selection components")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15024 "Components of the life cycle of an individual upon which natural selection can act. They are viability selection, sexual selection, meiotic drive, gametic selection, and fecundity selection.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15024 goldbook:14708)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15024 goldbook:14842)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15024 goldbook:15030)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15024 goldbook:15124)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15024 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15024 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15025))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15025 "Selyean stress")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15025 "Syndrome named for Hans Selye (1907–1982) that consists of all the nonspecifically induced changes within a biological system following and during environmental stress.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15025 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15025 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15026))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15026 "semelparous species")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15026 "Species that reproduces once.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15026 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15026 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15027))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15027 "semi-continuous activated sludge test")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15027 "Test for inherent biodegradability of organic substances in activated sludge by measurement of the decrease in dissolved oxygen content (DOC) in the test system.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15027 "SCAS")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15027 "SCAS test")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15027 goldbook:14596)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15027 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15027 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15028))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15028 "sentinel species")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15028 "Feral, caged, or endemic species used in measuring and indicating the level of contamination or effect during a biomonitoring exercise.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15028 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15028 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15029))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15029 "seston")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15029 "Minute living organisms and particles of nonliving matter that float in water and contribute to turbidity.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15029 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15029 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15030))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15030 "sexual selection")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15030 "Natural selection involving differential mating success of individuals.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15030 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15030 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15031))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15031 "Shannon–Wiener diversity index")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15031 "Index based on the assumption that all species are represented in the sample studied and that the sample was obtained randomly, giving the following mathematical relationship: \\[H = -\\sum \\limits_{i=1}^S p_{i} \\log p_{i}\\] where \\(p_{i}\\) is the fraction of individuals belonging to the \\(i\\)-th species and \\(S\\) is the number of species.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15031 "The Shannon index is affected by both the number of species and their equitability, or evenness. Both a greater number of species and a more even distribution increase diversity as measured by \\(H\\)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15031 "The most important source of error in this index is failure of sampling to include all species from the community of interest."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15031 goldbook:14531)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15031 goldbook:14599)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15031 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15031 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15032))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15032 "Shelford’s law of tolerance")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15032 "Species’ tolerance(s) along an environmental gradient (or series of environmental gradients) will determine its population distribution and size in the environment.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15032 goldbook:14932)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15032 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15032 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15033))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15033 "silt")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15033 "Sediment particles with a grain size between \\(\\pu{0.004 mm}\\) and \\(\\pu{0.062 mm}\\), i.e., coarser than clay particles but finer than sand.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15033 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15033 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15034))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15034 "Simpson’s diversity index")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15034 "Dominance index weighted toward the abundance of the most common species, giving the probability of any two individuals drawn at random from an infinitely large community belonging to different species. The bias corrected mathematical form of Simpson’s index is \\[D = \\sum \\limits_{i=1}^{S} p_{i}^{2}\\] where \\(p_{i}\\) is the fraction of all organisms which belong to the \\(i\\)-th species and \\(S\\) is the number of species.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15034 "Since \\(D\\) and diversity are negatively related, Simpson’s index is usually expressed as either a reciprocal or a complementary form (\\(1/D\\) or \\(1 - D\\)) so that as the index goes up, so does measure of diversity."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15034 goldbook:14531)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15034 goldbook:14599)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15034 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15034 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15035))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15035 "simulated field studies")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15035 "Experimental ecosystem that should be: physically confined; self-maintaining; multitrophic; have a duration time exceeding the generation time of the penultimate trophic level present; and of size sufficient to enable pertinent sampling and measurements to be made without seriously influencing the structure and dynamics of the system.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15035 goldbook:14619)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15035 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15035 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15036))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15036 "soil")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15036 "Naturally occurring, unconsolidated mineral and (or) organic material at the surface of the Earth that is capable of supporting plant growth. It extends from the surface to \\(\\pu{15 cm}\\) below the depth at which properties produced by soil-forming processes can be detected.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15036 "Soil formation results from an interaction between climate, living organisms, and surface relief acting on soil parent material."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15036 "Unconsolidated material includes material cemented or compacted by soil-forming processes. Soil may have water covering its surface to a depth of \\(\\pu{60 cm}\\) (or less in the driest part of the year)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15036 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15036 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15037))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15037 "solvent drag")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15037 "Movement of a solute (e.g., a contaminant) along with the bulk movement of the solvent.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15037 goldbook:14549)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15037 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15037 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15038))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15038 "somatic death")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15038 "Death of an individual organism.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15038 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15038 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15039))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15039 "somatic risk")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15039 "Risk of an adverse effect to the exposed individual associated with genetic damage to somatic cells, e.g., damage leading to cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15039 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15039 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15040))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15040 "sorbate")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15040 "Noncommittal term used instead of adsorbate or absorbate when the sorption process is undefined.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15040 goldbook:14413)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15040 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15040 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15041))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15041 "sorption constant")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15041 "Quantity describing the distribution of a substance between a solvent and a sorbent, typically water and sediment, at equilibrium, e.g., \\[K_{\\rm{d}} = [\\pu{C(sediment)}]/[\\pu{C(water)}]\\]")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15041 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15041 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15042))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15042 "source term")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15042 "Estimate of the total amount released, or the temporal pattern of the rate of release, of a pollutant from a source.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15042 goldbook:14928)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15042 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15042 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15043))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15043 "Spearman–Karber method")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15043 "Nonparametric method to estimate the \\(\\pu{LC_{50}}\\), \\(\\pu{EC_{50}}\\), or \\(\\pu{LD_{50}}\\) when it is difficult or unnecessary to assume a specific model for the dose- or concentration effect data.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15043 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15043 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15044))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15044 "species–area relationship")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15044 "Common pattern in which the number of species on islands decreases as island area decreases.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15044 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15044 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15045))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15045 "species assemblage")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15045 "Operationally defined subset of the entire community.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15045 goldbook:14531)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15045 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15045 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15046))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15046 "species–deletion stability")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15046 "Tendency in a model community for the remaining species to remain at locally stable equilibria after a species is made extinct.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15046 goldbook:14531)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15046 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15046 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15047))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15047 "species differences in sensitivity")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15047 "Quantitative or qualitative differences of response to the action(s) of a potentially toxic substance on various species of living organisms.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15047 goldbook:15100)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15047 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15047 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15048))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15048 "species diversity")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15048 "Heterogeneity of an ecological community, considering both species richness (\\(S\\)) and species evenness.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15048 goldbook:14531)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15048 goldbook:15049)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15048 goldbook:15051)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15048 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15048 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15049))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15049 "species evenness")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15049 "Degree to which the individuals in the community are evenly or uniformly distributed among species.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15049 goldbook:14531)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15049 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15049 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15050))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15050 "species imbalance")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15050 "Change in the species numbers or diversity in an ecosystem, or in their interactions, which results in change in ecological character and its functions and attributes.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15050 goldbook:14614)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15050 goldbook:14619)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15050 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15050 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15051))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15051 "species richness")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15051 "Total number of species in an ecosystem.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15051 "This index makes no use of relative abundances."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15051 goldbook:14479)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15051 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15051 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15052))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15052 "species sensitivity distribution")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15052 "Statistical relationship between exposure concentration and a defined effect derived from a combination of single-species test data to predict concentrations affecting only a certain percentage of the total number of species in a defined community.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15052 "SSD")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15052 "Single-species data [e.g., median lethal concentration (\\(\\pu{LC_{50}}\\)) or no-observed-effect concentration (NOEC) values] for many species are fitted to a distribution relationship such as the log-normal or log-logistic curve. From this distribution of species sensitivities, a hazardous concentration (\\(\\pu{HC_{\\textit{p}}}\\)) is identified at which a certain percentage (\\(p\\)) of all species is likely to be affected. The most conservative form of this approach uses the lower \\(\\pu{95\\%}\\) tolerance limit of the estimated percentage to ensure that the specified level of protection is achieved"^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15052 goldbook:14531)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15052 goldbook:14738)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15052 goldbook:14885)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15052 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15052 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15053))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15053 "species-specific sensitivity")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15053 "Quantitative and qualitative features of response to the action(s) of a potentially toxic substance that are characteristic for a particular species of living organism.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15053 goldbook:15100)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15053 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15053 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15054))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15054 "specific action concept")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15054 "Assumption made in radiotracer usage concerning specificity of action of a radionuclide used to trace or quantify the movement of a stable nuclide (e.g., \\(\\ce{^{14}C}\\) for stable \\(\\ce{C}\\)), implying that the radionuclide behaves identically in chemical and biological processes to its nonradioactive analog (e.g., stable \\(\\ce{C}\\)).")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15054 "specific activity concept")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15054 "Sometimes confusingly called the \"specific activity concept\"."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15054 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15054 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15055))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15055 "spiked bioassay approach")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15055 "Sediment toxicity test method to generate a concentration response model for effects to individuals placed in sediments spiked with different amounts of toxicant.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15055 "SB")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15055 "SB approach")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15055 "The method may also be used to test hypotheses regarding the mechanism of production of previously observed effects."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15055 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15055 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15056))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15056 "spillover hypothesis")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15056 "Hypothesis that toxic effects of metals will begin to occur after the metal concentration exceeds the capacity of the amount of metallothionein present to bind the metal. The unbound metals then 'spill over' to interact at sites of adverse action. This is based on the assumption that binding by metallothionein sequesters toxic metals away from sites of action.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15056 goldbook:15100)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15056 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15056 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15057))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15057 "stable age distribution")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15057 "Abundance of relative age classes that a population approaches if it is allowed to grow exponentially.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15057 goldbook:14415)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15057 goldbook:14932)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15057 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15057 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15058))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15058 "stable population")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15058 "Population with a constant distribution of individuals among the various age classes and a zero growth rate.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15058 "Stable populations do not change in size over time if environmental conditions do not change."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15058 goldbook:14932)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15058 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15058 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15059))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15059 "standard")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15059 "That which is established as a measure or model to which others of a similar nature should conform.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15059 goldbook:14645)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15059 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15059 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15060))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15060 "standard")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15060 "Technical specification, usually in the form of a document available to the public, drawn up with the consensus or general approval of all interests affected by it, based on the consolidated results of science, technology, and experience, aimed at the promotion of optimum community benefits and approved by a body recognized on the national, regional, or international level.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15060 "technical directive")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15060 goldbook:14531)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15060 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15060 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15061))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15061 "static-renewal test")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15061 "Modified static aquatic toxicity test in which solutions are completely or partially replaced with new solutions at set periods during exposures or in which organisms are periodically transferred to new solutions.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15061 "batch-replacement test")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15061 "renewal test")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15061 "renewed static test")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15061 "semi-static test")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15061 "static-replacement test")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15061 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15061 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15062))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15062 "static-toxicity test")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15062 "Aquatic toxicity test in which the exposure water is not changed during the test.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15062 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15062 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15063))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15063 "stratification")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15063 "Process by which materials form or are deposited in layers, as in sedimentary rocks and some igneous rocks. The atmosphere and the ocean also exhibit stratification, with the warmer air or water occupying the upper layers.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15063 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15063 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15064))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15064 "stratified sampling")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15064 "Sampling of individual subgroups (strata) of a population after its division into homogeneous strata.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15064 goldbook:14932)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15064 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15064 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15065))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15065 "stress")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15065 "Any condition that results in reduced growth of an organism or that prevents an organism from realizing its 'genetic potential'.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15065 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15065 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15066))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15066 "stressor")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15066 "Any physical, chemical, or biological factor causing an adverse response on any component of an ecosystem.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15066 goldbook:14619)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15066 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15066 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15067))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15067 "stress-protein fingerprinting")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15067 "Proposed use of the patterns of stress-protein induction seen in the field to suggest the particular toxicant inducing the response, after patterns from organisms sampled in the field are compared with those obtained with single-candidate toxicants in the laboratory.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15067 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15067 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15068))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15068 "stress proteins")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15068 "Several classes of proteins coded by genes transcriptionally activated by acute stresses, generally serving a protective or adaptive function.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15068 "These proteins include chaperones such as the heat shock proteins, enzymes protective against oxidative stress, metallothioneins, etc."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15068 "Stressors include physical agents such as heat and radiation, infection and inflammation, oxidative stress and hypoxia, desiccation and starvation, metals, xenobiotics, etc."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15068 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15068 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15069))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15069 "stress theory of aging")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15069 "Theory that stress shortens longevity by accelerating energy expenditure. Selection takes place for resistance to stress, and as an epiphenomenon, individuals resistant to stress will predominate in extreme age classes of a population. The diminution of homeostasis under stress with age should be slowest in individuals with highest longevity.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15069 goldbook:14744)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15069 goldbook:14932)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15069 goldbook:14971)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15069 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15069 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15070))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15070 "structural diversity")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15070 "Range of types of physical structure in a community that may provide habitats for species.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15070 goldbook:14531)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15070 goldbook:14728)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15070 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15070 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15071))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15071 "structure–metabolism relationship")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15071 "Association between the physicochemical and (or) the structural properties of a substance and its metabolic behavior.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15071 "SMR")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15071 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15071 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15072))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15072 "Sturm test")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15072 "Biodegradation test based on the measurement of \\(\\ce{CO2}\\) production.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15072 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15072 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15073))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15073 "stygobiont")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15073 "Organism that lives only in groundwater.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15073 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15073 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15074))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15074 "stygophile")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15074 "Organism that lives in groundwater and in surface water.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15074 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15074 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15075))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15075 "subcooled")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15075 "Term applied to a substance that is a liquid at a temperature lower than the saturation temperature for the existing pressure.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15075 "Sometimes such a substance is described as a \"compressed\" liquid since the existing pressure is greater than the saturation pressure for the given temperature."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15075 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15075 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15076))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15076 "subcooled liquid vapour pressure")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15076 "Vapor pressure of a subcooled liquid.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15076 "This physicochemical property is an important factor in determining the fate of chemicals in the environment and in allowing for the effects of environmental temperature variability."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15076 goldbook:15075)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15076 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15076 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15077))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15077 "succession")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15077 "Orderly sequential progression of changes in community composition that occurs during development of new populations in any area, from initial colonization to the attainment of the climax typical of a particular geographic area.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15077 goldbook:14437)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15077 goldbook:14457)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15077 goldbook:14459)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15077 goldbook:14528)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15077 goldbook:14531)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15077 goldbook:14742)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15077 goldbook:14932)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15077 goldbook:14951)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15077 goldbook:15023)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15077 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15077 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15078))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15078 "supercooled")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15078 "Term describing a substance that persists as a liquid at a temperature below its freezing point without solidification or crystallization.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15078 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15078 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15079))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15079 "surrogate organism")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15079 "Test organism, or population that is cultured under laboratory conditions to serve as a substitute in toxicity testing for indigenous organisms, communities, or populations.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15079 goldbook:14932)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15079 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15079 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15080))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15080 "surrogate toxicant")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15080 "Relatively well-studied substance whose properties are assumed to apply to an entire chemically and toxicologically related class.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15080 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15080 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15081))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15081 "surveillance")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15081 "Systematic ongoing collection, collation, and analysis of data and the timely dissemination of information to those who need to know in order that action can be taken to initiate investigative or control measures.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15081 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15081 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15082))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15082 "survival time")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15082 "Time interval between initial exposure of an organism to a harmful substance and death.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15082 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15082 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15083))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15083 "survivorship")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15083 "Proportion of animals surviving between two specified ages.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15083 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15083 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15084))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15084 "survivorship curve")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15084 "Graph showing how survivorship from birth varies with age.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15084 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15084 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15085))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15085 "susceptibility")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15085 "Condition of an organism or ecological system that makes it more vulnerable to a given exposure than the majority of the population or group of ecological systems to which it belongs.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15085 "Susceptibility is inversely proportional to the magnitude of the exposure required to cause a toxic effect."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15085 goldbook:14932)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15085 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15085 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15086))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15086 "suspension feeder")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15086 "Animal that feeds by straining suspended matter and food particles from water, typically by passing the water over a specialized structure, such as the baleen of baleen whales.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15086 "filter feeder")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15086 "Some animals that use this method of feeding are clams, barnacles, krill, mysids, sponges, whale sharks, and flamingoes."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15086 "Other types of feeder are deposit feeder, fluid feeder, and food-mass feeder."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15086 goldbook:14575)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15086 goldbook:14697)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15086 goldbook:14699)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15086 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15086 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15087))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15087 "syngenetic")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15087 "Describing mineral deposits formed at the same time as the enclosing rocks; characterized by or pertaining to a formation contemporaneous with the enclosing or surrounding rock.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15087 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15087 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15088))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15088 "systematics")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15088 "Study of the diversity of past and present life forms and of relationships among them through time.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15088 "taxonomy")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15088 "Relationships are visualized in cladograms (evolutionary trees, phylogenetic tree phylogenies). Systematics is used to understand the evolutionary history of life on Earth."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15088 goldbook:14527)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15088 goldbook:14667)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15088 goldbook:14913)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15088 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15088 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15089))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15089 "taxocene")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15089 "Taxonomically defined subset of an entire community.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15089 goldbook:14531)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15089 goldbook:15090)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15089 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15089 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15090))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15090 "taxonomy")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15090 "Science applied to the allocation of biological names and the rules of naming.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15090 "Classification (systematics) is the process of rank ordering of taxa according to presumptive evolutionary (phylogenetic) relationships."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15090 goldbook:14913)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15090 goldbook:15088)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15090 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15090 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15091))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15091 "teratogenic")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15091 "Capable of causing nonheritable permanent structural malformations or defects in the offspring of an exposed parent.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15091 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15091 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15092))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15092 "terrestrial")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15092 "Relating to land, as distinct from water or air.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15092 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15092 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15093))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15093 "threshold-effect concentration")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15093 "Concentration calculated as the geometric mean of no-observed-effect concentration (NOEC) and lowest-observed-effect concentration (LOEC).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15093 "TEC")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15093 "\"Chronic\" or \"subchronic\" may be added as qualifiers dependent on the duration of exposure in the test."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15093 "The TEC is equivalent to the maximum acceptable toxicant concentration (MATC) used in some countries."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15093 goldbook:14820)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15093 goldbook:14832)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15093 goldbook:14885)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15093 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15093 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15094))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15094 "threshold theory")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15094 "Theory that, for a given substance, no toxic effect can occur below a defined low dose.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15094 goldbook:15100)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15094 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15094 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15095))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15095 "tiered testing")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15095 "Structured approach to assessment of the fate and effects of substances, where a tier of relatively simple tests is used initially to select substances of concern and to define their toxicity. If the information from these tests is inadequate for regulatory decisions, further more complex tests (higher tier tests) may be required. For example, under a tiered structure, testing might progress from acute studies to chronic laboratory studies to field studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15095 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15095 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15096))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15096 "time-independent test")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15096 "Acute toxicity test with no predetermined temporal endpoint.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15096 "TI")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15096 "TI test")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15096 "This type of test, sometimes referred to as a \"threshold\" or \"incipient\" lethality test, is allowed to continue until acute toxicity (mortality or a defined sublethal effect) has ceased or nearly ceased and the toxicity curve (median survival time vs. test material concentration) indicates a threshold or incipient concentration. With most test materials, this point is reached within \\(\\pu{7\\!-\\! 10 d}\\), but it may not be reached within \\(\\pu{21 d}\\). Practical or economic reasons may dictate that the test be stopped at this point and a test be designed for longer duration."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15096 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15096 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15097))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15097 "tolerance index")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15097 "Quotient of an adequate parameter acquired under treated and control environments, multiplied by \\(\\pu{100}\\), thus: \\[\\rm{TI} = (\\rm{parameter\\ treated}/\\rm{parameter\\ control}) \\times 100\\]")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15097 "TI")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15097 "This index was originally defined in terms of root growth."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15097 goldbook:14432)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15097 goldbook:14930)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15097 goldbook:15010)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15097 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15097 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15098))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15098 "top-down ecotoxicological study")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15098 "Approach to investigating ecotoxicological effects that starts with a determination of the presence and nature of any adverse effects via responses at community and ecosystem levels of organization rather than the suborganismal levels of organization.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15098 goldbook:14509)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15098 goldbook:14531)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15098 goldbook:14619)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15098 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15098 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15099))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15099 "total organic carbon")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15099 "Organic matter content of soil, sediment, or water determined by measurement of organic carbon as the ratio of mass of organic carbon/mass of solid or of water.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15099 "TOC")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15099 "TOC is determined by oxidation of the organic matter into carbon dioxide (\\(\\ce{CO2}\\)) after removal of inorganic carbon such as carbonate or hydrogencarbonate. TOC includes all the carbon atoms covalently bonded in organic molecules."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15099 "Most of the organic carbon in water is dissolved organic carbon (DOC), with the remainder referred to as particulate organic carbon. In natural waters, TOC is composed primarily of nonspecific humic materials."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15099 goldbook:14595)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15099 goldbook:14746)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15099 goldbook:15036)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15099 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15099 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15100))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15100 "toxic")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15100 "Able to cause injury to living organisms as a result of physicochemical interaction.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15100 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15100 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15101))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15101 "toxic unit")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15101 "Dose or concentration of a toxicant expressed in units of lethality such as units of \\(\\pu{LD_{50}}\\) or \\(\\pu{LC_{50}}\\).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15101 "TU")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15101 "toxicity unit")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15101 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15101 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15102))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15102 "toxicity curve")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15102 "Curve obtained by plotting the median survival times of a group of test organisms against the concentration of a substance on a logarithmic scale.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15102 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15102 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15103))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15103 "toxicity equivalency factor")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15103 "Ratio of the toxicity of a chemical to that of another structurally related chemical (or index compound) chosen as a reference. In risk assessment, ratio of the toxicity of a chemical to that of another structurally related chemical (or index compound) chosen as a reference. Factor used to estimate the toxicity of a complex mixture, commonly a mixture of chlorinated dibenzo-p-dioxins [oxanthrenes], furans, and biphenyls: in this case, TEF is based on relative toxicity to 2,3,7,8-tetrachlorodibenzo-p-dioxin [2,3,7,8-tetrachlorooxanthrene] for which the \\(f = 1\\).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15103 "TEF")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15103 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15103 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15104))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15104 "toxicity equivalent")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15104 "Contribution of a specified component (or components) to the toxicity of a mixture of related substances.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15104 "TEQ")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15104 "The amount-of-substance (or substance) concentration of total toxicity equivalent is the sum of that for the components \\(\\ce{B, C … N}\\)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15104 "Toxicity equivalent is most commonly used in relation to the reference toxicant 2,3,7,8-tetrachlorodibenzo-p-dioxin [2,3,7,8-tetrachlorooxanthrene] by means of the toxicity equivalency factor (TEF, \\(f\\)) that is 1 for the reference substance. Hence, where \\(\\pu{c}\\) is the amount-of-substance concentration: \\[T_{\\rm{xe}} = \\sum \\limits_{i=B}^{N} f_{1} \\pu{c}_{i}\\]"^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15104 goldbook:15103)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15104 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15104 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15105))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15105 "toxicity identification and evaluation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15105 "Systematic pretreatment (e.g., \\(\\rm{pH}\\) change, filtration, or aeration) of a sample to obtain defined fractions that are subsequently tested for their toxicity. This fractionation is designed to separate out defined substances and thus to identify the agent(s) primarily responsible for lethal or sublethal toxicity of a complex mixture.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15105 "TIE")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15105 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15105 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15106))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15106 "toxicity value")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15106 "Factor used to estimate risk. It may be a reference dose or it may be calculated from the following equation: \\[T_{\\rm{x}} = m\\ C\\] where \\(m\\) is the slope of a published dose-effect relationship and \\(C\\) is the toxicant concentration.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15106 goldbook:14602)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15106 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15106 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15107))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15107 "trace nutrient")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15107 "Substance required in very small quantities by a defined organism to maintain health.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15107 "micronutrient")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15107 "The quantities required for health and the species must be stated before application of this term has any meaning."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15107 "Use of the term is often misleading since it is meaningless unless accompanied by a statement of which organisms show a requirement for the nutrient and the amount required."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15107 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15107 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15108))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15108 "trade-off")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15108 "Exchange of one advantageous character for another.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15108 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15108 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15109))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15109 "trigger values")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15109 "Criteria applied to results from tests (for fate or effects) which prompt further studies, e.g., moving to the next tier of tests, which are generally more complex.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15109 goldbook:15095)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15109 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15109 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15110))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15110 "trophic")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15110 "Relating to nutrition.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15110 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15110 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15111))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15111 "trophic cascade")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15111 "Situation arising when predators in a food chain suppress the abundance of their prey, thereby releasing the next lower trophic level from predation (or herbivory if the intermediate trophic level is an herbivore).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15111 "For example, if the abundance of large piscivorous fish is increased in a lake, the abundance of their prey, zooplanktivorous fish, should decrease, large zooplankton abundance should increase, and phytoplankton biomass should decrease."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15111 "Trophic cascades may also be important for understanding the effects of removing top predators from food webs, as humans have done in many places through hunting and fishing activities."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15111 goldbook:14698)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15111 goldbook:14918)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15111 goldbook:14922)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15111 goldbook:14923)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15111 goldbook:15113)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15111 goldbook:15139)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15111 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15111 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15112))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15112 "trophic dilution")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15112 "Decrease in contaminant concentration as trophic level increases; this results from a net balance of ingestion rate, uptake from food, internal transformation, and elimination processes favoring loss of contaminant that enters the organism via food.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15112 "biominification")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15112 "bioreduction")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15112 goldbook:14549)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15112 goldbook:15113)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15112 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15112 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15113))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15113 "trophic level")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15113 "Position in a food chain, assessed by the number of energy-transfer steps to reach that level.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15113 "trophic position")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15113 goldbook:14612)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15113 goldbook:14698)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15113 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15113 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15114))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15114 "trophic structure")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15114 "Organization of an ecological community described in terms of energy flow through its various trophic levels.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15114 goldbook:14531)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15114 goldbook:15113)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15114 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15114 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15115))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15115 "trophic transfer")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15115 "Transfer of a substance from one trophic level to another.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15115 goldbook:15113)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15115 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15115 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15116))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15116 "trophic transfer factor")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15116 "Ratio between the concentration of a compound in a predator and in its prey.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15116 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15116 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15117))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15117 "turbidity of water")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15117 "Extent to which the clarity of water is reduced by the presence of suspended or other matter that causes light to be scattered and absorbed rather than transmitted (in straight lines) through the sample.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15117 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15117 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15118))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15118 "twin-tracer technique")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15118 "Experimental method for evaluating assimilation that introduces simultaneously a radiotracer of the substance being assimilated and an inert tracer that will not be assimilated, thus providing a basis for evaluating the assimilation.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15118 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15118 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15119))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15119 "type A organism")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15119 "Animal or plant living in contact with sediments but unable to ingest particulates.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15119 "The classification implies that such organisms take up substances from interstitial water but not from sediment-associated particulates; examples of such organisms are rooted macrophytes and benthic algae."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15119 goldbook:14433)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15119 goldbook:14468)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15119 goldbook:14772)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15119 goldbook:14826)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15119 goldbook:15120)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15119 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15119 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15120))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15120 "type B organism")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15120 "Animal or plant living in contact with sediments and capable of ingesting particulates.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15120 "The classification implies that such organisms take up substances from both interstitial water and from sediment-associated particulates."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15120 goldbook:14772)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15120 goldbook:15119)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15120 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15120 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15121))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15121 "uncertainty factor")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15121 "In assay methodology, confidence interval or fiducial limit used to assess the probable precision of an estimate. In toxicology, value used in extrapolation from experimental animals to humans (assuming that humans may be more sensitive) or from selected individuals to the general population.Example: A value applied to the no-observed-effect-level (NOEL) or no-observed-adverse-effect-level (NOAEL) to derive an acceptable daily intake (ADI) or tolerable daily intake (TDI).Note: The NOEL or NOAEL is divided by the value to calculate the ADI or TDI.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15121 "UF")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15121 "application factor (AF)")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15121 "assessment factor")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15121 "modifying factor (MF)")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15121 "safety factor")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15121 goldbook:14932)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15121 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15121 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15122))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15122 "upstream water")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15122 "Water in a rivulet, river, or lake that is situated above a defined point, in a direction opposite to that of the current flow.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15122 "Upstream water is not influenced by incoming effluent at or below the defined point because the effluent is carried away by the flow."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15122 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15122 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15123))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15123 "uptake rate constant")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15123 "First-order one-compartment constant to describe the uptake of a substance by an organism from water.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15123 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15123 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15124))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15124 "viability selection")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15124 "Component of the life cycle of an individual in which natural selection can occur through the differential survival of individuals. It begins at the formation of the zygote and continues throughout the life of the individual.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15124 goldbook:14795)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15124 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15124 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15125))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15125 "vital rates")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15125 "Measures of how fast vital statistics change in a population (usually expressed per \\(\\pu{1000}\\) individuals).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15125 "There are two categories within vital rates, crude rates referring to change in the whole population (e.g., overall change in births and deaths per \\(\\pu{1000}\\)) and refined rates referring to change in a specific demographic such as age, sex, race, etc."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15125 goldbook:14932)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15125 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15125 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15126))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15126 "vulnerability")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15126 "Susceptibility to harm by toxicants.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15126 goldbook:15085)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15126 goldbook:14732)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15126 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15126 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15127))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15127 "Wahlund effect")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15127 "Net deficit of heterozygotes when two populations, each in Hardy–Weinberg equilibrium but with different allele frequencies, are mixed and the genotype frequencies quantified in a combined population sample.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15127 goldbook:14731)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15127 goldbook:14932)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15127 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15127 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15128))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15128 "waldsterben")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15128 "Widespread and substantial decline in growth and the change in behavior of many softwood and hardwood forest ecosystems in central Europe.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15128 goldbook:14619)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15128 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15128 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15129))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15129 "waste-water")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15129 "General term describing effluents, leachate, and elutriates which enter the natural environment.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15129 goldbook:14628)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15129 goldbook:14786)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15129 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15129 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15130))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15130 "weakest-link incongruity")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15130 "Questionable extension of the critical life-stage concept (see critical life-stage testing) that protection of the most sensitive life stage will ensure protection of all life stages; it assumes that exposure of field populations to concentrations identified in laboratory testing as causing significant mortality at a critical stage of life will result in significant impact on the field population")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15130 goldbook:14559)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15130 goldbook:14932)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15130 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15130 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15131))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15131 "Weibull model")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15131 "Dose–response model of the form \\[P(d) = \\gamma + (1 - \\gamma)(1 - e^{-\\beta d^{\\alpha}})\\] where \\(P(d)\\) is the probability of a tumor (or other response) from lifetime, continuous exposure at dose \\(d\\) until age \\(t\\) (when tumor is fatal), \\(\\alpha\\) is a fitted dose parameter (sometimes called the Weibull parameter), \\(\\beta\\) is a fitted dose parameter, and \\(\\gamma\\) is the background response rate.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15131 goldbook:14604)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15131 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15131 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15132))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15132 "weight composition")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15132 "Distribution of organisms among the various weight classes present in a population.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15132 "The sum of individual weights over all weight classes equals the population biomass."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15132 goldbook:14932)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15132 goldbook:14933)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15132 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15132 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15133))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15133 "weight of evidence")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15133 "(in general) Quantitative, semiquantitative, or qualitative estimate of the degree to which the evidence supports or undermines a given conclusion. (in toxicology) Estimate of the extent to which the available biomedical data support the hypothesis that a substance causes a defined toxic effect such as cancer in humans.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15133 goldbook:15100)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15133 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15133 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15134))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15134 "Weismannism")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15134 "Theory of evolution and heredity propounded by the German biologist, August Weismann, especially in regard to the continuity of the germ-plasm and the nontransmission of acquired characteristics.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15134 goldbook:14667)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15134 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15134 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15135))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15135 "wet deposition")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15135 "Transfer of chemicals from the atmosphere to the Earth’s surface in atmospheric water precipitation (atmospheric deposition), e.g., rain, snow, or hail, of pollutants that occur in the precipitation, e.g., as a result of Brownian capture, nucleation, dissolution, or impaction.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15135 goldbook:14454)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15135 goldbook:14928)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15135 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15135 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15136))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15136 "wetland")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15136 "Area of land consisting of soil that is saturated with moisture, such as a swamp, marsh, or bog.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15136 "As defined in terms of physical geography, a wetland is an environment \"at the interface between truly terrestrial ecosystems and aquatic systems making them inherently different from each other yet highly dependent on both\"."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15136 "Wetlands are ecotones. Wetlands often host considerable biodiversity and endemism."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15136 "In many locations such as the United Kingdom and United States, wetlands are the subject of conservation efforts and biodiversity action plans (BAPs)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15136 goldbook:14479)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15136 goldbook:14480)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15136 goldbook:14547)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15136 goldbook:14548)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15136 goldbook:14620)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15136 goldbook:14633)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15136 goldbook:15036)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15136 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15136 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15137))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15137 "whole-effluent toxicity")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15137 "Total toxic effect of an effluent measured directly with aquatic organisms in a toxicity test.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15137 "WET")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15137 goldbook:15100)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15137 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15137 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15138))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15138 "whole sediment")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15138 "Sediment and associated interstitial water that have had minimal manipulation.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15138 goldbook:14772)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15138 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15138 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15139))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15139 "zooplankton")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15139 "Small floating or weakly swimming animals that drift with water currents and which, with phytoplankton, make up the planktonic food supply upon which almost all oceanic organisms ultimately depend.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15139 goldbook:14918)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15139 goldbook:14924)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15139 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15139 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15140))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15140 "normal equivalent deviation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15140 "Proportion dying in a toxicity test expressed in terms of standard deviations from the mean of a normal curve.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15140 "NED")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15140 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-07-09)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15140 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15141))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15141 "absolute bioavailability")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15141 "Fraction of the administered dose of a drug from a dosage form absorbed intact into the systemic circulation.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15141 goldbook:15175)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15141 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15141 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15142))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15142 "active transport of drugs")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15142 "Carriage of a solute across a biological membrane, which requires a suitable carrier and the expenditure of energy.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15142 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15142 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15143))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15143 "administration")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15143 "Introduction of a substance to an organism by a defined route.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15143 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15143 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15144))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15144 "administration of drugs ocular route")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15144 "Administration of drugs through the eye.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15144 "Drugs used to treat eye disorders can be administered as liquid or semi-solid dosage forms. Solid inserts, which release the drug in slow-release pattern, are also available."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15144 "Ocular drugs are almost always used for their local effects. Some drugs produce a local effect after they are absorbed through the cornea and conjunctiva. Some of these drugs then enter the bloodstream and may have unwanted or wanted systemic effects."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15144 goldbook:15143)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15144 goldbook:15175)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15144 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15144 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15145))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15145 "administration of drugs oral route")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15145 "Administration of drugs through the mouth to swallow.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15145 "This is the most convenient and popular administration route."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15145 "Per-oral products can be powders, granules, uncoated or coated tablets, capsules, and liquids (solutions, emulsions, and suspensions). Liquids for oral use may contain antimicrobial preservatives and are supplied in multi- or single-dose containers."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15145 "It differs from intraoral administration."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15145 goldbook:15143)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15145 goldbook:15159)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15145 goldbook:15161)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15145 goldbook:15193)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15145 goldbook:15227)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15145 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15145 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15146))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15146 "administration of drugs parenteral route")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15146 "Method of introducing substances into an organism, avoiding the gastrointestinal tract.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15146 "Parenteral routes may be employed whenever enteral routes are contraindicated or inadequate."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15146 "Parenteral administration includes some conventional (intravenous, intramuscular, subcutaneous) and some special (intradermal, intraventricular, etc.) routes."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15146 "Parenteral products can be solutions, suspensions, and emulsions. They are presented as sterile products. It is commonly used to imply administration by injection or infusion."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15146 goldbook:15143)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15146 goldbook:15201)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15146 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15146 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15147))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15147 "administration of drugs rectal route")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15147 "Administration of drugs into the rectal cavity or through the rectum.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15147 "Products may be solid (suppositories) or liquid unit dosage preparations, or creams, ointments, and gels."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15147 "This is an important way of administering a medicinal product that may not be tolerated orally, especially in pediatrics and geriatrics or when the patient has an infection of the gastrointestinal tract; or when the drug is less suited for oral administration because of side effects, bad taste, or enzymatic degradation."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15147 "The rectal route has several drawbacks. These can be, in addition to psychological aversion, slow and incomplete absorption, and inadequacy where rapid absorption and high plasma levels are required."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15147 goldbook:15143)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15147 goldbook:15184)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15147 goldbook:15217)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15147 goldbook:15238)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15147 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15147 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15148))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15148 "administration of drugs respiratory route")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15148 "Delivery to the lower respiratory tract in order to obtain a local or systemic effect.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15148 "introduction of drugs by inhalation")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15148 "Products usually deliver the active substance in the form of aerosol droplets or solid particles (powders)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15148 goldbook:15143)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15148 goldbook:15200)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15148 goldbook:15227)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15148 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15148 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15149))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15149 "administration of drugs topical route")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15149 "Administration of drugs on surfaces of the body.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15149 "Topical products usually produce pharmacological effects at or near the point of application, such as the skin, eyes, nose, throat, ears, and vagina, etc., but sometimes may also have systemic effects."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15149 goldbook:15143)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15149 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15149 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15150))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15150 "administration of drugs transdermal route")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15150 "Introduction of products through unbroken skin by means of a specific drug delivery system (such as a patch containing a semi-solid formulation of the drug) for systemic and/or prolonged drug effect.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15150 "diadermic administration")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15150 "percutaneous administration")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15150 "transcutaneous administration")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15150 "transdermic administration")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15150 goldbook:15143)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15150 goldbook:15177)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15150 goldbook:15188)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15150 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15150 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15151))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15151 "administration of drugs vaginal route")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15151 "Introduction of products into the vagina normally for local effect.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15151 "Vaginal preparations may be liquid dispersions (solutions, foams), semi-solid (gels, creams, ointments), and solids (tablets, capsules, pessaries, tampons, sponges)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15151 goldbook:15143)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15151 goldbook:15159)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15151 goldbook:15217)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15151 goldbook:15241)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15151 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15151 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15152))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15152 "angle of repose")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15152 "Characteristic angle of slope formed with the horizontal by the side of a static conical mound of powder.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15152 "Angle of repose is determined by a balance of gravitational force and the frictional forces caused by interparticulate interactions."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15152 "A measure of cohesiveness in powders. The smaller the angle of repose the greater the ability of the powder to flow. A particle will begin to slide on a slope when the angle of inclination is sufficiently large to overcome the frictional forces, and conversely the particle will not move when the angle is below that required to overcome cohesion and adhesion."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15152 "The angle of repose depends on the method of measurement."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15152 goldbook:15227)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15152 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15152 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15153))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15153 "appertisation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15153 "Process by which food is rendered free from pathogenic, toxigenic, and spoilage organisms.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15153 "A term used in the food industry."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15153 "Appertization will not necessarily kill thermophilic spores, and thus products subjected to the process may not be sterile."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15153 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15153 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15154))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15154 "bioequivalence")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15154 "Relationship between two preparations of the same drug in the same dosage form that have a similar bioavailability. Dosage forms containing the same drug are said to be bioequivalent if they do not differ significantly in the bioavailability (e.g., AUC, \\(c_{\\rm{max}}\\), \\(t_{\\rm{max}}\\)) of the active constituent/ingredient, when administered in the same dose under similar experimental conditions.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15154 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15154 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15155))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15155 "biological product")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15155 "Virus, therapeutic serum, toxin, antitoxin, or analogous product applicable to the prevention, treatment, or cure of diseases or injuries in humans and/or animals.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15155 "The term \"analogous product\" may include essentially all biotechnology-derived products and procedures including gene therapy, transgenics, and somatic cell therapy."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15155 goldbook:15191)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15155 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15155 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15156))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15156 "biopharmaceutics")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15156 "Branch of pharmaceutical science that deals with the fate of drugs in the living system; particularly the release of the drug from its dosage form into a biological medium, its passage across membranes into the systemic circulation, metabolism, and elimination, and the application of this knowledge to obtain the desired therapeutic effect.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15156 goldbook:15175)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15156 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15156 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15157))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15157 "buccal tablet")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15157 "Usually a small, flat, and soft tablet, which is designed to be placed inside the cheek to be directly absorbed through the mucosa for systemic effect.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15157 goldbook:15241)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15157 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15157 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15158))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15158 "bulk density")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15158 "Characteristic of a powder rather than of individual particles given by the mass of powder occupying a known volume.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15158 "Characteristics of importance in tablet production."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15158 "The bulk density is always lower than the true density of its component particles."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15158 "A powder can have only one true density, but it can have many different bulk densities, depending on how tightly the particles are packed."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15158 goldbook:15227)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15158 goldbook:15241)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15158 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15158 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15159))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15159 "capsule")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15159 "Small edible package made usually from gelatin or other materials that can be filled with drugs (solids or liquids) to produce a unit dose, mainly for oral use. Hard capsules consist of two pieces that fit one inside the other which are produced empty and filled in a separate operation, and soft, liquid-filled capsules, which are manufactured and filled in one operation.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15159 goldbook:15145)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15159 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15159 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15160))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15160 "carrier-mediated drug transport")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15160 "Transfer of a drug across a membrane by a transporter (often a protein) constituent of the cytosol membrane. Also known as active transport as opposed to passive diffusion/absorption.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15160 goldbook:15142)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15160 goldbook:15171)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15160 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15160 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15161))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15161 "coating")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15161 "Technological process consisting of the application of a substance, which forms a layer (e.g., to protect the drug and/or the tablet, to mask taste, to control the rate of drug release (e.g., film coating, sugar coating).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15161 "Sugar coating is used to mask bad taste without altering release profile."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15161 goldbook:15241)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15161 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15161 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15162))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15162 "compressed tablet")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15162 "A solid dosage form prepared to a desired shape, usually in large-scale production, by means of high pressure in a punch and die.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15162 "Most compressed tablets consist of the active ingredient and a diluent (filler), binder, disintegrator, and lubricant."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15162 goldbook:15241)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15162 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15162 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15163))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15163 "controlled-release dosage form")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15163 "Medication, which due to its special technological construction provides for drug release having predefined kinetics (zero order, \\(t^{1/2}\\), first order, etc.) at a sufficient rate to maintain the desired therapeutic level over an extended period of time.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15163 "Also used to denote sustained-release products with zero-order release kinetics."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15163 goldbook:15239)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15163 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15163 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15164))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15164 "critical moisture content")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15164 "A stage in the drying of solids, above which the drying rate (derived from the plot of the loss of moisture content against time) is linear, at which the drying rate ceases to be linear, until it reaches the equilibrium moisture content.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15164 goldbook:15186)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15164 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15164 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15165))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15165 "crossover study")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15165 "Type of comparative bioavailability study designed in such a way as to take into account differences in bioavailability arising from differences between patients suffering from disease, participating in the study.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15165 "The differences between the subjects may be in age, stage or severity of the disease, and prior drug treatment that some may have received. In such a crossover study, the patients are divided into two equal size groups, uniform with respect to age, body weight, sex, etc. The first group is given a specific dose of the product studied, while the second group is given a second product of proven clinical efficacy, containing the same active ingredient. After taking an appropriate number of blood samples from each individual and a washout period, the groups are reversed and the first group is given the product of proven clinical efficacy and the second is given the product being studied. This way each patient serves as his or her own control."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15165 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15165 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15166))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15166 "crystalline")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15166 "Term that describes a solid of regular shape and the presence of three-dimensional order on the level of atomic dimensions, for a given molecule.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15166 "Crystallinity may be detected by diffraction techniques, heat-of-fusion measurements, etc."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15166 "Crystalline forms are often preferred, over amorphous forms, in pharmaceutical dosage forms, due to uniformity, reproducibility, and sometimes lack of hygroscopicity."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15166 goldbook:15175)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15166 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15166 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15167))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15167 "delayed-release dosage form")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15167 "Pharmaceutical preparation that releases the drug(s) at a time other than promptly after administration.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15167 "Typically, this is related to enteric coated tablets."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15167 goldbook:15185)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15167 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15167 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15168))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15168 "deliquescent")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15168 "Substance that absorbs sufficient moisture from the atmosphere to dissolve itself.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15168 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15168 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15169))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15169 "depot")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15169 "Deposit of a drug in a body created by injection or by a similar mode of introduction to form a source of slow release.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15169 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15169 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15170))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15170 "detergency")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15170 "Property, which serves as basis for the process whereby surfactants are used for the removal of foreign matter from surfaces (including dirt from clothes or body surfaces).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15170 goldbook:15233)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15170 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15170 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15171))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15171 "diffusion barrier")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15171 "Obstacle such as coating or embedding, which acts as a factor controlling the rate of drug release.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15171 "Body fluids or membranes can also act as barriers."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15171 goldbook:15161)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15171 goldbook:15183)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15171 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15171 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15172))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15172 "disperse system")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15172 "Dosage form in which the active ingredient is insoluble in the carrier; includes aerosols (solids or liquids in gas), suspensions (solids in liquids), emulsions (liquids in liquids), and foams (gas in liquid), or ointments/creams (solid in solid or in semi-solid, or liquid in solid).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15172 "These systems are thermodynamically unstable and need to be stabilized by suspensifying or emulsifying agents."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15172 goldbook:15217)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15172 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15172 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15173))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15173 "divided granule")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15173 "Formulation in which individual doses of a granulated dosage form are separated (e.g., gelatin capsules).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15173 goldbook:15188)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15173 goldbook:15159)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15173 goldbook:15194)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15173 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15173 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15174))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15174 "divided powder")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15174 "Powder formulation in which individual doses of a powdered dosage form are separately wrapped (e.g., sachets, envelopes, or gelatin capsules).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15174 goldbook:15227)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15174 goldbook:15159)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15174 goldbook:15175)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15174 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15174 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15175))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15175 "dosage form")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15175 "Formulated preparation of molecules/drugs that are rarely if ever suitable for administration to patients without additives.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15175 "They can be designed for administration by all possible administration routes to achieve the desired therapeutic response."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15175 goldbook:15188)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15175 goldbook:15143)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15175 goldbook:15238)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15175 goldbook:15240)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15175 goldbook:15241)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15175 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15175 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15176))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15176 "dosage regimen")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15176 "Dose and dosing interval of a drug.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15176 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15176 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15177))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15177 "drug delivery system")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15177 "Sophisticated dosage form, which, by its construction, is able to modify/control the availability of the drug substance to the body by temporal or spatial considerations.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15177 goldbook:15163)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15177 goldbook:15167)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15177 goldbook:15169)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15177 goldbook:15175)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15177 goldbook:15183)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15177 goldbook:15239)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15177 goldbook:15187)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15177 goldbook:15198)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15177 goldbook:15212)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15177 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15177 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15178))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15178 "drug-eluting stent")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15178 "Refers to a stent with an active drug that is intended to produce a therapeutic effect (e.g., reduction of restenosis).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15178 goldbook:15236)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15178 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15178 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15179))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15179 "dusting powder")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15179 "Usually intended for external use.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15179 "Usually contains ingredients used for therapeutic, prophylactic, or lubricant purposes."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15179 "Normally dispensed in containers with perforated lids."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15179 "The powder must flow well so that it can be dusted over the required area."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15179 "Examples are antibacterial and antifungal products."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15179 goldbook:15227)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15179 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15179 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15180))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15180 "effervescent tablet")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15180 "Solid preparation that on contact with water breaks apart by the effect of gas (usually \\(\\ce{CO2}\\)) evolution, resulting commonly from the reaction of hydrogen carbonate with citric or tartaric acid, in order to facilitate dissolution or dispersion of the active ingredient before ingestion.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15180 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15180 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15181))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15181 "efflorescent")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15181 "Substance that loses water to form a lower hydrate or becomes anhydrous spontaneously.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15181 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15181 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15182))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15182 "elixir")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15182 "Sweet (often colored) dilute alcohol-based, 'hydroalcoholic', liquid used in the compounding of drugs to be taken by mouth in order to improve palatability.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15182 "Elixirs are among the most common types of medicinal preparations taken orally in liquid form."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15182 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15182 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15183))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15183 "embedding")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15183 "Technological process, which consists of mixing or inclusion of the therapeutic substance with an excipient or their mixtures, typically as a matrix dosage form, in order to change the rate of release.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15183 goldbook:15175)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15183 goldbook:15207)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15183 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15183 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15184))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15184 "enemas")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15184 "Solutions (aqueous or oily), emulsions, or suspensions for rectal administration of medicaments for cleansing, diagnostic, or therapeutic purposes.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15184 goldbook:15147)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15184 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15184 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15185))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15185 "enteric coating")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15185 "Used on tablets, granules, pellets, and capsules to make them resistant to gastric fluids but designed to disintegrate, disrupt, or dissolve when the preparation enters the duodenum.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15185 "Enteric coating is used for one of the following reasons: To protect the drug from degradation by the acid in the stomach (e.g., erythromycin).To protect the stomach from the irritant effect of the drug (e.g., aspirin).To facilitate absorption of a drug distally to the stomach."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15185 goldbook:15159)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15185 goldbook:15167)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15185 goldbook:15193)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15185 goldbook:15221)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15185 goldbook:15241)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15185 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15185 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15186))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15186 "equilibrium moisture content")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15186 "Final stage reached after drying of a solid, beyond the critical moisture content.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15186 "EMC")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15186 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15186 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15187))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15187 "fast-dissolving tablet")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15187 "A tablet formulation intended for a rapid release of its active agent.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15187 goldbook:15198)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15187 goldbook:15239)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15187 goldbook:15241)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15187 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15187 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15188))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15188 "formulation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15188 "Summary of operations carried out to convert a pharmacologically active compound into a dosage form suitable for administration.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15188 goldbook:15143)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15188 goldbook:15175)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15188 goldbook:15177)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15188 goldbook:15233)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15188 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15188 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15189))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15189 "gargle")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15189 "Aqueous solution used for the prevention and treatment of mouth and throat infections.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15189 "mouthwash")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15189 "May contain antiseptics, antibacterials, analgesics, and/or astringents."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15189 "Usually diluted with water before use."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15189 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15189 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15190))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15190 "gastric emptying rate")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15190 "Pace at which a drug along with the stomach content leaves and enters the duodenum.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15190 "Often, gastric emptying rate is also expressed as gastric emptying time."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15190 "Gastric emptying rate (or time) is expressed typically in units of time or \\(t_{1/2}\\). It is also expressed as the amount of a given substance emptied per the total mass in the stomach, at a given time; or as the amount emptied, at a given time, of a given substance."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15190 "Since most drugs are optimally absorbed from the small intestine, the onset of drug action depends on the gastric emptying rate. Thus, the rate of gastric emptying determines the timing but not the extent of oral drug absorption."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15190 "The gastric emptying rate depends on several factors, e.g., stomach calorie content, \\(\\rm{pH}\\), hunger, anxiety, the nature of the drugs and body posture. High-calorie foods (e.g., fats) usually retard gastric emptying and delay drug absorption."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15190 goldbook:15145)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15190 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15190 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15191))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15191 "gene therapy")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15191 "Use of products containing genetic material (e.g., pDNA, antisense DNA, siRNA) to treat a disease or condition, or to modify or manipulate the expression of genetic material or to alter the biological properties of living cells.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15191 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15191 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15192))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15192 "generic")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15192 "Drug(s) or formulation(s) of drug(s) or dosage forms, which no longer have patent protection.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15192 "generics")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15192 "Generic or nonproprietary drugs that may enter the market after the expiry of the basic patent covering the original drugs."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15192 "Nonproprietary drugs are required to meet the same bioequivalency test as the original brand name drugs."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15192 "Generic products may themselves bear brand names."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15192 goldbook:15175)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15192 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15192 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15193))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15193 "granules")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15193 "Powder particles, which have been aggregated to form larger irregular particles, usually of \\(\\pu{0.5\\!{-}\\! 2 mm}\\) diameter.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15193 "Granules are also used as intermediates in tableting. These are typically of smaller sizes."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15193 "May also be used rarely as independent dosage form for oral administrations."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15193 goldbook:15227)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15193 goldbook:15175)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15193 goldbook:15145)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15193 goldbook:15241)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15193 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15193 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15194))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15194 "granulation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15194 "Process in which powder particles are made to aggregate to larger particles called granules.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15194 "In the majority of cases, granulation is required in the production of tablets or capsules, when granules are made as an intermediate product."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15194 "Granulation is preceded by mixing the necessary powdered ingredients to assure their uniform distribution in the granules."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15194 "Granulation may be carried out by two methods: wet granulations which utilize nontoxic volatile liquids, like water or low alcohols; or dry methods in which high pressure is applied."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15194 goldbook:15159)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15194 goldbook:15193)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15194 goldbook:15227)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15194 goldbook:15241)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15194 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15194 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15195))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15195 "hydrate")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15195 "Crystalline form of a compound in which water molecules are part of the crystal structure.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15195 "Association of water molecule(s) in a crystal can be of different strength."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15195 "The term \"hydrate\" may mean different things in different contexts. Common to all contexts is the content of water, which may be part of crystal structure or part of a molecule to which water has been added reversibly (e.g., chloral hydrate) or the elements of water incorporated covalently (e.g., carbohydrates)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15195 goldbook:15166)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15195 goldbook:15234)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15195 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15195 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15196))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15196 "hydrophile-lipophile balance system")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15196 "Empirical scale (of \\(0\\!-\\!20\\)) used to classify surfactants and emulsifying agents.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15196 "HLB")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15196 "HLB System")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15196 "The numerical value is determined by the expression (\\({\\rm{HLB}} = 20 M_{\\rm{h}}/M\\)) where \\(M_{\\rm{h}}\\) is the molecular mass of the hydrophilic portion of the molecule, and \\(M\\) is the molecular mass of the whole molecule, giving a result on an arbitrary scale of \\(0\\!-\\!20\\)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15196 "An HLB value of \\(0\\) corresponds to a completely hydrophobic molecule, while a value of \\(20\\) corresponds to a molecule made up completely of hydrophilic components."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15196 "The more hydrophilic the surfactant the more it favors the formation of o/w over w/o emulsions."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15196 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15196 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15197))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15197 "hygroscopicity")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15197 "Tendency of a substance to absorb water from the atmosphere.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15197 "A substance that absorbs moisture from the atmosphere is called hygroscopic."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15197 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15197 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15198))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15198 "immediate-release tablet")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15198 "Dosage form that releases the drug immediately.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15198 goldbook:15175)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15198 goldbook:15187)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15198 goldbook:15239)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15198 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15198 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15199))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15199 "inactivation factor")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15199 "Number that expresses the reduction in the numbers of a microorganism, brought about by a sterilization process.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15199 "IF")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15199 "The IF value is specific for a microorganism and a sterilization process."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15199 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15199 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15200))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15200 "inhalation therapy")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15200 "Administration of drugs directly to the respiratory tract, mostly by aerosols.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15200 "Since a drug is delivered directly to the site of action, lower dose is needed by this route than by other routes, e.g., the gastrointestinal or parenteral routes."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15200 "The incidence and the intensity of side effects are generally lower when this route is used as compared to other routes of drug administration."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15200 goldbook:15143)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15200 goldbook:15146)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15200 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15200 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15201))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15201 "injection")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15201 "Delivery of a generally sterile liquid medication into the body, or a vessel, tissue, or organ via syringe and needle.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15201 "Epidural injections are given into the epidural space of the spinal cord."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15201 "Intra-articular injections are made into the synovial fluid, which lubricates the articulating ends of bones in a joint."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15201 "Intrabursal injections are given into the bursae, which are small sacks of fluids between the tendons and bones."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15201 "Intracardial injections are given directly into the heart in emergencies."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15201 "Intracutaneous or intradermal injections are made into the skin between the inner layer (dermis) and the outer layer (epidermis)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15201 "Intramuscular injections are made by inserting the needle across the skin, subcutaneous tissue, and membrane enclosing the muscle."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15201 "Intraspinal injections are made into or around the spinal cord."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15201 "Intravascular injections (intra-arterial and -venous) are made directly into the blood stream for rapid effect."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15201 "Intrathecal injection is the introduction of material for diffusion throughout the subarachnoid space by means of lumbar puncture."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15201 "Ophthalmic injections include a variety of sites within the eye."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15201 "Subcutaneous or hypodermic injections are made under the skin into the subcutaneous tissue."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15201 "The same formulation cannot be used for all routes."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15201 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15201 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15202))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15202 "liniment")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15202 "Liquid intended for massaging into the skin.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15202 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15202 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15203))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15203 "loading dose")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15203 "Initial, typically larger than the maintenance dose of a drug given to a patient at the start of pharmacotherapy.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15203 "The objective is to reach quickly the therapeutically beneficial plasma level. This is followed by smaller (maintenance) doses in order to maintain the plasma concentration."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15203 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15203 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15204))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15204 "lotion")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15204 "Solution, emulsion, or suspension to be applied to the skin.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15204 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15204 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15205))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15205 "lozenge")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15205 "Tablet, which does not contain a disintegrant and which is sucked to dissolve in the mouth to produce either a local (e.g., antiseptic) or systemic (e.g., vitamins) effect.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15205 "Lozenges must be palatable and slowly soluble."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15205 goldbook:15241)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15205 goldbook:15243)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15205 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15205 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15206))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15206 "lubricant")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15206 "Used as processing aid in tablet and capsule manufacturing, to facilitate the movement of the formulation into the dye and punch and to reduce the energy of compression.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15206 goldbook:15159)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15206 goldbook:15241)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15206 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15206 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15207))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15207 "matrix formulation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15207 "Specific case of drug embedding in insoluble excipients (typically in a polymer) in order to achieve extended release.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15207 "Matrices can be monolithic or heterogeneous, dissolved or dispersed, or both."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15207 "This term also applies to a matrix made of hydrophilic substances, which, in contact with water, form a gel of high viscosity."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15207 goldbook:15183)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15207 goldbook:15239)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15207 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15207 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15208))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15208 "maximum additive concentration")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15208 "Maximum concentration of a drug, which will form a clear solution with a given concentration of surfactant.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15208 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15208 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15209))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15209 "maximum safe concentration")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15209 "Concentration of a drug in the plasma, above which side effects are likely to occur in a patient.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15209 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15209 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15210))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15210 "minimum effective plasma concentration")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15210 "Concentration of a drug that must be achieved in the plasma before any desired therapeutic or pharmacological effect can be obtained.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15210 "minimum therapeutic plasma concentration")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15210 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15210 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15211))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15211 "minimum inhibitory concentration")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15211 "Lowest concentration of an antibacterial drug necessary to inhibit the growth of a microorganism.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15211 "MIC")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15211 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15211 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15212))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15212 "modified release")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15212 "Release of a drug from a dosage form that it is not immediate (e.g., sustained release, retarded release, delayed-action preparations, controlled release, extended release, etc.).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15212 goldbook:15163)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15212 goldbook:15167)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15212 goldbook:15175)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15212 goldbook:15239)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15212 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15212 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15213))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15213 "moistening agents")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15213 "Usually water or low-molecular-weight alcohols or compounds, used in topical applications and in wet granulation, for the production of tablets.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15213 goldbook:15241)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15213 goldbook:15149)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15213 goldbook:15194)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15213 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15213 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15214))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15214 "multicompartment formulation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15214 "Dosage form (capsule, tablet) comprising several elements (e.g., microspheres or coated pellets) differing in the rate of drug release.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15214 goldbook:15175)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15214 goldbook:15159)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15214 goldbook:15161)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15214 goldbook:15241)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15214 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15214 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15215))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15215 "multilayer tablet")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15215 "Consists of several different layers that are compressed on top of each other, to form a single tablet composed of two or more layers.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15215 "Mainly used for incompatible substances and for sustained release."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15215 goldbook:15239)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15215 goldbook:15241)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15215 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15215 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15216))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15216 "nanoencapsulation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15216 "Formation of nanoparticles encapsulating a drug.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15216 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15216 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15217))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15217 "ointment")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15217 "Greasy, semi-solid preparation for external application, often anhydrous, containing dissolved or dispersed medicaments.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15217 goldbook:15172)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15217 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15217 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15218))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15218 "one-compartment model")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15218 "Kinetic model, where the whole body is thought of as a single compartment in which a substance is distributed rapidly, achieving an equilibrium between blood and tissue immediately.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15218 "In pharmacokinetics, the substance is a drug component which is assumed to be released from a dosage form and distributed instantly after absorption to reach an equilibrium between blood and tissues."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15218 goldbook:15175)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15218 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15218 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15219))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15219 "onset of drug action")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15219 "Time required to achieve the minimum effective plasma concentration following administration of the dosage form.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15219 goldbook:15143)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15219 goldbook:15175)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15219 goldbook:15210)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15219 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15219 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15220))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15220 "paste")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15220 "Ointment containing \\(\\gt \\pu{0\\%}\\) of powder, dispersed in a fatty base.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15220 goldbook:15217)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15220 goldbook:15172)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15220 goldbook:15227)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15220 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15220 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15221))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15221 "pellet")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15221 "Very small tablet or pilule. Implantable polymeric matrix. Spherical granule.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15221 goldbook:15193)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15221 goldbook:15207)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15221 goldbook:15241)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15221 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15221 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15222))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15222 "pelletisation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15222 "Process of agglomeration that converts fine powders or granules of bulk drugs and excipients into small, free-flowing, spherical, or semi-spherical units, referred to as pellets.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15222 "Pellets range typically between \\(\\pu{0.5 mm}\\) and \\(\\pu{1.5 mm}\\) in diameter."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15222 "The most widely used pelletization processes in the pharmaceutical industry are extrusion/spheronization, solution/suspension layering, and powder layering."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15222 goldbook:15221)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15222 goldbook:15193)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15222 goldbook:15227)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15222 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15222 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15223))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15223 "pharmaceutical equivalence")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15223 "To be pharmaceutically equivalent, the generic and proprietary formulations must (1) contain the same amount of active ingredient; (2) contain the same active ingredient in the same dosage form; (3) be intended for the same route of administration; and (4) generally be labeled for the same conditions of use.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15223 "It is not usually required that the generic and the reference drug contain the same excipients, or that the mechanism by which the active drug substance is released from the formulation be the same. But, the regulation authority approves the generic equivalent on the basis of certain in vitro and in vivo data."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15223 goldbook:15143)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15223 goldbook:15154)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15223 goldbook:15175)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15223 goldbook:15188)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15223 goldbook:15192)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15223 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15223 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15224))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15224 "pharmaceutics")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15224 "Science of preparation of drugs, dosage forms, and drug delivery systems taking into account the pharmacokinetics and pharmacodynamics of the drug as well as its physical and chemical properties.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15224 goldbook:15175)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15224 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15224 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15225))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15225 "polymorph")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15225 "Solid material that exists at least in two different molecular arrangements, i.e., distinctly different crystal species.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15225 "The differences between polymorphs disappear in solution or in the vapor phase."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15225 "Solubility, melting point, density, crystal shape, crystal structure, and some other physical properties often differ from one polymorph to the other."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15225 goldbook:15166)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15225 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15225 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15226))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15226 "powder grades")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15226 "Defined for powders used pharmaceutically, according to particle sizes.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15226 "It is required that when the fineness of a powder is described by a number, all particles must pass through a sieve with aperture diameter in microns equal to that number."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15226 goldbook:15227)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15226 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15226 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15227))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15227 "powder")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15227 "Dry solid material consisting of many, usually free flowing, fine particles. Conventionally, the title 'powder' should be restricted to powder mixes for internal use and alternative terms are used for other powdered formulations presented in this way, e.g., dusting powders, which are for external use.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15227 "powders")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15227 "The term \"powder\", when used to describe a dosage form, however, describes a formulation in which a drug powder has been mixed with other powdered excipients to produce the final product."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15227 goldbook:15179)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15227 goldbook:15188)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15227 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15227 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15228))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15228 "preformulation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15228 "Exploratory activity that begins early in pharmaceutics, involving studies designed to determine the compatibility of excipients with the active substance for a biopharmaceutical; physicochemical and bioanalytical investigation in support of promising experimental formulations.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15228 goldbook:15156)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15228 goldbook:15188)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15228 goldbook:15224)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15228 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15228 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15229))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15229 "pseudopolymorph")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15229 "Different crystalline form(s) of a solvated compound that differ in the identity and/or the stoichiometry of the solvating molecule.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15229 "pseudopolymorphs")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15229 goldbook:15166)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15229 goldbook:15234)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15229 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15229 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15230))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15230 "repeat action dosage form")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15230 "Tablet or capsule distinguished from a sustained-release dosage form, by the fact that it releases the medicinal agent, or part of it, at any time other than promptly after administration as opposed to a slow, controlled manner.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15230 "A repeat action tablet contains usually two doses of the drug, the first being released immediately following per-oral administration. The second dose is released later, when the layer of enteric coating is dissolved."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15230 goldbook:15241)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15230 goldbook:15159)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15230 goldbook:15185)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15230 goldbook:15145)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15230 goldbook:15239)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15230 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15230 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15231))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15231 "sieving")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15231 "Process that differentiates or separates solid particles according to their size using a meshed or perforated device.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15231 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15231 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15232))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15232 "slugging")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15232 "Method by which powder particles are compressed into a large tablet, called a slug, which is subsequently dry-screened and compressed into a tablet.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15232 goldbook:15227)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15232 goldbook:15241)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15232 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15232 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15233))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15233 "solubilising agents")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15233 "Additives making a substance soluble or more soluble, especially in water.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15233 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15233 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15234))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15234 "solvate")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15234 "Crystalline form of a compound in which one or more solvent molecules are part of the crystal structure.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15234 goldbook:15166)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15234 goldbook:15195)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15234 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15234 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15235))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15235 "spheronisation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15235 "Process of making dense, spherical pellets by means of special spheronizing or pelletizing equipment.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15235 goldbook:15221)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15235 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15235 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15236))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15236 "stent")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15236 "Scaffold placed into narrowed, diseased vessels (mainly coronary arteries) or a device implanted in a vessel used to help keep it open.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15236 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15236 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15237))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15237 "sublingual tablets")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15237 "Usually small, flat, and soft tablets, which are designed to be placed under the tongue to allow direct absorption of the active ingredient through the mucosa for systemic effect.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15237 goldbook:15241)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15237 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15237 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15238))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15238 "suppositories")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15238 "Dosage form, semi-solid, used for the administration of drugs via the rectal route, for systemic or local effect. When application is via other routes (e.g., the vaginal route), suppositories are termed differently, inserts, pessaries, etc.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15238 "The vehicles used in suppositories are of two types, i.e., fatty bases and water-soluble ones."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15238 "An important requirement for suppositories is a melting point (or disintegration/dissolution) at around \\(\\pu{{36}{-}{37} ^{\\circ}C}\\) so as to discharge the drug in the rectum."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15238 goldbook:15175)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15238 goldbook:15143)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15238 goldbook:15239)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15238 goldbook:15151)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15238 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15238 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15239))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15239 "sustained release")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15239 "Dosage form designed to release the drug contained therein at a continuous and controlled rate for a longer period of time that can normally be achieved with its conventional, nonsustained counterpart.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15239 "extended release")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15239 "gradual release")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15239 "long acting")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15239 "prolonged action")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15239 "slow release")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15239 "Per-oral administration of a single dose of a sustained-release product increases the duration of therapeutic action of the drug, beyond that achieved normally with a single dose of the corresponding non-sustained conventional counterpart."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15239 "Sustained-release injectables are also available."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15239 "Other terms used to describe the same concept include: \"controlled release\", \"extended release\", \"long-acting\", \"gradual release\", \"modified release\", \"prolonged action\", and \"slow release\"."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15239 goldbook:15175)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15239 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15239 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15240))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15240 "syrup")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15240 "Liquid preparation of high sugar concentration with or without medicinal and additional flavoring substances.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15240 "Syrup is a highly concentrated solution of sugar. Other polyols, such as glycerol or sorbitol, may be present to retard crystallization of sucrose or to increase the solubility of added ingredients."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15240 "When the syrup contains a medicinal substance, it is termed \"medicated syrup\"; and the syrup is diluted since USP syrup is close to a saturated solution. Although syrup tends (due to its very high [approximately \\(\\pu{85\\%}\\)] sucrose content) to resist mold or bacterial contamination, syrup may contain antimicrobial agents to prevent bacterial and mold growth."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15240 "It is often required to add a cosolvent or water to the medicated syrup in order to dissolve the drug."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15240 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15240 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15241))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15241 "tablet")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15241 "Solid dosage form compressed into a specific shape containing medicinal substances with or without suitable diluents.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15241 "pastille")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15241 "pellet")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15241 "pill")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15241 "troche")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15241 "Tablets may vary in shape, size, color and weight, and may be classified according to the method of manufacture, as molded tablet and compressed tablet."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15241 goldbook:15157)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15241 goldbook:15162)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15241 goldbook:15185)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15241 goldbook:15205)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15241 goldbook:15221)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15241 goldbook:15239)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15241 goldbook:15237)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15241 goldbook:15243)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15241 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15241 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15242))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15242 "tablet coating")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15242 "Solid layers based typically on cellulose derivatives and may include plasticizers and pigments. They are usually employed for one or more of the following reasons:  Protection of the ingredients (from light or moisture). Masking the bad taste of the drug. Masking possible batchwise differences in the appearance of raw materials and hence allaying possible patient concern over tablets of differing appearance. Coating confers mechanical strength and facilitates handling. Colored coating aids in the rapid identification of a product. Functional film coating is used to impart enteric or controlled-release properties to the tablet.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15242 goldbook:15163)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15242 goldbook:15185)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15242 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15242 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15243))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15243 "troche")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15243 "Applied to compressed lozenges. In lay language, lozenge and troche are used interchangeably.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15243 goldbook:15205)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15243 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-04-10-14)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15243 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15244))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15244 "acrylic polymer")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15244 "Polymer prepared from acrylic acid or a derivative of acrylic acid.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15244 "acrylate polymer")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15244 "acrylic")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15244 "polyacrylic")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15244 "An acrylic polymer formed from methacrylic acid and related monomers is often referred to as a methacrylic polymer or a polymethacrylic or a methacrylate polymer. Methacrylic polymers are a subclass of acrylic polymers."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15244 "The macromolecule of a regular acrylic homopolymer can be described by a constitutional repeating unit of general formula: \\(\\ce{-CR(X)-CH2\\bond{-}}\\), where \\(\\ce{R}\\) is \\(\\ce{COOH}\\), \\(\\ce{COOR^1}\\), \\(\\ce{CN}\\), or \\(\\ce{CONR^1R^2}\\) and \\(\\ce{X}\\) is \\(\\ce{H}\\), alkyl, aryl, heteroaryl, or \\(\\ce{CN}\\)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15244 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15244 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15245))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15245 "amino polymer")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15245 "Polymer prepared by polycondensation of an amino component such as amine or amide with an aldehyde, or by curing reactive oligomers prepared from an amino component and an aldehyde.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15245 "amide-aldehyde polymer")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15245 "amine-aldehyde polymer")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15245 "Formaldehyde is commonly used as the aldehyde and (a) melamine or (b) urea as the amino component. The resulting polymer is named (a) melamine polymer or melamineformaldehyde polymer, (b) urea polymer or urea-formaldehyde polymer."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15245 "A mixture of the reactive oligomers prepared by the condensation of an amino component with an aldehyde is, in a public (popular) use and technological practice, usually referred to as an amino resin, e.g., melamine-formaldehyde resin or urea-formaldehyde resin. Examples of the oligomers present in melamine-formaldehyde and ureaformaldehyde resins are: "^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15245 "Use of the term \"resin\" for cured reactive oligomers is discouraged; the cured resin should be named as an amino polymer."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15245 "An amino polymer is usually a network polymer. To form the polymer, polycondensation takes place at the hydroxymethyl groups of an amino resin. Examples of the network-structure motifs of that form are: "^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15245 "Melamine polymers can be regarded as a subclass of polytriazines."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15245 goldbook:15307)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15245 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15245 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15246))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15246 "coumarone-indene polymer")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15246 "Polymer prepared from a mixture containing 1-benzofuran (formerly coumarone) and indene.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15246 "1-benzofuran-indene polymer")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15246 "A mixture of coal-tar and gas-tar distillates is commonly used to prepare a coumaroneindene polymer."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15246 "A coumarone-indene polymer contains structural units such as: "^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15246 "Coumarone-indene polymers are film-forming materials."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15246 "Coumarone-indene polymers are sometimes, particularly in a public (popular) use and technological practice, called coumarone resins or coumarone-indene resins. Use of these terms is discouraged."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15246 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15246 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15247))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15247 "epoxy polymer")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15247 "Polymer prepared by reaction of compounds carrying two or more epoxy groups (reactive epoxides) with curing agents.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15247 "The reactive epoxides are commonly prepared by condensation of (chloromethyl)oxirane (commonly called epichlorohydrin) with a di- or multi-functional acid, alcohol, amine, or phenol, most often with 4,4′-(propane-2,2-diyl)diphenol (bisphenol A) to give in this case: "^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15247 "The reactive epoxide is cured by reactions with a di- or higher-functional amine, carboxylic acid, anhydride, or dicyandiamide (i.e., cyanoguanidine)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15247 "A reactive epoxide or a mixture of reactive epoxides, and also its admixture with curing agent or agents, is usually referred to as an epoxy resin, particularly in a public (popular) use and technological practice. Use of the term \"epoxy resin\" for a cured epoxide is discouraged; it should be named \"epoxy polymer\"."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15247 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15247 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15248))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15248 "furan polymer")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15248 "Polymer prepared from furan or a furan derivative.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15248 "The most widely used furan polymers are linear, branched, and network polymers prepared from (2-furyl)methanol, such as poly(furan-2,5-diylmethylene)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15248 "Furan polymers prepared from furan-2-carbaldehyde (formerly furfural), such as poly(furan-2,5-diylcarbonyl), are usually referred to as furfural polymers, and they are conjugated polymers. "^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15248 "Branching and network formation can occur through the condensation of methylene groups with terminal \\(\\ce{-CH2OH}\\) groups."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15248 "Comonomers such as phenols, aldehydes, and ketones are often used in preparation of furan polymers."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15248 "Use of the terms \"furan resin\" or \"furfural resin\" for \"furan polymer\" or \"furfural polymer\", respectively, is discouraged."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15248 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15248 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15249))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15249 "phenolic polymer")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15249 "Polymer prepared by the polycondensation of phenols and aldehydes or by curing reactive oligomers prepared from phenols and aldehydes.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15249 "phenol-aldehyde polymer")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15249 "A phenolic polymer is usually a network polymer."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15249 "Formaldehyde is commonly used as the aldehyde and (a) phenol itself, or (b) a cresol is used as the phenol. Phenol-formaldehyde polymer is a phenolic polymer resulting from the reaction of phenol with formaldehyde."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15249 "A mixture of the reactive oligomers prepared by the condensation of a phenol and aldehyde, and also its admixture with a curing agent is, in a public (popular) use and technological practice, usually referred to as a phenolic resin or a phenol-aldehyde resin."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15249 "Use of the term \"phenolic resin\" for cured reactive oligomers is discouraged; they should be called \"phenolic polymers\"."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15249 "A phenol-formaldehyde polymer prepared under alkaline conditions with an aldehydeto-phenol mole ratio between 1.5 and 3 is known as a resol. A resol spontaneously undergoes polycondensation at hydroxymethyl groups, to give a network, phenolformaldehyde polymer known as a resit. "^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15249 "A phenol-formaldehyde polymer prepared under acidic conditions with a formaldehyde-to-phenol molar ratio less then 1 is known as a novolak. A novolak can be cured with formaldehyde or a multifunctional reagent such as 1,3,5,7-tetraazaadamantane (hexamethylenetetramine) to give a network, phenol-formaldehyde polymer. "^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15249 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15249 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15250))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15250 "polybismaleimide")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15250 "Polymer prepared from a bismaleimide.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15250 "Bismaleimides are usually copolymerized with diamines, dicyanates, or aromatic diallyl derivatives."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15250 "A polybismaleimide is usually a branched polymer or, upon curing, a network polymer."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15250 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15250 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15251))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15251 "polycarborane")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15251 "Polymer prepared from a carborane.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15251 "A polycarborane is usually an ionic polymer."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15251 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15251 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15252))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15252 "polydiene")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15252 "Polymer prepared from a diene, or a substituted diene, or both in admixture.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15252 "A polydiene prepared from propadiene (allene) or a substituted propadiene (e.g., buta-1,2,-diene) is usually referred to as a polyallene or a polypropadiene (see the last two examples)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15252 "Commercially widely spread polydienes, namely, polybutadienes and polyisoprenes, are commonly named with a use of numerical prefixes based on the addition mode taking place during the transformation of a monomer molecule into monomeric unit. The names are, for example: 1,2-polybutadiene for poly(1-vinylethylene) since the addition takes place at only one double bond located between carbon atoms \\(\\ce{C^1}\\) and \\(\\ce{C^2}\\) of a buta-1,3-diene molecule and 1,4-polybutadiene for poly(but-1-ene-1,4-diyl) since the conjugative addition resulting in enchainment of a buta-1,3-diene molecule via carbon atoms \\(\\ce{C^1}\\) and \\(\\ce{C^4}\\) takes place in the polymerization process. Use of these names is discouraged because a nomenclature locant should always refer to a molecule structure feature and not to a process of the molecule formation."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15252 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15252 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15253))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15253 "polyisocyanate")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15253 "Polymer prepared from an isocyanate.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15253 "An isocyanate monomer can be transformed into polymers belonging to various structure-based classes, such as a polyisocyanurate (by cyclopolymerization), polycarbodiimide (by decarboxylation), polyurea (by reaction with water), or polycarbamate (by reaction with a diol or a polyol)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15253 goldbook:15273)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15253 goldbook:15274)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15253 goldbook:15285)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15253 goldbook:15308)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15253 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15253 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15254))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15254 "polyisocyanide")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15254 "Polymer prepared from an isocyanide.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15254 "The class name polyisocyanide is preferably used for polymers in which every isocyanide monomeric unit contributes only one atom to a macromolecule backbone; the majority of these polymers are helical polymers."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15254 "Isocyanide monomers are also polymerized by cyclopolymerization to give polytriazines."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15254 goldbook:15307)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15254 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15254 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15255))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15255 "polyolefin")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15255 "Polymer prepared from an olefin.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15255 "A typical polyolefin macromolecule is derived from an alkene and is described by the monomeric unit: \\(\\ce{-CR^1R^2\\bond{-}CH2\\bond{-}}\\), where \\(\\ce{R^1}\\) and \\(\\ce{R^2}\\) are hydrogen, alkyl, or cycloalkyl. Polyolefins with 1,2-disubstituted monomeric units \\(\\ce{-CHR^1\\bond{-}CHR^2\\bond{-}}\\) are rather rare, owing to low thermodynamic stability of their main chains caused by steric effects of the substituents."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15255 "The structure-based name of a polyolefin prepared from an alkene is a polyalkylene."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15255 goldbook:15265)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15255 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15255 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15256))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15256 "polyvinyl acetal")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15256 "Polymer prepared by acetalization of poly(vinyl alcohol) with an aldehyde.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15256 "The name \"polyvinyl acetal\" is derived using both source- and structure-based principles: \"polyvinyl\" comes from the source polymer: poly(vinyl alcohol), and \"acetal\" indicates the structure of constitutional units that are present in the resulting modified polymer. This approach is reflected in commonly used trivial names of polyvinyl acetals given in the above examples below systematic names."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15256 "A common polyvinyl acetal does not have the ideal structure shown above but it also contains a low fraction of unreacted hydroxy groups.  "^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15256 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15256 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15257))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15257 "polyvinyl ester")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15257 "Polymer prepared from a vinyl ester.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15257 "A molecule of a regular polyvinyl ester is described by the constitutional repeating unit:  where \\(\\ce{R}\\) is alkyl, aryl, or heteroaryl or substituted alkyl, substituted aryl, or substituted heteroaryl."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15257 "Polyvinyl esters are a subclass of vinyl polymers."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15257 goldbook:15262)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15257 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15257 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15258))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15258 "polyvinyl ether")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15258 "Polymer prepared from a vinyl ether.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15258 "A molecule of a regular polyvinyl ether is described by the constitutional repeating unit:  where \\(\\ce{R}\\) is alkyl, aryl, or heteroaryl or substituted alkyl, substituted aryl, or substituted heteroaryl."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15258 "Polyvinyl ethers are a subclass of vinyl polymers."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15258 goldbook:15262)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15258 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15258 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15259))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15259 "polyvinyl halide")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15259 "Polymer prepared from a vinyl halide (monohalogenoethene).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15259 "A molecule of a regular polyvinyl halide is described by the constitutional repeating unit: \\[\\ce{-[-CHX-CH2\\bond{-}]_{n}\\bond{-}}\\] where \\(\\ce{X}\\) is \\(\\ce{F}\\), \\(\\ce{Cl}\\), \\(\\ce{Br}\\), or \\(\\ce{I}\\)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15259 "Polyvinyl halides are a subclass of vinyl polymers."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15259 goldbook:15262)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15259 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15259 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15260))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15260 "polyvinyl ketone")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15260 "Polymer prepared from a vinyl ketone.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15260 "A molecule of a regular polyvinyl ketone is described by the constitutional repeating unit:  where \\(\\ce{R}\\) is alkyl, aryl, or heteroaryl or substituted alkyl, substituted aryl, or substituted heteroaryl."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15260 "Polyvinyl ketones are a subclass of vinyl polymers."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15260 goldbook:15262)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15260 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15260 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15261))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15261 "styrene polymer")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15261 "Polymer prepared from styrene, or a substituted styrene, or both in admixture.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15261 "polystyrene")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15261 "Macromolecule of a regular styrene homopolymer is described by the constitutional repeating unit:  where \\(\\ce{R^{\\upalpha}}\\) and \\(\\ce{R^1}\\) to \\(\\ce{R^5}\\) are each \\(\\ce{H}\\), alkyl, aryl, or heteroaryl."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15261 "Styrene polymers are a subclass of vinyl polymers."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15261 "In common usage, \"polystyrene\" means a polymer prepared from pure styrene, frequently cross-linked with 1,4-divinylbenzene, rather than a styrene polymer."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15261 goldbook:15262)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15261 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15261 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15262))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15262 "vinyl polymer")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15262 "Polymer prepared from a monomer containing the vinyl group \\(\\ce{-CH=CH2}\\).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15262 "Macromolecule of a regular vinyl homopolymer is described by the constitutional repeating unit: \\(\\ce{-CHR-CH2\\bond{-}}\\), where \\(\\ce{R}\\) is alkyl, aryl, heteroaryl, halogen, or a heteroatom containing pendent group."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15262 "Acrylic polymers, polyolefins, polyvinyl acetals, polyvinyl esters, polyvinyl ethers, polyvinyl halides, polyvinyl ketones, and styrene polymers, with \\(\\ce{R^{\\upalpha} = \\ce{H}}\\) are subclasses of vinyl polymers."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15262 goldbook:15244)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15262 goldbook:15255)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15262 goldbook:15256)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15262 goldbook:15257)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15262 goldbook:15258)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15262 goldbook:15259)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15262 goldbook:15260)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15262 goldbook:15261)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15262 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15262 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15263))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15263 "vinylidene polymer")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15263 "Polymer prepared from a monomer containing the ethene-1,1-diyl group \\(\\gt\\!\\ce{C=CH2}\\), formerly called vinylidene.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15263 "A macromolecule of a regular vinylidene polymer is described by the constitutional repeating unit: \\(\\ce{-CR^1R^2\\bond{-}CH2\\bond{-}}\\), where \\(\\ce{R^1}\\) and \\(\\ce{R^2}\\) are each alkyl, aryl, heteroaryl, or halogen, such as by the units: "^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15263 "Vinylidene is correctly defined as ethenylidene only, meaning a divalent attachment to the same atom of a senior group, i.e., it is the correct name for the group \\(\\ce{=C=CH2}\\) but not for the group \\(\\gt\\!\\ce{C=CH2}\\)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15263 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15263 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15264))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15264 "polyalkenylene")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15264 "Polymer composed of macromolecules containing exclusively alkene-α,ω-diyl (formerly alkenylene) constitutional repeating units: \\[\\ce{-[-CH=CH-[CH2]_{m}\\bond{-}]_{n}\\bond{-}}\\]")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15264 "Polyalkenylenes are sometimes referred to as polyalkenamers; use of this term is discouraged."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15264 "Polyvinylenes (\\(m = 0\\)) are excluded."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15264 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15264 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15265))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15265 "polyalkylene")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15265 "Polymer composed of macromolecules containing exclusively alkane-α,ω-diyl (formerly alkylene) constitutional repeating units: \\[\\ce{-[-CR^{1}R^{2}\\bond{-}]_{n}\\bond{-}}\\] where \\(\\ce{R^1}\\) and \\(\\ce{R^2}\\) are each hydrogen, alkyl, or cycloalkyl.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15265 "Polyolefins are the most common polyalkylenes."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15265 goldbook:15255)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15265 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15265 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15266))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15266 "polyalkynylene")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15266 "Polymer composed of macromolecules containing exclusively alkyne-α,ω-diyl (formerly alkynylene) constitutional repeating units: \\[\\ce{-[-C#C-[CH2]_m\\bond{-}]_n\\bond{-}}\\]")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15266 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15266 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15267))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15267 "polyamide")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15267 "Polymer composed of macromolecules containing carboxamide groups as linkages in the backbone: \\[\\ce{-NR-CO\\bond{-}}\\] where \\(\\ce{R}\\) is hydrogen, alkyl, aryl, or heteroaryl.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15267 "A polyamide containing, besides \\(\\ce{-NR-CO\\bond{-}}\\) linkages, exclusively aliphatic constitutional units is an aliphatic polyamide; examples are:  Trivial names of the type: polyamide \\(m\\) and polyamide \\(m,n\\) are only used for aliphatic polyamides. Polyamide \\(m\\) stands for a homopolymeric polyamide derived from an amino acid or a lactam comprising \\(m\\) carbon atoms; polyamide \\(m,n\\) stands for a copolymeric polyamide derived from an alkane-1,m-diamine containing \\(m\\) carbon atoms and an alkanedioic acid containing \\(n\\) carbon atoms (including those in \\(\\ce{CO}\\) groups)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15267 "A polyamide containing, besides \\(\\ce{-NR-CO\\bond{-}}\\) linkages, exclusively aromatic constitutional units is an aromatic polyamide commonly referred to as an aramide; example is: "^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15267 "A polyamide containing pendent carboxy groups is a polyamide acid commonly referred to as a polyamic acid."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15267 "A polymer containing only pendent amide groups is excluded, e.g., polyacrylamide."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15267 goldbook:15268)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15267 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15267 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15268))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15268 "polyamide acid")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15268 "Polyamide containing pendent carboxy groups:   where \\(\\ce{R}\\) is a constitutional unit with a connectivity three or higher.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15268 "polyamic acid")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15268 "A polyamide acid is mostly prepared as a processable precursor giving a polyimide upon thermal curing. The polyamide acid prepared from benzene-1,2:4,5-tetracarboxylic dianhydride (formerly pyromellitic anhydride) and hexane-1,6-diamine (formerly hexamethylenediamine) is an example of such a precursor: "^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15268 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15268 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15269))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15269 "polyamine")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15269 "Polymer composed of macromolecules containing imino groups as linkages in the backbone: \\[\\ce{-NR\\bond{-}}\\] where \\(\\ce{R}\\) is hydrogen, alkyl, aryl, or heteroaryl.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15269 "A polymer containing only pendent amino groups is excluded. However, in organic chemistry, low-molecular-weight compounds containing three or more amino groups are also called polyamines."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15269 "Quaternized polyamines have iminio linkages, \\(\\ce{-N^{+}R^{1}R^{2}\\bond{-}}\\), in the backbone (\\(\\ce{R^1}\\) and \\(\\ce{R^2}\\) are each hydrogen, or an alkyl, aryl, or heteroaryl group) and they are a structure-based subclass of ionenes."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15269 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15269 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15270))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15270 "polyanhydride")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15270 "Polymer composed of macromolecules containing carboxylic anhydride groupings as linkages in the backbone: \\[\\ce{-CO-O-CO\\bond{-}}\\]")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15270 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15270 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15271))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15271 "polybenzothiazole")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15271 "Polymer composed of macromolecules containing benzothiazole groups in the backbone, such as the groups:")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15271 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15271 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15272))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15272 "polybenzoxazole")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15272 "Polymer composed of macromolecules containing benzoxazole linkages in the backbone, such as the linkages:")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15272 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15272 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15273))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15273 "polycarbamate")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15273 "Polymer composed of macromolecules containing carbamate (formerly urethane) or N-substituted carbamate linkages in the backbone: \\[\\ce{-NR-CO-O\\bond{-}}\\] where \\(\\ce{R}\\) is hydrogen, alkyl, aryl, heteroaryl, substituted alkyl, substituted aryl, or substituted heteroaryl.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15273 "polyurethane")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15273 "A polymer containing only pendent carbamate (urethane) groups is excluded."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15273 "The commonly used class name polyurethane has been derived from the historic name urethane for ethyl carbamate."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15273 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15273 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15274))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15274 "polycarbodiimide")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15274 "Polymer composed of macromolecules containing carbodiimide linkages in the backbone: \\[\\ce{-N=C=N\\bond{-}}\\]")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15274 "A polymer containing only pendent carbodiimide linkages is excluded."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15274 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15274 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15275))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15275 "polycarbonate")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15275 "Polymer composed of macromolecules containing carbonate linkages in the backbone: \\[\\ce{-O-CO-O\\bond{-}}\\]")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15275 "A polymer containing only pendent carbonate linkages is excluded."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15275 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15275 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15276))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15276 "polycarbosilane")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15276 "Polymer composed of macromolecules containing carbon-silicon linkages in the backbone: \\[\\ce{-SiR^{1}R^{2}\\bond{-}CR^{3}R^{4}\\bond{-}}\\] where \\(\\ce{R^1}\\), \\(\\ce{R^2}\\), \\(\\ce{R^3}\\), and \\(\\ce{R^4}\\) are each hydrogen, alkyl, aryl, or heteroaryl.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15276 "A polycarbosilane containing, in addition to silanediyl groups, exclusively alkanediyl (formerly alkylene) or substituted alkanediyl constitutional repeating units is referred to as a polysilalkylene, whereas that involving exclusively arenediyl (formerly arylene) constitutional repeating units is referred to as a polysilarylene."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15276 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15276 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15277))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15277 "polycyanurate")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15277 "Polymer composed of macromolecules containing 1,3,5-triazine-2,4,6-triyltrioxy constitutional units (formerly cyanurate groups) in the backbone:")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15277 "Cyanurate is not an IUPAC approved name for 1,3,5-triazinetris(olate)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15277 "Polycyanurates are isomeric with polyisocyanurates."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15277 "Polycyanurates can be regarded as a subclass of polytriazines."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15277 goldbook:15285)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15277 goldbook:15307)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15277 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15277 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15278))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15278 "polyester")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15278 "Polymer composed of macromolecules containing carboxylic ester linkages in the backbone: \\[\\ce{-O-CO\\bond{-}}\\]")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15278 "A polyester comprising unsaturated constitutional units such as a polyester prepared from maleic anhydride or from but-2-yne-1,4-diol is referred to as an unsaturated polyester. "^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15278 "A polyester prepared from a polyol (typically a triol or tetrol), and a mixture of dicarboxylic anhydrides and fatty acids (e.g., linseed oil or tall oil) is referred to as an alkyd polymer or alkyd. Structure motifs of an alkyd polymer prepared from phthalic anhydride, glycerol, pentaerythritol [2,2-bis(hydroxymethyl)propane-1,3-diol], and fatty acids are shown below (MU stands for monomeric unit): "^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15278 "Polycarbonates, polythioesters, and unsaturated polyesters are subclasses of polyesters."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15278 "A polymer containing only pendent ester groups is excluded, for example, an acrylic polymer."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15278 goldbook:15275)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15278 goldbook:15244)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15278 goldbook:15306)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15278 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15278 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15279))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15279 "polyether")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15279 "Polymer composed of macromolecules containing ether linkages in the backbone: \\[\\ce{-O\\bond{-}}\\]")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15279 "Polyoxyalkylenes and polyoxyarylenes are subclasses of polyethers."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15279 "A polymer containing only pendent ether groups is excluded."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15279 goldbook:15288)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15279 goldbook:15289)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15279 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15279 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15280))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15280 "polygermane")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15280 "Polymer composed of macromolecules containing exclusively germanium atoms in the backbone: \\[\\ce{-[-GeR2\\bond{-}]_{n}\\bond{-}}\\] where \\(\\ce{R}\\) is alkyl, aryl or heteroaryl.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15280 "Polygermanes are sometimes referred to as polygermylenes. Use of this term is discouraged."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15280 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15280 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15281))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15281 "polyglutarimide")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15281 "Polymer composed of macromolecules containing glutarimide rings in the backbone:   where \\(\\ce{R}\\) is hydrogen or alkyl (usually methyl) and \\(\\ce{R^1}\\) is hydrogen, or an alkyl, aryl, or heteroaryl group.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15281 "A polyglutarimide is commonly prepared by modification of a poly(alkyl acrylate) with an amine, such as aniline, so it also contains residual acrylic units: "^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15281 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15281 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15282))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15282 "polyhydantoin")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15282 "Polymer composed of macromolecules containing hydantoin (imidazolidine-2,4-dione) rings in the backbone:   where \\(\\ce{R}\\) is hydrogen, or an alkyl, aryl, or heteroaryl group.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15282 "Polyhydantoins are a subclass of polyimides."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15282 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15282 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15283))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15283 "polyhydrazide")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15283 "Polymer composed of macromolecules containing hydrazide linkages in the backbone: \\[\\ce{-CO-NR^1\\bond{-}NR^2\\bond{-}CO\\bond{-}}\\] where \\(\\ce{R^1}\\) and \\(\\ce{R^2}\\) are each hydrogen, alkyl, aryl, or heteroaryl.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15283 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15283 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15284))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15284 "polyimidazole")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15284 "Polymer composed of macromolecules containing imidazole rings in the backbone:   where \\(\\ce{R^1}\\) and \\(\\ce{R^2}\\) are each hydrogen, or an alkyl or aryl group.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15284 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15284 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15285))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15285 "polyisocyanurate")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15285 "Polymer composed of macromolecules containing 2,4,6-trioxo-1,3,5-triazinane-1,3,5-triyl (formerly isocyanurate) rings in the backbone:")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15285 "An example of structure motifs of a polyisocyanurate is shown below: "^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15285 "Polyisocyanurates are isomeric with polycyanurates."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15285 goldbook:15277)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15285 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15285 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15286))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15286 "polyketone")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15286 "Polymer composed of macromolecules containing keto groups as linkages in the backbone: \\[\\ce{-CO\\bond{-}}\\]")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15286 "A polyketone containing in addition to keto groups also ether linkages in the main chains is usually referred to as a polyetherketone. "^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15286 "A polymer containing only pendent keto groups, such as a polyvinyl ketone, as well as a polymer containing main-chain carbonyl groups directly linked to a main-chain heteroatom, such as a polyester or a polyamide, is excluded."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15286 goldbook:15267)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15286 goldbook:15278)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15286 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15286 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15287))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15287 "polymetaloxane")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15287 "Organometallic polymer composed of macromolecules containing exclusively alternating metal and oxygen atoms in the main chain: \\[\\ce{-ML_{x}-O\\bond{-}}\\] where \\(\\ce{M}\\) is a metal atom such as \\(\\ce{Al}\\), \\(\\ce{Ge}\\), \\(\\ce{Sn}\\), or \\(\\ce{Ti}\\), and \\(\\ce{L}\\) is a metal-bonded substituent (ligand).")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15287 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15287 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15288))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15288 "polyoxyalkylene")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15288 "Polymer composed of macromolecules containing exclusively oxyalkane-α,ω-diyl (formerly oxyalkylene) constitutional repeating units in the backbone: \\[\\ce{-[-O-Y\\bond{-}]_{n}\\bond{-}}\\] where \\(\\ce{Y}\\) is an alkane-α,ω-diyl (formerly alkylene) or substituted alkane-α,ω-diyl group contributing at least two carbon atoms to the main chain.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15288 "An analog of polyoxyalkylene, for which \\(\\ce{Y}\\) is \\(\\ce{-CR2\\bond{-}}\\) (\\(\\ce{R = H}\\), alkyl, aryl, etc.) is a polyoxymethylene."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15288 "Polyoxyalkylenes are a subclass of polyethers."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15288 goldbook:15279)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15288 goldbook:15290)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15288 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15288 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15289))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15289 "polyoxyarylene")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15289 "Polymer composed of macromolecules containing exclusively oxyarenediyl (formerly oxyarylene) constitutional repeating units in the backbone: \\[\\ce{-[-O-Ar\\bond{-}]_{n}\\bond{-}}\\] where \\(\\ce{Ar}\\) is an arenediyl (formerly arylene), heteroarenediyl (formerly heteroarylene), substituted arenediyl or substituted heteroarenediyl.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15289 "Polyoxyarylenes are a subclass of polyethers."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15289 "A polyoxyarylene in which arenediyl is phenylene or a substituted phenylene is a polyoxyphenylene."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15289 goldbook:15279)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15289 goldbook:15291)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15289 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15289 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15290))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15290 "polyoxymethylene")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15290 "Polymer composed of macromolecules containing exclusively oxymethylene or substituted oxymethylene constitutional repeating units in the backbone:   where \\(\\ce{R^1}\\) and \\(\\ce{R^2}\\) are each hydrogen, alkyl, aryl, or heteroaryl.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15290 "polyacetal")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15290 "polyketal")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15290 "A polyoxymethylene is also referred to as a polyacetal, polyketal, or acetal resin. Use of the last term is discouraged."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15290 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15290 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15291))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15291 "polyoxyphenylene")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15291 "Polymer composed of macromolecules containing exclusively oxyphenylene or ring-substituted oxyphenylene constitutional repeating units in the backbone:   where \\(\\ce{R^1}\\), \\(\\ce{R^2}\\), \\(\\ce{R^3}\\), and \\(\\ce{R^4}\\) are each hydrogen or an alkyl, aryl, or aralkyl group.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15291 "Polyoxyphenylenes are a subclass of polyoxyarylenes as well as a subclass of polyethers."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15291 goldbook:15279)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15291 goldbook:15289)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15291 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15291 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15292))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15292 "polyparabanic acid")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15292 "Polymer composed of macromolecules containing imidazolidine-2,4,5-trione (parabanic acid) rings in the backbone:")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15292 "Polyparabanic acids are a subclass of polyimides."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15292 "Parabanic acid is not an IUPAC-approved name for imidazolidine-2,4,5-trione."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15292 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15292 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15293))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15293 "polyphenylenemethylene")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15293 "Polymer composed of macromolecules containing exclusively alternating phenylene or substituted phenylene and methylene or substituted methylene constitutional units in the backbone:   where \\(\\ce{R^1}\\), \\(\\ce{R^2}\\), \\(\\ce{R^3}\\), \\(\\ce{R^4}\\), \\(\\ce{R^5}\\), and \\(\\ce{R^6}\\) are each hydrogen, alkyl, aryl, halogen, trialkylsilyl, etc.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15293 "Polyphenylenemethylenes were also referred to as polybenzyls; this name is obsolete and strongly discouraged."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15293 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15293 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15294))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15294 "polyphosphate")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15294 "Polymer composed of macromolecules containing phosphate constitutional repeating units:   where \\(\\ce{R}\\) is hydrogen, alkyl, aryl, or heteroaryl.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15294 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15294 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15295))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15295 "polyphosphazene")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15295 "Polymer composed of macromolecules containing exclusively nitrilophosphanylylidene (formerly phosphazene) constitutional repeating units in the backbone:   where \\(\\ce{R^1}\\) and \\(\\ce{R^2}\\) are each a monovalent group, such as a halogen or an alkoxy group.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15295 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15295 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15296))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15296 "polypyrrone")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15296 "Polymer composed of single strand or ladder macromolecules comprising isoindolo[2,1-a]benzimidazole (formerly pyrrone) constitutional repeating units such as:  where \\(\\ce{Z}\\) is a divalent linking group or atom.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15296 "polybenzimidazolimides")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15296 "polybenzimidazolones")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15296 "polybenzimidazopyrrolones")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15296 "polyimidazopyrrolones")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15296 "polyisoindolobenzimidazole")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15296 "polyisoindolobenzimidazoles")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15296 "Polypyrrones are also referred to as polybenzimidazolimides, polybenzimidazolones, polybenzimidazopyrrolones, polybenzoylenebenzimidazoles (usage strongly discouraged), polyimidazopyrrolones, and polyisoindolobenzimidazoles."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15296 "Pyrrone is not an IUPAC approved name."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15296 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15296 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15297))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15297 "polyquinoline")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15297 "Polymer composed of macromolecules containing quinoline moieties in the backbone:")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15297 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15297 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15298))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15298 "polyquinoxaline")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15298 "Polymer composed of macromolecules containing quinoxaline groups in the backbone:")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15298 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15298 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15299))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15299 "polysilazane")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15299 "Polymer composed of macromolecules containing exclusively alternating nitrogen and silicon atoms in the backbone: \\[\\ce{-[-NR^{1}\\bond{-}SiR^{2}\\!\\,R^{3}\\bond{-}]_{n}\\bond{-}}\\] where \\(\\ce{R^1}\\), \\(\\ce{R^2}\\), and \\(\\ce{R^3}\\) are each hydrogen or an alkyl or aryl group.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15299 "Polysilazanes can comprise both silicon and nitrogen branching points, the former being formed from ammonia and the latter from, for example, alkyltrichlorosilanes or tetrachlorosilane used as monomers:  where \\(\\ce{R^1}\\), \\(\\ce{R^2}\\), and \\(\\ce{R^3}\\) are each hydrogen or an alkyl or aryl group."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15299 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15299 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15300))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15300 "polysiloxane")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15300 "Polymer composed of macromolecules containing alternating oxygen and silicon atoms in the backbone: \\[\\ce{-[-O\\bond{-}SiR^{1}\\!\\,R^{2}\\bond{-}]_{n}\\bond{-}}\\] where \\(\\ce{R^1}\\) and \\(\\ce{R^2}\\) are each hydrogen or an alkyl or aryl group.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15300 "polyoxysilylenes")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15300 "silicones")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15300 "Polysiloxanes are often referred to as silicones or polyoxysilylenes. Use of the last term is discouraged."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15300 "Polysilsesquioxanes are a subclass of polysiloxanes."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15300 goldbook:15301)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15300 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15300 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15301))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15301 "polysilsesquioxane")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15301 "Polymer composed of macromolecules containing silicon and oxygen atoms in the ratio \\(1{:}1.5\\) (ideal ratio for infinite macromolecule), which alternate in a hyperbranched or ladder structure such as:   where \\(\\ce{R}\\) is alkyl, aryl, or heteroaryl.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15301 "The ideal value of the \\(\\ce{O{:}Si}\\) ratio of \\(1.5{:}1\\) is achieved only in the case of a ladder polymer. For hyperbranched polysilsesquioxanes, the value of the \\(\\ce{O{:}Si}\\) ratio is higher."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15301 "Polysilsesquioxanes are a subclass of polysiloxanes."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15301 goldbook:15300)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15301 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15301 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15302))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15302 "polystannane")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15302 "Polymer composed of macromolecules containing exclusively tin atoms in the backbone: \\[\\ce{-[-SnR^{1}\\!\\,R^{2}\\bond{-}]_{n}\\bond{-}}\\] where \\(\\ce{R^1}\\) and \\(\\ce{R^2}\\) are each hydrogen or an alkyl or aryl group.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15302 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15302 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15303))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15303 "polysulfonamide")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15303 "Polymer composed of macromolecules containing sulfonamide linkages in the backbone: \\[\\ce{-SO2-NR\\bond{-}}\\] where \\(\\ce{R}\\) is hydrogen or an alkyl, aryl, or heteroaryl group.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15303 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15303 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15304))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15304 "polysulfone")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15304 "Polymer composed of macromolecules containing sulfonyl linkages in the backbone: \\[\\ce{-SO2\\bond{-}}\\]")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15304 "Polysulfones that also comprise ether linkages in the backbone are more exactly classified as polyethersulfones. Similarly, other subclasses of polysulfones can be derived."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15304 "Polysulfonamides and polysulfonates are excluded."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15304 goldbook:15303)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15304 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15304 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15305))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15305 "polythioester")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15305 "Polymer composed of macromolecules containing thiocarboxylate (thioester) linkages in the backbone:\\(\\ce{-S-CO\\bond{-}}\\) or \\(\\ce{-O-CS\\bond{-}}\\) or \\(\\ce{-S-CS\\bond{-}}\\)")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15305 "A polymer containing only pendent thioester groups is excluded."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15305 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15305 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15306))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15306 "polythioether")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15306 "Polymers composed of macromolecules containing thioether (sulfide) linkages in the backbone: \\[\\ce{-S\\bond{-}}\\]")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15306 "A polymer containing only pendent thioether groups is excluded."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15306 "A polymer with sulfanediylalkan-α,ω-diyl (formerly thioalkylene), sulfanediylarenediyl (formerly thioarylene), sulfanediylmethylene, or sulfanediylphenylene constitutional repeating units is classified more narrowly as a polythioalkylene, polythioarylene, polythiomethylene, or polythiophenylene."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15306 "A polymer with \\(\\ce{S_{x}} (x \\gt 1)\\) linkages is a polysulfide."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15306 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15306 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15307))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15307 "polytriazine")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15307 "Polymer composed of macromolecules containing triazine rings in the backbone:")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15307 "A polytriazine is usually a branched or network polymer: "^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15307 "A polycyanurate and an amino polymer prepared from 1,3,5-triazine-2,4,6-triamine (trivial name: melamine) are excluded; however, these polymers can be regarded as subclasses of polytriazines."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15307 "A molecule of a typical polytriazine contains 1,3,5-triazine rings, however, polytriazines containing 1,2,4-triazine rings and, less likely, 1,2,3-triazine rings are also possible."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15307 goldbook:15245)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15307 goldbook:15277)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15307 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15307 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15308))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15308 "polyurea")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15308 "Polymer composed of macromolecules containing ureylene or N-substituted ureylene linkages in the backbone: \\[\\ce{-NR-CO-NR\\bond{-}}\\] where \\(\\ce{R}\\) is hydrogen, alkyl, aryl, heteroaryl, substituted alkyl, substituted aryl, or substituted heteroaryl.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15308 "polyureylene")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15308 "An amino polymer prepared from urea and an aldehyde is excluded."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15308 "A polymer containing only pendent ureylene groups is excluded."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15308 goldbook:15245)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15308 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15308 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15309))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15309 "cardo polymer")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15309 "Polymer composed of macromolecules consisting of a single-strand main chain and many ring units, each having one atom in common with the main chain.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15309 "A cardo polymer can be represented graphically as follows: "^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15309 "A cardo polymer can also be defined as a polymer composed of macromolecules containing loop-like cyclic side groups, one ring atom of which is part of the backbone."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15309 "The adjective \"cardo\" is derived from the Latin word for heart because the cyclic unit, together with adjacent parts of the main chain, resembles the shape of a heart with arteries."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15309 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15309 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15310))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15310 "catenane polymer")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15310 "Polymer composed of macromolecules consisting of physically catenated macrorings that have no atom in common and cannot be separated unless chemical bonds are broken.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15310 "A catenane polymer can be graphically represented as follows: "^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15310 "A catenane-polymer main chain resembles a jewelry or technical chain of physically interlocked rings."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15310 "A catenane polymer can be a linear, branched, or network polymer."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15310 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15310 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15311))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15311 "helical polymer")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15311 "Polymer composed of macromolecules that adopt partly or completely a helical conformation.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15311 "Biopolymers such as nucleic acids, amylose, and some proteins are typical helical polymers."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15311 "A helical structure is generated by regularly repeating rotations around the backbone bonds of a linear macromolecule."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15311 doi:10.1351/PAC-REC-08-01-30)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15311 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15312))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15312 "activity coefficient at infinite dilution")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15312 "For a substance \\(\\ce{B}\\), activity coefficient \\(f_{\\ce{B}}\\) extrapolated to infinite dilution: \\[\\ln (f_{\\ce{B}}^{\\infty}) = \\lim \\limits_{x_{\\ce{B}} \\to 0} (\\frac{\\mu_{\\ce{B}} - \\mu_{\\ce{B}}^{\\ast}}{RT} - \\ln x_{\\ce{B}})\\]")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15312 "Useful for dilute mixtures as an alternative to the standard chemical potential on a molality basis."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15312 "The relation between the activity coefficient at infinite dilution and the standard chemical potentials is, for a solute \\(\\ce{B}\\) in a solvent \\(\\ce{A}\\), \\[\\ln f_{\\ce{B}}^{\\infty} = \\frac{\\mu_{m,\\ce{B}}^{_{^⦵\\!}} - \\mu_{\\ce{B}}^{\\ast}}{RT} - \\ln (M_{\\ce{A}}m_{\\ce{B}}^{_{^⦵\\!}})\\] where \\(M_{\\ce{A}}\\) is the molar mass of the solvent."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15312 goldbook:15333)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15312 goldbook:16270)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15312 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15312 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15313))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15313 "analytical method")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15313 "Class of experimental procedures for solubility determination in which a saturated solution is prepared and then analyzed to determine composition.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15313 goldbook:15364)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15313 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15313 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15314))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15314 "aquamolality")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15314 "For a solute \\(\\ce{B}\\) in a system containing solvent \\(\\ce{A}\\) and a reference solvent \\(\\ce{C}\\), \\[m_{\\ce{B}}^{(\\ce{C})} = m_{\\ce{B}} \\overline M/M_{\\ce{C}}\\] where \\(m_{\\ce{B}}\\) is the molality of \\(\\ce{B}\\), \\(M_{\\ce{C}}\\) is the molar mass of a reference component, and \\(\\overline{M}\\) is the average molar mass of a mixed solvent, defined for a system containing two solvents as \\[\\overline M = x_{ u,\\ce{A}} M_{\\ce{A}} + (1 - x_{ u,\\ce{A}}) M_{\\ce{C}}\\] the solvent amount fraction of solvent \\(\\ce{A}\\).")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15314 "solvomolality")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15314 "Used most frequently in discussing comparative solubilities in water (\\(\\ce{C}\\)) and heavy water (\\(\\ce{A}\\)) and their mixtures, but applies to any reference component, where solvomolality is a more appropriate term."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15314 goldbook:15376)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15314 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15314 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15315))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15315 "azeotropic point")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15315 "For a mixture, temperature and pressure (the azeotropic temperature and pressure) at which the compositions of the liquid and vapor phases become equal (the azeotropic composition), but the intensive properties of the two phases (such as molar volume) are different.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15315 "azeotrope")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15315 goldbook:16270)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15315 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15315 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15316))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15316 "binary system")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15316 "System containing two components.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15316 goldbook:16268)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15316 goldbook:15332)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15316 goldbook:15366)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15316 goldbook:15368)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15316 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15316 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15317))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15317 "Bunsen coefficient")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15317 "Volume \\(V^{\\rm{g}}\\) of an amount \\(n_{\\ce{B}}^{\\rm{l}}\\) of a gas dissolved at a given standard temperature \\(T^{^⦵\\!}\\) (usually \\(\\pu{273.15 K}\\)) and given standard (partial) pressure \\(p_{\\ce{B}}^{_{^⦵\\!}}\\) (\\(\\pu{1 bar} = \\pu{0.1 MPa}\\) or, in older literature, \\(\\pu{1 atm}\\)) divided by the volume of the solvent \\(V^{\\rm{l}}\\) containing an amount \\(n_{\\ce{A}}\\) of solvent at temperature \\(T\\) and the given total pressure \\(p^{_{^⦵\\!}}\\).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15317 "There are two Bunsen coefficients, depending on whether the liquid is the equilibrium solution or the pure liquid, with mathematical definitions:- Bunsen coefficient, solution reference \\(\\alpha_{\\ce{B}} = V^{\\rm{g}}(T^{^⦵\\!}, p^{_{^⦵\\!}}, n_{\\ce{B}}^{1})/V^{\\rm{l}}(T, p^{_{^⦵\\!}}, n_{\\ce{A}}, n_{\\ce{B}}^{1})\\)- Bunsen coefficient, pure solvent reference \\(\\alpha_{\\ce{B}}^{\\ast} = V^{\\rm{g}}(T^{^⦵\\!}, p^{_{^⦵\\!}}, n_{\\ce{B}}^{1})/V^{\\rm{l}}(T, p^{_{^⦵\\!}}, n_{\\ce{A}})\\)where \\(n_{\\ce{B}}^{\\rm{l}}\\) is the amount of dissolved gas in the liquid solution."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15317 "The relations between the molality \\(m_{\\ce{B}}(p^{_{^⦵\\!}})\\) or mole fraction \\(x_{\\ce{B}}(p^{_{^⦵\\!}})\\) of dissolved gas and the Bunsen coefficients are \\[\\begin{array}{l} \\frac{1}{x_{\\ce{B}}(p^{_{^⦵\\!}})} = 1 + \\frac{1}{m_{\\ce{B}}(p^{_{^⦵\\!}})M_{\\ce{A}}} = 1 + \\frac{RT^{^⦵\\!}Z_{\\ce{B}}^{^⦵\\!}(T^{^⦵\\!})}{p^{_{^⦵\\!}}V_{\\ce{A}}\\alpha_{\\ce{B}}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{x_{\\ce{B}}(p^{_{^⦵\\!}})} = 1 + \\frac{1}{m_{\\ce{B}}(p^{_{^⦵\\!}})M_{\\ce{A}}} = 1 + \\frac{RT^{^⦵\\!}Z_{\\ce{B}}^{^⦵\\!}(T^{^⦵\\!})}{p^{_{^⦵\\!}}V_{m,\\ce{A}}\\alpha_{\\ce{B}}} \\end{array}\\] where \\(V_{\\ce{A}}\\), \\(V_{m,{\\ce{A}}}\\) are the respective partial molar volume and molar volume of the solvent and \\(Z_{\\ce{B}}\\) is the compression factor of the gas."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15317 "The Bunsen coefficient and the related quantities for expression of gas solubility; absorption coefficient, Kuenen coefficient, and Ostwald coefficient appear frequently in the older literature of gas solubility determination. However, the modern practice, recommended here, is to express gas solubility as molality, mole fraction, or mole ratio."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15317 goldbook:15374)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15317 goldbook:15377)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15317 goldbook:15376)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15317 goldbook:15341)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15317 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15317 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15318))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15318 "Clarke–Glew equation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15318 "Semi-empirical equation describing the temperature dependence of the standard Gibbs energy of solution, \\[\\Delta_{\\rm{sln}}G^{^⦵\\!}(T, p^{_{^⦵\\!}})/RT = A_{0} + A_{1}(T_{\\rm{ref}}/T) + A_{2}\\ln(T/T_{\\rm{ref}}) + A_{3}(T/T_{\\rm{ref}}) + A_{4}(T/T_{\\rm{ref}})^{2} + \\ldots\\] where the \\(A_{i}\\) are constants that can be related to thermodynamic quantities (but subject to uncertainty because of statistical correlations among the fitting coefficients) and \\(T_{\\rm{ref}}\\) is a reference temperature.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15318 goldbook:15319)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15318 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15318 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15319))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15319 "Clarke–Glew–Weiss equation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15319 "Clarke–Glew equation with \\(T_{\\rm{ref}} = \\pu{100 K}\\).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15319 goldbook:15318)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15319 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15319 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15320))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15320 "coexistence curve")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15320 "Boundary of stable phase separation (limits of solubility) in a liquid or solid system of two or more components.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15320 "binodal curve")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15320 "conodal curve")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15320 "The locus of the compositions of two co-existing phases on a phase diagram."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15320 "In a binary system, a plot of experimental variables such as temperature or pressure, or of theoretical variables such as Gibbs energy, against mole fraction displays the coexistence curve. In ternary or higher-order systems, coexistence curves are displayed on a plot of composition at constant temperature or pressure, usually on a ternary diagram."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15320 goldbook:15316)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15320 goldbook:16268)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15320 goldbook:15321)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15320 goldbook:15332)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15320 goldbook:15376)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15320 goldbook:15366)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15320 goldbook:15365)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15320 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15320 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15321))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15321 "conjugate phases")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15321 "Two phases of variable composition in mutual thermodynamic equilibrium.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15321 goldbook:15320)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15321 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15321 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15322))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15322 "critical index")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15322 "Index in the basic equation describing a coexistence curve \\[\\beta = \\lim \\limits_{T \\to T_{\\rm{c}}} \\left(\\frac{\\partial \\ln (x'' - x')}{\\partial \\ln \\vert T - T_{\\rm{c}}\\vert} \\right)\\] where \\(x''\\), \\(x'\\) are the mole fractions of one component in the respective concentrated and dilute phases and \\(T_{\\rm{c}}\\) is the critical solution temperature.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15322 goldbook:15320)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15322 goldbook:16268)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15322 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15322 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15323))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15323 "data")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15323 "Experimental results, often numerical.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15323 "The term is plural; its singular form is datum."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15323 "Data directly obtained from experimental apparatus may be referred to as raw data. Raw data may be subjected to numerical operations (unit conversions, etc.) to give transformed data, which maintain a point-for-point correspondence with the raw data. However, the use of the term \"data\" to refer to the results of numerical modeling operations or other elaborate calculations is controversial and discouraged. The latter are better referred to as \"results\" and, when presented graphically, are usually represented by smooth lines."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15323 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15323 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15324))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15324 "dystectic reaction")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15324 "Isobaric, reversible melting or dissolution with either complete or partial dissociation on heating of a solid compound, \\(\\ce{A_{\\rm{a}}B_{\\rm{b}}}\\), formed by components \\(\\ce{A}\\) and \\(\\ce{B}\\) \\[\\ce{A_{\\rm{a}}B_{\\rm{b}}(s)  A_{\\rm{a}}B_{\\rm{b}}(l)  {\\rm{a}}A(l) + {\\rm{b}}B(l)}\\] where the forward arrows indicate the direction of heating.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15324 "congruent melting")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15324 "indifferent melting")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15324 "The dystectic temperature is a maximum (\\({\\rm{d}}T/{\\rm{d}}x = 0\\)) of the melting temperature-composition curve. The dystectic point is the isobarically invariant maximum at the dystectic composition and dystectic temperature, where the compositions of the liquid and solid phases are equal. The composition of a non-stoichiometric compound is also equal to that of the melt at the dystectic temperature and composition."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15324 "From Greek δύστηκτος, difficult (or highest) melting."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15324 "Occasionally, a similar reaction takes place in the subsolidus region. Quite appropriately, it is called a dystectoid reaction."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15324 goldbook:16268)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15324 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15324 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15325))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15325 "dystonic reaction")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15325 "Reversible dissolution in an isothermal, isobaric system of three or more components characterized by dissolution and saturation with a stoichiometric compound consisting of two or more of these components. The equilibrium process is, for example, \\[\\ce{AB.p H2O  A(aq, sat) + B(aq, sat) + p H2O(l)}\\]")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15325 "The chemical potential of solvent and consequently its partial pressure reaches a maximum value at the dystonic composition or point, which is isothermally and isobarically invariant."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15325 "Dystonic points have been detected in aqueous media only."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15325 "From Greek δύστονος, difficult (highest) tension (vapor pressure)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15325 goldbook:16268)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15325 goldbook:15327)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15325 goldbook:15344)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15325 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15325 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15326))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15326 "eutectoid reaction")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15326 "Isothermal reversible reaction of a solid mixture phase \\(\\upgamma\\) which is transformed into two (or more) different solid (pure, binary compound or mixture) phases \\(\\upalpha\\) and \\(\\upbeta\\) during the cooling of a system. In a binary system, \\[\\ce{\\upgamma  \\upalpha + \\upbeta}\\] where the forward arrow indicates the direction of cooling. The equilibrium reaction occurs along the eutectoid line at the eutectoid temperature. At the eutectoid composition, the compositions of the high temperature solid phase and the mechanical mixture of the low-temperature solid phases are equal, and intermediate to the compositions of the pure solid phases \\(\\upalpha\\) and \\(\\upbeta\\). This composition and the eutectoid temperature, which are isobaric invariants of the system, define the eutectoid point.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15326 "Derived from Greek and Latin, meaning \"resembling a eutectic\"."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15326 goldbook:15316)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15326 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15326 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15327))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15327 "eutonic reaction")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15327 "Reversible dissolution in a system of three or more components characterized by the composition of a solution that is simultaneously saturated with respect to all (at least two or more) dissolved solutes. The two simultaneous equilibrium processes are, for example, \\[\\begin{array}{l}\\ce{A.p H2O  A{(aq, sat)} + p H2O(l)} \\\\ \\ce{B.q H2O  B{(aq, sat)} + q H2O(l)}\\end{array}\\]")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15327 "(isothermally and isobarically invariant) reaction of double saturation")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15327 "isothermally invariant reaction")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15327 "The eutonic point is invariant in a ternary system at a given temperature and pressure."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15327 "The chemical potential of solvent decreases along the two solubility curves that intersect at the eutonic point, and thus reaches a minimum value at that point. Thus, colligative properties (that depend on solvent activity) reach a minimum value at the eutonic point. For example, if the solutes are nonvolatile and the solvent is volatile, the vapor pressure reaches a minimum value."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15327 "Eutonic points have been detected in aqueous media only."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15327 "From Greek ευτονος, easy (or lowest) tension (or vapor pressure)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15327 goldbook:16268)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15327 goldbook:15344)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15327 goldbook:15366)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15327 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15327 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15328))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15328 "fitting equation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15328 "Theoretically based or empirical equation for interpolation of data over a range of temperature, pressure, composition, or other variable.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15328 "smoothing equation")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15328 "The use of a fitting equation for extrapolation of data beyond the equation’s known range of validity is a potential source of extreme error."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15328 goldbook:15323)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15328 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15328 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15329))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15329 "Gibbs–Duhem equation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15329 "Equation relating the intensive variables \\(T\\), \\(p\\) and the \\(C\\) chemical potentials \\(\\mu_{i}\\) in a phase \\[S{\\rm{d}}T - V{\\rm{d}}p + \\sum \\limits_{i=1}^{C} n_{i} {\\rm{d}}\\mu_{i} = 0\\] where \\(C\\) is the total number of components, \\(i\\) in a phase.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15329 "Note that the variables in this equation are the intensive quantities \\(T\\), \\(p\\) and \\(\\mu_{i}\\)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15329 "The Gibbs–Duhem equation may be written in terms of intensive quantities, \\[\\sum \\limits_{i=1}^{C} n_{i}(S_{i}{\\rm{d}}T - V_{i}{\\rm{d}}p + {\\rm{d}}\\mu_{i}) = 0\\] where \\(S_{i}\\), \\(V_{i}\\), \\(x_{i}\\) are the respective partial molar entropy, partial molar volume, and mole fraction of component \\(i\\)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15329 "There is a Gibbs–Duhem equation for each phase in a system exhibiting multiphase equilibria. Application of the conditions for an equilibrium state leads to the phase rule as one example of the application of this equation. When equilibrium conditions are applied, \\(T\\), \\(p\\) and \\(\\mu\\) are equal in all phases of an equilibrated system, while \\(S_{i}\\), \\(V_{i}\\), and \\(x_{i}\\) are not."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15329 goldbook:16268)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15329 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15329 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15330))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15330 "Gibbs energy of transfer")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15330 "Change in Gibbs energy at a given temperature and pressure for transfer of a substance between two different phases.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15330 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15330 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15331))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15331 "Gibbs–Konovalov equations")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15331 "Pair of equations for a binary mixture of components \\(\\ce{A}\\) and \\(\\ce{B}\\) that relate the variables \\(T\\), \\(p\\), in one phase of variable composition, \\(\\upalpha\\), to the variables \\(T\\), \\(p\\), in a coexisting equilibrium phase of variable composition, \\(\\upbeta\\): \\[\\begin{array}{c} -\\frac{\\left(1 - x_{\\ce{B}}^{\\beta} \\right)\\Delta_{\\alpha}^{\\beta} H_{\\ce{A}} + x_{\\ce{B}}^{\\beta} \\Delta_{\\alpha}^{\\beta} H_{\\ce{B}}}{T}{\\rm{d}}T + \\left[\\left(1 - x_{\\ce{B}}^{\\beta} \\right)\\Delta_{\\alpha}^{\\beta}V_{\\ce{A}} + x_{\\ce{B}}^{\\beta}\\Delta_{\\alpha}^{\\beta}V_{\\ce{B}} \\right]{\\rm{d}}p +\\left(x_{\\ce{B}}^{\\alpha} - x_{\\ce{B}}^{\\beta} \\right)\\left(\\frac{\\partial^{2} G_{\\rm{m}}^{\\alpha}}{\\partial x_{\\ce{B}}^{\\alpha 2}} \\right)_{T,p} {\\rm{d}}x_{\\ce{B}}^{\\alpha} = 0 \\\\ -\\frac{\\left(1 - x_{\\ce{B}}^{\\alpha} \\right)\\Delta_{\\alpha}^{\\beta} H_{\\ce{A}} + x_{\\ce{B}}^{\\alpha} \\Delta_{\\alpha}^{\\beta} H_{\\rm{B}}}{T}{\\rm{d}}T + \\left[\\left(1 - x_{\\ce{B}}^{\\alpha} \\right)\\Delta_{\\alpha}^{\\beta}V_{\\ce{A}} + x_{\\ce{B}}^{\\alpha}\\Delta_{\\alpha}^{\\beta}V_{\\ce{B}} \\right]{\\rm{d}}p +\\left(x_{\\ce{B}}^{\\alpha} - x_{\\ce{B}}^{\\beta} \\right)\\left(\\frac{\\partial^{2} G_{\\rm{m}}^{\\alpha}}{\\partial x_{\\ce{B}}^{\\beta 2}} \\right)_{T,p} {\\rm{d}}x_{\\ce{B}}^{\\beta} = 0 \\end{array}\\] where \\(\\Delta_{\\upalpha}^{\\upbeta} H_{\\ce{A}} = H_{\\ce{A}}^{\\upbeta} - H_{\\ce{A}}^{\\upalpha}\\), \\(\\Delta_{\\upalpha}^{\\upbeta} V_{\\ce{A}} = V_{\\ce{A}}^{\\upbeta} - V_{\\ce{A}}^{\\upalpha}\\) are the enthalpy and volume of transfer of component \\(\\ce{A}\\) from phase \\(\\upalpha\\) to phase \\(\\upbeta\\), and similarly for component \\(\\ce{B}\\).")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15331 "Gibbs–Konovalow equations")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15331 "van der Waals’ equations")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15331 "\\(\\left(\\frac{\\partial^{2} G_{\\rm{m}}}{\\partial x_{\\ce{B}}^{2}} \\right)_{T,p} \\gt 0\\) (condition for diffusional stability). This quantity may also be expressed in terms of the derivatives of the chemical potentials, using \\[\\left(\\frac{\\partial^{2} G_{\\rm{m}}}{\\partial x_{\\ce{B}}^{2}} \\right)_{T,p} = -\\frac{1}{x_{\\ce{B}}} \\left(\\frac{\\partial\\mu_{\\ce{A}}}{\\partial x_{\\ce{B}}} \\right)_{T,p} = \\frac{1}{x_{\\ce{A}}} \\left(\\frac{\\partial\\mu_{\\ce{B}}}{\\partial x_{\\ce{B}}} \\right)_{T,p}\\]"^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15331 "These equations show that an extremum occurs for each phase equation when the compositions of the two phases are equal, and that the slope of the \\(T\\)-composition or \\(p\\)-composition curve is zero for each phase equation at the extremum."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15331 "Sometimes the German transliteration Konovalow is found."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15331 goldbook:16268)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15331 goldbook:16270)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15331 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15331 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15332))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15332 "higher-order system")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15332 "System containing more than three components.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15332 "multicomponent system")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15332 goldbook:15316)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15332 goldbook:16268)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15332 goldbook:15366)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15332 goldbook:15368)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15332 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15332 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15333))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15333 "infinite dilution")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15333 "Limiting composition or other variable in a solution obtained by extrapolating to a value of zero for the variable describing the composition of the solution.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15333 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15333 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15334))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15334 "infinite miscibility")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15334 "Property of a system of forming a single phase at all relative proportions of its components.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15334 "miscibility in all proportions")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15334 goldbook:16268)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15334 goldbook:15342)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15334 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15334 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15335))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15335 "ionic mole fraction")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15335 "For an ionized salt \\(\\ce{B}\\) in solution, \\[x_{+\\rm{B}} = \\frac{ u_{+\\ce{B}}x_{\\ce{B}}}{1 + \\sum \\limits_{i=1}^{s} \\left( u_{i} - 1 \\right)x_{i}},x_{-\\ce{B}} = \\frac{ u_{-\\ce{B}}x_{+\\ce{B}}}{ u_{+\\ce{B}}}\\] where the summation is over all $s$ solute components \\(i\\) and \\( u_{i} =  u_{+i} +  u_{-i}\\) is the sum of the stoichiometric numbers of the ions formed from salt \\(i\\). For a single solvent \\(\\ce{A}\\) in an ionic solution, \\[x'_{\\ce{A}} = \\frac{x_{\\ce{A}}}{1 + \\sum \\limits_{i=1}^{s} \\left( u_{i} - 1 \\right)x_{i}}\\] Note 1: These are generalizations of terms and are used in formulating fitting equations for solubility of salts, in defining activity coefficients on the mole fraction scale, and in discussing salt effects on solubilities of gases.Note 2: Note that \\[\\sum \\limits_{i=1}^{s} \\left(x_{+i} - x_{-i} \\right) + x'_{\\ce{A}} = 1\\]")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15335 "ionic amount fraction")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15335 "species amount fraction")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15335 "species mole fraction")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15335 goldbook:16268)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15335 goldbook:15376)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15335 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15335 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15336))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15336 "isopleth")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15336 "Line joining points of equal composition on a phase diagram.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15336 goldbook:15346)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15336 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15336 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15337))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15337 "mass ratio")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15337 "Mass of one constituent \\(\\ce{A}\\) divided by the mass of a second constituent \\(\\ce{B}\\) in the same system. \\[\\zeta_{\\ce{A,B}} = m_{\\ce{A}}/m_{\\ce{B}}\\]")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15337 goldbook:16269)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15337 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15337 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15338))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15338 "mass solubility")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15338 "Obsolete term for molality of a saturated solution of a gas.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15338 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15338 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15339))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15339 "metatectic reaction")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15339 "Isothermal reversible reaction of a solid mixture phase \\(\\upbeta\\) which is transformed into a different solid phase \\(\\upalpha\\) plus a liquid phase \\(\\ce{l}\\) during cooling of a system. For a binary system, \\[\\ce{\\upbeta  \\upalpha + 1}\\] where the forward arrow indicates the direction of cooling. The equilibrium transformation occurs along the metatectic line characterized by the metatectic temperature. The metatectic composition and temperature, isobaric invariants of the system, define the metatectic point, which lies between the compositions of liquid \\(\\ce{l}\\) and solid phase \\(\\upalpha\\).")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15339 "catatectic reaction")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15339 "From Greek μετα-, referring to position of melting relative to eutectectic and monotectic + -τηκτος, fusible."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15339 "The alternate name catatectic reaction, from Greek κατα, down + -τηκτος, fusible has been suggested to emphasize the phenomenon of melting during cooling."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15339 "Occasionally, a similar reaction takes place in the subsolidus region. Quite appropriately, it is called metatectoid reaction."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15339 goldbook:15316)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15339 goldbook:16270)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15339 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15339 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15340))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15340 "mole percent")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15340 "Deprecated term that includes both a quantity and a unit. Replace by mole fraction expressed as percent.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15340 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15340 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15341))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15341 "mole ratio")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15341 "Amount of one constituent divided by the amount of a second constituent in the same system. For constituents 1 and 2, \\[r_{12} = n_{1}/n_{2}\\]")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15341 "amount ratio")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15341 goldbook:16269)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15341 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15341 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15342))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15342 "mutual solubility")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15342 "In a system of two or more liquid or solid components, solubility of all components in all phases.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15342 "If mutual solubility is limited over a range of temperature and composition, the liquids or solids are said to exhibit partial miscibility and the system possesses a miscibility gap."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15342 goldbook:16268)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15342 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15342 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15343))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15343 "non-saturating solute")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15343 "Solute which forms an unsaturated solution.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15343 "Together with the term saturating solute used to distinguish among solutes in ternary and higher-order systems."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15343 goldbook:15332)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15343 goldbook:15355)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15343 goldbook:15366)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15343 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15343 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15344))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15344 "peritonic reaction")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15344 "Isothermal, isobaric reversible reaction between two phases, a saturated liquid and a solid, that results, on removal of the solvent component of a ternary system in one new solid phase. For example, \\[\\ce{l + \\upalpha  \\upbeta}\\] where the forward arrow indicates the direction of removal of the solvent component. The system is in equilibrium along the peritonic line, on which is found the peritonic composition or point, an isothermal, isobaric invariant of the system which lies between the compositions of phases \\(\\ce{l}\\) and \\(\\upalpha\\).")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15344 "transition reaction (in phase equilibria)")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15344 goldbook:16268)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15344 goldbook:15325)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15344 goldbook:15327)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15344 goldbook:15366)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15344 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15344 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15345))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15345 "permil")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15345 "One part in a thousand parts.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15345 "per mille")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15345 "permille")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15345 "promille")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15345 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15345 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15346))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15346 "phase diagram")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15346 "Graphical representation, by use of points, lines, and surfaces, of the phases present at chemical equilibrium in unary, binary, ternary, and higher-order systems containing two or more phases.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15346 "Phase diagrams may employ any pairs of the variables temperature, pressure, and compositions of various phases. Thus, temperature-composition and pressure-composition phase diagrams are possible, as well as diagrams showing only compositions under isothermal or isobaric conditions."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15346 goldbook:15316)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15346 goldbook:15332)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15346 goldbook:15336)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15346 goldbook:15366)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15346 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15346 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15347))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15347 "Poynting correction")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15347 "Factor used to convert experimentally determined Henry’s law constants at the saturation vapor pressure of the solvent \\(\\ce{A}\\), \\(p_{\\ce{A}}^{\\ast}\\), to a reference pressure \\(p\\) \\[\\begin{array}{c} I_{\\rm{p}} = \\int_{p_{\\ce{A}}^{\\ast}}^p \\frac{V_{\\ce{B}}^{\\infty {\\rm{l}}}}{RT}{\\rm{d}}p \\\\ k_{\\rm{H},\\ce{B}}(p) = k_{\\rm{H},\\ce{B}}(p^{\\ast}) \\exp \\left[I_{\\rm{p}}(p) \\right]\\end{array}\\] is the partial molar volume of liquid \\(\\ce{B}\\) at infinite dilution in solvent \\(\\ce{A}\\). The second equation gives the relation between the two Henry’s law constants.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15347 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15347 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15348))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15348 "primary data")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15348 "Data reported in peer-reviewed scientific reports of original research which allow an assessment of data quality.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15348 "Primary data are distinguished from secondary data appearing in reviews, handbooks, compendia, etc. which hold the possibility of error and bias through transcription error, incomplete coverage of the primary literature, etc."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15348 goldbook:15323)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15348 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15348 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15349))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15349 "Raoult’s law")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15349 "Fugacity (\\(\\tilde{p}_{\\ce{B}}\\)) of a gaseous component (\\(\\ce{B}\\)) in equilibrium with a liquid or solid mixture containing \\(\\ce{B}\\) is directly proportional to the activity (\\(a_{\\ce{B}}\\)) of the component in the mixture \\[\\tilde{p}_{\\ce{B}} = \\tilde{p}_{\\ce{B}}^{\\ast} f_{\\ce{B}} x_{\\ce{B}}\\] where \\(f_{\\ce{B}}\\) is the activity coefficient of \\(\\ce{B}\\) referenced to Raoult’s law at mole fraction \\(x_{\\ce{B}}\\) and \\(\\tilde{p}_{\\ce{B}}\\) is the fugacity of pure \\(\\ce{B}\\).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15349 "An ideal mixture is defined by replacing fugacities with partial pressures and setting the activity coefficient equal to unity \\[p_{\\ce{B}} = p_{\\ce{B}}^{\\ast} x_{\\ce{B}} = y_{\\ce{B}}p\\] The total pressure, \\(p\\), is then simply the sum of the partial pressures of all components."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15349 goldbook:16270)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15349 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15349 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15350))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15350 "reciprocal salt system")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15350 "System containing \\(n\\) ionic species with or without a single solvent. Because of electrical neutrality, the system has \\(n\\) components in an aqueous system with a single solvent and \\(n - 1\\) components in a molten salt system.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15350 "There is a special notation for reciprocal salt systems that involves use of double vertical bars. All ionic species are specified. For example, \\[\\ce{K^{+},Na^{+} \\Vert\\ Cl^{-},NO3^{-} + H2O}\\] denotes a four-component (quaternary) aqueous reciprocal salt system in which each cation can combine with each anion to produce anhydrous, hydrated, binary, or ternary solid components; i.e., the solution may become saturated with respect to any one of \\(\\ce{KCl}\\), \\(\\ce{NaCl}\\), \\(\\ce{KNO3}\\), \\(\\ce{NaNO3}\\), their hydrates, or anhydrous or hydrated binary compounds of the simple salts."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15350 "Ternary aqueous systems containing a common ion can be considered as a limiting case of this class of system, where there is only one cation or one anion. For example, \\[\\ce{Na^{+},Zn^{2+} \\Vert\\ SO4^{2-} + H2O}\\]"^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15350 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15350 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15351))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15351 "reduced pressure")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15351 "Pressure divided by the critical pressure.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15351 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15351 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15352))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15352 "reduced temperature")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15352 "Temperature divided by the critical temperature.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15352 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15352 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15353))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15353 "reference data")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15353 "Data that are critically evaluated and verified, obtained from an identified source, and related to a property of a phenomenon, body, or substance, or a system of components of known composition and structure.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15353 goldbook:15323)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15353 goldbook:16268)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15353 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15353 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15354))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15354 "retrograde solubility")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15354 "Solubility that decreases with an increase in conditions such as temperature or added component, where an increase is expected as the usual case. In ternary liquid systems with coexisting phases, where the critical solution point is not a maximum on a ternary diagram, passing from a homogeneous mixture in which the composition of a given component is greater than that of the critical mixture to a heterogeneous mixture and back to a homogeneous mixture by altering the relative amounts of the two other components.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15354 goldbook:16268)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15354 goldbook:15365)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15354 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15354 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15355))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15355 "saturating solute")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15355 "Solute that forms a saturated solution.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15355 "Together with the term non-saturating solute, used to distinguish among solutes in ternary and higher-order systems."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15355 goldbook:15332)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15355 goldbook:15343)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15355 goldbook:15366)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15355 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15355 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15356))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15356 "scaling equation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15356 "Dimensionless equation representing mutual solubilities in a number of chemically related liquid systems. Each mutual solubility is subtracted from the solubility at the critical solution point, and the temperature is divided by the critical solution temperature.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15356 goldbook:15342)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15356 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15356 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15357))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15357 "Sechenov equation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15357 "Expression of the salt effect that relates the change in solubility of a nonelectrolyte (e.g., gas or organic liquid) to changing ionic strength of aqueous solutions, \\[\\lg (s_{\\rm{o}}/s) = K_{s} I_{s}\\] where \\(s_{o}\\), \\(s\\) are the solubilities of nonelectrolyte in pure water and saline solution, respectively, \\(K_{s}\\) the Sechenov parameter (an empirical proportionality constant), and \\(I_{s}\\) the ionic strength of the saline solution.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15357 "Setschenow equation")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15357 "Positive values of the Sechenov parameter correspond to the commonly observed salting-out effect; negative values to the less common salting-in effect."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15357 "Sechenov is the international and Setschenow the German transliteration of Сеченоь."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15357 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15357 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15358))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15358 "Sieverts’ law")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15358 "Solubility of a diatomic gas in a molten metal is proportional to the square root of the partial pressure.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15358 "The law follows from the solubility constant for equilibrium dissolution of an ideal diatomic gas \\(\\ce{X2}\\) in a metal \\(\\ce{M}\\) to form an ideal solution of dissociated atoms: \\[\\ce{X2(g)  2X(M)}\\] for which, and for dilute solutions of the gas, \\[K_{{\\rm{s}},x} = a(\\ce{X},\\ce{M})^{2}/a(\\ce{X2},{\\rm{g}}) \\approx x(\\ce{X},\\ce{M})^{2} p^{_{^⦵\\!}}/p (\\ce{X2},\\rm{g})\\] where \\(x(\\ce{X},\\ce{M})\\) is the solubility of the gas in the molten metal expressed as a mole fraction of \\(\\ce{H\\mbox{-}atoms}\\). The solubility constant \\(K_{\\rm{s},x}\\) is called the Sieverts constant."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15358 "Other forms of the solubility constant are common, especially in terms of amount concentrations or mass fractions (especially in metallurgical papers) instead of mole fractions."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15358 goldbook:15359)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15358 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15358 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15359))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15359 "solubility constant")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15359 "Generalization of solubility product to include, for example, undissociated salt or uncharged cation-anion pair as solute, reaction between solution species and the cation or anion of the solid salt, and gas-solution equilibria.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15359 "The solubility constant can also be considered in many cases as relating to a solubility equilibrium as described under solubility product plus one or more simultaneous homogeneous equilibria in solution."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15359 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15359 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15360))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15360 "solubilisation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15360 "Process by which an agent increases the solubility or the rate of dissolution of a solid or liquid solute.Modified from entry 'micellar solubilization' in.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15360 "The solute that is solubilized is called the solubilizate."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15360 "Solubilization is sometimes used loosely to include processes caused by agents such as surfactants which hold a component in micelles or colloidal suspension rather than in solution."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15360 goldbook:16268)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15360 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15360 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15361))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15361 "solvent mole fraction")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15361 "Mole or mass fraction of a solvent in a solution containing \\(s\\) solute constituents (\\(i = 1, 2, \\ldots, s\\)) and \\(p\\) solvent constituents (\\(i = s + 1, s + 2, \\ldots, p\\)). For a solvent \\(\\ce{A}\\), \\[x_{{\\rm{v}},{\\ce{A}}} = x_{\\ce{A}}/\\sum \\limits_{i=s+1}^{p} x_{i}\\] where \\[\\sum \\limits_{i=1}^{p} x_{i} = \\sum \\limits_{i=1}^{s} x_{i} + \\sum \\limits_{i=s+1}^{p} x_{i} = 1\\] and analogously for \\(w_{{\\rm{v}},{\\ce{A}}}\\), where the first and last summations are over all solvent constituents.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15361 goldbook:15373)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15361 goldbook:15376)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15361 goldbook:16269)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15361 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15361 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15362))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15362 "solvent volume fraction")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15362 "For a solvent \\(\\ce{A}\\), volume fraction of \\(\\ce{A}\\) divided by the sum of the volume fractions of solvent in a solution containing both \\(s\\) solutes (\\(i = 1, 2, \\ldots, s\\)) and \\(p\\) solvents (\\(i = s + 1, s + 2, \\ldots, p\\)) \\[\\varphi_{{\\rm{v}},{\\ce{A}}} = \\varphi_{\\ce{A}}/\\sum \\limits_{i=s+1}^{p} \\varphi_{i}\\] where the summation is over the \\(p\\) solvent components only.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15362 "Used to express solvent composition for a system containing a solute in a mixed solvent."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15362 goldbook:16268)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15362 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15362 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15363))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15363 "standard amount concentration")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15363 "Chosen value of amount concentration.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15363 "standard concentration")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15363 "In principle, one may choose any value for the standard concentration, although the choice must be specified. The most common choice for standard concentration is \\(c^{_{^⦵\\!}} = \\pu{1 mol dm-3}\\), which is universally accepted."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15363 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15363 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15364))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15364 "synthetic method")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15364 "Class of experimental procedures for solubility determination in which a solution of known composition is prepared. Two major subclasses are recognized. In the isothermal method, one liquid component is titrated with a second liquid component at constant temperature until persistent turbidity is observed (i.e., to the cloud point). In the polythermal method, a mixture of known composition is heated above its solution temperature and monitored visually during cooling until turbidity (the cloud point) is observed.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15364 goldbook:16268)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15364 goldbook:16270)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15364 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15364 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15365))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15365 "ternary diagram")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15365 "Triangular plot (usually an equilateral or right-angled triangle) whose vertices represent the pure components of a ternary system at constant temperature and pressure. Any point within the triangle represents the composition in terms of the two independent mole (or mass) fractions. Lines parallel to the sides of the triangle represent constant proportions of the respective components (isopleths).")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15365 "Gibbs’ triangular representation")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15365 "In an isobaric diagram, an axis perpendicular to the plane of the triangle may be added to represent temperature."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15365 "In addition, any triangle of any shape, including any triangle within the main triangle, can be used to obtain the composition of the system represented by a point within the triangle in terms of the compositions represented by its vertices."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15365 goldbook:16268)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15365 goldbook:15336)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15365 goldbook:15366)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15365 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15365 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15366))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15366 "ternary system")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15366 "System containing three components.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15366 goldbook:15316)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15366 goldbook:16268)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15366 goldbook:15368)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15366 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15366 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15367))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15367 "tie-line")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15367 "Straight line connecting compositions of independent coexisting phases in equilibrium on a phase diagram.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15367 "connodal")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15367 "conodal")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15367 goldbook:15346)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15367 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15367 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15368))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15368 "unary system")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15368 "System containing one component.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15368 goldbook:15316)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15368 goldbook:16268)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15368 goldbook:15332)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15368 goldbook:15366)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15368 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15368 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15369))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15369 "unsaturated solution")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15369 "Solution that has a lower proportion of a solute than one that is in equilibrium with undissolved solute at specified values of temperature and pressure.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15369 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15369 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15370))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15370 "unsaturation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15370 "State of an unsaturated solution.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15370 "undersaturation")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15370 goldbook:15369)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15370 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15370 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15371))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15371 "wet residue method")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15371 "Method for determining composition of a solid phase in a ternary system at constant temperature and pressure by analysis of the total mixture of solid and liquid in equilibrium.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15371 "initial complex method")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15371 "Schreinemakers’ method")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15371 "The method relies on the fact that the wet residue lies on the tie-line connecting the solid phase and the saturated liquid phase. Equally well, the initial mixture of solid and liquid used in the solubility experiment can be used, when it is referred to as the \"initial complex\" method. In either case, two or more tie-lines intersect at the composition of the solid phase."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15371 "The method is generally more reliable than isolation and analysis of the solid phase, especially when the solid phase is a hydrate."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15371 goldbook:15366)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15371 goldbook:15367)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15371 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15371 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15372))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15372 "Ising model")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15372 "Theory of coexistence curves or other discontinuities in the properties of phases (such as order-disorder or magnetic transitions) in binary systems, based on a one-, two-, or three-dimensional statistical mechanical nearest-neighbor lattice theory.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15372 "The theory predicts phase separation in a wide variety of systems, including binary liquid or solid systems that possess critical solution points."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15372 goldbook:15316)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15372 goldbook:15320)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15372 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15372 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15373))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15373 "Jänecke coordinates")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15373 "Coordinates used mainly in representation of multicomponent phase diagrams that distinguish solutes and a single solvent. The mole or mass fractions of the \\(s\\) solutes are chosen as the primary composition variables and the mole or mass fraction of solvent as a secondary variable, so that the solute amount (mass) fractions may be represented, for example, in ternary and quaternary systems, as linear (ternary) or planar triangular or square planar (quaternary) diagrams, with the solvent amount or mass fraction along an axis perpendicular to the chosen diagram of solute variables. Quantitatively, \\[x_{{\\rm{s}},{\\ce{B}}} = x_{\\ce{B}}/\\sum \\limits_{i=1}^{s}x_{i}\\] where the summation is over the \\(s\\) solute substances. Note that \\(\\sum \\limits_{i=1}^{s}x_{{\\rm{s}},{\\ce{B}}} = 1\\).")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15373 "solute mole (or mass) fraction coordinates")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15373 "The mole fraction of solvent component \\(\\ce{A}\\) in a mixture containing \\(p - s\\) solvents (total species \\(p\\)) is replaced by a special case of the solvent mole fraction \\(x_{{\\rm{s}},{\\ce{A}}} = x_{\\ce{A}}/\\sum \\limits_{i=s+1}^{p}x_{i}\\), which becomes infinite for pure solvent."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15373 "This quantity can be scaled to a finite value by adding an arbitrary constant to the denominator."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15373 goldbook:15376)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15373 goldbook:15346)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15373 goldbook:15361)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15373 goldbook:15366)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15373 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15373 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15374))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15374 "Kuenen coefficient")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15374 "Volume \\(V^{\\rm{g}}\\) of an amount \\(n_{\\ce{B}}^{\\rm{l}}\\) of a dissolved gas at a given standard temperature \\(T^{^⦵\\!}\\) (usually \\(\\pu{273.15 K}\\)) and given standard pressure \\(p^{_{^⦵\\!}}\\) (\\(\\pu{1 bar} = \\pu{0.1 MPa}\\) or, in older literature, \\(\\pu{1 atm}\\)) divided by the mass \\(m^{\\rm{l}}\\) of the dissolving liquid containing an amount $n_{\\ce{A}}$ of solvent at temperature $T$ and the given pressure \\(p^{_{^⦵\\!}}\\).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15374 "There are two Kuenen coefficients, depending on whether the liquid is the equilibrium solution or the pure liquid, with mathematical definitions:- Kuenen coefficient, solution reference \\(S_{\\ce{B}} = V^{\\rm{g}}(T^{^⦵\\!}, p^{_{^⦵\\!}}, n_{\\ce{B}}^{1})/m^{\\rm{l}}(T, p^{_{^⦵\\!}}, n_{\\ce{A}}, n_{\\ce{B}}^{\\rm{l}})\\)- Kuenen coefficient, pure solvent reference \\(S_{\\ce{B}}^{\\ast} = V^{\\rm{g}}(T^{^⦵\\!}, p^{_{^⦵\\!}}, n_{\\ce{B}}^{1})/m^{\\rm{l}}(T, p^{_{^⦵\\!}}, n_{\\ce{A}})\\)"^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15374 "The relations between the molality \\(m_{\\ce{B}}(p^{_{^⦵\\!}})\\) or mole fraction \\(x_{\\ce{B}}(p^{_{^⦵\\!}})\\) of dissolved gas and the Kuenen coefficients are \\[\\begin{array}{l} \\frac{1}{x_{\\ce{B}}(p^{⦵})} = 1 + \\frac{1}{m_{\\ce{B}}(p^{⦵})M_{\\ce{A}}} = 1 + \\frac{RT^{⦵}Z_{\\ce{B}}^{⦵}(T^{⦵})}{p^{⦵}M_{\\ce{A}}S_{\\ce{B}}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{x_{\\ce{B}}(p^{⦵})} = 1 + \\frac{1}{m_{\\ce{B}}(p^{⦵})M_{\\ce{A}}} = 1 + \\frac{RT^{⦵}Z_{\\ce{B}}^{⦵}(T^{⦵})}{p^{⦵}M_{\\rm{A}}S_{\\ce{B}}^{\\ast}} \\end{array}\\] where \\(M_{\\ce{A}}\\) is the molar mass the solvent and \\(Z_{\\ce{B}}\\) is the compression factor of the gas."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15374 "The Kuenen coefficient and the related quantities for expression of gas solubility: absorption coefficient, Bunsen coefficient, and Ostwald coefficient appear frequently in the older literature of gas solubility determination. However, the modern practice, recommended here, is to express gas solubility as molality, mole fraction, or mole ratio."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15374 goldbook:15317)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15374 goldbook:15377)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15374 goldbook:15376)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15374 goldbook:15341)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15374 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15374 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15375))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15375 "mass percent")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15375 "Deprecated term that includes both a quantity and a unit. Replace by mass fraction expressed as percent.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15375 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15375 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15377))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15377 "Ostwald coefficient")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15377 "Volume \\(V^{\\rm{g}}\\) of an amount \\(n_{\\ce{B}}^{\\rm{l}}\\) of a dissolved gas calculated at given temperature \\(T\\) and pressure \\(p\\) divided by the volume of the dissolving liquid of volume \\(V^{\\rm{l}}\\) and containing an amount \\(n_{\\ce{A}}\\) of solvent at the same temperature \\(T\\) and pressure \\(p\\).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15377 "There are two Ostwald coefficients, depending on whether the liquid is the equilibrium solution or the pure liquid, with mathematical definitions:Ostwald coefficient, solution reference \\[L_{\\ce{B}} = V^{\\rm{g}}(T,p,n_{\\ce{B}}^{\\rm{l}})/V^{\\rm{l}}(T,p,n_{\\ce{A}}, n_{\\ce{B}}^{\\rm{l}}) = c_{\\ce{B}}^{\\rm{l}}/c_{\\ce{B}}^{\\rm{g}}\\] Ostwald coefficient, pure solvent reference \\[L_{\\ce{B}}^{\\ast} = V^{\\rm{g}}(T,p,n_{\\ce{B}}^{\\rm{l}})/V^{\\rm{l}}(T,p,n_{\\ce{A}})\\]"^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15377 "The relations between the molality \\(m_{\\ce{B}}(p)\\) or mole fraction \\(x_{\\ce{B}}(p)\\) of dissolved gas and the Ostwald coefficients are \\[\\begin{array}{l} \\frac{1}{x_{\\ce{B}}(p)} = 1 + \\frac{1}{m_{\\ce{B}}(p)M_{\\ce{A}}} = 1 + \\frac{RTZ_{\\ce{B}}}{V_{\\ce{A}}p_{\\ce{B}}L_{\\ce{B}}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{x_{\\ce{B}}(p)} = 1 + \\frac{1}{m_{\\ce{B}}(p)M_{\\ce{A}}} = 1 + \\frac{RTZ}{pV_{m,\\ce{A}}L_{\\ce{B}}^{\\ast}} \\end{array}\\] where \\(V_{\\ce{A}}\\), \\(V_{m,\\ce{A}}\\) are the respective partial molar volume and molar volume of the solvent and \\(Z_{\\ce{B}}\\) is the compression factor of the gas."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15377 "The Ostwald coefficient and the related quantities for expression of gas solubility, the absorption, Bunsen, and Kuenen coefficients, appear frequently in the older literature of gas solubility determination. However, the modern practice, recommended here, is to express gas solubility as molality, mole fraction, or mole ratio."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15377 goldbook:15317)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15377 goldbook:15374)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15377 goldbook:15376)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15377 goldbook:15341)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15377 doi:10.1351/pac200880020233)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15377 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15378))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15378 "acyclic diene metathesis polymerisation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15378 "Metathesis polymerization of an acylic diene monomer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003012) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15378 "ADMET")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15378 doi:10.1351/pac200880102163)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15378 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15379))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15379 "apparent rate constant of polymerisation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15379 "Measured rate of polymerization divided by the concentration of the reactant (if there is only one) or the product of concentrations of the presumed reactants.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15379 "The apparent rate constant of a polymerization should not be confused with the rate coefficients or the rate constants of the elementary reaction steps."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15379 goldbook:15418)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15379 doi:10.1351/pac200880102163)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15379 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15380))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15380 "auto-acceleration")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15380 "Increase in the rate of polymerization with increasing conversion of the reactant(s).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15380 goldbook:15418)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15380 doi:10.1351/pac200880102163)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15380 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15381))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15381 "azeotropic copolymerisation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15381 "Binary copolymerization in which the two monomer reactivity ratios, \\(r_{12}\\) and \\(r_{21}\\) are not both equal to unity yet the copolymerization forms a copolymer with its molar ratio of monomer units equal to the molar ratio of monomers in the monomer feed.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15381 "An azeotropic polymerization occurs at only one specific molar ratio of monomers in the feed."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15381 "Although, in its equality of copolymer and monomer-feed compositions, an azeotropic polymerization has the same feature as an ideal binary copolymerization in which \\(r_{12} = r_{21} = 1\\), it is not an ideal copolymerization as it has \\(r_{12} r_{21} \\neq 1\\)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15381 goldbook:15383)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15381 goldbook:15405)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15381 goldbook:15406)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15381 goldbook:15410)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15381 doi:10.1351/pac200880102163)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15381 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15382))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15382 "backbiting")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15382 "Chain transfer from an active center on a macromolecule to another part of the same macromolecule.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15382 "intramolecular chain transfer")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15382 "An active center may be located anywhere along a macromolecular chain."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15382 "Often, branching occurs or cyclic structures are formed as a result of backbiting."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15382 goldbook:15408)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15382 doi:10.1351/pac200880102163)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15382 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15383))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15383 "binary copolymerisation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15383 "Copolymerization involving two species of monomer.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15383 doi:10.1351/pac200880102163)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15383 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15384))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15384 "bulk polymerisation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15384 "Polymerization of an undiluted liquid monomer.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15384 doi:10.1351/pac200880102163)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15384 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15385))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15385 "ceiling temperature")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15385 "Temperature above which, in a given chain polymerization, polymer of high molar mass is not formed.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15385 "A ceiling temperature is only observed for enthalpy-driven chain polymerizations in which \\(\\Delta H_{\\rm{m}} \\lt 0\\) and \\(\\Delta S_{\\rm{m}} \\lt 0\\), where \\(\\Delta H_{\\rm{m}}\\) and \\(\\Delta S_{\\rm{m}}\\) are respectively the enthalpy and entropy change per mole of monomer reacted."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15385 "For most chain polymerizations, \\(\\Delta H_{\\rm{m}} \\lt 0\\) and \\(\\Delta S_{\\rm{m}} \\lt 0\\)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15385 "Below \\(T_{\\rm{c}}\\), \\(\\Delta G_{\\rm{m}} (= \\Delta H_{\\rm{m}} - T\\Delta S_{\\rm{m}}) \\lt 0\\); at \\(T_{\\rm{c}}\\), \\(\\Delta G_{\\rm{m}} = 0\\); and above \\(T_{\\rm{c}}\\), \\(\\Delta G_{\\rm{m}} \\gt 0\\)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15385 "Because \\(\\Delta G_{\\rm{m}} = 0\\) at the ceiling temperature, \\(T_{\\rm{c}} = \\Delta H_{\\rm{m}}/\\Delta S_{\\rm{m}}\\). If \\(\\Delta H_{\\rm{m}}^{\\circ}\\) and \\(\\Delta S_{\\rm{m}}^{\\circ}\\) are the enthalpy and entropy changes in the standard state, and the monomer behaves ideally, then \\[T_{\\rm{c}} = \\Delta H_{\\rm{m}}^{\\circ}/\\{\\Delta S_{\\rm{m}}^{\\circ} + R\\ln ([{\\rm{M}}]_{0}/c^{\\circ})\\}\\] where \\(c^{\\circ} = \\pu{1 mol dm-3}\\) is the standard concentration and \\([{\\rm{M}}]_{0}\\) is the initial monomer concentration. Thus, \\(T_{\\rm{c}}\\) depends on the initial monomer concentration."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15385 "The symbol \\(T_{\\rm{c}}(c^{\\circ})\\) is used to denote the ceiling temperature when the initial monomer concentration, \\([{\\rm{M}}]_{0}\\), is equal to \\(c^{\\circ}\\)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15385 "The symbol \\(T_{\\rm{c}}({\\rm{bulk}})\\) is used to denote the ceiling temperature when the initial monomer concentration is equal to its undiluted concentration."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15385 goldbook:15401)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15385 doi:10.1351/pac200880102163)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15385 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15386))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15386 "chain copolymerisation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15386 "Chain polymerization in which a copolymer is formed.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15386 doi:10.1351/pac200880102163)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15386 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15387))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15387 "chain depropagation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15387 "Chemical reaction that results in the formation of a monomer molecule at an active center on the terminal unit of a chain carrier and decreases the degree of polymerization of the chain carrier by one.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15387 "depropagation")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15387 "Chain depropagation is the reverse of chain propagation."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15387 goldbook:15426)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15387 doi:10.1351/pac200880102163)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15387 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15388))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15388 "chain-end reactivity ratio")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15388 "In a binary copolymerization, the ratio of two rate constants defining the relative activity of an active center on a given type of terminal unit of a chain carrier toward one type of monomer, in the two cases where the penultimate unit of the chain carrier is identical to and different from the terminal unit.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15388 "radical reactivity ratio")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15388 "The reactions involved are defined in accordance with the penultimate-unit effect, namely, \\[\\begin{array}{l} ...-{\\rm{m}}_{11}^{\\ast} + {\\rm{M}}_{1}\\ce{->[\\textit{k}_{111}]} ...-{\\rm{m}}_{11}^{\\ast} \\\\ ...-{\\rm{m}}_{21}^{\\ast} + {\\rm{M}}_{1}\\ce{->[\\textit{k}_{211}]} ...-{\\rm{m}}_{11}^{\\ast} \\\\ ...-{\\rm{m}}_{11}^{\\ast} + {\\rm{M}}_{2}\\ce{->[\\textit{k}_{112}]} ...-{\\rm{m}}_{12}^{\\ast} \\\\ ...-{\\rm{m}}_{21}^{\\ast} + {\\rm{M}}_{2}\\ce{->[\\textit{k}_{212}]} ...-{\\rm{m}}_{12}^{\\ast} \\\\ ...-{\\rm{m}}_{12}^{\\ast} + {\\rm{M}}_{1}\\ce{->[\\textit{k}_{121}]} ...-{\\rm{m}}_{21}^{\\ast} \\\\ ...-{\\rm{m}}_{22}^{\\ast} + {\\rm{M}}_{1}\\ce{->[\\textit{k}_{221}]} ...-{\\rm{m}}_{21}^{\\ast} \\\\ ...-{\\rm{m}}_{12}^{\\ast} + {\\rm{M}}_{2}\\ce{->[\\textit{k}_{122}]} ...-{\\rm{m}}_{22}^{\\ast} \\\\ ...-{\\rm{m}}_{22}^{\\ast} + {\\rm{M}}_{2}\\ce{->[\\textit{k}_{222}]} ...-{\\rm{m}}_{22}^{\\ast}, \\end{array}\\] where \\({\\rm{M}}_{1}\\) and \\({\\rm{M}}_{2}\\) are the two monomers involved in the binary copolymerization and \\(-{\\rm{m}}_{ij}^{\\ast} (i,j = 1,2)\\) denotes a chain carrier having an active site on its terminal monomer unit of type \\({\\rm{M}}_{j}\\) and having the adjacent, penultimate monomer unit of type \\({\\rm{M}}_{i}\\) (see chain carrier)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15388 "The chain-end reactivity ratios are expressed mathematically by the equations \\[s_{1} = k_{211}/k_{111};\\ s_{2} = k_{122}/k_{222}\\]."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15388 "The monomer reactivity ratios, defined in accordance with the penultimate-unit effect, are \\[r_{112} = k_{111}/k_{112};\\ r_{212} = k_{211}/k_{212};\\ r_{221} = k_{222}/k_{221};\\ r_{121} = k_{122}/k_{121}\\]. The symbols for the monomer reactivity ratios are often abbreviated to \\(r_{1}\\), \\(r_{1}^{\\prime}\\), \\(r_{2}\\), \\(r_{2}^{\\prime}\\), respectively (see monomer reactivity ratios for the definitions of \\(r_{1}\\) and \\(r_{2}\\) ignoring the penultimate-unit effect)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15388 goldbook:15383)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15388 goldbook:15410)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15388 goldbook:15413)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15388 doi:10.1351/pac200880102163)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15388 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15389))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15389 "chain-transfer constant")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15389 "In a homopolymerization, rate constant for chain transfer, \\(k_{\\rm{tr}}\\), divided by the rate constant for chain propagation, \\(k_{\\rm{p}}\\), i.e., \\(C_{\\rm{tr}} = k_{\\rm{tr}}/k_{\\rm{p}}\\).")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15389 doi:10.1351/pac200880102163)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15389 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15390))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15390 "comonomer")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15390 "Monomer used in copolymerization.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15390 doi:10.1351/pac200880102163)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15390 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15391))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15391 "copolymerisation composition equation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15391 "Equation relating the instantaneous composition of a binary copolymer to the monomer reactivity ratios and the ratio of instantaneous monomer concentrations.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15391 "Mayo–Lewis equation")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15391 "The instantaneous composition of copolymer generally changes during the course of a copolymerization due to the changing composition of the monomer mixture (but see azeotropic polymerization)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15391 "See also chain-end reactivity ratio, monomer reactivity ratios."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15391 "Integrated forms of the copolymer composition equation have been developed to relate polymer composition to monomer reactivity ratios and monomer conversions."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15391 "The copolymer composition equation is known also as the Mayo–Lewis equation."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15391 goldbook:15381)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15391 goldbook:15388)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15391 goldbook:15410)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15391 doi:10.1351/pac200880102163)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15391 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15392))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15392 "coupling reaction")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15392 "Linking of two macromolecules through chemical reaction.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15392 "The coupling may proceed with or without interaction with an added coupling agent."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15392 doi:10.1351/pac200880102163)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15392 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15393))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15393 "cross-propagation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15393 "Propagation reaction in a copolymerization in which a chain carrier, bearing at its active end a monomer unit of one kind, reacts with a monomer molecule of another kind.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15393 "The recommended symbol for the rate constant of cross-propagation in a binary copolymerization is \\(k_{ij}\\) , in which \\(i\\) and \\(j\\) refer to (a) the type of terminal monomer unit of the chain carrier and (b) the reacting monomer molecule, respectively."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15393 goldbook:15383)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15393 doi:10.1351/pac200880102163)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15393 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15394))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15394 "cross-termination")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15394 "Termination reaction in a copolymerization between two chain carriers with different chemical structures.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15394 "Usually only the chemical structures of the units at the active centers are considered."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15394 "Cross-termination may occur by combination or disproportionation."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15394 doi:10.1351/pac200880102163)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15394 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15395))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15395 "dead-end polymerisation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15395 "Radical polymerization that stops, as a consequence of the depletion of the initiator, before the monomer has reacted fully.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15395 doi:10.1351/pac200880102163)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15395 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15396))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15396 "degradative chain transfer")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15396 "Chain transfer reaction that generates a new chain carrier of much lower reactivity than that of the original chain carrier.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15396 doi:10.1351/pac200880102163)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15396 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15397))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15397 "diffusion-controlled termination")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15397 "Chain termination in a chain polymerization in which the rate-determining step is a diffusion process.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15397 doi:10.1351/pac200880102163)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15397 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15398))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15398 "end-capping")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15398 "Reaction in which end-groups of a desired structure are intentionally formed.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15398 doi:10.1351/pac200880102163)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15398 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15399))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15399 "enthalpy of polymerisation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15399 "Change of enthalpy, in a chain polymerization forming a homopolymer, associated with the conversion of one mole of monomer into polymer under isobaric and isothermal conditions.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15399 "molar enthalpy of polymerization")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15399 "Under defined standard conditions the enthalpy of polymerization is designated \\(\\Delta H_{\\rm{m}}^{\\circ}\\)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15399 "The subscripts in \\(\\Delta_{\\rm{ab}} H_{\\rm{m}}\\) denote (a) the state of the monomer and (b) the state of polymer, as follows: g: gaseous state (hypothetical in the case of polymer);l: liquid state (must be specified in the case of a mesophase);s: in solution (solvent and mesophases, if any, must be specified);c: (condensed) amorphous, glassy states;c′: crystalline or partly crystalline state; e.g., \\(\\Delta_{\\rm{lc}} H_{\\rm{m}}\\) means: from liquid state to amorphous or glassy state; \\(\\Delta_{\\rm{ss}} H_{\\rm{m}}\\) means: from monomer in solvent to polymer in solvent."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15399 "The symbol \\(\\Delta H_{\\rm{ab}}\\), in common usage in polymer chemistry, is discouraged as the IUPAC-recommended symbol is \\(\\Delta_{\\rm{ab}} H_{\\rm{m}}\\)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15399 doi:10.1351/pac200880102163)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15399 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15400))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15400 "entropy of polymerisation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15400 "Change of entropy, in a chain polymerization forming a homopolymer, associated with the conversion of one mole of monomer into polymer under isobaric and isothermal conditions.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15400 "molar entropy of polymerization")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15400 "Under defined standard conditions, the entropy of polymerization is designated \\(\\Delta S_{\\rm{m}}^{\\circ}\\); thus, if the standard state refers to standard concentration, and the monomer behaves ideally, \\(\\Delta S_{\\rm{m}} = \\Delta S_{\\rm{m}}^{\\circ} + R\\ln ([{\\rm{M]}}_{0}/c^{\\circ})\\), where \\([{\\rm{M}}]_{0}\\) denotes the starting monomer concentration and \\(c^{\\circ} = \\pu{1 mol dm-3}\\) is the standard concentration."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15400 "The subscripts in \\(\\Delta_{\\rm{ab}} S_{\\rm{m}}\\) denote the state of the monomer (a) and the state of polymer (b) (see enthalpy of polymerization (Note 2))."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15400 goldbook:15399)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15400 doi:10.1351/pac200880102163)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15400 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15401))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15401 "floor temperature")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15401 "Temperature below which, in a given chain polymerization, polymer of high molar mass is not formed.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15401 "A floor temperature is only observed for entropy-driven chain polymerizations in which \\(\\Delta H_{\\rm{m}} \\gt 0\\) and \\(\\Delta S_{\\rm{m}} \\gt 0\\), where \\(\\Delta H_{\\rm{m}}\\) and \\(\\Delta S_{\\rm{m}}\\) are respectively the enthalpy and entropy change per mole of monomer reacted."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15401 "Examples of chain polymerizations for which \\(\\Delta H_{\\rm{m}} \\gt 0\\) and \\(\\Delta S_{\\rm{m}} \\gt 0\\) are polymerizations of larger cyclic monomers, e.g., elemental sulfur (\\(\\ce{S8}\\)) and octamethylcyclotetrasiloxane [2,2,4,4,6,6,8,8-octamethyl-1,3,5,7,2,4,6,8-tetraoxatetrasilocane], proceeding via ring-opening mechanisms."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15401 "Above \\(T_{\\rm{f}}\\), \\(\\Delta G_{\\rm{m}} (= \\Delta H_{\\rm{m}} - T \\Delta H_{\\rm{m}}) \\lt 0\\); at \\(T_{\\rm{f}}\\), \\(\\Delta G_{\\rm{m}} = 0\\); and below \\(T_{\\rm{f}}\\), \\(\\Delta G_{\\rm{m}} \\gt 0\\)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15401 "Because \\(\\Delta G_{\\rm{m}} = 0\\) at the floor temperature, \\(T_{\\rm{f}} = \\Delta H_{\\rm{m}}/\\Delta S_{\\rm{m}}\\). If \\(\\Delta H_{\\rm{m}}^{\\circ}\\) and \\(\\Delta S_{\\rm{m}}^{\\circ}\\) are the enthalpy and entropy changes in the standard state, and the monomer behaves ideally, then \\[T_{\\rm{f}} = \\Delta H_{\\rm{m}}^{\\circ}/ \\{\\Delta S_{\\rm{m}}^{\\circ} + R\\ln ([{\\rm{M]}}_{0}/c^{\\circ})\\}\\] where \\(c^{\\circ} = \\pu{1 mol dm-3}\\) is the standard concentration and \\([{\\rm{M}}]_{0}\\) is the initial monomer concentration. Thus, \\(T_{\\rm{f}}\\) depends on the initial monomer concentration."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15401 "The symbol \\(T_{\\rm{f}}(c^{\\circ})\\) is used to denote the floor temperature when the initial monomer concentration, \\([{\\rm{M}}]_{0}\\), is equal to \\(c^{\\circ}\\)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15401 "The symbol \\(T_{\\rm{f}}({\\rm{bulk}})\\) is used to denote the floor temperature when the initial monomer concentration is equal to its undiluted concentration."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15401 goldbook:15385)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15401 doi:10.1351/pac200880102163)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15401 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15402))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15402 "free ion")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15402 "Ion whose behavior is independent of the influence of a counterion.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15402 "A free ion is a distinct kinetic entity, and its reactivity is usually different from that of an ion pair."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15402 "The behavior of a free ion may still be influenced by neighboring atoms or molecules."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15402 doi:10.1351/pac200880102163)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15402 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15403))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15403 "heat of polymerisation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15403 "Heat absorbed or given off from the conversion of a specified amount of monomer into polymer.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15403 "The molar heat of polymerization is denoted by the symbol \\(Q_{\\rm{m}}\\) and is the heat of polymerization of one mole of monomer. SI unit: \\(\\pu{J mol-1}\\)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15403 "The molar heat of polymerization is equal to the enthalpy of polymerization under isobaric and isothermal conditions."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15403 goldbook:15399)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15403 doi:10.1351/pac200880102163)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15403 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15404))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15404 "homopropagation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15404 "Addition of a monomer to a chain carrier bearing a terminal group derived from the same monomer species.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15404 doi:10.1351/pac200880102163)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15404 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15405))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15405 "ideal binary copolymerisation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15405 "Binary copolymerization in which the relative rates of incorporation of the two types of monomer into the copolymer are independent of the nature of the monomer unit at the end of a propagating chain.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15405 "In an ideal binary copolymerization, \\(k_{11}/k_{21} = k_{12}/k_{22}\\) and \\(r_{12} r_{21} = 1\\). See monomer reactivity ratios."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15405 "In the special case of an ideal binary copolymerization in which \\(r_{12} = r_{21} = 1\\), the two monomers show equal reactivities toward both types of propagating species. Thus, \\(k_{11} = k_{21}\\) and \\(k_{12} = k_{22}\\). Hence, copolymerization of a mixture of two monomers with any ratio of monomer concentrations in the monomer feed gives rise to a copolymer in which the molar ratio of monomer units is identical to that in the monomer feed. (See also azeotropic copolymerization.)"^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15405 goldbook:15383)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15405 goldbook:15381)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15405 goldbook:15410)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15405 doi:10.1351/pac200880102163)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15405 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15406))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15406 "ideal copolymerisation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15406 "Copolymerization in which all types of propagating species show the same relative reactivity toward the monomers present.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15406 doi:10.1351/pac200880102163)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15406 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15407))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15407 "interfacial polycondensation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15407 "Polycondensation involving two monomers separately dissolved in immiscible solvents, forming a twophase system, with polycondensation taking place at (or near) an interface between the two phases.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15407 doi:10.1351/pac200880102163)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15407 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15408))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15408 "intermolecular chain transfer")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15408 "Chain transfer from an active center on a macromolecule to a different macromolecule.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15408 "An active center may be located anywhere along a macromolecular chain."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15408 goldbook:15382)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15408 doi:10.1351/pac200880102163)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15408 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15409))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15409 "kinetic-chain length")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15409 "In a chain polymerization, the rate of chain propagation divided by the sum of the rates of all of the chain-termination processes.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15409 "Chain-termination processes include termination by combination or disproportionation but do not include chain transfer."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15409 "In the absence of chain transfer, the kinetic-chain length will be equal to the degree of polymerization."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15409 doi:10.1351/pac200880102163)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15409 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15410))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15410 "monomer reactivity ratios")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15410 "In binary copolymerization, (a) the ratio (\\(r_{12}\\)) of the rate constant (\\(k_{11}\\)) for the homopropagation of monomer \\(\\rm{M}_{1}\\) to the rate constant (\\(k_{12}\\)) for the cross-propagation of the chain carrier \\(\\ldots -{\\rm{m}}_{1}^{\\ast}\\) with the monomer \\(\\rm{M}_{2}\\) and (b) the ratio (\\(r_{21}\\)) of the rate constant (\\(k_{22}\\)) for the homopropagation of monomer \\(\\rm{M}_{2}\\) to the rate constant for the cross-propagation (\\(k_{21}\\)) of the chain carrier \\(\\ldots -{\\rm{m}}_{2}^{\\ast}\\) with monomer \\(\\rm{M}_{1}\\). Thus, \\(r_{12} = k_{11}/k_{12}, r_{21} = k_{22}/k_{21}\\).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15410 "The reactions involved are \\[\\begin{array}{l} ...-{\\rm{m}}_{1}^{\\ast} + {\\rm{M}}_{1}\\ce{->[\\textit{k}_{11}]} ...-{\\rm{m}}_{1}^{\\ast} \\\\ ...-{\\rm{m}}_{1}^{\\ast} + {\\rm{M}}_{2}\\ce{->[\\textit{k}_{12}]} ...-{\\rm{m}}_{2}^{\\ast} \\\\ ...-{\\rm{m}}_{2}^{\\ast} + {\\rm{M}}_{2}\\ce{->[\\textit{k}_{22}]} ...-{\\rm{m}}_{2}^{\\ast} \\\\ ...-{\\rm{m}}_{2}^{\\ast} + {\\rm{M}}_{1}\\ce{->[\\textit{k}_{21}]} ...-{\\rm{m}}_{1}^{\\ast} \\\\ \\end{array}\\] where \\(\\rm{M}_{1}\\) and \\(\\rm{M}_{2}\\) are the two monomers involved in the binary copolymerization and \\(\\ldots -{\\rm{m}}_{i}^{\\ast} (i = 1,2)\\) denotes a chain carrier having an active site on its terminal monomer unit of type \\({\\rm{M}}_{i}\\)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15410 "The symbols \\(r_{12}\\) and \\(r_{21}\\) are often abbreviated to \\(r_{1}\\) and \\(r_{2}\\), respectively."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15410 "The present definition ignores the penultimate-unit effect. For the definition of monomer reactivity ratios accounting for the penultimate-unit effect, see chain-end reactivity ratios (Note 3)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15410 goldbook:15383)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15410 goldbook:15388)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15410 goldbook:15393)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15410 goldbook:15404)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15410 goldbook:15413)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15410 doi:10.1351/pac200880102163)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15410 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15411))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15411 "monomer reactivity scale")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15411 "Relative scale defined by the values of the rate constants for the addition of monomers to a reference active center.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15411 goldbook:15416)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15411 goldbook:15412)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15411 doi:10.1351/pac200880102163)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15411 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15412))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15412 "patterns of reactivity scheme")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15412 "Method for the prediction of monomer reactivity ratios in binary copolymerization, based exclusively on experimentally determined parameters.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15412 "Jenkins’ scheme")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15412 "The parameters may be the monomer reactivity ratios for the separate copolymerizations of the monomers concerned, namely, 1 and 2, with a nonpolar monomer, e.g., styrene (\\(\\rm{S}\\)), and a polar monomer, e.g., acrylonitrile (\\(\\rm{A}\\)). The equations for the desired monomer reactivity ratios, \\(r_{12}\\) and \\(r_{21}\\), are then as follows: \\[\\ln r_{12} = \\ln (r_{1\\rm{S}} r_{\\rm{S}2}) - [\\ln\\,(r_{\\rm{AS}} r_{\\rm{S}2}/r_{\\rm{A}2)}][\\ln\\,(r_{\\rm{SA}} r_{1\\rm{S}}/r_{1\\rm{A}})]/\\ln\\,(r_{\\rm{AS}} r_{\\rm{SA}})\\] \\[\\ln r_{21} = \\ln (r_{2\\rm{S}} r_{\\rm{S}1}) - [\\ln\\,(r_{\\rm{AS}} r_{\\rm{S}1}/r_{\\rm{A}1)}][\\ln\\,(r_{\\rm{SA}} r_{2\\rm{S}}/r_{2\\rm{A}})]/\\ln\\,(r_{\\rm{AS}} r_{\\rm{SA}})\\]"^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15412 "The patterns of reactivity scheme is known also as Jenkins’ scheme."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15412 goldbook:15383)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15412 doi:10.1351/pac200880102163)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15412 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15413))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15413 "penultimate-unit effect")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15413 "Phenomenon that the penultimate monomer unit preceding the active center on the terminal unit of an active polymer chain affects the reactivity of that active center.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15413 goldbook:15388)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15413 doi:10.1351/pac200880102163)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15413 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15414))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15414 "primary-radical termination")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15414 "Termination reaction involving a radical chain carrier and a primary radical.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15414 doi:10.1351/pac200880102163)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15414 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15415))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15415 "pulsed-laser polymerisation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15415 "Polymerization initiated by successive pulses of laser light.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15415 "PLP")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15415 "In a radical polymerization, PLP allows determination of the propagation rate constants."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15415 doi:10.1351/pac200880102163)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15415 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15416))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15416 "<i>Q-e</i> scheme")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15416 "Empirical equations expressing the monomer reactivity ratios in a binary radical copolymerization, \\(r_{12}\\) and \\(r_{21}\\), in terms of the empirical parameters \\(Q\\) and \\(e\\) for the two monomers, namely, \\(\\rm{Q}_{1}\\), \\(\\rm{Q}_{2}\\), \\(\\rm{e}_{1}\\), and \\(\\rm{e}_{2}\\), with\\(r_{12} = (Q_{1}/Q_{2})\\exp [-{e_{1}}(e_{1} - e_{2})]\\) and \\(r_{21} = (Q_{2}/Q_{1}) \\exp [-{e_{2}}(e_{2} - e_{1})]\\)")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15416 "Alfrey–Price scheme")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15416 "Although the parameters are empirically derived, the parameter \\(Q\\) is considered to be a measure of the stabilization by conjugation of a monomer and the radical derived from it, while the parameter \\(e\\) is considered to be a measure of the polar effects of substituents on the monomer and the radical derived from it."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15416 "The Q-e scheme is known also as the Alfrey–Price scheme."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15416 goldbook:15383)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15416 goldbook:15410)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15416 doi:10.1351/pac200880102163)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15416 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15417))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15417 "radical reactivity scale")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15417 "Scale of the values of the rate constants for the reaction of radicals with a reference monomer.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15417 doi:10.1351/pac200880102163)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15417 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15418))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15418 "rate of polymerisation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15418 "Rate of consumption of monomers in a chain polymerization, or the rate of consumption of the functional groups in the reaction mixture of a polycondensation or polyaddition.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15418 doi:10.1351/pac200880102163)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15418 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15419))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15419 "secondary radical")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15419 "Radical formed by the rearrangement or fragmentation of a primary radical that is capable of initiating a polymerization.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15419 "The term \"secondary radical\" is also used to designate a radical centered on a secondary carbon atom, e.g., a 2-propyl radical."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15419 doi:10.1351/pac200880102163)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15419 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15420))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15420 "self-initiated polymerisation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15420 "Polymerization in which initiating species are formed exclusively from the monomer.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15420 doi:10.1351/pac200880102163)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15420 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15421))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15421 "solid-state polymerisation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15421 "Polymerization of a crystalline monomer.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15421 "The initiating species can be formed by the action of heat, irradiation of the monomer with, e.g., ultraviolet light or γ-rays, or (less frequently) by chemical initiation."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15421 "A solid-state polymerization may lead to a semi-crystalline polymer having a crystal structure different from that of the crystalline monomer, or alternatively it may proceed as a topochemical polymerization."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15421 "Depending on the initiation mode and the structure of the monomer, a solid-state polymerization may proceed by a radical or an ionic mechanism."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15421 "Use of the term \"bulk polymerization\" to describe solid-state polymerization is discouraged."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15421 goldbook:15423)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15421 doi:10.1351/pac200880102163)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15421 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15422))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15422 "spontaneous termination")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15422 "Chain termination proceeding as a unimolecular process.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15422 doi:10.1351/pac200880102163)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15422 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15423))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15423 "topochemical polymerisation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15423 "Solid-state polymerization, resulting in the formation of a polymer having essentially the same crystal structure as that of the monomer.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15423 "A topochemical polymerization is usually initiated by irradiation of the crystalline monomer with, e.g., ultraviolet light, γ-rays, or by chemical initiators."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15423 "A topochemical polymerization does not involve significant atomic or molecular motions."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15423 goldbook:15421)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15423 doi:10.1351/pac200880102163)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15423 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15424))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15424 "transamidation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15424 "Interchange reaction involving amide groups.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15424 "amide interchange")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15424 "Transamidations commonly occur during polycondensations to form polyamides."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15424 doi:10.1351/pac200880102163)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15424 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15425))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15425 "transesterification")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15425 "Interchange reaction involving ester groups.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:15425 "ester interchange")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15425 "Transesterifications commonly occur during polycondensations to form polyesters."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15425 doi:10.1351/pac200880102163)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15425 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15427))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15427 "zwitterionic copolymerisation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15427 "Copolymerization that is a zwitterionic polymerization.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15427 "A zwitterionic copolymerization usually involves a nucleophilic monomer and an electrophilic monomer, and it may produce an alternating copolymer."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15427 goldbook:15428)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15427 doi:10.1351/pac200880102163)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15427 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15428))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15428 "zwitterionic polymerisation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15428 "Chain polymerization in which a growing macromolecule bears two ionic chain carriers of opposite signs, at one or both of its ends.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15428 "Chains in a zwitterionic polymerization may grow from one or both of their ends."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15428 doi:10.1351/pac200880102163)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15428 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15429))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15429 "cyclic macromolecule")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15429 "Macromolecule in which the termini of the backbone are connected to form a ring.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15429 "Linear macromolecules comprising constitutional units that include small cyclic structures [e.g., the phenylene groups in poly(ethylene terephthalate)] are not cyclic macromolecules. However, a cyclic molecule comprising such constitutional (repeating) units is a cyclic macromolecule."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15429 doi:10.1351/pac200880020201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15429 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15430))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15430 "main ring")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15430 "Macrocycle in a bridged polycyclic macromolecule or polycyclic macromolecular portion that contains the subunits of highest seniority.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15430 "In macrocyclic molecules with macrocyclic substituents, the ring that contains the subunits of highest seniority is called the parent macrocycle or macrocyclic system."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15430 goldbook:15432)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15430 doi:10.1351/pac200880020201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15430 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15431))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15431 "path length")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15431 "Number of polymer main-chain (backbone) atoms between two subunits.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15431 "Where a ring or ring system constitutes all or part of a path between two subunits, the shortest continuous chain of atoms in the ring or ring system is selected."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15431 doi:10.1351/pac200880020201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15431 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15432))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15432 "polycyclic macromolecule")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15432 "Molecule that includes more than one macrocycle, all of which have at least one atom in common with another macrocycle.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15432 "Molecules that have two rings without any common atom are not considered polycyclic, e.g., biphenyl. In general terminology, however, they are often regarded as polycyclic."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15432 "\"Multicyclic\" or \"pluricyclic\" have been proposed as alternative terms for polycyclic. In accordance with nomenclature of organic chemistry, the term \"polycyclic\" is used here, since it does not lead to confusion with respect to \"poly\" in polymer. Therefore, the use of \"multicyclic\" or \"pluricyclic\" is discouraged as an alternative for \"polycyclic\"."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15432 doi:10.1351/pac200880020201)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15432 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15433))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15433 "abiotic degradation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15433 "Process in which a substance is converted to simpler products by physical or chemical mechanisms.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15433 doi:10.1351/pac200779071153)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15433 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15434))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15434 "abortifacient")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15434 "Substance that causes pregnancy to end prematurely and causes an abortion.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15434 doi:10.1351/pac200779071153)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15434 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15435))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15435 "abuse")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15435 "Improper use of drugs or other substances.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15435 doi:10.1351/pac200779071153)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15435 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15436))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15436 "acaricide")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15436 "Substance intended to kill mites, ticks, or other Acaridae.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15436 doi:10.1351/pac200779071153)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15436 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15437))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15437 "acceptable residue level")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15437 "Acceptable concentration of a residue that has been established for an antibiotic found in human or animal foods.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15437 doi:10.1351/pac200779071153)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15437 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15438))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15438 "acceptable risk")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15438 "Probability of suffering disease or injury that is considered to be sufficiently small to be 'negligible'.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15438 "Calculated risk of an increase of one case in a million people per year for cancer is usually considered to be negligible."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15438 doi:10.1351/pac200779071153)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15438 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15439))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15439 "accepted risk")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15439 "Probability of suffering disease or injury that is accepted by an individual.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15439 doi:10.1351/pac200779071153)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15439 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15440))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15440 "accidental exposure")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15440 "Unintended contact with a substance or change in the physical environment (including, e.g., radiation) resulting from an accident.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15440 doi:10.1351/pac200779071153)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15440 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15441))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15441 "acid dissociation constant")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15441 "Equilibrium constant for the following reaction of an acid \\(\\ce{HB}\\): \\[\\begin{gathered} \\ce{HB(aq)  H^{+}(aq) + B^{-}(aq)} \\\\ K_{\\rm{a}} = [\\ce{H^{+}}][\\ce{B^{-}}]/[\\ce{HB}]c^{\\rm{o}} \\end{gathered}\\] where \\(c^{\\rm{o}} = \\pu{1 mol L-1}\\) is the standard amount concentration and activity coefficients have been neglected.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15441 "This constant, because activity coefficients are neglected, is valid at a specified ionic strength. The thermodynamic dissociation constant is found by suitable extrapolation of the conditional constant to zero ionic strength. Note that it is defined as a dimensionless quantity, but sometimes it is given dimensions by omitting the standard amount concentration."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:15441 "Because this constant differs for each acid and varies over many degrees of magnitude, the acidity constant is often represented by the additive inverse of its common logarithm, represented by the symbol \\(\\pu{p}K_{\\rm{a}}\\) (using the same mathematical relationship as [\\(\\ce{H^{+}}\\)] is to \\(\\rm{pH}\\)), viz.: \\[\\pu{p}K_{\\rm{a}} = -\\log_{10}K_{\\rm{a}}\\] In general, a larger value of \\(K_{\\rm{a}}\\) (or a smaller value of \\(\\pu{p}K_{\\rm{a}}\\)) indicates a stronger acid, since the extent of dissociation is larger at the same concentration."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15441 doi:10.1351/pac200779071153)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15441 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15442))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15442 "action level")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15442 "Concentration of a substance in air, soil, water, or other defined medium at which specified emergency counter-measures, such as the seizure and destruction of contaminated materials, evacuation of the local population or closing down the sources of pollution, are to be taken. Concentration of a pollutant in air, soil, water, or other defined medium at which some kind of preventive action (not necessarily of an emergency nature) is to be taken.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15442 doi:10.1351/pac200779071153)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15442 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15443))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15443 "active ingredient")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:15443 "Component of a mixture responsible for the biological effects of the mixture.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:15443 goldbook:15815)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:15443 doi:10.1351/pac200779071153)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:15443 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:15444))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:15444 "active metabolite")
