AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:16211 "Photochemical induction of molecular chirality.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:16211 doi:10.1351/pac200779030293)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:16211 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:16212))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:16212 "photoenolisation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:16212 "A special case of phototautomerization.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:16212 goldbook:16217)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:16212 doi:10.1351/pac200779030293)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:16212 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:16213))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:16213 "photorefractive effect")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:16213 "Photoinduced change in refractive index.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:16213 doi:10.1351/pac200779030293)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:16213 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:16214))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:16214 "photoremovable protecting group")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:16214 "Release of a reactive species by photolysis of a molecular entity. The release may be induced by direct excitation, by triplet sensitization, or by photoinduced electron transfer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:16214 "PPG")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:16214 "Photoremovable protecting groups have numerous applications in synthesis (\"orthogonal deprotection\"), biochip production, imaging, time-resolved X-ray crystallography, etc. When excited with pulsed lasers, photoremovable protecting groups that release bioactive molecular species such as neurotransmitters rapidly can provide spatial and temporal control of their concentration, so that physiological response times can be determined."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:16214 "Bioactive molecular species that are inactivated by a photoremovable protecting group are often called caged compounds or photocages (e.g., ATP)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:16214 goldbook:16199)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:16214 doi:10.1351/pac200779030293)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:16214 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:16215))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:16215 "photostimulated unimolecular radical nucleophilic substitution")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:16215 "Nucleophilic substitution in a substrate through processes that involve electron transfer steps. The reaction occurs through chain steps. The most extensively used method of initiation is photoinitiation.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:16215 "Many types of compounds, i.e., aliphatic and aromatic species, such as perfluoroalkyl-, cycloalkyl-, neopentyl-, bridgehead-, and alkylmercury halides, as well as carbanions derived from various compounds, are substrates in \\(S_{\\rm{RN}}1\\) reactions."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:16215 doi:10.1351/pac200779030293)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:16215 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:16216))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:16216 "photosubstitution")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:16216 "Photochemical process leading to a substitution reaction.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:16216 doi:10.1351/pac200779030293)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:16216 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:16217))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:16217 "phototautomerisation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:16217 "Photoisomerization of the general form \\[\\ce{G-X-Y=Z [h u] X=Y-Z-G}\\]")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:16217 "The commonest case, when \\(\\rm{G} = \\ce{H^{+}}\\), is also known as \"prototropy\"."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:16217 doi:10.1351/pac200779030293)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:16217 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:16218))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:16218 "polar driving force")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:16218 "The negative of the standard Gibbs energy change (i.e., \\(-\\Delta G^{\\circ}\\)) for outer-sphere electron transfer in polar solvents, where the electrostatic work terms in the expression used for the calculation of the Gibbs energy of photoinduced electron transfer are in general negligibly small.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:16218 "The work term might not be negligibly small even in polar solvents for large molecules undergoing a large change in dipole moment upon electron transfer."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:16218 doi:10.1351/pac200779030293)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:16218 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:16219))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:16219 "polarisation spectroscopy")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:16219 "In absorption experiments, polarization spectroscopy is performed with polarized light on anisotropic samples.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:16219 "Spectroscopy with natural (unpolarized) light on anisotropic samples will show directional effects, since the electric vectors of natural light are not isotropic, but are restricted to a plane perpendicular to the beam. In two-photon processes, for example, luminescence measured with linear polarizers in both beams, an aligned sample is not required since it will be created by the exciting photon through photoselection. However, aligned samples allow a larger number of independent experiments to be recorded and thus contain more information."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:16219 doi:10.1351/pac200779030293)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:16219 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:16221))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:16221 "spectral fluence")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:16221 "Derivative of fluence, \\(H_{\\rm{o}}\\), with respect to wavelength, _010366_.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:16221 "All spectral terms may also be defined as derivatives with respect to frequency, \\(\\nu\\), or wavenumber, \\(\\tilde{\\nu}\\), and are referred to, when necessary, as in terms of wavelength or frequency or wavenumber, respectively."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:16221 doi:10.1351/pac200779030293)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:16221 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:16224))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:16224 "genetic epidemiology")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:16224 "Study of the correlations between phenotypic trends and genetic variation across population groups and the application of the results of such a study to control of health problems.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:16224 doi:10.1351/pac200779071153)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:16224 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:16225))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:16225 "risk ratio")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:16225 "Value obtained by dividing the probability of occurrence of a specific effect in one group by the probability of occurrence of the same effect in another group, or the value obtained by dividing the probability of occurrence of one potentially hazardous event by the probability of occurrence of another.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:16225 "Calculation of such ratios is used in choosing between options in risk management."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:16225 doi:10.1351/pac200779071153)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:16225 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:16226))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:16226 "toxicity exposure ratio")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:16226 "Ratio of the measure of the effects (e.g., \\(\\pu{LD_{50}}\\), \\(\\pu{LC_{50}}\\), NOEC) to the estimated exposure.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:16226 "TER")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:16226 "It is the reciprocal of a risk quotient or hazard quotient."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:16226 doi:10.1351/pac200779071153)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:16226 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:16228))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:16228 "bowtie entanglement")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:16228 "Chain entanglement with topology similar to that of a bowtie.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:16228 "butterfly entanglement")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:16228 doi:10.1351/pac200779101801)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:16228 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:16229))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:16229 "acute effect")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:16229 "Effect of finite duration occurring rapidly (usually in the first \\(\\pu{24 h}\\) or up to \\(\\pu{14 d}\\)) following a single dose or short exposure to a substance or radiation.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:16229 doi:10.1351/pac200779091583)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:16229 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:16230))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:16230 "acute exposure")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:16230 "Exposure of short duration.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:16230 goldbook:16232)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:16230 doi:10.1351/pac200779091583)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:16230 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:16231))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:16231 "chronic")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:16231 "Long-term (in relation to exposure or effect).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:16231 "In experimental toxicology, chronic refers to mammalian studies lasting considerably more than 90 days or to studies occupying a large part of the lifetime of an organism."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:16231 "In clinical medicine, long-established or long-lasting."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:16231 doi:10.1351/pac200779091583)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:16231 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:16232))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:16232 "chronic exposure")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:16232 "Continued exposures occurring over an extended period of time, or a significant fraction of the test species’ or of the group of individuals’, or of the population’s lifetime.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:16232 "long-term exposure")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:16232 goldbook:16230)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:16232 doi:10.1351/pac200779091583)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:16232 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:16233))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:16233 "benchmark concentration")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:16233 "Statistical lower CL on the concentration that produces a defined response (called the benchmark response or BMR, usually \\(\\pu{5\\%}\\) or \\(\\pu{100\\%}\\)) for an adverse effect compared to background, defined as \\(\\pu{0\\%}\\).Dose–response curve showing BMC and BMCL (BMC 10 % lower CL).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:16233 "BMC")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:16233 doi:10.1351/pac200779091583)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:16233 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:16234))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:16234 "physiologically based pharmacokinetic modeling")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:16234 "Mathematical modeling of kinetic behavior of a substance, based on measured physiological parameters.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:16234 "PBPK")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:16234 "toxicologically based pharmacokinetic modeling")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:16234 doi:10.1351/pac200779091583)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:16234 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:16235))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:16235 "deterministic effect")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:16235 "Phenomenon committed to a particular outcome determined by fundamental physical principles.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:16235 "deterministic process")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:16235 doi:10.1351/pac200779091583)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:16235 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:16236))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:16236 "stochastic")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:16236 "Pertaining to or arising from chance and hence obeying the laws of probability.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:16236 doi:10.1351/pac200779091583)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:16236 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:16237))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:16237 "effect")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:16237 "Change in biochemistry, morphology, physiology, growth, development, or lifespan of an organism which results in impairment of functional capacity or impairment of capacity to compensate for additional stress or increase in susceptibility to other environmental influences.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:16237 doi:10.1351/pac200779091583)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:16237 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:16238))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:16238 "elimination rate")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:16238 "Derivative with respect to time of the concentration or amount of a substance in the body, or a part thereof, resulting from elimination.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:16238 doi:10.1351/pac200779091583)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:16238 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:16239))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:16239 "local effect")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:16239 "Change occurring at the site of contact between an organism and a toxicant.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:16239 doi:10.1351/pac200779091583)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:16239 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:16240))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:16240 "toxicant")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:16240 "This is the preferred term for a substance that is considered to be toxic under circumstances which are thought likely to happen.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:16240 "This word comes from the Greek toxikos \"of or for the bow\" and was originally applied to the poison used to tip arrows. The term \"poison\" is nearly a synonym, but tends to be applied to substances that may be deliberately used for poisoning, such as pesticides, and often has overtones of criminal use."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:16240 doi:10.1351/pac200779091583)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:16240 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:16241))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:16241 "medicine")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:16241 "Any drug or remedy.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:16241 "This definition depends on usage. Any substance, e.g., herbs, willow bark, or honey, may be used as a drug or a remedy and, as always, the end effect will depend on the dose."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:16241 doi:10.1351/pac200779091583)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:16241 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:16242))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:16242 "suspension of solid charged particles")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:16242 "Dispersion of solid electrically charged particles, commonly larger in size range than colloidal particles (of approximate diameter range \\(\\pu{{1}{-}{1000} nm}\\)) (dispersed phase), in water or an aqueous solution (continuous, liquid phase).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:16242 "Suspension can be a uniform system, i.e., an optically equable (uniform) mixture of both phases, or a combined system in which a part of the liquid phase of the equilibrated suspension eqs is separated from the rest of the suspension. By sedimentation of particles, a concentrated phase (sediment) can be formed, in which particles are still surrounded by the intrinsic liquid phase, the eqs. Both parts remain in physical and electrical contact."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:16242 doi:10.1351/pac200779010081)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:16242 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:16243))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:16243 "suspension potentiometric cell")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:16243 "Galvanic cell containing, as its essential component, a uniform or combined suspension or one of its separated parts alone, the eqs or sediment.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:16243 doi:10.1351/pac200779010081)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:16243 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:16244))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:16244 "anomalous liquid junction potential")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:16244 "Electrochemical potential that arises at the reference electrode–measurement solution interface when, during a potentiometric measurement, the filling solution of the salt bridge of the reference electrode contacts the charged particles of a suspension.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:16244 "The value of the anomalous liquid junction potential can exceed significantly the commonly occurring liquid junction potential, depending on the suspension species and the concentration of the filling solution. The contact between the electrolyte in the reference electrode (or its salt bridge) and the charged particles can change the ion arrangement around the particles and modify the approximate equality of the ion transport numbers in the electrolyte diffusion front (e.g., by ion exchange of \\(\\ce{H^{+}}\\) or \\(\\ce{OH^{-}}\\)); this ion exchange will diminish the suppression of the diffusion potential."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:16244 doi:10.1351/pac200779010081)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:16244 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:16245))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:16245 "pIon")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:16245 "General mathematical expression form of any ion X activity: \\[\\rm{p(ion\\ X)} = {\\rm{pX}} = -\\lg {\\rm{a_{X}}} = -\\lg ({\\rm{m_{X}} \\gamma_{X}/m^{\\circ}})\\], analogously to \\[\\pu{pH} = -\\lg {\\rm{a_{H}}} = -\\lg ({\\rm{m_{H}} \\gamma_{H}/m^{\\circ}})\\].")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:16245 "Practical pIon measurement with the proper reversible ISE can be carried out by means of a galvanic cell, composed correspondently to cell V. The accuracy and uncertainty of results obtained with ISEs depend analogously as in pH measurement for all on validity of standard solutions used, if the common guidelines for potentiometric measurement are taken in account."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:16245 "The term \"pIon\" is used mainly in the literature, oriented to the practical routine work."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:16245 doi:10.1351/pac200779010081)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:16245 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:16246))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:16246 "suspension pH")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:16246 "Readings on a pH-meter scale obtained for a suspension of soil (in water or electrolyte) by any method for potentiometric pH measurement, performed in a manner analogous to the pH measurement in solutions.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:16246 "soil suspension pH")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:16246 "suspension soil pH")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:16246 "Most of the reported \"suspension (soil) pH\" values have no known quantitative connection with the hydrogen ion activity in suspensions; nevertheless, they are more or less repeatable characteristic values of the measured suspensions."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:16246 doi:10.1351/pac200779010081)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:16246 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:16247))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:16247 "bridgehead atom")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:16247 "Atom that is part of two or more rings in a polycyclic molecule and that is separated from another bridgehead atom by bridges all of which contain at least one other atom.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:16247 "bridgehead")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:16247 doi:10.1515/pac-2018-1010)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:16247 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:16248))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:16248 "unimolecular")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:16248 "Feature of a reaction in which only one molecular entity is involved.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:16248 doi:10.1515/pac-2018-1010)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:16248 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:16249))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:16249 "initialisation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:16249 "Process for converting a starting initiator or chain transfer agent into a macro-initiator or macro-chain-transfer agent during reversible-deactivation polymerization (RDP).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:16249 "In RAFT polymerization, initialization is sometimes known as the pre-equilibrium step."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:16249 goldbook:08935)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:16249 goldbook:08947)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:16249 goldbook:08962)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:16249 goldbook:08963)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:16249 goldbook:08912)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:16249 doi:10.1515/pac-2020-1211)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:16249 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:16250))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:16250 "conjugate")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:16250 "Molecule or compound designed to support, transport, and/or deliver one or several active species in order to take advantage of their specificity.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:16250 doi:10.1515/pac-2020-0502)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:16250 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:16251))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:16251 "scattering coefficient")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:16251 "Negative Napierian logarithm of the ratio of the intensity of radiation scattered (\\(I_{\\rm{s}}\\)) by a non-absorbing sample to the incident intensity (\\(I_{0}\\)), divided by the path-length, \\(l\\). \\[s = -\\ln(I_{s}/I_{0})/l\\]")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:16251 "SI unit: \\(\\pu{m-1}\\)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:16251 goldbook:08278)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:16251 doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:16251 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:16252))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:16252 "numerical aperture")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:16252 "For an optical fibre, \\(n_{\\rm{o}}\\) sin \\(\\theta_{\\alpha}\\), where \\(n_{\\rm{o}}\\) is the refractive index of the exterior medium and \\(\\theta_{\\alpha}\\) is the maximum input half angle that can support propagation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:16252 "NA")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:16252 doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0203)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:16252 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:16253))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:16253 "molar activity (material)")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:16253 "Activity of a specified radionuclide (\\(\\ce{R}\\)) in a material (\\(\\ce{M}\\)) divided by amount of substance of that material.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:16253 "The SI unit of molar activity is \\(\\pu{Bq mol-1}\\), but molar activity is often expressed in unit \\(\\pu{Ci mmol-1}\\). (Curie, symbol \\(\\pu{Ci}\\), is a former unit of activity equal to exactly \\(\\pu{3.7E10 Bq}\\).)"^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:16253 "If the term 'molar activity' is used without qualification, it should be made clear whether it refers to a material or a radionuclide. See: molar activity of a radionuclide."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:16253 goldbook:08763)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:16253 doi:10.1515/pac-2019-0302)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:16253 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:16254))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:16254 "Nernstian response")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:16254 "Response of an ion-selective electrode according to a local thermodynamic equilibrium, over a given range of activity (or concentration) that follows the Nernst equation.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:16254 "For the Nernstian response, the potential difference of the ion-selective electrode cell is proportional to the decadic logarithm of the ionic activity of a given species (\\(a_{\\rm{A}}\\)) with coefficient \\((RT/z_{\\rm{A}}F)/\\log_{10}(\\rm{e})\\) (about \\(0.0592/z_{\\rm{A}}\\,\\pu{V}\\) at \\(\\pu{298.15 K}\\)), where \\(R\\) is the gas constant, \\(T\\) the thermodynamic temperature, \\(F\\) the Faraday constant, and \\(z_{\\rm{A}}\\) the electron number of an electrochemical reaction of species \\(\\ce{A}\\)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:16254 "Nernstian response implies ideal sensitivity, but not necessarily ideal selectivity, since interfering ions may also give a Nernstian response when they are present as the sole potential determining species."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:16254 goldbook:09068)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:16254 goldbook:09063)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:16254 doi:10.1515/pac-2018-0109)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:16254 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:16256))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:16256 "pre-column derivatisation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:16256 "Technique in chromatography in which the sample is chemically derivatized before entering the column.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:16256 doi:10.1515/pac-2017-0111)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:16256 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:16257))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:16257 "phase volume ratio")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:16257 "Volume of the mobile phase divided by volume of the stationary phase in a column in counter-current chromatography.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:16257 "The stationary phase volume retention ratio (\\(S_{\\rm{f}}\\)) has been defined as the ratio of the volume of stationary phase (\\(V_{\\rm{s}}\\)) to the total column/coil volume (\\(V_{\\rm{c}}\\)), \\(S_{\\rm{f}} = V_{\\rm{s}}/V_{\\rm{c}}\\)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:16257 "It is recommended that phase ratio in counter-current chromatography be given the subscript V (i.e. \\(\\beta_{\\rm{V}} = V_{\\rm{M}}/V_{\\rm{S}}\\)) to emphasize phase volume ratio."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:16257 "The \\(\\beta\\) in counter-current chromatography has been defined as the ratio of planetary radius (\\(r\\)) over main rotor radius (\\(R\\)), \\(\\beta = r/R\\)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:16257 goldbook:09887)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:16257 doi:10.1515/pac-2017-0111)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:16257 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:16258))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:16258 "total mobile-phase volume in column")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:16258 "Sum of the interparticle volume of the column and intraparticle volume of the column: \\(V_{\\rm{t}} = V_{0} + V_{\\rm{i}}\\)")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:16258 "In the definition of \\(V_{\\rm{t}}\\) the extra-column volume of the system (\\(V_{\\rm{ext}}\\)) is neglected. If it is not negligible, it must also be added: \\[V_{\\rm{t}} = V_{0} + V_{\\rm{i}} + V_{\\rm{ext}}\\]"^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:16258 goldbook:11549)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:16258 doi:10.1515/pac-2017-0111)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:16258 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:16259))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:16259 "retention time")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:16259 "Retention time of a sample component, the molecules of which are smaller than the largest pores of the particles of the stationary phase but larger than the smallest pores.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:16259 "The retention time is related to the retention volume (in size-exclusion chromatography) (\\(V_{\\rm{R}}\\)) and the flow rate (\\(F_{\\rm{c}}\\)) by \\(t_{\\rm{R}} = V_{\\rm{R}}/F_{\\rm{c}}\\) ."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:16259 goldbook:09963)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:16259 doi:10.1515/pac-2017-0111)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:16259 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:16260))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:16260 "total mobile phase time")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:16260 "Retention time of a sample component the molecules of which are smaller than the smallest pores of the particles of the stationary phase.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:16260 "The total mobile phase time is related to the total mobile phase volume (in size-exclusion chromatography) (\\(V_{\\rm{t}}\\)) and the flow rate (\\(F_{\\rm{c}}\\)) by \\(t_{\\rm{t}} = V_{\\rm{t}}/F_{\\rm{c}}\\) ."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:16260 goldbook:16259)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:16260 doi:10.1515/pac-2017-0111)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:16260 "current"^^xsd:string)
