AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:A00228 "alkyl groups")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:A00228 "Univalent groups derived from alkanes by removal of a hydrogen atom from any carbon atom $\\ce{–C_{n}H_{2n+1}}$. The groups derived by removal of a hydrogen atom from a terminal carbon atom of unbranched alkanes form a subclass of normal alkyl ($n$-alkyl) groups $\\ce{H(CH2)_{n}}$. The groups $\\ce{RCH2}$, $\\ce{R2CH}$ ($\\ce{R  eq H}$), and $\\ce{R3C}$ ($\\ce{R  eq H}$) are primary, secondary and tertiary alkyl groups, respectively.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:A00228 goldbook:A00222)
