Declaration(Class(goldbook:A00420))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:A00420 "apparent viscosity")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:A00420 "The ratio of stress to rate of strain, calculated from measurements of forces and velocities as though the liquid were Newtonian. If the liquid is actually non-Newtonian, the apparent viscosity depends on the type and dimensions of the apparatus used.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:A00420 goldbook:S06037)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:A00420 goldbook:V06627)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:A00420 doi:10.1351/pac197951051213)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:A00420 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:A00421))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:A00421 "appearance energy")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:A00421 "Refers to ionization of a molecule or atom by electron collision or photon absorption. In mass spectrometry it has often been reported as the voltage which corresponds to the minimum energy of the electrons in the ionizing beam necessary for the production of a given fragment ion. In photoionization it is the minimum energy of the quantum of light which produces ionization of the absorbing molecule.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:A00421 "appearance potential")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:A00421 goldbook:I03183)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:A00421 goldbook:M03746)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:A00421 goldbook:P04620)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:A00421 doi:10.1351/pac199062112167)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:A00421 doi:10.1351/pac199163101541)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:A00421 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:A00423))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:A00423 "appearance temperature")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:A00423 "The temperature of the atomization surface at which the analyte signal/noise (S/N) ratio reaches a value of 3 when the quantity of analyte in the atomizer is one hundred times the characteristic mass for peak high absorption.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:A00423 goldbook:N04175)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:A00423 doi:10.1351/pac199264020253)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:A00423 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:A00424))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:A00424 "applied potential")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:A00424 "The difference of potential measured between identical metallic leads to two electrodes of a cell. The applied potential is divided into two electrode potentials, each of which is the difference of potential existing between the bulk of the solution and the interior of the conducting material of the electrode, an \\(i\\ R\\) or ohmic potential drop through the solution, and another ohmic potential drop through each electrode. In the electroanalytical literature this quantity has often been denoted by the term voltage, whose continued use is not recommended.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:A00424 goldbook:E01956)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:A00424 goldbook:V06635)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:A00424 doi:10.1351/pac198557101491)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:A00424 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:A00425))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:A00425 "aprotic solvent")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:A00425 "Non-protogenic (in a given situation). (With extremely strong Brønsted acids or bases, solvents that are normally aprotic may accept or lose a proton. For example, acetonitrile is in most instances an aprotic solvent, but it is protophilic in the presence of concentrated sulfuric acid and protogenic in the presence of potassium tert-butoxide. Similar considerations apply to benzene, trichloromethane, etc.)")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:A00425 "aprotic")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:A00425 goldbook:B00744)
