Declaration(Class(goldbook:AT06947))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:AT06947 "artificial neural networks")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:AT06947 "Artificial neural networks (ANN) are algorithms simulating the functioning of human neurons and may be used for pattern recognition problems, e.g., to establish quantitative structure-activity relationships.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:AT06947 "ANN")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:AT06947 goldbook:PT06976)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:AT06947 doi:10.1351/pac199769051137)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:AT06947 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:AT06983))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:AT06983 "<i>ab initio</i> quantum mechanical methods")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:AT06983 "Methods of quantum mechanical calculations independent of any experiment other than the determination of fundamental constants. The methods are based on the use of the full Schrödinger equation to treat all the electrons of a chemical system. In practice, approximations are necessary to restrict the complexity of the electronic wavefunction and to make its calculation possible.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:AT06983 doi:10.1351/pac199971101919)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:AT06983 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:AT06984))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:AT06984 "agostic interaction")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:AT06984 "The manner of interaction (termed according to the Greek 'to hold or clasp to oneself as a shield') of a coordinatively unsaturated metal atom with a ligand, when the metal atom draws the ligand towards itself. An important type of agostic interaction is the C–H–Metal coordination providing for the activation of the C–H bond in transition metal complexes.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:AT06984 goldbook:A00093)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:AT06984 goldbook:A00187)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:AT06984 goldbook:C01329)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:AT06984 doi:10.1351/pac199971101919)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:AT06984 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:AT06985))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:AT06985 "alternancy symmetry")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:AT06985 "A topological property of the molecular graphs of alternant hydrocarbons which allows the carbon atoms to be divided into two subsets in such a way that no two atoms of the same subset are adjacent. A consequence of this property is the symmetrical arrangement of the energy levels of bonding and antibonding Hückel MOs relative to the level of a nonbonding orbital (energy level of the p AO of a carbon atom).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:AT06985 goldbook:A00249)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:AT06985 goldbook:H02889)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:AT06985 doi:10.1351/pac199971101919)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:AT06985 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:AT06986))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:AT06986 "angular overlap model")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:AT06986 "A method of description of transition metal–ligand interactions and main group stereochemistry, whose basic assumption is that the strength of a bond formed using atomic orbitals on two atoms is related to the magnitude of overlap of the two orbitals.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:AT06986 "AOM")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:AT06986 doi:10.1351/pac199971101919)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:AT06986 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:AT06987))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:AT06987 "antiaromaticity")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:AT06987 "Those cyclic molecules for which cyclic electron delocalization provides for the reduction (in some cases, loss) of thermodynamic stability compared to acyclic structural analogues are classified as antiaromatic species. In contrast to aromatic compounds, antiaromatic ones are prone to reactions causing changes in their structural type, and display tendency to alternation of bond lengths and fluxional behavior (see fluxional molecules) both in solution and in the solid. Antiaromatic molecules possess negative (or very low positive) values of resonance energy and a small energy gap between their highest occupied and lowest unoccupied molecular orbitals. In antiaromatic molecules, an external magnetic field induces a paramagnetic electron current. Whereas benzene represents the prototypical aromatic compound, cyclobuta-1,3-diene exemplifies the compound with most clearly defined antiaromatic properties.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:AT06987 "antithetical to aromaticity")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:AT06987 goldbook:D01583)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:AT06987 goldbook:F02463)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:AT06987 goldbook:P04404)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:AT06987 goldbook:R05333)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:AT06987 doi:10.1351/pac199971101919)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:AT06987 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:AT06988))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:AT06988 "antibonding molecular orbital")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:AT06988 "The molecular orbital whose occupation by electrons decreases the total bonding (as usual, increases the total energy) of a molecule. The energy level of an antibonding MO lies higher than the average of the valence atomic orbitals of the atoms constituting the molecule.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:AT06988 "MO")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:AT06988 goldbook:M03996)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:AT06988 goldbook:V06588)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:AT06988 doi:10.1351/pac199971101919)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:AT06988 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:AT06989))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:AT06989 "antisymmetry principle")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:AT06989 "The postulate that electrons must be described by wavefunctions which are antisymmetric with respect to interchange of the coordinates (including spin) of a pair of electrons. A corollary of the principle is the Pauli exclusion principle. All particles with half-integral spin (fermions) are described by antisymmetric wavefunctions, and all particles with zero or integral spin (bosons) are described by symmetric wavefunctions.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:AT06989 goldbook:PT07089)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:AT06989 doi:10.1351/pac199971101919)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:AT06989 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:AT06990))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:AT06990 "apicophilicity")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:AT06990 "In trigonal bipyramidal structures with a five-coordinate central atom, the stabilization achieved through a ligand changing its position from equatorial to apical (axial). The apicophilicity of an atom or a group is evaluated by either the energy difference between the stereoisomers (permutational isomers) containing the ligand in apical and equatorial positions or the energy barrier to permutational isomerization (see also Berry pseudorotation). In general, the greater the electronegativity and the stronger the $\\ce{\\uppi\\!\\mbox{-}electron}$-withdrawing properties of a ligand (as for $\\ce{Cl}$, $\\ce{F}$, $\\ce{CN}$), the higher is its apicophilicity. The notion of apicophilicity has been extended to four-coordinate bisphenoidal and three-coordinate T-shaped structures, which can be viewed as trigonal bipyramidal species where, respectively, one or two vertices are occupied by phantom ligands (lone electron pairs).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:AT06990 goldbook:P04934)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:AT06990 goldbook:C00930)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:AT06990 goldbook:E01990)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:AT06990 goldbook:E02174)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:AT06990 goldbook:I03295)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:AT06990 goldbook:L03518)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:AT06990 goldbook:S05984)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:AT06990 doi:10.1351/pac199971101919)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:AT06990 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:AT06992))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:AT06992 "atom-atom polarizability")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:AT06992 "A quantity used in perturbation HMO theory as a measure of the change in electron density, \\(q\\), of atom \\(s\\) caused by a change in the electronegativity (or coulomb integral) of atom \\(r\\): \\[\\pi _{\\rm{sr}}=\\frac{\\partial q_{\\rm{s}}}{\\partial a_{\\rm{r}}}\\]")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:AT06992 goldbook:C01366)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:AT06992 goldbook:E01986)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:AT06992 goldbook:E01990)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:AT06992 doi:10.1351/pac199971101919)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:AT06992 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:AT06993))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:AT06993 "atom-bond polarizability")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:AT06993 "A quantity used in perturbation HMO theory as a measure of the change in electron density, \\(q\\), of atom \\(m\\) caused by a change in the resonance integral, \\(\\beta \\), of bond \\(rs\\): \\[\\pi _{\\rm{m,rs}}=\\frac{\\partial q_{\\rm{m}}}{\\partial \\beta _{\\rm{rs}}}\\]")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:AT06993 goldbook:E01986)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:AT06993 goldbook:R05337)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:AT06993 doi:10.1351/pac199971101919)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:AT06993 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:AT06994))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:AT06994 "atomic charge")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:AT06994 "The charge attributed to an atom \\(A\\) within a molecule defined as \\(\\zeta =Z_{\\rm{A}}- q_{\\rm{A}}\\), where \\(Z_{\\rm{A}}\\) is the atomic number of \\(A\\) and \\(q_{\\rm{A}}\\) is the electron density assigned to \\(A\\). The method of calculation of \\(q_{\\rm{A}}\\) depends on the choice of the scheme of partitioning electron density. In the framework of the Mulliken population analysis \\(q_{\\rm{A}}\\) is associated with the so-called gross atomic population: \\(q_{\\rm{A}}=\\sum q_{\\unicode[Times]{x3BC}}\\), where \\(q_{\\unicode[Times]{x3BC}}\\) is a gross population for an orbital \\(\\unicode[Times]{x3BC}\\) in the basis set employed defined according to \\[q_{\\unicode[Times]{x3BC}} = P_{\\unicode[Times]{x3BC}\\unicode[Times]{x3BC}}+\\sum _{\\begin{array}{c}   u  eq \\unicode[Times]{x3BC}   \\end{array}}P_{\\unicode[Times]{x3BC} u}\\ S_{\\unicode[Times]{x3BC} u}\\] where \\(P_{\\unicode[Times]{x3BC}\\unicode[Times]{x3BD} }\\) and \\(S_{\\unicode[Times]{x3BC}\\unicode[Times]{x3BD}}\\) are the elements of density matrix and overlap matrix, respectively (see overlap integral). In the Hückel molecular orbital theory (where \\(S_{\\unicode[Times]{x3BC} u} = \\delta _{\\unicode[Times]{x3BC} u}\\)), \\(q_{\\unicode[Times]{x3BC}} = n_{\\unicode[Times]{x3BC}}\\ P_{\\unicode[Times]{x3BC}\\unicode[Times]{x3BC}}\\), where \\(n_{\\unicode[Times]{x3BC}}\\) is the number of electrons in the \\(\\rm{MO}\\,\\unicode[Times]{x3BC}\\).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:AT06994 "MO")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:AT06994 goldbook:A00499)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:AT06994 goldbook:BT06999)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:AT06994 goldbook:E01986)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:AT06994 goldbook:M03996)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:AT06994 goldbook:O04357)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:AT06994 doi:10.1351/pac199971101919)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:AT06994 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:AT06996))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:AT06996 "aufbau principle")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:AT06996 "A rule for building up the electronic configuration of atoms and molecules. It states that a maximum of two electrons are put into orbitals in the order of increasing orbital energy: the lowest-energy orbitals are filled before electrons are placed in higher-energy orbitals.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:AT06996 goldbook:E01995)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:AT06996 goldbook:O04318)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:AT06996 doi:10.1351/pac199971101919)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:AT06996 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:AT07196))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:AT07196 "ampholytic polymer")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:AT07196 "Polyelectrolyte composed of macromolecules containing both cationic and anionic groups, or corresponding ionizable groups.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:AT07196 "An ampholytic polymer in which ionic groups of opposite sign are incorporated into the same pendant groups is called, depending on the structure of the pendant groups, a zwitterionic polymer, polymeric inner salt, or polybetaine."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:AT07196 goldbook:P04728)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:AT07196 goldbook:PT07220)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:AT07196 goldbook:PT07226)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:AT07196 goldbook:ZT07228)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:AT07196 doi:10.1351/pac200678112067)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:AT07196 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:AT07198))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:AT07198 "anionic polymer")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:AT07198 "Polymer composed of negatively charged macromolecules and an equivalent amount of counter-cations.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:AT07198 "If a substantial fraction of constitutional units carries negative charges, then an anionic polymer is a polyelectrolyte."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:AT07198 "The term anionic polymer should not be used to denote a polymer prepared by anionic polymerization."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:AT07198 goldbook:A00361)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:AT07198 goldbook:P04728)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:AT07198 doi:10.1351/pac200678112067)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:AT07198 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:AT07312))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:AT07312 "absorbed photon flux density")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:AT07312 "Number of photons of a particular wavelength per time interval (spectral photon flux, number basis, \\(q_{\\rm{p},\\lambda }\\), or spectral photon flux, amount basis, \\(q_{n,\\rm{p},\\lambda }\\)) absorbed by a system per volume, \\(V\\). On number basis, SI unit is \\(\\rm{s}^{-1}\\ \\rm{m}^{-4}\\), and the  common unit is \\(\\rm{s}^{-1}\\ \\rm{cm}^{-3}\\ \\rm{nm}^{-1}\\). On amount basis, SI unit is \\(\\pu{mol s-1 m-4}\\), and a common unit is \\(\\pu{einstein s-1 cm-3 nm-1}\\).")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:AT07312 "absorbed spectral photon flux density")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:AT07312 "Mathematical expression: \\(\\frac{q_{p,\\lambda }^{0}[1 - 10^{-A(\\lambda )} ]}{V}\\) on number basis, \\(\\frac{q_{n,p,\\lambda }^{0}[ 1 - 10^{-A(\\lambda )} ]}{V}\\) on amount basis, where \\(A(λ)\\) is the absorbance at wavelength \\(λ\\) and superscript \\(0\\) (zero) indicates incident photons."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:AT07312 "Absorbed spectral photon flux density (number basis or amount basis) should be used in the denominator when calculating a differential quantum yield and using in the numerator the rate of change of the number concentration, \\(\\frac{dC}{dt}\\) or the rate of change of the amount concentration, \\(\\frac{dc}{dt}\\), respectively."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:AT07312 goldbook:A00028)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:AT07312 goldbook:A00295)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:AT07312 goldbook:Q04991)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:AT07312 goldbook:S05821)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:AT07312 goldbook:W06659)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:AT07312 doi:10.1351/pac200779030293)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:AT07312 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:AT07313))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:AT07313 "absorbed radiant power density")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:AT07313 "Spectral radiant energy per time interval (spectral radiant power, \\(P_{\\lambda}\\)) absorbed by a system per volume, \\(V\\). SI unit is \\(\\rm{W m}^{-4}\\); common unit is \\(\\rm{W cm}^{-3}\\ \\rm{nm}^{-1}\\).")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:AT07313 "absorbed spectral radiant power density")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:AT07313 "Mathematical expression: \\(\\frac{P_{\\lambda}^{0}[1 - 10^{-A(\\lambda)}]}{V}\\), where \\(A(\\lambda)\\) is the absorbance at wavelength \\(\\lambda\\) and superscript \\(0\\) (zero) indicates incident radiant power."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:AT07313 goldbook:ST07480)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:AT07313 goldbook:A00028)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:AT07313 goldbook:R05046)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:AT07313 goldbook:S05828)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:AT07313 goldbook:W06659)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:AT07313 doi:10.1351/pac200779030293)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:AT07313 "current"^^xsd:string)
