Declaration(Class(goldbook:AT07327))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:AT07327 "aromatic photocycloaddition")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:AT07327 "Inter- and intramolecular photochemical processes involving the addition of a $\\ce{C–C}$ double (or triple) bond (i) to the 1,2-positions of an arene in which case it is called an ortho photocycloaddition, with formation of a benzocyclobutene (or a benzocyclobutadiene) derivative, (ii) to the 1,3-positions of an arene in which case it is called a meta photocycloaddition, with formation of tricyclo[3.3.0.02,8]oct-3-ene (or octa-3,6-diene) derivatives, or (iii) to the 1,4-positions of an arene in which case it is called a para photocycloaddition, with formation of bicyclo[2,2,2]oct-2-ene (or octa-2,5-diene) derivatives.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:AT07327 goldbook:I03130)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:AT07327 goldbook:PT07451)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:AT07327 doi:10.1351/pac200779030293)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:AT07327 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:AT07328))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:AT07328 "asymmetric photochemistry")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:AT07328 "Photochemical process leading to a chiral substance from an achiral precursor such that one enantiomer predominates over the other.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:AT07328 "Asymmetric induction may be achieved by the use of chiral reagents, a chiral environment, or circularly polarized light."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:AT07328 goldbook:A00483)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:AT07328 goldbook:A00069)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:AT07328 goldbook:C01057)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:AT07328 goldbook:E02069)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:AT07328 doi:10.1351/pac200779030293)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:AT07328 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:AT07329))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:AT07329 "aza-di-π-methane rearrangement")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:AT07329 "Photochemical reaction of a 1-aza-1,4-diene or a 2-aza-1,4-diene in the triplet excited state to form the corresponding cyclopropylimine.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:AT07329 "The rearrangement formally amounts to a 1,2-shift of the imino group and 'bond formation' between the C(3) and C(5) carbon atoms of the azadiene skeleton. 1-Aza-1,4-dienes also undergo the rearrangement to cyclopropylimines using electron-acceptor and electron-donor sensitizers via radical-cation and radical-anion intermediates, respectively. 2-Aza-1,4-dienes rearrange to N-vinylaziridines on irradiation using electron-acceptor sensitizers. In this instance the reaction amounts to a 1,2-shift of the alkene unit and 'bond formation' between the C(1) and C(3) carbon atoms of the azadiene skeleton. "^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:AT07329 goldbook:P04585)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:AT07329 goldbook:A00358)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:AT07329 goldbook:C00907)
