Declaration(Class(goldbook:BT07335))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:BT07335 "branching plane")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:BT07335 "At a conical intersection point, the plane spanned by the gradient difference vector (\\(\\boldsymbol{x_{1}}\\)) and the gradient of the interstate coupling vector (\\(\\boldsymbol{x_{2}}\\)): \\[x_{1} = \\frac{\\delta(E_{2}-E_{1})}{\\delta Q}\\boldsymbol{q}\\] \\[x_{2} = \\boldsymbol{q}\\] where \\(\\boldsymbol{C_{1}}\\) and \\(\\boldsymbol{C_{2}}\\) are the configuration interaction eigenvectors (i.e., the excited and ground-state adiabatic wavefunctions) in a conical intersection problem, \\(H\\) is the conical intersection Hamiltonian, \\(\\textbf{Q}\\) represents the nuclear configuration vector of the system, and thus \\(\\textbf{q}\\) is a unit vector in the direction of vector \\(\\textbf{q}\\). \\(E_{1}\\) and \\(E_{2}\\) are the energies of the lower and upper states, respectively.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:BT07335 "The branching plane is also referred to as the g-h plane. Inspection of \\(\\boldsymbol{x_{1}}\\) and \\(\\boldsymbol{x_{2}}\\) provides information on the geometrical deformation imposed on an excited state molecular entity immediately after decay at a conical intersection. Consequently, these vectors provide information on the ground-state species that will be formed after the decay."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:BT07335 goldbook:A00141)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:BT07335 goldbook:CT07347)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:BT07335 goldbook:C01025)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:BT07335 goldbook:E02257)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:BT07335 goldbook:G02669)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:BT07335 goldbook:G02704)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:BT07335 doi:10.1351/pac200779030293)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:BT07335 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:BT07336))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:BT07336 "Brewster angle")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:BT07336 "When an unpolarized planar electromagnetic wavefront impinges on a flat dielectric surface, there is a unique angle (\\(\\theta_{\\rm{B}}\\)), commonly referred to as Brewster angle, at which the reflected waves are all polarized into a single plane.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:BT07336 "Expression for Brewster angle: \\[\\theta_{\\rm{B}} = \\rm{arctan} \\frac{n_{2}}{n_{1}} = \\rm{arctan} \\left (\\frac{\\varepsilon_{2}}{\\varepsilon_{1}} \\right)^{1/2}\\] where \\(n_{2}\\) and \\(n_{1}\\) are the refractive indices of the receiving surface and the initial medium, respectively, and \\(\\varepsilon_{2}\\) and \\(\\varepsilon_{1}\\) are the relative static permittivities (formerly called dielectric constants)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:BT07336 "For a randomly polarized beam incident at Brewster angle, the electric fields of the reflected and refracted waves are perpendicular to each other"^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:BT07336 "For a wave incident from air on water (\\(n = 1.333\\)), glass (\\(n = 1.515\\)), and diamond (\\(n = 2.417\\)), the Brewster angles are \\(53\\), \\(57\\), and \\(67.5\\ \\rm{degrees}\\), respectively."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:BT07336 goldbook:A00346)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:BT07336 goldbook:D01671)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:BT07336 doi:10.1351/pac200779030293)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:BT07336 "current"^^xsd:string)
