AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:C00860 "carrier")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:C00860 "A substance in appreciable amount which, when associated with a tracer of a specified substance, will carry the tracer with it through a chemical or physical process, or prevent the tracer from undergoing nonspecific processes due to its low concentration.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C00860 goldbook:T06422)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:C00860 doi:10.1351/pac199466122513)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:C00860 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:C00861))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:C00861 "carrier atom")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:C00861 "A participant atom which is neither core nor peripheral and which carries other groups to and from the molecule containing the core atom(s) but which does not itself become covalently attached to that molecule.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C00861 goldbook:C01341)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:C00861 doi:10.1351/pac198961010023)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:C00861 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:C00863))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:C00863 "carrier gas")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:C00863 "A gas introduced in order to transport a sample for analytical purposes. In gas chromatography it is the gas which is passed continuously through the column and whose passage promotes the elution of the components of the sample. The carrier gas together with the portions of the sample present in this phase constitutes the mobile phase.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C00863 goldbook:C00859)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C00863 goldbook:C01075)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C00863 goldbook:E02042)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C00863 goldbook:M03952)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:C00863 doi:10.1351/pac199062112167)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:C00863 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:C00866))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:C00866 "carry-over")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:C00866 "A process by which materials are carried into a reaction mixture to which they do not belong. These materials can be either parts of a specimen, or reagents including the diluent or wash solution. In such cases, carry-over means the transfer of material (specimen or reagents) from one container, or from one reaction mixture, to another one. It can be either unidirectional or bidirectional in a series of specimens or assays. The term carry-over effect is used for carry-over from specimen to specimen.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:C00866 doi:10.1351/pac198961091657)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:C00866 doi:10.1351/pac199163020301)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:C00866 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:C00869))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:C00869 "cascade impactor")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:C00869 "An instrument used for the classification of aerosols according to size and for possible subsequent chemical analysis. Air is drawn through a series of orifices of decreasing size; the air flow is normal to collecting surfaces on which aerosols are collected by inertial impaction. The particles, separated stepwise by their momentum differences into a number of size ranges, are collected simultaneously.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C00869 goldbook:I02985)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C00869 goldbook:M04007)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:C00869 doi:10.1351/pac199062112167)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:C00869 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:C00870))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:C00870 "catabolism")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:C00870 "Reactions involving the oxidation of organic substrates to provide chemically available energy (e.g. ATP) and to generate metabolic intermediates.Generally, the process of breakdown of complex molecules into simpler ones, often providing biologically available energy.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C00870 goldbook:A00314)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C00870 goldbook:O04362)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C00870 goldbook:S06083)
