AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:C00884 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:C00885))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:C00885 "catalytic coefficient")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:C00885 "If the rate of reaction, \\( u\\), is expressible in the form: \\[ u = (k_{0}+\\sum _{\\begin{array}{c}  i  \\end{array}}k_{i}\\ [C_{i}]^{n_{i}})\\ [A]^{\\alpha }\\ [B]^{\\beta }\\ ...\\] where $\\ce{A}$, $\\ce{B}$, ... are reactants and \\(C_{i}\\) represents one of a set of catalysts, then the proportionality factor \\(k_{i}\\) is the catalytic coefficient of the particular catalyst \\(C_{i}\\). Normally the partial order of reaction \\(n_{i}\\) with respect to a catalyst is unity, so that \\(k_{i}\\) is an \\(\\left ( \\mathit{\\alpha } + \\mathit{\\beta } + ... + 1 \\right )\\)th order rate coefficient. The proportionality factor \\(k_{0}\\) is the \\(\\left ( \\mathit{\\alpha } + \\mathit{\\beta } + ...\\right )\\)th order rate coefficient of the uncatalysed component of the total reaction. For example, if there is catalysis by hydrogen and hydroxide ions, and the order of reaction can be expressed in the form: \\[k = k_{0}+k_{\\rm{H}^{+}}\\ [\\rm{H}^{+}]+k_{\\rm{OH}^{-}}\\ [\\rm{OH}^{-}]\\] then \\(k_{H^{+}}\\) and \\(k_{\\rm{OH}^{-}}\\) are the catalytic coefficients for $\\ce{H^{+}}$ and $\\ce{OH^{-}}$, respectively. The constant \\(k_{0}\\) relates to the uncatalysed reaction.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C00885 goldbook:C00874)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C00885 goldbook:C00876)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C00885 goldbook:C01124)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C00885 goldbook:O04322)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C00885 goldbook:R05137)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C00885 goldbook:R05156)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C00885 goldbook:R05163)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:C00885 doi:10.1351/pac199466051077)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:C00885 doi:10.1351/pac199668010149)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:C00885 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:C00889))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:C00889 "catalytic current")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:C00889 "The faradaic current that is obtained with a solution containing two substances B and A may exceed the sum of the faradaic currents that would be obtained with B and A separately, but at the same concentrations and under the same experimental conditions. In either of the two following situations the increase is termed a catalytic current. B is reduced or oxidized at the electrode-solution interface to give a product B' that then reduces or oxidizes A chemically. The reaction of B with A may yield either B or an intermediate in the overall half-reaction by which B' was obtained from B. In this situation the increase of current that results from the addition of A to a solution of B may be termed a regeneration current. The presence at the electrode-solution interface of one substance, which may be either A or the product A' of its reduction or oxidation, decreases the over-potential for the reduction or oxidation of B. In either case the magnitude of the catalytic current depends on the applied potential. If the current observed with a mixture of A and B is smaller than the sum of the separate currents, the term non-additive current should be used.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C00889 goldbook:A00134)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C00889 goldbook:A00424)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C00889 goldbook:F02321)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C00889 goldbook:I03082)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C00889 goldbook:O04362)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:C00889 doi:10.1351/pac198557101491)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:C00889 "current"^^xsd:string)
