AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:C00949 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:C00952))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:C00952 "chain fission yield")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:C00952 "The fraction of fissions giving rise to nuclei of a particular mass number.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C00952 goldbook:N04229)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C00952 goldbook:M03726)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C00952 goldbook:N04256)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:C00952 doi:10.1351/pac198254081533)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:C00952 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:C00955))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:C00955 "chain initiation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:C00955 "The process in a chain reaction that is responsible for the formation of a chain carrier.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C00955 goldbook:C00949)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C00955 goldbook:C00960)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:C00955 doi:10.1351/pac199668010149)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:C00955 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:C00956))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:C00956 "chain length")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:C00956 "In a chain reaction, the average number of times the closed cycle of reactions (involving the chain-propagating reactions) is repeated. It is equal to the rate of the overall reaction divided by the rate of the initiation reaction.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C00956 goldbook:C00960)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C00956 goldbook:C00959)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C00956 goldbook:I03042)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:C00956 doi:10.1351/pac199668010149)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:C00956 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:C00958))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:C00958 "chain polymerization")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:C00958 "A chain reaction in which the growth of a polymer chain proceeds exclusively by reaction(s) between monomer(s) and reactive site(s) on the polymer chain with regeneration of the reactive site(s) at the end of each growth step.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:C00958 "A chain polymerization consists of initiation and propagation reactions, and may also include termination and chain transfer reactions."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:C00958 "The adjective 'chain' in 'chain polymerization' denotes a 'chain reaction' rather than a 'polymer chain'."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:C00958 "Propagation in chain polymerization usually occurs without the formation of small molecules. However, cases exist where a low-molar-mass by-product is formed, as in the polymerization of oxazolidine-2,5-diones derived from amino acids (commonly termed amino-acid N-carboxy anhydrides). When a low-molar-mass by-product is formed, the adjective 'condensative' is recommended to give the term 'condensative chain polymerization'."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:C00958 "The growth steps are expressed by: \\[\\rm{P}_{x} + \\rm{M}\\rightarrow \\rm{P}_{x + 1}\\hspace{5pt}(+\\ \\rm{L}) \\hspace{35pt} \\{x\\}\\in \\{1,2,\\ \\dots \\infty\\};\\] where \\(P_{x}\\) denotes the growing chain of degree of polymerization \\(x\\), \\(M\\) a monomer and \\(L\\) a low-molar-mass by-product formed in the case of condensative chain polymerization."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:C00958 "The term 'chain polymerization' may be qualified further, if necessary, to specify the type of chemical reactions involved in the growth step, e.g. ring-opening chain polymerization, cationic chain polymerization."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:C00958 "There exist, exceptionally, some polymerizations that proceed via chain reactions that, according to the definition, are not chain polymerizations. For example, the polymerization:  proceeds via a radical chain reaction with intermolecular transfer of the radical centre. The growth step, however, involves reactions between molecules of all degrees of polymerization and, hence, the polymerization is classified as a polyaddition. If required, the classification can be made more precise and the polymerization described as a chain-reaction polyaddition."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C00958 goldbook:P04881)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C00958 goldbook:A00354)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C00958 goldbook:C00946)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C00958 goldbook:C00960)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C00958 goldbook:C00963)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C00958 goldbook:D01569)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C00958 goldbook:I03042)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C00958 goldbook:I03098)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C00958 goldbook:M04017)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C00958 goldbook:P04720)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C00958 goldbook:P04740)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C00958 goldbook:T06274)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:C00958 doi:10.1351/pac199668122287)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:C00958 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:C00959))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:C00959 "chain-propagating reaction")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:C00959 "A chain-propagating reaction, or more simply a propagating reaction, is an elementary step in a chain reaction in which one chain carrier is converted into another. The conversion can be a unimolecular reaction or a bimolecular reaction with a reactant molecule.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:C00959 "propagating reaction")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C00959 goldbook:C00949)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C00959 goldbook:C00960)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C00959 goldbook:M03989)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:C00959 doi:10.1351/pac199668010149)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:C00959 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:C00960))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:C00960 "chain reaction")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:C00960 "A reaction in which one or more reactive reaction intermediates (frequently radicals) are continuously regenerated, usually through a repetitive cycle of elementary steps (the 'propagation step'). For example, in the chlorination of methane by a radical mechanism, $\\ce{Cl^{.}}$ is continuously regenerated in the chain propagation steps:   In chain polymerization reactions, reactive intermediates of the same types, generated in successive steps or cycles of steps, differ in relative molecular mass, as in:")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C00960 goldbook:C00948)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C00960 goldbook:C00958)
