Declaration(Class(goldbook:C01205))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:C01205 "complex mechanism")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:C01205 "This term is sometimes applied to an elementary reaction which proceeds via an intermediate species having a lifetime longer than a few rotational periods, in contrast to a direct reaction. However, in view of the danger of confusion with a reaction occurring in more than one step (a composite reaction) this usage is not to be recommended; it is better to use the terms complex-mode mechanism or complex-mode reaction.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C01205 goldbook:C01206)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C01205 goldbook:C01211)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C01205 goldbook:D01773)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C01205 goldbook:E02035)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C01205 goldbook:M03958)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:C01205 doi:10.1351/pac199668010149)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:C01205 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:C01206))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:C01206 "complex-mode reaction")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:C01206 "An elementary reaction which proceeds via an intermediate species having a lifetime longer than a few rotational periods is known as a complex-mode reaction, or as an indirect reaction.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C01206 goldbook:D01773)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C01206 goldbook:E02035)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C01206 goldbook:I03011)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C01206 goldbook:M03958)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:C01206 doi:10.1351/pac199668010149)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:C01206 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:C01210))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:C01210 "composite mechanism")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:C01210 "A reaction that involves more than one elementary reaction is said to occur by a composite mechanism. The terms complex mechanism, indirect mechanism, and step-wise mechanism are also commonly used. There are two main kinds of evidence for a composite mechanism: The kinetic equation for the reaction does not correspond to its stoichiometry.There is experimental evidence, direct or indirect, for intermediates of such a nature that it is necessary to conclude that more than one elementary reaction is involved. There are many types of composite mechanisms, for example: Reactions occurring in parallel, such as:  are called parallel reactions or simultaneous reactions. When there are simultaneous reactions there is sometimes  competition, as in the scheme:  where B and C compete with one another for A.Reactions occurring in forward and reverse directions are called opposing reactions: Reactions occurring in sequence, such as  are known as consecutive reactions.Reactions are said to exhibit feedback if a substance formed in one step affects the rate of a previous step. For example, in the scheme: The intermediate Y may catalyse the reaction  (positive feedback) or it may inhibit it (negative feedback).Chain reactions")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C01210 goldbook:C00960)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C01210 goldbook:C01205)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C01210 goldbook:CT07545)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C01210 goldbook:C01276)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C01210 goldbook:E02035)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C01210 goldbook:I03011)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C01210 goldbook:O04302)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C01210 goldbook:P04403)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C01210 goldbook:ST06775)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C01210 goldbook:S05680)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C01210 goldbook:S05970)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C01210 goldbook:S06026)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:C01210 doi:10.1351/pac199668010149)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:C01210 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:C01211))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:C01211 "composite reaction")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:C01211 "A chemical reaction for which the expression for the rate of disappearance of a reactant (or rate of appearance of a product) involves rate constants of more than a single elementary reaction. Examples are 'opposing reactions' (where rate constants of two opposed chemical reactions are involved), 'parallel reactions' (for which the rate of disappearance of any reactant is governed by the rate constants relating to several simultaneous reactions to form different respective products from a single set of reactants), and stepwise reactions.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C01211 goldbook:C01033)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C01211 goldbook:E02035)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C01211 goldbook:O04302)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C01211 goldbook:R05156)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C01211 goldbook:R05148)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C01211 goldbook:S05680)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C01211 goldbook:S05970)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:C01211 doi:10.1351/pac199365102291)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:C01211 doi:10.1351/pac199466051077)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:C01211 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:C01212))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:C01212 "composite sample")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:C01212 "Often prepared as a representative mixture of several different (usually bulk) samples, and from which the laboratory sample is taken.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C01212 goldbook:B00756)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:C01212 goldbook:L03433)
