AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:D01577 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:D01578))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:D01578 "delayed coking process")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:D01578 "A thermal process which increases the molecular aggregation or association in petroleum-based residues or coal tar pitches leading to extended mesophase domains. This is achieved by holding them at an elevated temperature (usually \\(750{-}765\\ \\rm{K}\\)) over a period of time (\\(12\\ \\rm{to}\\ 36\\ \\rm{h}\\)). It is performed in a coking drum and is designed to ultimately produce delayed coke. The feed is rapidly pre-heated in a tubular furnace to about \\(760\\ \\rm{K}\\).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:D01578 "Needle coke is the premium product of the delayed coking process. It is generally produced from highly aromatic residues from, for instance, the steam cracking of gas oil. Its appearance and preferred orientation of the graphene layers is a consequence of the evolved gaseous products percolating through the mesophase which must not have too high a viscosity. A close control of temperature, time and feedstock is essential. Lower grades, for instance isotropic cokes, are used for carbon electrodes applied, for example, in the production of aluminium."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:D01578 goldbook:N04095)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:D01578 goldbook:A00472)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:D01578 goldbook:C00829)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:D01578 goldbook:C01121)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:D01578 goldbook:C01144)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:D01578 goldbook:C01387)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:D01578 goldbook:D01577)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:D01578 goldbook:G02683)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:D01578 goldbook:I03353)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:D01578 goldbook:M03849)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:D01578 goldbook:V06627)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:D01578 doi:10.1351/pac199567030473)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:D01578 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:D01579))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:D01579 "delayed fluorescence")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:D01579 "Three types of delayed fluorescence are known:   E-type delayed fluorescence: The process in which the first excited singlet state becomes populated by a thermally activated radiationless transition from the first excited triplet state. Since in this case the populations of the singlet and triplet states are in thermal equilibrium, the lifetimes of delayed fluorescence and the concomitant phosphorescence are equal.   P-type delayed fluorescence: The process in which the first excited singlet state is populated by interaction of two molecules in the triplet state (triplet-triplet annihilation) thus producing one molecule in the excited singlet state. In this biphotonic process the lifetime of delayed fluorescence is half the value of the concomitant phosphorescence.   Recombination fluorescence: The first excited singlet state becomes populated by recombination of radical ions with electrons or by recombination of radical ions of opposite charge.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:D01579 goldbook:A00366)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:D01579 goldbook:B00669)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:D01579 goldbook:D01580)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:D01579 goldbook:F02453)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:D01579 goldbook:L03515)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:D01579 goldbook:P04569)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:D01579 goldbook:R05057)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:D01579 goldbook:R05073)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:D01579 goldbook:S05699)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:D01579 goldbook:T06503)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:D01579 doi:10.1351/pac198456020231)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:D01579 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:D01580))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:D01580 "delayed luminescence")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:D01580 "Luminescence decaying more slowly than that expected from the rate of decay of the emitting state. The following mechanisms of luminescence provide examples:triplet-triplet or singlet-singlet annihilation to form one molecular entity in its excited singlet state and another molecular entity in its electronic ground state (sometime referred to as P type),  thermally activated delayed fluorescence involving reversible intersystem crossing (sometimes referred to as E type), and   combination of oppositely charged ions or of an electron and a cation. For emission to be referred to in this case as delayed luminescence at least one of the two reaction partners must be generated in a photochemical process.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:D01580 goldbook:L03641)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:D01580 goldbook:C00907)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:D01580 goldbook:D01579)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:D01580 goldbook:G02704)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:D01580 goldbook:I03123)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:D01580 goldbook:S05699)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:D01580 goldbook:S05697)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:D01580 goldbook:T06305)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:D01580 doi:10.1351/pac198860071055)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:D01580 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:D01581))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:D01581 "delayed neutrons")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:D01581 "Neutrons emitted by fission products formed by nuclear decay (the observed delay is due to the preceding nuclear decay or decays).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:D01581 goldbook:F02400)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:D01581 goldbook:N04227)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:D01581 doi:10.1351/pac198254081533)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:D01581 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:D01582))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:D01582 "deliquescence")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:D01582 "The process that occurs when the vapour pressure of the saturated aqueous solution of a substance is less than the vapour pressure of water in the ambient air. When water vapour is collected by the pure solid compound, a mixture of the solid and liquid or an aqueous solution of the compound forms until the substance is dissolved and is in equilibrium with its environment; at this time the vapour pressure of water over the aqueous solution will equal the partial pressure of water in the atmosphere in contact with it. A crystalline salt aerosol particle will deliquesce in the atmosphere when the relative humidity surpasses a characteristic value, the so-called deliquescence point.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:D01582 goldbook:A00176)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:D01582 goldbook:P04420)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:D01582 goldbook:R05267)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:D01582 goldbook:S05447)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:D01582 doi:10.1351/pac199062112167)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:D01582 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:D01583))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:D01583 "delocalization")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:D01583 "A quantum mechanical concept most usually applied in organic chemistry to describe the $\\ce{\\uppi\\!\\mbox{-}bonding}$ in a conjugated system. This bonding is not localized between two atoms: instead, each link has a 'fractional double bond character' or bond order. There is a corresponding 'delocalization energy', identifiable with the stabilization of the system compared with a hypothetical alternative in which formal (localized) single and double bonds are present. Some degree of delocalization is always present and can be estimated by quantum mechanical calculations. The effects are particularly evident in aromatic systems and in symmetrical molecular entities in which a lone pair of electrons or a vacant p-orbital is conjugated with a double bond (e.g. carboxylate ions, nitro compounds, enamines, the allyl cation). Delocalization in such species may be represented by partial bonds or as resonance (here symbolized by a two-headed arrow) between contributing structures.   These examples also illustrate the concomitant delocalization of charge in ionic conjugated systems. Analogously, delocalization of the spin of an unpaired electron occurs in conjugated radicals.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:D01583 goldbook:A00441)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:D01583 goldbook:B00707)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:D01583 goldbook:C00907)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:D01583 goldbook:C01267)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:D01583 goldbook:C01309)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:D01583 goldbook:E02066)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:D01583 goldbook:M03845)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:D01583 goldbook:M03986)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:D01583 goldbook:N04158)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:D01583 goldbook:R05066)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:D01583 goldbook:R05326)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:D01583 doi:10.1351/pac199466051077)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:D01583 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:D01585))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:D01585 "demister")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:D01585 "Apparatus made of wire mesh or glass fibre which is used to help remove acid mist as in the manufacture of sulfuric acid. Demisters are also components of wet arrestment plants.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:D01585 doi:10.1351/pac199062112167)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:D01585 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:D01586))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:D01586 "denaturation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:D01586 "The process of partial or total alteration of the native structure of a macromolecule resulting from the loss of tertiary or tertiary and secondary structure that is a consequence of the disruption of stabilizing weak bonds. Denaturation can occur when proteins and nucleic acids are subjected to elevated temperature or to extremes of pH, or to non-physiological concentrations of salt, organic solvents, urea or other chemical agents.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:D01586 goldbook:N04245)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:D01586 goldbook:P04898)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:D01586 goldbook:S05447)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:D01586 goldbook:S05530)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:D01586 doi:10.1351/pac199264010143)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:D01586 doi:10.1351/pac199466122587)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:D01586 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:D01587))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:D01587 "denaturation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:D01587 "Addition of methanol or acetone to alcohol to make it unfit for drinking.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:D01587 doi:10.1351/pac199365092003)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:D01587 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:D01589))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:D01589 "denitrification")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:D01589 "The reduction of nitrates to nitrites, dinitrogen oxide (nitrous oxide) or dinitrogen catalysed by microoganisms, e.g. facultative aerobic soil bacteria under anaerobic conditions.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:D01589 goldbook:A00171)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:D01589 goldbook:A00316)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:D01589 doi:10.1351/pac199264010143)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:D01589 "current"^^xsd:string)
