Declaration(Class(goldbook:G02597))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:G02597 "Gaussian band shape")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:G02597 "A band shape described by the Gaussian function: \\[F\\left( u -  u _{0}\\right) = \\frac{a}{\\sqrt{\\pi }}\\ \\rm{e}^{-a^{2}\\ ( u -  u _{0})^{2}}\\] In this equation, \\(a^{-1}\\) is proportional to the width of the band, and \\( u _{0}\\) is the frequency of the band maximum.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:G02597 goldbook:L03628)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:G02597 doi:10.1351/pac199668122223)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:G02597 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:G02598))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:G02598 "Geiger counter")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:G02598 "A gas-filled X-ray detector in which gas amplification reaches saturation and proportionality no longer exists. The output signal does not depend on the incident energy. The time taken for the counter to recover from the saturation is called dead time.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:G02598 goldbook:D01529)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:G02598 goldbook:G02582)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:G02598 goldbook:S05472)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:G02598 doi:10.1351/pac199567101745)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:G02598 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:G02599))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:G02599 "Geiger–Muller counter tube")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:G02599 "A counter tube operated under such conditions that the magnitude of each pulse is independent of the amount of energy deposited in it.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:G02599 goldbook:C01373)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:G02599 doi:10.1351/pac198254081533)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:G02599 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:G02600))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:G02600 "gel")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:G02600 "Non-fluid colloidal network or polymer network that is expanded throughout its whole volume by a fluid.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:G02600 "A gel has a finite, usually rather small, yield stress."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:G02600 "A gel can contain: a covalent polymer network, e.g., a network formed by crosslinking polymer chains or by non-linear polymerization;a polymer network formed through the physical aggregation of polymer chains, caused by hydrogen bonds, crystallization, helix formation, complexation, etc, that results in regions of local order acting as the network junction points. The resulting swollen network may be termed a thermoreversible gel if the regions of local order are thermally reversible;a polymer network formed through glassy junction points, e.g., one based on block copolymers. If the junction points are thermally reversible glassy domains, the resulting swollen network may also be termed a thermoreversible gel;lamellar structures including mesophases, e.g., soap gels, phospholipids and clays;particulate disordered structures, e.g., a flocculent precipitate usually consisting of particles with large geometrical anisotropy, such as in $\\ce{V2O5}$ gels and globular or fibrillar protein gels."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:G02600 "Corrected from previous definition where the definition is via the property identified in Note 1 (above) rather than of the structural characteristics that describe a gel."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:G02600 goldbook:AT06776)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:G02600 goldbook:B00682)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:G02600 goldbook:CT07563)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:G02600 goldbook:CT07136)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:G02600 goldbook:C01434)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:G02600 goldbook:H02769)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:G02600 goldbook:NT07562)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:G02600 goldbook:P04559)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:G02600 goldbook:P04742)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:G02600 goldbook:P04740)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:G02600 goldbook:S05721)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:G02600 goldbook:TT07531)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:G02600 goldbook:Y06727)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:G02600 doi:10.1351/pac200779101801)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:G02600 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:G02602))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:G02602 "geminate pair")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:G02602 "Pair of molecular entities in close proximity in solution within a solvent cage and resulting from reaction (e.g. bond scission, electron transfer, group transfer) of a precursor that constitutes a single kinetic entity.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:G02602 goldbook:C00769)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:G02602 goldbook:E02011)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:G02602 goldbook:I03231)
