Declaration(Class(goldbook:H02762))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:H02762 "helicenes")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:H02762 "ortho-Fused polycyclic aromatic or heteroaromatic compounds in which all rings (minimum five) are angularly arranged so as to give helically shaped molecules, which are thus chiral, e.g. hexahelicene.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:H02762 goldbook:A00441)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:H02762 goldbook:C01057)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:H02762 doi:10.1351/pac199567081307)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:H02762 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:H02763))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:H02763 "helicity")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:H02763 "The chirality of a helical, propeller or screw-shaped molecular entity. A right-handed helix is described as P (or plus), a left-handed one as M (or minus).    The application of this system to the description of conformations considers the torsion angle between two specified (fiducial) groups that are attached to the atoms linked by that bond. The sign of the smaller torsion angle between the fiducial groups defines the chirality sense of the helix. Rules for the selection of fiducial groups according to priority are given by R.S. Cahn, C.K. Ingold and V. Prelog, Angew. Chem. 78, 413-447 (1966), Angew. Chem. Internat. Ed. Eng. 5, 385-415, 511 (1966).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:H02763 goldbook:A00547)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:H02763 goldbook:C01058)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:H02763 goldbook:C01063)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:H02763 goldbook:H02769)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:H02763 goldbook:P04854)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:H02763 goldbook:T06406)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:H02763 goldbook:D01511)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:H02763 doi:10.1351/pac199668122193)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:H02763 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:H02765))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:H02765 "helium–cadmium laser")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:H02765 "A continuous wave laser emitting mainly at \\(325.0\\) and \\(441.6\\ \\rm{nm}\\) from singly ionized cadmium.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:H02765 "cadium–helium laser")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:H02765 goldbook:G02585)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:H02765 goldbook:L03459)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:H02765 doi:10.1351/pac199668122223)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:H02765 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:H02766))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:H02766 "helium dead-space")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:H02766 "The position of the Gibbs surface is often defined experimentally as that surface which encloses the volume of space from which the solid excludes helium gas (the so-called helium dead-space), and is associated with the assumptions that the volume of the solid is unaffected by the adsorption of component i, and that helium is not adsorbed by the solid. This requires that the measurement of the helium dead-space be made at a sufficiently high temperature.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:H02766 goldbook:G02635)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:H02766 goldbook:A00155)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:H02766 doi:10.1351/pac197231040577)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:H02766 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:H02767))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:H02767 "helium ionization detector")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:H02767 "A weak beta source and a high potential raise the helium atom of the carrier gas to a metastable state. All other substances having an ionization potential lower than \\(18\\ \\rm{eV}\\) are ionized, and the current that results is used to measure the components. The detector is usually employed to measure inorganic compounds at concentrations between \\(0.1\\) and \\(10\\ \\rm{ppmv}\\). It has a linear range of about \\(10^{2}\\) but is somewhat unstable and requires great care to ensure the helium purity and to eliminate all leaks in the system.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:H02767 goldbook:C00863)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:H02767 goldbook:I03208)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:H02767 goldbook:L03558)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:H02767 goldbook:M03872)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:H02767 goldbook:U06569)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:H02767 doi:10.1351/pac199062112167)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:H02767 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:H02768))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:H02768 "helium–neon laser")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:H02768 "A continuous wave laser emitting mainly at \\(632.8\\ \\rm{nm}\\), \\(1152.3\\ \\rm{nm}\\), and \\(3391.3\\ \\rm{nm}\\) from excited neutral $\\ce{Ne}$ atoms.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:H02768 goldbook:G02585)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:H02768 goldbook:L03459)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:H02768 doi:10.1351/pac199668122223)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:H02768 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:H02773))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:H02773 "hemes")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:H02773 "Complexes consisting of an iron ion coordinated to a porphyrin acting as a tetradentate ligand, and to one or two axial ligands.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:H02773 "heme derivatives")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:H02773 goldbook:L03518)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:H02773 doi:10.1351/pac199567081307)
