AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:I03293 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:I03294))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:I03294 "isomerism")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:I03294 "The relationship between isomers.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:I03294 goldbook:I03289)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:I03294 doi:10.1351/pac199668122193)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:I03294 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:I03295))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:I03295 "isomerization")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:I03295 "A chemical reaction, the principal product of which is isomeric with the principal reactant. An intramolecular isomerization that involves the breaking or making of bonds is a special case of a molecular rearrangement. Isomerization does not necessarily imply molecular rearrangement (e.g. in the case of the interconversion of conformational isomers).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:I03295 goldbook:I03130)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:I03295 goldbook:I03291)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:I03295 goldbook:M03997)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:I03295 doi:10.1351/pac199466051077)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:I03295 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:I03296))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:I03296 "isomer shift")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:I03296 "Measure of the energy difference between the source (\\(E_{\\rm{s}}\\)) and the absorber (\\(E_{\\rm{a}}\\)) transition. The measured Doppler velocity shift, \\(\\delta \\), is related to the energy difference by \\[E_{\\rm{a}}- E_{\\rm{s}}=\\frac{\\delta \\ E_{\\gamma }}{c}\\] where \\(E_{\\gamma }\\) is the Mössbauer gamma energy and \\(c\\) is the speed of light in vacuum.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:I03296 goldbook:A00034)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:I03296 doi:10.1351/pac197645030211)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:I03296 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:I03298))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:I03298 "isometric")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:I03298 "Two molecular entities that are superposable or can be made superposable by reflection of one of them in a mirror are isometric; otherwise they are anisometric.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:I03298 goldbook:M03986)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:I03298 doi:10.1351/pac199668122193)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:I03298 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:I03302))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:I03302 "isooptoacoustic point")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:I03302 "Wavelength, wavenumber or frequency at which the total energy emitted by a sample as heat does not change upon a chemical reaction in or a physical change of the sample. Its position depends on the experimental conditions.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:I03302 "The spectral differences between the @I03310@ points and the iso-optoacoustic points are the result of the non-linear relationship between the @M03972@ and the photoacoustic signal."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:I03302 goldbook:W06659)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:I03302 goldbook:F02525)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:I03302 goldbook:I03310)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:I03302 goldbook:M03972)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:I03302 goldbook:W06664)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:I03302 doi:10.1351/pac200779030293)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:I03302 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:I03304))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:I03304 "isopotential point")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:I03304 "For an ion-selective electrode cell, there is often a particular activity of the measured ion for which the emf of the cell is independent of temperature. That activity, and the corresponding potential difference, defines the isopotential point. The specification of the ion-selective electrode and outer reference electrode must be described. Comment: When an isothermal cell is used with identical reference electrodes, the isopotential point is the activity of sensed species that gives zero net membrane potential, e.g. sensed activity is the same in the inner and outer (test) solution. Calibration lines for different cell temperatures have different slopes, but intersect at a common activity point. Cells with temperature gradients are not recommended.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:I03304 goldbook:I03244)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:I03304 goldbook:I03245)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:I03304 goldbook:M03825)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:I03304 goldbook:R05229)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:I03304 doi:10.1351/pac199466122527)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:I03304 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:I03306))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:I03306 "isoprenoids")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:I03306 "Compounds formally derived from isoprene (2-methylbuta-1,3-diene), the skeleton of which can generally be discerned in repeated occurrence in the molecule. The skeleton of isoprenoids may differ from strict additivity of isoprene units by loss or shift of a fragment, commonly a methyl group. The class includes both hydrocarbons and oxygenated derivatives.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:I03306 goldbook:C00858)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:I03306 goldbook:H02889)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:I03306 goldbook:P04816)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:I03306 goldbook:S06005)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:I03306 goldbook:T06278)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:I03306 goldbook:T06279)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:I03306 doi:10.1351/pac199567081307)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:I03306 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:I03308))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:I03308 "isopycnic separation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:I03308 "Chromatographic separations carried out using constant density conditions. The temperature and pressure may be altered during the run (originally the term 'isoconfertic separation' was used but this term is not recommended).")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:I03308 "isoconfertic separation")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:I03308 doi:10.1351/pac199365112397)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:I03308 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:I03310))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:I03310 "isosbestic point")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:I03310 "Wavelength, wavenumber or frequency at which the total absorbance of a sample does not change during a chemical reaction or a physical change of the sample.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:I03310 "isoabsorption point")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:I03310 "A simple example occurs when one molecular entity is converted into another that has the same molar absorption coefficient at a given wavelength. As long as the sum of the concentrations of the two molecular entities in the solution is held constant there will be no change in absorbance at this wavelength as the ratio of the concentrations of the two entities is varied."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:I03310 "The name derives from the Greek words: isos: equal, the same, and sbestos: extinguishable."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:I03310 "Contrary to a widely accepted idea, the existence of an isosbestic point does not prove that the reaction is a quantitative conversion of one species into a unique other species or that an equilibrium exists between only two species. The observation of isosbestic points only indicates that the stoichiometry of the reaction remains unchanged during the chemical reaction or the physical change of the sample, and that no secondary reactions occur during the considered time range, since \\(A_{\\lambda}l^{-1} = \\sum_{i=1}^{n}\\varepsilon_{i}(\\lambda) c_{i}\\) is invariant (\\(A_{\\lambda}\\) is the absorbance at wavelength \\(\\lambda\\), \\(I\\) is the optical path, \\(\\varepsilon_{i}\\) is the molar decadic absorption coefficient of the species \\(i\\) of concentration \\(c_{i}\\)). For the reaction $\\ce{A + B → cC + dD + eE}$ with $c$, $d$, and $e$ the percentages of the products $\\ce{C}$, $\\ce{D}$, and $\\ce{E}$, an isosbestic point will be observed at every wavelength where the condition \\(\\varepsilon_{A} + \\varepsilon_{B} = c\\, \\varepsilon_{C} + d\\, \\varepsilon_{D} + e\\, \\varepsilon_{E}\\), provided that the values of the percentages $c$, $d$, and $e$ remain constant during the chemical reaction or the physical change. The use of the obsolete term 'isoabsorption point' is not recommended."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:I03310 goldbook:W06659)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:I03310 goldbook:A00028)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:I03310 goldbook:F02525)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:I03310 goldbook:M03972)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:I03310 goldbook:S06026)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:I03310 goldbook:W06664)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:I03310 doi:10.1351/pac200779030293)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:I03310 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:I03311))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:I03311 "isoselective relationship")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:I03311 "A relationship analogous to the isokinetic relationship, but applied to selectivity data of reactions. At the isoselective temperature, the selectivities of the series of reactions following the relationship are identical.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:I03311 goldbook:I03280)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:I03311 goldbook:I03285)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:I03311 goldbook:S05565)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:I03311 doi:10.1351/pac199466051077)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:I03311 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:I03312))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:I03312 "isoselenocyanates")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:I03312 "Selenium analogues of isocyanates $\\ce{RN=C=Se}$.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:I03312 goldbook:I03269)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:I03312 doi:10.1351/pac199567081307)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:I03312 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:I03313))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:I03313 "isosteric enthalpy of adsorption")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:I03313 "When the addition of the differential amount of component \\(i\\) \\(\\mathrm{d}n_{i}^{\\sigma }\\) or \\(\\mathrm{d}n_{i}^{\\rm{s}}\\) is effected at constant pressure \\(p\\), the differential molar enthalpy of adsorption, \\(\\Delta _{a}H_{i}^{\\sigma}\\) or \\(\\Delta _{a}H_{i}^{\\rm{s}}\\) also called the isosteric enthalpy of adsorption (\\(q^{\\rm{st}}\\)) is defined as: \\[\\Delta _{a}H_{i}^{\\sigma} = -q^{\\rm{st},\\sigma} = U_{i}^{\\sigma} - H_{i}^{\\rm{g}}\\] \\[\\Delta _{a}H_{i}^{\\rm{s}} = -q^{\\rm{st},\\sigma} = H_{i}^{\\sigma} - H_{i}^{\\rm{g}}\\] where \\(H_{i}^{\\rm{s}}=(\\frac{\\partial H^{\\rm{s}}}{\\partial n_{i}^{\\rm{s}}})_{T,p,m,n_{j}^{\\rm{s}}}\\) and \\(H_{i}^{\\rm{g}}\\) is the partial molar enthalpy of component \\(i\\) in the gas phase, i.e. \\((\\frac{\\partial H^{\\rm{g}}}{\\partial n_{i}^{\\rm{g}}})_{T,p,n_{i}^{\\rm{g}}}\\)")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:I03313 goldbook:E02141)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:I03313 doi:10.1351/pac197231040577)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:I03313 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:I03314))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:I03314 "isostilbic point")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:I03314 "Same as isoemissive point.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:I03314 "From the Greek words: isos: equal, and stilbein: to shine."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:I03314 goldbook:I03277)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:I03314 doi:10.1351/pac200779030293)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:I03314 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:I03315))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:I03315 "isotactic macromolecule")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:I03315 "A tactic macromolecule, essentially comprising only one species of configurational base unit, which has chiral or prochiral atoms in the main chain in a unique arrangement with respect to its adjacent constitutional units.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:I03315 "In an isotactic macromolecule, the configurational repeating unit is identical with the configurational base unit."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:I03315 "An isotactic macromolecule consists of meso diads."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:I03315 goldbook:C01057)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:I03315 goldbook:C01250)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:I03315 goldbook:C01253)
