AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:J03359 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:J03360))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:J03360 "Jablonski diagram")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:J03360 "Originally, a diagram showing that the fluorescent state of a molecular entity is the lowest excited state from which the transition to the ground state is allowed, whereas the phosphorescent state is a metastable state below the fluorescent state, which is reached by radiationless transition. In the most typical cases the fluorescent state is the lowest singlet excited state and the phosphorescent state the lowest triplet state, the ground state being a singlet. Presently, modified Jablonski diagrams are frequently used and are actually state diagrams in which molecular electronic states, represented by horizontal lines displaced vertically to indicate relative energies, are grouped according to multiplicity into horizontally displaced columns. Excitation and relaxation processes that interconvert states are indicated in the diagram by arrows. Radiative transitions are generally indicated with straight arrows (→), while radiationless transitions are generally indicated with wavy arrows ⇝.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:J03360 goldbook:E02248)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:J03360 goldbook:E02257)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:J03360 goldbook:G02704)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:J03360 goldbook:M03872)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:J03360 goldbook:M03986)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:J03360 goldbook:R05057)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:J03360 goldbook:R05285)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:J03360 goldbook:T06503)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:J03360 doi:10.1351/pac199668122223)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:J03360 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:J03361))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:J03361 "Jahn–Teller effect")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:J03361 "Molecular distortions due to an electronically degenerate @G02704-1@ state. For non-linear molecular entities in a geometry described by a point symmetry group possessing degenerate irreducible representations there always exists at least one non-totally symmetric vibration that makes electronically degenerate states unstable at this geometry. The nuclei are displaced to new equilibrium positions of lower symmetry causing a splitting of the originally degenerate states (first-order Jahn–Teller effect).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:J03361 "Effect due to the odd terms in the vibronic perturbation expansion. In the case of molecules with a non-degenerate @G02704-2@ but with a low-lying degenerate excited state, distortions of proper symmetry arise that result in mixing of the ground and excited states, thereby lowering the ground-state energy (pseudo Jahn–Teller effect). The pseudo Jahn–Teller effect manifests itself in fluxional behaviour (see fluxional) and stereochemical non-rigidity of molecules and ions. The Jahn–Teller effect generates a surface crossing (e.g., a conical intersection) whereas a pseudo Jahn–Teller effect generates an avoided crossing."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:J03361 goldbook:R05290)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:J03361 goldbook:A00544)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:J03361 goldbook:CT07347)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:J03361 goldbook:E02257)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:J03361 goldbook:F02463)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:J03361 goldbook:G02704)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:J03361 goldbook:ST07107)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:J03361 goldbook:S06166)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:J03361 goldbook:U06569)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:J03361 doi:10.1351/pac200779030293)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:J03361 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:J03362))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:J03362 "Jahn–Teller transition")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:J03362 "A displacive crystal distortion to lower symmetry that cooperatively removes a localized-electron orbital degeneracy at an array of like atoms so as to leave the atoms in the centre of symmetry of their distorted sites. Example: The crystallographic distortion in $\\ce{Mn3O4}$.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:J03362 goldbook:D01556)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:J03362 doi:10.1351/pac199466030577)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:J03362 "current"^^xsd:string)
