Declaration(Class(goldbook:L03549))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:L03549 "linear electron accelerator")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:L03549 "An evacuated metal tube in which electrons pass through a series of small gaps (usually in the form of cavity resonators in the high frequency range) so arranged and spaced that, at a specific excitation frequency, the stream of electrons on passing through successive gaps gains additional energy from the electric field in each gap.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:L03549 doi:10.1351/pac198254081533)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:L03549 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:L03550))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:L03550 "linear energy transfer")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:L03550 "The average energy locally imparted to a medium by a charged particle of specified energy, per unit distance traversed.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:L03550 doi:10.1351/pac198254081533)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:L03550 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:L03551))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:L03551 "linear free-energy relation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:L03551 "A linear correlation between the logarithm of a rate constant or equilibrium constant for one series of reactions and the logarithm of the rate constant or equilibrium constant for a related series of reactions. Typical examples of such relations (also known as linear Gibbs energy relations) are the Brønsted relation, and the Hammett equation.The name arises because the logarithm of an equilibrium constant (at constant temperature and pressure) is proportional to a standard free energy (Gibbs energy) change, and the logarithm of a rate constant is a linear function of the free energy (Gibbs energy) of activation.It has been suggested that this name should be replaced by linear Gibbs energy relation, but at present there is little sign of acceptance of this change. The area of physical organic chemistry which deals with such relations is commonly referred to as 'Linear Free-Energy Relationships'.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:L03551 "linear Gibbs energy relation")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:L03551 goldbook:B00746)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:L03551 goldbook:H02732)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:L03551 goldbook:A00093)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:L03551 goldbook:E02177)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:L03551 goldbook:F02515)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:L03551 goldbook:O04322)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:L03551 goldbook:C05438)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:L03551 doi:10.1351/pac199466051077)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:L03551 "current"^^xsd:string)
