AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:LT06965 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:LT07064))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:LT07064 "least motion principle")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:LT07064 "The statement that those elementary reactions are the most favoured which exhibit the fewest possible alterations in the positions of the atomic nuclei and in the electronic configuration. The most frequently used mathematical formulation of the principle rests on a mechanical model of a molecule in which the energy of structural deformation, when reactants (r) turn into products (p), is assumed to be proportional to the sum of the squares of the changes in the positions of the nuclei common to both reactants and products \\[E=\\sum _{\\begin{array}{c} i \\end{array}}f_{i}\\ (q^{\\rm{p}_{i}}- q^{\\rm{r}_{i}})^{2}\\] where \\(f_{i}\\) is the force constant (in many applications set equal to unity). The equation coincides with the relationship for the potential energy of small vibrations, hence it is valid only at a very early stage of a reaction. This is one of the reasons why many reactions violate the principle of least motion.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:LT07064 "principle of least motion")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:LT07064 goldbook:C01248)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:LT07064 doi:10.1351/pac199971101919)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:LT07064 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:LT07065))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:LT07065 "Lewis octet rule")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:LT07065 "A classical rule for describing the electronic configuration of atoms in molecules: the maximum number of electron pairs that can be accommodated in the valence shell of a first-row element is four. For the second and subsequent row elements there are many exceptions to this rule.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:LT07065 goldbook:C01248)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:LT07065 goldbook:V06588)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:LT07065 doi:10.1351/pac199971101919)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:LT07065 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:LT07066))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:LT07066 "localized molecular orbitals")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:LT07066 "The molecular orbitals located on certain fragments of a molecular system and spatially separated from each other as much as possible. The LMOs are derived from the electron occupied canonical molecular orbitals by subjecting them to a unitary transformation determined by an appropriate physical criterion, e.g. by maximizing the sum of squares of the centroids of occupied MOs (the Foster–Boys procedure) or by minimizing the sum of the exchange (or Coulomb) repulsion integrals between the occupied MOs (the Edmiston–Ruedenberg procedure).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:LT07066 "LMO")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:LT07066 goldbook:C01365)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:LT07066 goldbook:T06446)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:LT07066 doi:10.1351/pac199971101919)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:LT07066 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:LT07067))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:LT07067 "low-spin state")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:LT07067 "When the separation between the highest occupied and the lowest unoccupied molecular orbitals is not large, two alternative electronic states may be considered. The state with two electrons paired up in the HOMO is called a low-spin state. The low-spin state is the ground state when the one-electron energy needed to promote an electron to the LUMO is larger than the Coulomb and exchange repulsion energies required to pair up two electrons in the HOMO.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:LT07067 goldbook:C01365)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:LT07067 goldbook:ET07034)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:LT07067 goldbook:G02704)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:LT07067 goldbook:LT06788)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:LT07067 doi:10.1351/pac199971101919)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:LT07067 "current"^^xsd:string)
