AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:LT07411 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:LT07412))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:LT07412 "laser-jet photochemical technique")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:LT07412 "Technique by which high concentrations of excited states are generated in a jet, permitting the readily determination of spectroscopic properties of those states.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:LT07412 goldbook:E02257)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:LT07412 doi:10.1351/pac200779030293)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:LT07412 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:LT07413))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:LT07413 "LED")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:LT07413 "Acronym for light-emitting diode.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:LT07413 "LED")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:LT07413 goldbook:LT07414)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:LT07413 doi:10.1351/pac200779030293)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:LT07413 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:LT07414))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:LT07414 "light-emitting diode")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:LT07414 "Semiconductor (often a combination of gallium, arsenic and phosphorous or gallium and nitrogen) containing an n region (where electrons are more numerous than positive charges) separated from a p region (where positive charges are more numerous than negative charges). Upon application of a voltage, charges move and emission of ultraviolet, visible or infrared radiation is produced each time a charge recombination takes place. Although a LED emits incoherent monochromatic light, normally a very narrow frequency range is obtained.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:LT07414 "LED")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:LT07414 "This effect is a form of electroluminescence."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:LT07414 "The colour depends on the semi-conducting material used, and can be ultraviolet, visible or infrared."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:LT07414 "Organic light-emitting devices (OLEDs) contain diodes made of small molecules or made of polymeric materials. The latter are sometimes called PLEDs."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:LT07414 goldbook:S05591)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:LT07414 goldbook:C00998)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:LT07414 goldbook:E01966)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:LT07414 goldbook:F02525)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:LT07414 goldbook:IT07399)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:LT07414 goldbook:M03667)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:LT07414 goldbook:UT07492)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:LT07414 goldbook:VT07496)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:LT07414 doi:10.1351/pac200779030293)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:LT07414 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:LT07415))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:LT07415 "linear dichroism")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:LT07415 "For a uniaxial sample with sample axis \\(Z\\) is defined as: \\[\\Delta A_{\\rm{l}} = A_{Z} - A_{Y}\\] where \\(A_{Z}\\) and \\(A_{Y}\\) are the absorption spectra measured with the electric vector of linearly polarized light along and perpendicular to the sample axis, respectively. For an isotropic sample \\(\\Delta A_{\\rm{l}} = 0\\).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:LT07415 "LD")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:LT07415 "Sometimes the reduced dichroism is used instead. It is defined as \\[\\Delta A_{\\rm{r}} = \\frac{A_{Z}\\,-\\,A_{Y}}{A_{Z}\\,+\\,2\\,A_{Y}} = \\frac{A_{Z}\\,-\\,A_{Y}}{3\\,A_{\\rm{iso}}}\\] with \\(A_{\\rm{iso}}\\) the isotropic absorbance. Thus, \\(\\Delta A_{\\rm{r}}\\) is analogous to emission anisotropy and the denominator in the equation corresponds to three times the absorbance measured in a similar but isotropic sample."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:LT07415 "The dichroic ratio \\(d(\\lambda)\\) is also a frequently used function of the wavelength. It is defined as \\[d(\\lambda) = \\frac{A_{Z}}{A_{Y}}\\]"^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:LT07415 "Most naturally-occurring solid samples exhibit linear dichroism. It may also be produced in the laboratory by dissolving the sample molecules in anisotropic solvents such as nematic liquid crystals or stretched polymers. This procedure tends to produce uniaxial samples. Also crystals may be used as aligned solvents and if the sample forms suitable crystals by itself these may be used directly. Other molecular alignment techniques include application of electric or magnetic fields."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:LT07415 "Photoselection is a commonly used technique for the production of aligned samples; both the photoselected subset and the set of remaining molecules may be studied."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:LT07415 goldbook:PT07461)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:LT07415 goldbook:A00028)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:LT07415 goldbook:DT07357)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:LT07415 goldbook:ET07370)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:LT07415 goldbook:I03353)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:LT07415 goldbook:UT07493)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:LT07415 goldbook:W06659)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:LT07415 doi:10.1351/pac200779030293)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:LT07415 "current"^^xsd:string)
