Declaration(Class(goldbook:N04095))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:N04095 "needle coke")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:N04095 "The commonly used term for a special type of coke with extremely high graphitizability resulting from a strong preferred parallel orientation of its turbostratic layer structure and a particular physical shape of the grains.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:N04095 "Needle coke is derived mainly from clean (i.e. lacking hetero atoms and solids) and highly aromatic (i.e. several condensed rings per cluster) feedstocks with a very low concentration of insolubles. Upon solidification a material with a distinctive streaked or flow-like macroscopic appearance is produced. Upon grinding the coke breaks up first into macroscopic needles and then, after further grinding, into microplatelets. Sometimes the word 'acicular' is used as a synonym for needle-like."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:N04095 goldbook:CT06769)
