Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04401))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04401 "paraffin")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04401 "Obsolescent term for saturated hydrocarbons, commonly but not necessarily acyclic. Still widely used in the petrochemical industry, where the term designates acyclic saturated hydrocarbons, and stands in contradistinction to naphthenes.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04401 goldbook:H02889)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04401 goldbook:N04084)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04401 doi:10.1351/pac199567081307)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04401 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04404))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04404 "paramagnetic")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04404 "Substances having a magnetic susceptibility greater than 0 are paramagnetic. They are drawn into a magnetic field.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04404 goldbook:D01668)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04404 goldbook:M03689)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04404 doi:10.1351/pac199466051077)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04404 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04405))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04405 "parent hydride")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04405 "An unbranched acyclic or cyclic structure or an acyclic/cyclic structure having a semisystematic or trivial name to which only hydrogen atoms are attached.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04405 goldbook:T06516)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04405 doi:10.1351/pac199971071327)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04405 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04406))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04406 "parent ion")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04406 "An electrically charged molecular moiety which may dissociate to form fragments, one or more of which may be electrically charged, and one or more neutral species. A parent ion may be a molecular ion or an electrically charged fragment of a molecular ion.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04406 goldbook:M03968)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04406 doi:10.1351/pac199163101541)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04406 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04407))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04407 "partial anodic current")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04407 "When a single electrochemical reaction occurs at an electrode (i.e. all other electrochemical reactions may be neglected): \\[I=I_{\\rm{a}}+I_{\\rm{c}}\\] where \\(I\\) is the total current, \\(I_{\\rm{a}}\\) is the positive partial anodic current and \\(I_{\\rm{c}}\\) is the negative partial cathodic current. When more than one reaction is significant the reactions may be numbered and the numbers used as subscripts: \\(I_{\\rm{1,a}}\\), \\(I_{\\rm{1,c}}\\), \\(I_{\\rm{2,a}}\\), etc. Then: \\[I=\\sum I_{i,\\rm{a}}+\\sum I_{i,\\rm{c}}\\]")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04407 doi:10.1351/pac197437040499)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04407 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04408))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04408 "partial charge exchange reaction")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04408 "Synonymous with partial charge transfer reaction.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04408 goldbook:P04409)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04408 doi:10.1351/pac199163101541)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04408 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04409))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04409 "partial charge transfer reaction")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04409 "An ion/neutral species reaction wherein the charge on a multiply-charged reactant ion is reduced.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04409 doi:10.1351/pac199163101541)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04409 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04410))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04410 "partial decay constant")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04410 "For a radionuclide: the probability in unit time for the decay of one of its nuclei by one of several modes of decay.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04410 goldbook:P04855)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04410 goldbook:R05116)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04410 doi:10.1351/pac198254081533)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04410 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04411))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04411 "partial digestion")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04411 "In partial digestion and/or selective digestion procedures only part or some of the analytes present are brought into solution. This may be preferred to total decomposition if relative concentrations of the analyte in the test samples provide sufficient information (e.g. materials for geochemical exploration).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04411 goldbook:D01547)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04411 doi:10.1351/pac198860091461)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04411 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04412))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04412 "partial isotherm")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04412 "The function relating, at constant temperature and pressure, the amount of a particular component in the interfacial layer per unit area (or per unit mass of adsorbent) with its mole fraction (or concentration) in the liquid phase. This function can be evaluated only when the location and the thickness of the interfacial layer have been defined.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:P04412 "individual isotherm")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04412 goldbook:A00153)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04412 goldbook:I03085)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04412 goldbook:A00296)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04412 doi:10.1351/pac197231040577)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04412 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04413))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04413 "partial kinetic current")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04413 "The current which would flow if mass transport were infinitely fast.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04413 doi:10.1351/pac197437040499)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04413 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04415))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04415 "partial mass density")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04415 "Change in mass due to addition of a small amount of component to a system divided by the change in volume of the system. The systematic name is partial volumic mass.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04415 goldbook:S06236)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04415 goldbook:V06651)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04415 doi:10.1351/pac199668040957)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04415 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04421))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04421 "partial rate factor")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04421 "The rate of substitution at one specific site in an aromatic compound relative to the rate of substitution at one position in benzene. For example, the partial rate factor \\(f_{p}^{\\rm{Z}}\\) for para-substitution in a monosubstituted benzene $\\ce{C6H5Z}$ is related to the rate constants \\(k\\left(\\rm{C}_{6}\\rm{H}_{5}\\rm{Z}\\right)\\) and \\(k\\left(\\rm{C}_{6}\\rm{H}_{6}\\right)\\) for the total reaction (i.e. at all positions) of $\\ce{C6H5Z}$ and benzene, respectively, and % para (the percentage para-substitution in the total product formed from $\\ce{C6H5Z}$) by the relation: \\[f_{p}^{\\rm{Z}} = \\frac{6\\ k\\left(\\rm{C}_{6}\\rm{H}_{5}\\rm{Z}\\right)}{k\\left(\\rm{C}_{6}\\rm{H}_{6}\\right)}\\ \\frac{\\%\\ \\rm{para}}{100}\\] Similarly for meta-substitution: \\[f_{m}^{\\rm{Z}} = \\frac{6\\ k\\left(\\rm{C}_{6}\\rm{H}_{5}\\rm{Z}\\right)}{2\\ k\\left(\\rm{C}_{6}\\rm{H}_{6}\\right)}\\ \\frac{\\%\\ \\rm{meta}}{100}\\] (The symbols \\(p_{f}^{\\rm{Z}}\\), \\(m_{f}^{\\rm{Z}}\\), \\(o_{f}^{\\rm{Z}}\\) are also in use.) The term applies equally to the ipso position, and it can be extended to other substituted substrates undergoing parallel reactions at different sites with the same reagent according to the same rate law.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04421 goldbook:A00441)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04421 goldbook:P04403)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04421 goldbook:R05141)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04421 goldbook:R05190)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04421 goldbook:S05565)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04421 doi:10.1351/pac199466051077)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04421 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04422))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04422 "partial specific volume")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04422 "Change in volume of a system when a small amount of component is added divided by the mass of the added component. The systematic name is partial massic volume.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04422 goldbook:M03723)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04422 goldbook:S06236)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04422 doi:10.1351/pac199668040957)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04422 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04423))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04423 "particle concentration")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04423 "Commonly expressed in several ways: mass concentration (usually as \\(\\unicode[times]{x3BC}\\rm{g}\\ \\rm{m}^{-3}\\)) or number concentration (number of particles \\(\\pu{cm-3}\\)); modern instrumentation allows measurement of the number of particles as a function of size as well as the total number present in a given air volume. For atmospheric aerosols, this is a complex distribution for which diameters range from below \\(0.01\\) to above \\(100\\ \\unicode[Times]{x3BC}\\rm{m}\\); the particles making the highest contribution to the total number density are in the size range below \\(0.1\\ \\unicode[times]{x3BC}\\rm{m}\\), those contributing most to the total surface area are in the \\(0.1\\) to \\(1.0\\ \\unicode[times]{x3BC}\\rm{m}\\) range, while those with the highest contribution to the volume or mass of the aerosol come from both the \\(0.1\\) to \\(1.0\\ \\unicode[times]{x3BC}\\rm{m}\\) and \\(1.0\\) to \\(100\\ \\unicode[Times]{x3BC}\\rm{m}\\) ranges.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04423 goldbook:A00176)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04423 goldbook:N04262)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04423 doi:10.1351/pac199062112167)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04423 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04424))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04424 "particle density")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04424 "The number of particles (nuclear or elementary) divided by the containing volume.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04424 goldbook:E02034)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04424 goldbook:N04237)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04424 doi:10.1351/pac198254081533)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04424 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04426))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04426 "particle induced X-ray emission analysis")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04426 "A kind of analysis based on the measurement of the energies and intensities of characteristic X-radiation emitted by a test portion during irradiation with charged particles other than electrons.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04426 goldbook:C00985)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04426 goldbook:I03255)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04426 goldbook:T06284)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04426 doi:10.1351/pac199466122513)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04426 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04430))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04430 "particle size")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04430 "To describe the size of liquid or solid particles (aerosol) the average or equivalent diameter is used. For non-spherical particles collected in an impactor, for example, the aerodynamic diameter of a particle of arbitrary shape and density refers to the size of a spherical particle of unit density that would deposit on a given impactor surface.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04430 goldbook:A00176)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04430 goldbook:E02191)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04430 doi:10.1351/pac199062112167)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04430 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04431))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04431 "particle size distribution")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04431 "The size of the liquid or solid particles in the atmosphere usually extends from \\(>0.01\\) to \\(< 100\\ \\unicode[Times]{x3BC}\\rm{m}\\) in diameter. In the earth's atmosphere the distribution function which describes the number of particles as a function of diameter, mass or surface area of the aerosol can be determined reasonably well with modern instrumentation.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04431 goldbook:A00176)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04431 doi:10.1351/pac199062112167)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04431 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04432))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04432 "particular property")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04432 "A property of a given object (phenomenon, body or substance). 'Particular property' includes the concept of particular quantity. The adjective 'particular' may be omitted, if no ambiguity is caused.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04432 goldbook:P04883)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04432 doi:10.1351/pac199567081563)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04432 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04433))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04433 "particulate carbon")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04433 "A carbon material consisting of separated monolithic particles.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:P04433 "Distinctions should be made between coarse particulate carbon or granular carbon (larger than about \\(100\\ \\unicode[Times]{x3BC}\\rm{m}\\), but smaller than about \\(1\\ \\rm{cm}\\) in average size), fine particulate carbon or powder or flour (between \\(1\\) and \\(100\\ \\unicode[Times]{x3BC}\\rm{m}\\) in average size) and colloidal carbon (below approximately \\(1\\ \\unicode[Times]{x3BC}\\rm{m}\\) in size in at least one direction), e.g. carbon blacks and colloidal carbon."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04433 goldbook:C00824)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04433 goldbook:C00841)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04433 goldbook:C01173)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04433 goldbook:G02682)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04433 doi:10.1351/pac199567030473)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04433 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04434))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04434 "particulate matter")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04434 "A general term used to describe airborne solid or liquid particles of all sizes. The term aerosol is recommended for general use in describing airborne particulate matter.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04434 goldbook:A00176)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04434 doi:10.1351/pac199062112167)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04434 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04435))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04435 "partition")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04435 "This term is often used as a synonym for distribution and extraction. However, an essential difference exists by definition between distribution constant or partition ratio and partition constant. The term partition should be, but is not invariably, applied to the distribution of a single definite chemical species between the two phases.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04435 goldbook:D01813)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04435 goldbook:E02301)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04435 goldbook:P04438)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04435 goldbook:P04440)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04435 doi:10.1351/pac199365112373)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04435 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04436))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04436 "partition chromatography")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04436 "Chromatography in which separation is based mainly on differences between the solubility of the sample components in the stationary phase ( gas chromatography), or on differences between the solubilities of the components in the mobile and stationary phases (liquid chromatography).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04436 goldbook:C01075)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04436 goldbook:G02578)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04436 goldbook:L03578)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04436 goldbook:S05740)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04436 doi:10.1351/pac199365040819)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04436 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04437))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04437 "partition coefficient")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04437 "This term is not recommended and should not be used as a synonym for partition constant, partition ratio or distribution ratio.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04437 goldbook:D01813)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04437 goldbook:D01817)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04437 goldbook:P04438)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04437 goldbook:P04440)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04437 doi:10.1351/pac199365112373)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04437 doi:10.1351/pac199668040957)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04437 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04438))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04438 "partition constant")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04438 "The ratio of activity of a given species A in the extract to its activity in the other phase with which it is in equilibrium, thus: \\[\\left(K_{\\rm{D}}^{\\rm{o}}\\right)_{\\rm{A}} = \\frac{a_{\\rm{A,org}}}{a_{\\rm{A,aq}}}\\] Its value should not vary with composition but depends on the choice of standard states and on the temperature (and eventually the pressure).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04438 goldbook:D01813)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04438 goldbook:T06442)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04438 doi:10.1351/pac199365112373)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04438 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04440))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04440 "partition ratio")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04440 "The ratio of the concentration of a substance in a single definite form, A, in the extract to its concentration in the same form in the other phase at equilibrium, e.g. for an aqueous/organic system: \\[\\left (K_{\\rm{D}} \\right )_{A} = \\frac{\\left [ A \\right ]_{\\rm{org}}}{\\left [ A \\right ]_{\\rm{aq}}}\\]")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:P04440 "distribution constant")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:P04440 "\\(K_{\\rm{D}}\\) is sometimes called the 'distribution constant'; this is a good synonym. The terms distribution coefficient, distribution ratio, partition constant and extraction constant should not be used as synonyms for partition ratio."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:P04440 "The use of the inverse ratio (aqueous/organic) may be appropriate in certain cases, e.g. where the organic phase forms the feed but its use in such cases should be clearly specified. The ratio of the concentration in the denser phase to the less dense phase is not recommended as it can be ambiguous."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:P04440 "If the pure solvent and infinitely dilute feed are taken as the standard states, \\(K_{\\rm{D}} \\rightarrow K_{\\rm{D}}^{\\,\\unicode{x26ac}}\\) as the total concentration of dissolved materials decreases."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04440 goldbook:D01817)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04440 goldbook:E02301)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04440 goldbook:P04435)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04440 goldbook:P04438)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04440 doi:10.1351/pac199365112373)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04440 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04442))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04442 "pascal")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04442 "SI derived unit of pressure, \\(\\pu{Pa} = \\pu{N m-2} = \\pu{kg m-1 s-2}\\).")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04442 doi:10.1351/pac199668040957)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04442 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04443))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04443 "passivation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04443 "The process of transition from the active to the passive state by formation of the passivating film. Passivation is achieved by an anodic current which at the respective electrode potential must be larger than the maximum current, or by the presence of an oxidized substance in the neighbouring solution which passivates by being reduced (passivator).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04443 goldbook:A00111)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04443 goldbook:E01956)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04443 goldbook:F02366)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04443 goldbook:P04447)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04443 doi:10.1351/pac198961010019)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04443 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04444))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04444 "passivation potential")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04444 "The most negative electrode potential at which the passivating film is formed. The passivation potential is equal to or more positive than the equilibrium potential of formation of the phase constituting the film. Usually, the corrosion current goes through a maximum at the passivation potential.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04444 goldbook:C01351)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04444 goldbook:C01358)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04444 goldbook:E01956)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04444 goldbook:F02366)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04444 goldbook:P04447)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04444 doi:10.1351/pac198961010019)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04444 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04445))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04445 "passive metal")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04445 "A metal corroding in the passive state.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04445 goldbook:P04447)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04445 doi:10.1351/pac198961010019)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04445 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04446))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04446 "passive sampler")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04446 "A device for preconcentration of trace substances from gaseous media based on molecular diffusion without controlled conveyance of the gas to be investigated (e.g. work place air).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04446 goldbook:D01716)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04446 doi:10.1351/pac199062112167)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04446 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04447))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04447 "passive state")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04447 "The passive state is characterized by a contiguous 'passivating film' of solid corrosion products separating the metallic phase from the adjacent electrolyte. Corrosion in the passive state involves growth of the passivating film and/or transfer of metal ions through the film into the electrolyte.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04447 goldbook:C01351)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04447 goldbook:F02366)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04447 doi:10.1351/pac198961010019)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04447 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04448))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04448 "Paterno–Büchi reaction")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04448 "The photocycloaddition of an electronically excited carbonyl group to a ground state olefin yielding an oxetane.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04448 goldbook:G02704)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04448 goldbook:PT07451)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04448 doi:10.1351/pac199668122223)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04448 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04449))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04449 "paucidisperse system")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04449 "A colloidal system in which only a few particle-sizes occur.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04449 goldbook:C01172)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04449 doi:10.1351/pac197231040577)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04449 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04451))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04451 "peak")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04451 "The portion of a differential chromatogram recording the detector response when a single component is eluted from the column. If separation is incomplete, two or more components may be eluted as one 'unresolved peak'.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04451 goldbook:C01071)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04451 doi:10.1351/pac199365040819)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04451 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04452))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04452 "peak analysis")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04452 "The extraction of relevant peak parameters (i.e. position, area) from a measured spectrum.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04452 goldbook:E02301)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04452 goldbook:M03792)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04452 doi:10.1351/pac198254020533)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04452 doi:10.1351/pac199466122513)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04452 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04454))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04454 "peak area method")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04454 "A kind of peak analysis in which a peak area is calculated by subtracting an estimate of the underlying continuum in a relevant part of a measured spectrum.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04454 goldbook:M03792)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04454 goldbook:P04452)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04454 doi:10.1351/pac199466122513)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04454 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04456))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04456 "peak concentration")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04456 "The highest concentration of a given trace component which was measured with a continuous analyser during a specified sampling period.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04456 goldbook:C01298)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04456 doi:10.1351/pac199062112167)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04456 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04457))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04457 "peak current")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04457 "In linear-sweep voltammetry, triangular-wave voltammetry, cyclic triangular-wave voltammetry, and similar techniques, the maximum value of the faradaic current due to the reduction or oxidation of a substance B during a single sweep. This maximum value is attained after an interval during which the concentration of B at the electrode-solution interface decreases monotonically, while the faradaic current due to the reduction or oxidation of B increases monotonically, with time. It is attained before an interval during which this current decreases monotonically with time because the rate of transport of B toward the electrode-solution interface is smaller than the rate at which it is removed from the interface by electrolysis. The term has also been used to denote the maximum value of the faradaic current attributable to the reduction or oxidation of an electroactive substance in techniques such as ac polarography, differential pulse polarography, and derivative polarography. However, these techniques give curves that arise in ways different from that cited above, and the terms summit, summit current, and summit potential are therefore recommended for use in connection with such techniques.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04457 goldbook:A00412)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04457 goldbook:E01940)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04457 goldbook:F02321)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04457 goldbook:I03082)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04457 goldbook:O04362)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04457 goldbook:P04716)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04457 goldbook:S06132)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04457 goldbook:S06133)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04457 doi:10.1351/pac198557101491)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04457 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04458))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04458 "peak elution volume")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04458 "The volume of mobile phase entering the column between the start of the elution and the emergence of the peak maximum, or the corresponding time. In most of the cases, this is equal to the total retention volume (time). There are, however, cases when the elution process does not start immediately at sample introduction. For example, in liquid chromatography, sometimes the column is washed with a liquid after the application of the sample to displace certain components which are of no interest and during this treatment the sample does not move along the column. In gas chromatography, there are also cases when a liquid sample is applied to the top of the column but its elution starts only after a given period. This term is useful in such cases.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04458 goldbook:C01075)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04458 goldbook:E02042)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04458 doi:10.1351/pac199365040819)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04458 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04460))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04460 "peak fitting")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04460 "A kind of peak analysis in which a relevant part of a spectrum is fitted with a theoretical response function.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04460 goldbook:P04452)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04460 doi:10.1351/pac199466122513)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04460 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04464))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04464 "peak potential")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04464 "In linear-sweep voltammetry, triangular-wave voltammetry, cyclic triangular-wave voltammetry, and similar techniques, the potential of the indicator electrode at which the peak current is attained.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04464 goldbook:I03006)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04464 goldbook:P04457)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04464 doi:10.1351/pac198557101491)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04464 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04465))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04465 "peak resolution")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04465 "The separation of two peaks in terms of their average peak width at base (\\(t_{\\rm{R2}}>t_{\\rm{R1}}\\)): \\[R_{\\rm{s}}=\\frac{t_{\\rm{R2}}\\,-\\,t_{\\rm{R1}}}{\\frac{w_{\\rm{b1}}\\,+\\,w_{\\rm{b2}}}{2}}=\\frac{2\\ (t_{\\rm{R2}}- t_{\\rm{R1}})}{w_{\\rm{b1}}\\,+\\,w_{\\rm{b2}}}\\] In the case of two adjacent peaks it may be assumed that \\(w_{\\rm{b1}}\\approx w_{\\rm{b2}}\\), and thus, the width of the second peak may be substituted for the average value: \\[R_{\\rm{s}}\\approx \\frac{t_{\\rm{R2}}\\,-\\,t_{\\rm{R1}}}{w_{\\rm{b2}}}\\]")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04465 doi:10.1351/pac199365040819)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04465 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04466))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04466 "peak widths")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04466 "Peak widths represent retention dimensions (time or volume) parallel to the baseline. If the baseline is not parallel to the axis representing time or volume, then the peak widths are to be drawn parallel to this axis. Three peak-width values are commonly used in chromatography. Peak width at base (\\(w_{\\rm{b}}\\)) is the segment of the peak base intercepted by the tangents drawn to the inflection points on either side of the peak. Peak width at half height (\\(w_{\\rm{h}}\\)) is the length of the line parallel to the peak base at 50% of the peak height that terminates at the intersection with the two limbs of the peak. Peak width at inflection points (\\(w_{\\rm{i}}\\)) is the length of the line drawn between the inflection points parallel to the peak base. The peak width at base may be called the 'base width'. However, the peak width at half height must never be called the 'half width' because that has a completely different meaning. Also, the symbol \\(w_{1/2}\\) should never be used instead of \\(w_{\\rm{h}}\\).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04466 goldbook:C01075)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04466 doi:10.1351/pac199365040819)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04466 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04467))
