AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04479 goldbook:P04898)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04479 goldbook:R05370)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04479 doi:10.1351/pac199567081307)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04479 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04480))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04480 "peptidoglycan")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04480 "A glycosaminoglycan formed by alternating residues of ᴅ-glucosamine and either muramic acid {2-amino-3-O-[(S)-1-carboxyethyl]-2-deoxy-ᴅ-glucose} or ʟ-talosaminuronic acid (2-amino-2-deoxy-ʟ-taluronic acid), which are usually N-acetylated or N-glycoloylated. The carboxyl group of the muramic acid is commonly substituted by a peptide containing residues of both ʟ- and ᴅ-amino acids, whereas that of ʟ-talosaminuronic acid is substituted by a peptide consisting of ʟ-amino acids only.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04480 goldbook:G02659)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04480 doi:10.1351/pac198860091389)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04480 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04485))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04485 "percentage exposed")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04485 "The accessibility of the atoms of metal in metallic catalysts, supported or unsupported, depends upon the percentage of the total atoms of metal which are surface atoms. It is recommended that the term percentage exposed be employed for this quantity rather than the term dispersion which has been frequently employed.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04485 doi:10.1351/pac197646010071)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04485 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04486))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04486 "percentage relative error")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04486 "The relative error expressed in percent. It can be calculated from the relative error by multiplying by 100. Comment: The term 'percentage relative error' should always be quoted in full, rather than 'error' or 'percentage error' to avoid confusion.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:P04486 "percentage error")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04486 goldbook:P04483)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04486 goldbook:R05266)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04486 doi:10.1351/pac199466030595)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04486 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04487))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04487 "percentage standard deviation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04487 "The value of the relative standard deviation, expressed in percent. It can be calculated from the relative standard deviation by multiplying by 100. Comment: It is recommended that the 'relative standard deviation' be reported, rather than the 'percentage standard deviation', in order to avoid confusion where results themselves are expressed as percentages. The term 'coefficient of variation' in place of 'relative standard deviation' is not recommended.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04487 goldbook:C01124)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04487 goldbook:P04483)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04487 goldbook:R05280)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04487 goldbook:S05911)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04487 doi:10.1351/pac199466030595)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04487 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04490))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04490 "perfectly polarized interphase")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04490 "Differences from the behaviour of interphases containing only neutral species arise when the interphase may be described as perfectly polarized. This term is used when no charged component is common to both phases adjoining the interphase. This may arise as a result of the equilibrium conditions or from the kinetics of charge transfer and leads to an interphase impermeable to electric charge.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04490 goldbook:E01923)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04490 goldbook:I03118)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04490 doi:10.1351/pac198355081251)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04490 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04491))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04491 "pericyclic reaction")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04491 "A chemical reaction in which concerted reorganization of bonding takes place throughout a cyclic array of continuously bonded atoms. It may be viewed as a reaction proceeding through a fully conjugated cyclic transition state. The number of atoms in the cyclic array is usually six, but other numbers are also possible. The term embraces a variety of processes, including cycloadditions, cheletropic reactions, electrocyclic reactions, sigmatropic rearrangements, etc. (provided they are concerted).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04491 goldbook:C01014)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04491 goldbook:C01033)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04491 goldbook:C01234)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04491 goldbook:C01267)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04491 goldbook:C01496)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04491 goldbook:E01948)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04491 goldbook:M04043)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04491 goldbook:S05660)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04491 goldbook:T06468)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04491 doi:10.1351/pac199466051077)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04491 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04492))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04492 "perikinetic aggregation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04492 "The rate of aggregation is in general determined by the frequency of collisions and the probability of cohesion during collision. If the collisions are caused by Brownian motion, the process is called perikinetic aggregation.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04492 goldbook:B00748)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04492 goldbook:P04855)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04492 doi:10.1351/pac197231040577)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04492 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04493))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04493 "period")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04493 "Time for one cycle of a periodic phenomenon.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04493 doi:10.1351/pac199668040957)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04493 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04494))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04494 "periodic copolymer")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04494 "A copolymer consisting of macromolecules comprising more than two species of monomeric units in regular sequence.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04494 goldbook:C01335)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04494 goldbook:M03667)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04494 goldbook:M04018)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04494 goldbook:ST06775)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04494 doi:10.1351/pac199668122287)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04494 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04495))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04495 "periodic copolymerization")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04495 "A copolymerization in which a periodic copolymer is formed.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04495 goldbook:C01336)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04495 goldbook:P04494)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04495 doi:10.1351/pac199668122287)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04495 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04496))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04496 "periodic voltage")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04496 "This general term is applicable to square, triangular, and other wave forms.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04496 doi:10.1351/pac198557101491)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04496 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04497))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04497 "peripheral atom")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04497 "A secondary reference (non-core) atom which at some point in the mechanistic sequence is situated in the molecule containing the core atom(s).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04497 goldbook:C01341)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04497 goldbook:R05227)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04497 goldbook:ST06775)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04497 doi:10.1351/pac198961010023)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04497 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04499))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04499 "periselectivity")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04499 "The differentiation between two symmetry-allowed processes, for example the [2+4] vs. [4+6] cycloaddition of cyclopentadiene to tropone.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04499 goldbook:C01496)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04499 doi:10.1351/pac199466051077)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04499 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04500))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04500 "peritectic reaction")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04500 "An isothermal, reversible reaction between two phases, a liquid and a solid, that results, on cooling of a binary, ternary, ... , \\(n\\) system in one, two, ... (\\(n- 1\\)) new solid phases. Synonymous with incongruent reaction.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:P04500 "incongruent reaction")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04500 doi:10.1351/pac199466030577)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04500 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04501))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04501 "peritectoid reaction")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04501 "An isothermal, reversible reaction in the solid state, that, on cooling of a binary, ternary, ... , \\(n\\) system, results in one, two, ... (\\(n-1\\)) new solid phases. For example, in a binary system containing two solids \\(\\alpha'\\) and \\(\\alpha''\\) \\[\\alpha' + \\alpha'' \\rightarrow \\beta\\] Synonymous with metatectoid reaction.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:P04501 "metatectoid reaction")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04501 doi:10.1351/pac199466030577)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04501 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04502))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04502 "peritectoid temperature")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04502 "The maximum temperature at which a peritectoid reaction can occur.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04502 goldbook:P04501)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04502 doi:10.1351/pac199466030577)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04502 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04506))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04506 "permeation tube")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04506 "A device used for dynamic preparation of test gas mixtures by means of controlled permeation of a gaseous analyte out of a container through polymer material into a carrier gas stream. These devices containing certain condensable gases (e.g. $\\ce{NO2}$, $\\ce{SO2}$, etc.) when operated at closely controlled temperatures can be used as primary standards calibrated in terms of the weight loss per unit time.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04506 goldbook:C00863)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04506 goldbook:W06668)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04506 doi:10.1351/pac199062112167)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04506 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04508))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04508 "permittivity of vacuum")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04508 "Fundamental physical constant \\(\\varepsilon_{0}=\\frac{1}{\\mu _{0}\\ c_{0}^{2}}\\) exactly, where \\(\\mu_{0}\\) is the permeability of vacuum and \\(c_{0}\\) the speed of light in vacuum. It is equal to \\(8.854\\ 187\\ 817\\,...\\times\\ 10^{-12}\\ \\rm{F m}^{-1}\\).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04508 goldbook:P04504)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04508 doi:10.1103/RevModPhys.80.633)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04508 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04509))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04509 "permselectivity")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04509 "A term used to define the preferential permeation of certain ionic species through ion-exchange membranes.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04509 goldbook:IT07155)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04509 doi:10.1351/pac199365040819)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04509 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04510))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04510 "peroxides")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04510 "Compounds of structure $\\ce{ROOR}$ in which $\\ce{R}$ may be any organyl group (The term is also used in an inorganic sense to denote salts of the anion $\\ce{O2^{2−}}$).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04510 goldbook:A00358)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04510 goldbook:H02905)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04510 goldbook:O04329)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04510 doi:10.1351/pac199567081307)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04510 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04511))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04511 "peroxisome")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04511 "Organelle, similar to a lysosome, characterized by its content of catalase (EC 1.11.1.6), peroxidase (EC 1.11.1.7) and other oxidative enzymes.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04511 goldbook:CT06762)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04511 goldbook:E02159)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04511 doi:10.1351/pac199365092003)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04511 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04513))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04513 "peroxy acids")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04513 "Acids in which an acidic $\\ce{–OH}$ group has been replaced by an $\\ce{–OOH}$ group, e.g. $\\ce{CH3C(=O)OOH}$ peroxyacetic acid, $\\ce{PhS(=O)2OOH}$ benzeneperoxysulfonic acid.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:P04513 "per acids")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:P04513 "peracids")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04513 doi:10.1351/pac199567081307)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04513 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04516))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04516 "persistent")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04516 "A term used to characterize radicals which have lifetimes of several minutes or greater in dilute solution in inert solvents. Persistence is a kinetic or reactivity property. In contrast, radical stability, which is a thermodynamic property, is expressed in terms of the $\\ce{C–H}$ bond strength of the appropriate hydrocarbon. The lifetime of a radical is profoundly influenced by steric shielding of the radical centre by bulky substituents.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04516 goldbook:D01739)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04516 goldbook:I03026)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04516 goldbook:L03515)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04516 goldbook:R05066)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04516 goldbook:S05644)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04516 goldbook:S05900)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04516 goldbook:T06451)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04516 doi:10.1351/pac199466051077)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04516 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04517))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04517 "perspective formula")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04517 "A geometric representation of stereochemical features of a molecule or model which appears as a view from an appropriate direction.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04517 goldbook:F02391)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04517 goldbook:N04134)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04517 goldbook:P04873)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04517 goldbook:S05480)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04517 goldbook:S05974)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04517 goldbook:W06667)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04517 goldbook:Z06747)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04517 doi:10.1351/pac199668122193)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04517 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04519))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04519 "pesticide")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04519 "Strictly, a substance intended to kill pests: in common usage, any substance used for controlling, preventing, or destroying animal, microbiological or plant pests.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04519 doi:10.1351/pac199365092003)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04519 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04520))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04520 "pesticide residue")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04520 "Any substance or mixture of substances in food for man or animals resulting from the use of a pesticide including any specified derivatives, such as degradation and conversion products, metabolites, reaction products and impurities considered to be of toxicological significance.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04520 goldbook:P04519)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04520 doi:10.1351/pac199365092003)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04520 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04522))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04522 "petroleum coke")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04522 "A carbonization product of high-boiling hydrocarbon fractions obtained in petroleum processing (heavy residues). It is the general term for all special petroleum coke products such as green, calcined and needle petroleum coke.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:P04522 "High-boiling hydrocarbon fractions (heavy residues) used as feedstock for petroleum coke are residues from distillation (atmospheric pressure, vacuum) or cracking (e.g. thermal, catalytic, steam-based) processes. The nature of feedstock has a decisive influence on the graphitizability of the calcined coke."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04522 goldbook:C00774)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04522 goldbook:C00840)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04522 goldbook:C01142)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04522 goldbook:C01387)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04522 goldbook:G02697)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04522 goldbook:N04095)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04522 doi:10.1351/pac199567030473)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04522 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04523))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04523 "petroleum pitch")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04523 "A residue from heat treatment and distillation of petroleum fractions. It is solid at room temperature, consists of a complex mixture of numerous predominantly aromatic and alkyl-substituted aromatic hydrocarbons, and exhibits a broad softening range instead of a defined melting temperature.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:P04523 "The hydrogen aromaticity (ratio of aromatic to total hydrogen atoms) varies between 0.3 and 0.6. The aliphatic hydrogen atoms are typically present in alkyl groups substituted on aromatic rings or as naphthenic hydrogen."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04523 goldbook:A00228)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04523 goldbook:A00442)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04523 goldbook:H02889)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04523 goldbook:M03821)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04523 doi:10.1351/pac199567030473)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04523 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04524))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04524 "pH")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04524 "The quantity pH is defined in terms of the activity of hydrogen(1+) ions (hydrogen ions) in solution: \\[\\rm{pH} = -\\rm{lg}[a(\\rm{H}^{+})] = -\\rm{lg}[\\rm{m}(\\rm{H}^{+})\\gamma_{\\rm{m}}(\\rm{H}^{+})/m^{\\unicode{x29B5} }]\\] where \\(a(\\rm{H}^{+})\\) is the activity of hydrogen ion (hydrogen 1+) in aqueous solution, \\(\\rm{H}^{+}\\rm{(aq)}\\), \\(\\gamma_{\\rm{m}}(\\rm{H}^{+})\\) is the activity coefficient of \\(\\rm{H}^{+}\\rm{(aq)}\\) (molality basis) at molality \\(m(\\rm{H}^{+})\\), and \\(m^{⦵} = \\pu{1 mol kg-1}\\) is the standard molality.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:P04524 "pH cannot be measured independently because calculation of the activity involves the activity coefficient of a single ion. Thus it can be regarded only as a notional definition."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:P04524 "The establishment of primary pH standards requires the application of the concept of 'primary method of measurement', assuring full traceability of the results of all measurements and their uncertainties. Any limitation in the theory of determination of experimental variables must be included in the estimated uncertainty of the method."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:P04524 "The primary method for measurement of pH involves the use of a cell without transference, known as the Harned cell: $\\ce{Pt(s)}$|$\\ce{H2(g)}$|Buffer S, $\\ce{Cl^{-}(aq)}$|$\\ce{AgCl(s)}$|$\\ce{Ag(s)}$ The equation for this cell can be rearranged to give: \\[-\\rm{lg}[a(\\rm{H}^{+})\\gamma(\\rm{Cl}^{-})] = \\frac{E - E^{\\unicode{x29B5} }}{(R\\:T\\:\\rm{ln}10)/F}+ \\rm{lg}[m(\\rm{Cl}^{-})/m^{\\unicode{x29B5}}]\\] where \\(E\\) is the potential difference of the cell and \\(E^{\\unicode{x29B5}}\\) is the known standard potential of the $\\ce{AgCl(s)}$|$\\ce{Ag(s)}$ electrode. Measurements of \\(E^{\\unicode{x29B5}}\\) as a function of \\(m(\\rm{Cl}^{-})\\) are made and the quantity \\(a(\\rm{H}^{+})\\gamma(\\rm{Cl}^{-})\\) (called the acidity function) is found by extrapolation to \\(m(\\rm{Cl}^{-})/m^{\\unicode{x29B5}} = 0\\). The value of \\(\\gamma(\\rm{Cl}^{-})\\) is calculated using the Bates–Guggenheim convention based on Debye–Hückel theory. Then \\(\\rm{lg}[a(\\rm{H}^{+})]\\) is calculated and identified as \\(\\rm{pH(PS)}\\), where \\(\\rm{PS}\\) signifies primary standard. The uncertainties in the two estimates are typically \\(0.001\\) in \\(\\rm{lg}[a(\\rm{H}^{+})\\gamma(\\rm{Cl}^{-})]\\) and \\(0.003\\) in pH. Materials for primary standard buffers must also meet the appropriate requirements for reference materials, including chemical purity and stability, and applicability of the Bates–Guggenheim convention for the estimation of \\(-\\rm{lg}[\\gamma(\\rm{Cl}^{-})]\\). This convention requires that the ionic strength be \\(\\pu{\\leq 0.1 mol kg-1}\\). Primary standard buffers should also lead to small liquid junction potentials when used in cells with liquid junctions. Secondary standards, \\(\\rm{pH(SS)}\\), are also available, but carry a greater uncertainty in measured values."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:P04524 "Practical pH measurements generally use cells with liquid junctions in which, consequently, liquid junction potentials, \\(E_{\\rm{j}}\\), are present. Measurements of pH are not normally performed using the $\\ce{Pt}$|$\\ce{H2}$ electrode, but rather the glass (or other $\\ce{H^{+}}$- selective) electrode, whose response factor (\\(\\rm{d}E/\\rm{dpH}\\)) usually deviates from the Nernst slope. The associated uncertainties are significantly larger than those associated with fundamental measurements using the Harned cell. Nonetheless, incorporation of the uncertainties for the primary method, and for all subsequent measurements, permits the uncertainties for all procedures to be linked to the primary standards by an unbroken chain of comparisons."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:P04524 "Reference values for standards in $\\ce{D2O}$ and aqueous-organic solvent mixtures exist."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04524 goldbook:B00617)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04524 goldbook:D01533)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04524 goldbook:A00081)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04524 goldbook:A00116)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04524 goldbook:C01124)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04524 goldbook:I03180)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04524 goldbook:L03584)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04524 goldbook:P04837)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04524 goldbook:S05924)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04524 goldbook:T06420)
