AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04539 "phenols")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04539 "Compounds having one or more hydroxy groups attached to a benzene or other arene ring, e.g. 2-naphthol:")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04539 doi:10.1351/pac199567081307)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04539 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04540))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04540 "phenomenological equation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04540 "In the following only media which are isotropic with respect to mass transport (i.e. the transport coefficients are independent of direction) are being considered. In the linear range (not too far from equilibrium), for uniform temperature and neglecting external fields such as the earth's gravitational field, the flux density of species B is related to the gradients of the electrochemical potentials of all species by the phenomenological equation: \\[N_{\\rm{B}}- c_{\\rm{B}}\\ v_{\\rm{A}}=- \\sum _{\\begin{array}{c} i\\\\ i eq A \\end{array}}L_{\\rm{B}i}^{\\rm{A}}\\  abla \\mu _{i}\\] with \\[i=\\rm{B},\\rm{C},...\\] where \\( abla \\mu _{i}\\) is the gradient of the electrochemical potential of species i. The proportionality factors \\(L_{\\rm{B}i}^{\\rm{A}}\\) are called phenomenological coefficients. Their values depend on the frame of reference. The latter is taken here to move with the velocity \\(v_{\\rm{A}}\\) of species A, and hence: \\[L_{\\rm{A}i}^{\\rm{A}}=0\\]")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04540 goldbook:E01945)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04540 goldbook:G02669)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04540 goldbook:I03353)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04540 goldbook:L03558)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04540 doi:10.1351/pac198153101827)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04540 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04541))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04541 "phenonium ions")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04541 "The traditional generic name for those cyclohexadienyl cations that are spiro-annulated with a cyclopropane unit. Phenonium ions constitute a subclass of arenium ions.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04541 goldbook:A00436)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04541 goldbook:B00737)
