AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04546 "pH gradient")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04546 "The differential change of pH with distance (\\(\\frac{\\rm{dpH}}{\\rm{d}I}\\)).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04546 goldbook:P04524)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04546 doi:10.1351/pac199466040891)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04546 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04547))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04547 "phonon")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04547 "Elementary excitation in the quantum mechanical treatment of vibrations in a crystal lattice. An energy bundle that behaves as a particle of energy \\(h\\  u \\), with \\( u \\) the vibration frequency and \\(h\\) the Planck constant.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:P04547 "A phonon can be considered as an acoustic mode of thermal vibration of a crystal lattice (or liquid helium II)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:P04547 "Every harmonic vibration can be decomposed in phonons, which are the elementary vibrations. The total number of phonons in a system that has internal vibrations (e.g., a crystal) is related to the temperature of the system."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:P04547 "The concept of phonons provides a simplification in the theories of thermal and electrical conduction in solids."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:P04547 "For example, interactions between phonons and electrons are thought to be responsible for such phenomena as 'superconductivity'."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04547 goldbook:P04685)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04547 goldbook:M03958)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04547 doi:10.1351/pac200779030293)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04547 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04548))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04548 "phosphanes")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04548 "The saturated hydrides of tervalent phosphorus having the general formula $\\ce{P_{n}H_{n+2}}$. Individual members having an unbranched phosphorus chain are named phosphane, diphosphane, triphosphane, etc. The name of a saturated hydride of phosphorus wherein one or more phosphorus atoms have a bonding number of 5 is formed by prefixing locants and \\(\\lambda ^{5}\\) symbols to the name of the corresponding phosphane. Hydrocarbyl derivatives of $\\ce{PH3}$ belong to the class phosphines.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04548 goldbook:B00703)
