Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04753))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04753 "polysulfanes")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04753 "Compounds having an unbranched chain of sulfur atoms ($\\ce{s2}$ or higher) terminating in H: $\\ce{HS_{n}H}$. Some chemists exclude disulfane, $\\ce{HS2H}$, from the class polysulfanes.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04753 doi:10.1351/pac199567081307)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04753 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04754))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04754 "polysulfides")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04754 "Compounds $\\ce{R–[S]_{n}–R}$, with a chain of sulfur atoms (\\(n\\geq 2\\)) and $\\ce{R}  eq \\ce{H}$. Some chemists exclude disulfides, $\\ce{RS2R}$, from the class polysulfides.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04754 doi:10.1351/pac199567081307)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04754 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04755))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04755 "polytopal rearrangement")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04755 "Stereoisomerization interconverting different or equivalent spatial arrangements of ligands about a central atom or of a cage of atoms, where the ligand or cage defines the vertices of a polyhedron. For example pyramidal inversion of amines, Berry pseudorotation of $\\ce{PF5}$, rearrangements of polyhedral boranes.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04755 goldbook:P04934)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04755 goldbook:A00274)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04755 goldbook:B00709)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04755 goldbook:C00769)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04755 goldbook:C00930)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04755 goldbook:L03518)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04755 goldbook:P04956)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04755 doi:10.1351/pac199668122193)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04755 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04756))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04756 "polytypic transition")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04756 "A transition of a crystalline structure into one or more forms which differ in the way identical layers of atoms are stacked. Example: $\\ce{ZnS}$ consists of two identical close packings, one of $\\ce{Zn}$ atoms, the other $\\ce{S}$ atoms, with the one displaced to the other along the c-axis through one-quarter of the layer spacing. In sphalerite-type $\\ce{ZnS}$ the layers have the face-centred-cubic (ABC ABC) sequence, in wurtzite-type $\\ce{ZnS}$ they have the hexagonal-close-packed (AB AB) sequence. The transition of sphalerite-type $\\ce{ZnS}$ to wurtzite-type $\\ce{ZnS}$ occurs at \\(1297\\ \\rm{K}\\).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04756 goldbook:ST06775)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04756 doi:10.1351/pac199466030577)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04756 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04758))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04758 "pooled standard deviation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04758 "A problem often arises when the combination of several series of measurements performed under similar conditions is desired to achieve an improved estimate of the imprecision of the process. If it can be assumed that all the series are of the same precision although their means may differ, the pooled standard deviations \\(s_{\\rm{p}}\\) from \\(k\\) series of measurements can be calculated as \\[s_{\\rm{p}}=\\sqrt{\\frac{(n_{1}- 1)\\ s_{1}^{2}+(n_{2}- 1)\\ s_{2}^{2}+...+(n_{k}- 1)\\ s_{k}^{2}}{n_{1}+n_{2}+...+n_{k}- k}}\\] The suffices \\(1,2,...,k\\) refer to the different series of measurements. In this case it is assumed that there exists a single underlying standard deviation \\(\\sigma \\) of which the pooled standard deviation \\(s_{\\rm{p}}\\) is a better estimate than the individual calculated standard deviations \\(s_{1},s_{2},...,s_{k}\\), For the special case where \\(k\\) sets of duplicate measurements are available, the above equation reduces to \\[s_{\\rm{p}}=\\sqrt{\\frac{\\sum (x_{i1}- x_{i2})^{2}}{2\\ k}}\\] Results from various series of measurements can be combined in the following way to give a pooled relative standard deviation \\(s_{\\rm{r,p}}\\): \\[s_{\\rm{r,p}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{\\sum (n_{i}-1)\\ s_{\\rm{r,}i}^{2}}{\\sum n_{i}- 1}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{\\sum (n_{i}-1)\\ s_{i}^{2}\\ x_{i}^{-2}}{\\sum n_{i}-1}}\\]")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04758 goldbook:P04799)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04758 goldbook:R05280)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:P04758 goldbook:S05911)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04758 doi:10.1351/pac198153091805)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04758 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04759))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04759 "population inversion")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04759 "A situation in which a higher energy state is more populated than a lower energy state.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04759 doi:10.1351/pac199668122223)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04759 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04760))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04760 "pore size distribution")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04760 "The distribution of pore volume with respect to pore size; alternatively, it may be defined by the related distribution of pore area with respect to pore size.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04760 doi:10.1351/pac197646010071)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04760 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04762))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04762 "porosity")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04762 "A concept related to texture, referring to the pore space in a material.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:P04762 doi:10.1351/pac197646010071)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:P04762 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:P04763))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:P04763 "porous-layer open-tabular column")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:P04763 "A column in which there is a porous layer on the inner wall. porosity can be achieved by either chemical means (e.g. etching) or by the deposition of porous particles on the wall from a suspension. The porous layer may serve as a support for a liquid stationary phase or as the stationary phase itself.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003012) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:P04763 "PLOT")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:P04763 "PLOT column")
