Declaration(Class(goldbook:R05035))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:R05035 "radial elution")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:R05035 "A mode of operation in which the sample is spotted at a point source at or near the middle of the plane and is carried outward in a circle by the mobile phase, also applied at that place.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:R05035 "radial development")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:R05035 "circular elution")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:R05035 "circular development")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05035 goldbook:M03958)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:R05035 doi:10.1351/pac199365040819)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:R05035 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:R05036))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:R05036 "radian")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:R05036 "SI derived unit of plane angle, \\(\\rm{rad} = 1\\).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05036 goldbook:P04686)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:R05036 doi:10.1351/pac199668040957)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:R05036 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:R05037))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:R05037 "radiance")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:R05037 "Radiant power, \\(P\\), leaving or passing through a small transparent element of surface in a given direction from the source about the solid angle \\(\\varOmega\\), divided by the solid angle and by the orthogonally projected area of the element in a plane normal to the given beam direction, \\(\\rm{d}S_{\\perp } = \\rm{d}S\\, \\rm{cos}\\,\\theta\\)")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:R05037 "Mathematical definition: \\[L = \\frac{\\rm{d}^{2}P}{\\rm{d}\\Omega \\, \\rm{d}S_{\\perp }} = \\frac{\\rm{d}^{2}P}{\\rm{d}\\Omega \\, \\rm{d}S\\, \\rm{cos}\\,\\theta}\\] for a divergent beam propagating in an elementary cone of the solid angle \\(\\varOmega\\) containing the direction \\(\\theta\\). SI unit is \\(\\rm{W m}^{-2}\\ \\rm{sr}^{-1}\\)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:R05037 "For a parallel beam it is the radiant power, \\(P\\), of all wavelengths leaving or passing through a small element of surface in a given direction from the source divided by the orthogonally projected area of the element in a plane normal to the given direction of the beam, \\(\\theta\\). Mathematical definition in this case: \\(\\rm{d}P/(\\rm{d}S\\, \\rm{cos}\\,\\theta)\\). If the @R05046-1@ is constant over the surface area considered, \\(P/(S\\, \\rm{cos}\\,\\theta)\\). SI unit is \\(\\rm{W m}^{-2}\\)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:R05037 "Equivalent to \\(L = \\int_{\\lambda}L_{\\lambda}\\, \\rm{d}\\lambda\\), where \\(L_{\\lambda}\\) is the spectral radiance at wavelength \\(\\lambda\\)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05037 goldbook:A00346)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05037 goldbook:R05046)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05037 goldbook:S05824)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05037 goldbook:W06659)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:R05037 doi:10.1351/pac200779030293)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:R05037 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:R05039))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:R05039 "radiant energy")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:R05039 "The total energy emitted, transferred or received as radiation in a defined period of time (\\(Q=\\int Q_{\\lambda }  \\ \\mathrm{d}\\lambda \\)). It is the product of radiant power, \\(P\\), and time, \\(t\\): \\(Q=P\\ t\\) when the radiant power is constant over the time considered.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05039 goldbook:R05046)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:R05039 doi:10.1351/pac199668122223)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:R05039 doi:10.1351/pac199668040957)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:R05039 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:R05041))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:R05041 "radiant exitance")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:R05041 "Radiant power, \\(P\\), emitted at all wavelengths by an element of surface containing the source point under consideration divided by the area of the source. SI unit is \\(\\rm{W m}^{-2}\\).")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:R05041 "radiant emittance")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:R05041 "exitance")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:R05041 "spherical radiant exitance")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:R05041 "Mathematical definition: \\(M = \\rm{d}P/\\rm{d}S\\). If the radiant power \\(P\\) is constant over the surface area considered, \\(M = P/S\\)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:R05041 "Equivalent to the integration of the radiant power leaving a source over the solid angle and over the whole wavelength range. Mathematical definition: \\(M = \\int_{\\lambda}M_{\\lambda}\\, \\rm{d}\\lambda\\), where \\(M_{\\lambda}\\) is the spectral radiant exitance at wavelength \\(\\lambda\\)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:R05041 "Same as spherical radiant exitance. Formerly called radiant emittance."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05041 goldbook:R05046)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05041 goldbook:A00346)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05041 goldbook:S05825)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05041 goldbook:W06659)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:R05041 doi:10.1351/pac200779030293)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:R05041 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:R05042))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:R05042 "radiant exposure")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:R05042 "Radiant energy, \\(Q\\), incident from all upward directions on a small sphere divided by the cross-sectional area of that sphere. SI unit is \\(\\pu{J m-2}\\).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:R05042 "Equivalent definition: Irradiance, \\(E\\) integrated over the time of irradiation."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:R05042 "Mathematical definition: \\(H = \\rm{d}Q/\\rm{d}S = \\int _{t} E\\, \\rm{d}t\\). If \\(Q\\) is constant over the area, \\(H = Q/S\\). If \\(E\\) is constant over the time interval, \\(H = E\\, t\\)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:R05042 "This term refers to a beam not scattered or reflected by the target or its surroundings. For a beam incident from all directions fluence&nbsp;(\\(H_{\\rm{o}}\\), \\(F_{\\rm{o}}\\)) is an equivalent term."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05042 goldbook:R05039)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05042 goldbook:I03255)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:R05042 doi:10.1351/pac200779030293)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:R05042 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:R05045))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:R05045 "radiant intensity")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:R05045 "Radiant power, \\(P\\), at all wavelengths per solid angle, \\(\\varOmega\\). The @R05046-2@ emitted in a given direction by a source or an element of the source in a small cone containing the given direction divided by the solid angle of the cone. SI unit is \\(\\rm{W sr}^{-1}\\).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:R05045 "Mathematical definition: \\(I = \\rm{d}P/\\rm{d}\\varOmega\\). If the radiant power is constant over the solid angle considered, \\(I = P/\\varOmega\\)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:R05045 "Equivalent to \\(I = \\int_{\\lambda}I_{\\lambda}\\, \\rm{d}\\lambda\\), where \\(I_{\\lambda}\\) is the spectral radiant intensity at wavelength \\(\\lambda\\)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:R05045 "It is not recommended to abbreviate this term to just intensity because it is confusing."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05045 goldbook:A00346)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05045 goldbook:R05046)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05045 goldbook:S05827)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05045 goldbook:W06659)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:R05045 doi:10.1351/pac200779030293)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:R05045 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:R05046))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:R05046 "radiant power")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:R05046 "Power emitted, transferred or received as radiation. SI unit is \\(\\pu{J s-1} = \\pu{W}\\).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:R05046 "Mathematical definition: \\(P = \\rm{d}Q/\\rm{d}t\\). If the radiant energy \\(Q\\) is constant over the time interval, \\(P = Q/t\\)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:R05046 "In radiometry, flux (\\(\\varPhi\\)) is used with the same units as \\(P\\). The symbol \\(\\varPhi\\) is reserved for quantum yield in photochemistry. Therefore, the use of flux (\\(\\varPhi\\)) is not recommended."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05046 goldbook:P04792)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05046 goldbook:P04588)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05046 goldbook:Q04991)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05046 goldbook:R05039)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05046 goldbook:R05115)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:R05046 doi:10.1351/pac200779030293)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:R05046 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:R05048))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:R05048 "radiation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:R05048 "A term embracing electromagnetic waves as well as fast moving particles. In radioanalytical chemistry the term usually refers to radiation emitted during a nuclear process (radioactive decay, nuclear reaction, nuclear fission, accelerators).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05048 goldbook:N04229)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05048 goldbook:R05083)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05048 goldbook:A00338)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:R05048 doi:10.1351/pac199466122513)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:R05048 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:R05050))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:R05050 "radiation chemistry")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:R05050 "The part of chemistry which deals with the chemical effects of ionizing radiation, as distinguished from photochemistry associated with visible and ultraviolet electromagnetic radiation.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05050 goldbook:I03216)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05050 goldbook:P04588)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05050 goldbook:UT07492)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05050 goldbook:VT07496)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:R05050 doi:10.1351/pac199466122513)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:R05050 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:R05051))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:R05051 "radiation constants")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:R05051 "Fundamental physical constants characterizing black body radiation. The first radiation constant is \\(c_{1} = 2\\ \\pi \\ h\\ c_{0}^{2}=3.741\\,7749(22)\\times 10^{-16}\\ \\rm{W m}^{2}\\), the second is \\(c_{2} = \\frac{h\\ c_{0}}{k}=1.438\\,769(12)\\times 10^{-2}\\ \\rm{m K}\\), where \\(h\\) is the Planck constant \\(c_{0}\\) the speed of light and \\(k\\) the Boltzmann constant.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05051 goldbook:B00695)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05051 goldbook:P04685)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:R05051 doi:10.6028/jres.092.010)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:R05051 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:R05052))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:R05052 "radiation continuum")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:R05052 "Continuous (in the wavelength, not time sense) radiation arising for example from non-quantized free-free transitions of electrons in the fields of the ions, free-bound transitions or radiative recombinations of electrons and ions, incandescent radiation emitted by hot solids (when the radiation distribution conforms to that described by Planck's law, it is considered black-body radiation) and unresolvable band spectra, i.e. where the spectral lines are wider than the spacings between them.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05052 goldbook:B00595)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05052 goldbook:R05048)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05052 goldbook:W06659)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:R05052 doi:10.1351/pac198557101453)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:R05052 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:R05053))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:R05053 "radiation counter")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:R05053 "Radiation measuring assembly comprising a radiation detector in which individual ionizing events cause electrical pulses and the associated equipment for processing and counting the pulses. Often an expression is added indicating the type of radiation detector (e.g. scintillation, semiconductor).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05053 goldbook:R05048)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05053 goldbook:R05054)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05053 goldbook:S05505)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05053 goldbook:S05592)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:R05053 doi:10.1351/pac199466122513)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:R05053 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:R05054))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:R05054 "radiation detector")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:R05054 "A device in which incident radiation produces a measurable effect. If this effect is a rise in temperature it is called a thermal detector. If it is a rise in pressure it is called a photoacoustic detector. In the case where an electrical signal is produced it is called a photoelectric detector. Photoelectric detectors can be classified as photo-emissive detectors and semiconductor detectors. Where the radiation produces a chemical reaction, it is termed a photochemical detector. A detector yielding an output signal that is independent of the wavelength of the radiation over a specific region is called a nonselective detector. Where it is wavelength specific it is a selective detector. A detector having a quantum efficiency independent of the wavelength is a nonselective quantum counter. Certain detectors are able to distinguish between different quantum energies. This property is described by the energy resolution \\(\\Delta E\\) and the energy resolving power \\(\\frac{E}{\\Delta E}\\). These detectors are called energy dispersive detectors. In X-ray spectroscopy, the reciprocal \\(\\frac{\\Delta E}{E}\\) is often used but this is discouraged.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05054 goldbook:X06718)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05054 goldbook:P04574)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05054 goldbook:P04792)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05054 goldbook:Q04988)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05054 goldbook:S05591)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05054 goldbook:W06659)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:R05054 doi:10.1351/pac199466122513)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:R05054 doi:10.1351/pac199567101745)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:R05054 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:R05055))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:R05055 "radiation hazard")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:R05055 "Hazard that exists in a region where there is a radiation field, other than what is considered to be normal background radiation.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05055 goldbook:HT06827)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05055 goldbook:B00580)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05055 goldbook:R05048)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:R05055 doi:10.1351/pac198254081533)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:R05055 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:R05056))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:R05056 "radiationless deactivation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:R05056 "Loss of electronic excitation energy without photon emission or chemical change. Often, ultrafast radiationless decays are mediated by conical intersections.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:R05056 "radiationless decay")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05056 goldbook:E02250)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:R05056 doi:10.1351/pac200779030293)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:R05056 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:R05057))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:R05057 "radiationless transition")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:R05057 "A transition between two states of a system without photon emission or absorption.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05057 goldbook:R05065)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:R05057 doi:10.1351/pac199668122223)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:R05057 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:R05059))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:R05059 "radiation spectrum")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:R05059 "The components of radiation arranged in order of their wavelengths, frequencies or quantum energies. For particle radiation they are arranged in order of their kinetic energies.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05059 goldbook:R05048)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:R05059 doi:10.1351/pac198254081533)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:R05059 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:R05060))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:R05060 "radiative absorption")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:R05060 "A process by which a particle in the ground state or an excited state may undergo transition to a higher energy level by absorption of a photon. For a given particle in the lower state of probability per second of such a transition in a field with a continuous spectrum is proportional to the spectral radiant energy density of the absorption line. The proportionality constant is termed the transition probability for absorption. The transition probability for stimulated emission is defined in a similar way for the reverse radiative de-excitation process that is induced by the same radiation field.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05060 goldbook:A00036)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05060 goldbook:A00041)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05060 goldbook:E02257)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05060 goldbook:G02704)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05060 goldbook:P04855)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05060 goldbook:R05062)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05060 goldbook:ST07480)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05060 goldbook:S06015)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:R05060 doi:10.1351/pac198557101453)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:R05060 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:R05061))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:R05061 "radiative capture")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:R05061 "Capture of a particle by a nucleus followed by immediate emission of gamma radiation.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05061 goldbook:C00796)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05061 goldbook:R02568)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05061 goldbook:N04256)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05061 goldbook:N04237)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:R05061 doi:10.1351/pac198254081533)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:R05061 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:R05062))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:R05062 "radiative de-excitation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:R05062 "The change in the internal energy of a particle may be due to radiative processes, i.e. the emission or absorption of a photon. A particle in an excited state may undergo a transition to a lower energy level by emission of a photon. This is known as radiative de-excitation. If such a transition occurs spontaneously its probability per second for a given excited particle is termed the transition probability for spontaneous emission.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05062 goldbook:E02257)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05062 goldbook:I03103)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05062 goldbook:P04855)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05062 goldbook:S05886)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:R05062 doi:10.1351/pac198557101453)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:R05062 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:R05063))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:R05063 "radiative energy transfer")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:R05063 "Transfer of excitation energy by radiative deactivation of a donor molecular entity and reabsorption of the emitted radiation by an acceptor molecular entity.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:R05063 "trivial energy transfer")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:R05063 "Radiative transfer results in a decrease of the donor fluorescence intensity in the region of spectral overlap. Such a distortion of the fluorescence spectrum is called inner-filter effect."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:R05063 "Radiative energy transfer depends on the shape and size of the vessel utilized and on the configuration of the latter with respect to excitation and observation."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:R05063 "The fraction \\(a\\) of photons emitted by D and absorbed by A is given by \\[a = \\frac{1}{\\mathit{\\Phi}_{\\rm{D}}^{0}}\\int _{_{\\lambda }}I_{\\lambda}^{\\rm{D}}(\\lambda)\\left [ 1 - 10^{-\\varepsilon_{\\rm{A}}(\\lambda)c_{\\rm{A}}\\, l} \\right ]\\rm{d}\\lambda\\] where \\(c_{\\rm{A}}\\) is the molar concentration of acceptor, \\(\\mathit{\\Phi} _{\\rm{D}}^{0}\\) is the fluorescence quantum yield in the absence of acceptor, \\(l\\) is the thickness of the sample, \\(I_{\\lambda}^{\\rm{D}}(\\lambda)\\) and \\(\\varepsilon_{\\rm{A}}(\\lambda )\\) are the spectral distribution of the spectral radiant intensity of the donor fluorescence and the molar decadic absorption coefficient of the acceptor, respectively, with the normalization condition \\(\\mathit{\\Phi} _{\\rm{D}}^{0} = \\int_{\\lambda}I_{\\lambda}^{\\rm{D}}(\\lambda)\\, \\rm{d}\\lambda\\).For relatively low absorbance, \\(a\\) can be approximated by \\[a = \\frac{2.3}{\\mathit{\\Phi}_{\\rm{D}}^{0}}c_{\\rm{A}}\\, l\\int _{\\lambda}I_{\\lambda}^{\\rm{D}}(\\lambda)\\varepsilon_{\\rm{A}}(\\lambda)\\rm{d}\\lambda\\] where the integral represents the overlap between the donor fluorescence spectrum and the acceptor absorption spectrum."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05063 goldbook:A00028)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05063 goldbook:A00043)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05063 goldbook:D01528)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05063 goldbook:E02250)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05063 goldbook:F02384)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05063 goldbook:F02453)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05063 goldbook:M03972)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05063 goldbook:NT07086)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05063 goldbook:Q04991)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05063 goldbook:S05813)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05063 goldbook:S05818)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05063 goldbook:S05827)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:R05063 doi:10.1351/pac200779030293)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:R05063 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:R05064))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:R05064 "radiative lifetime")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:R05064 "Lifetime of an excited molecular entity in the absence of radiationless transitions. The reciprocal of the first-order rate constant for the radiative step, or the reciprocal of the sum of these rate constants if there is more than one such step. The equivalent term, natural lifetime, is discouraged.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:R05064 "Approximate expressions exist relating \\(\\tau_{0}\\) to the oscillator strength of the emitting transition."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:R05064 "The subscript \\(0\\) is used in this definition, whereas the superscript \\(0\\) is used to indicate a non-quenched lifetime in the Stern–Volmer kinetic relationships."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05064 goldbook:L03515)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05064 goldbook:S06004)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05064 goldbook:O04339)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05064 goldbook:O04322)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:R05064 doi:10.1351/pac200779030293)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:R05064 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:R05065))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:R05065 "radiative transition")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:R05065 "A transition between two states of a molecular entity, the energy difference being emitted or absorbed as photons. In principle, radiative and radiationless transitions can be distinguished in molecules. The first occur by absorption or emission of light quanta, and the latter is the result of the transformation of electronic excitation energy into vibrational/rotational energy.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05065 goldbook:E02250)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05065 goldbook:M03986)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05065 goldbook:P04627)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05065 goldbook:R05057)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05065 goldbook:T06446)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:R05065 doi:10.1351/pac198456020231)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:R05065 doi:10.1351/pac199668122223)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:R05065 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:R05066))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:R05066 "radical")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:R05066 "A molecular entity such as $\\ce{^{.}CH3}$, $\\ce{^{.}SnH3}$, $\\ce{Cl^{.}}$ possessing an unpaired electron. (In these formulae the dot, symbolizing the unpaired electron, should be placed so as to indicate the atom of highest spin density, if this is possible.) Paramagnetic metal ions are not normally regarded as radicals. However, in the 'isolobal analogy' the similarity between certain paramagnetic metal ions and radicals becomes apparent. At least in the context of physical organic chemistry, it seems desirable to cease using the adjective 'free' in the general name of this type of chemical species and molecular entity, so that the term 'free radical' may in future be restricted to those radicals which do not form parts of radical pairs. Depending upon the core atom that possesses the unpaired electron, the radicals can be described as carbon-, oxygen-, nitrogen-, metal-centered radicals. If the unpaired electron occupies an orbital having considerable s or more or less pure p character, the respective radicals are termed $\\ce{\\upsigma\\!\\mbox{-}}$ or $\\ce{\\uppi\\!\\mbox{-}radicals}$. In the past, the term 'radical' was used to designate a substituent group bound to a molecular entity, as opposed to 'free radical', which nowadays is simply called radical. The bound entities may be called groups or substituents, but should no longer be called radicals.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:R05066 "free radical")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05066 goldbook:P04404)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05066 goldbook:B00671)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05066 goldbook:CT01038)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05066 goldbook:F02519)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05066 goldbook:G02705)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05066 goldbook:I03288)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05066 goldbook:M03986)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05066 goldbook:S05864)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05066 goldbook:S06076)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:R05066 doi:10.1351/pac199466051077)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:R05066 doi:10.1351/pac199567081307)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:R05066 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:R05069))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:R05069 "radical centre")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:R05069 "The atom (or group of atoms) in a polyatomic radical on which an unpaired electron is largely localized. attachment of a monovalent atom to a radical centre gives a molecule for which it is possible to write a Lewis formula in which the normal stable valencies are assigned to all atoms.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:R05069 "radical centres")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:R05069 "radical center")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:R05069 "radical centers")
