Declaration(Class(goldbook:R05129))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:R05129 "random sample")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:R05129 "The sample so selected that any portion of the population has an equal (or known) chance of being chosen. Haphazard or arbitrary choice of units is generally insufficient to guarantee randomness.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:R05129 doi:10.1351/pac199062061193)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:R05129 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:R05134))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:R05134 "range of measurement")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:R05134 "The range of concentration between the measurement threshold and the maximum usable indication.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:R05134 doi:10.1351/pac199062112167)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:R05134 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:R05136))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:R05136 "rate")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:R05136 "Derived quantity in which time is a denominator quantity. Rate of \\(x\\) is \\(\\frac{\\rm{d}x}{\\rm{d}t}\\).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05136 goldbook:D01614)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:R05136 doi:10.1351/pac199668040957)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:R05136 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:R05139))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:R05139 "rate-controlling step")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:R05139 "A rate-controlling (rate-determining or rate-limiting) step in a reaction occurring by a composite reaction sequence is an elementary reaction the rate constant for which exerts a strong effect — stronger than that of any other rate constant — on the overall rate. It is recommended that the expressions rate-controlling, rate-determining and rate-limiting be regarded as synonymous, but some special meanings sometimes given to the last two expressions are considered under a separate heading. A rate-controlling step can be formally defined on the basis of a control function (or control factor) CF, identified for an elementary reaction having a rate constant \\(k_{i}\\) by: \\[\\rm{CF}=\\frac{\\partial (\\ln  u)}{\\partial \\ln k_{i}}\\] where \\( u\\) is the overall rate of reaction. In performing the partial differentiation all equilibrium constants \\(K_{j}\\) and all rate constants except \\(k_{i}\\) are held constant. The elementary reaction having the largest control factor exerts the strongest influence on the rate \\( u\\), and a step having a CF much larger than any other step may be said to be rate-controlling. A rate-controlling step defined in the way recommended here has the advantage that it is directly related to the interpretation of kinetic isotope effects. As formulated this implies that all rate constants are of the same dimensionality. Consider however the reaction of A and B to give an intermediate C, which then reacts further with D to give products:      (1)      (2)   Assuming that C reaches a steady state, then the observed rate is given by: \\[ u = \\frac{k_{1}\\,k_{2}\\,\\left[\\rm{A}\\right]\\left[\\rm{B}\\right]\\left[\\rm{D}\\right]}{k_{-1}+k_{2}\\left[\\rm{D}\\right]}\\] Considering \\(k_{2}\\left[\\rm{D}\\right]\\) a pseudo-first order rate constant, then \\(k_{2}\\left[\\rm{D}\\right]\\gg k_{-1}\\), and the observed rate \\( u = k_{1}\\ \\left[\\rm{A}\\right]\\left[\\rm{B}\\right]\\) and \\(k_{\\rm{obs}}=k_{1}\\). Step (1) is said to be the rate-controlling step. If \\(k_{2}\\left[\\rm{D}\\right]\\ll k_{-1}\\), then the observed rate: \\[ u = \\frac{k_{1}\\ k_{2}}{k_{-1}}\\left[\\rm{A}\\right]\\left[\\rm{B}\\right]\\left[\\rm{D}\\right]=K\\ k_{2}\\left[\\rm{A}\\right]\\left[\\rm{B}\\right]\\left[\\rm{D}\\right]\\] where \\(K\\) is the equilibrium constant for the pre-equilibrium (1) and is equal to \\(\\frac{k_{1}}{k_{-1}}\\), and \\(k_{\\rm{obs}}=K\\ k_{2}\\). Step (2) is said to be the rate-controlling step.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05139 goldbook:G02630)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05139 goldbook:C01211)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05139 goldbook:E02035)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05139 goldbook:E02177)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05139 goldbook:K03405)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05139 goldbook:M03912)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05139 goldbook:M03946)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05139 goldbook:O04322)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05139 goldbook:R05156)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05139 goldbook:R05140)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05139 goldbook:ST06775)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05139 goldbook:S05962)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:R05139 doi:10.1351/pac199466051077)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:R05139 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:R05140))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:R05140 "rate-determining step")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:R05140 "These terms are best regarded as synonymous with rate-controlling step. However, other meanings that have been given to them should be mentioned, as it is necessary to be aware of them in order to avoid confusion. Sometimes the term rate-determining is used as a special case of rate-controlling, being assigned only to an initial slow step which is followed by rapid steps. Such a step imposes an upper limit on the rate, and has also been called rate-limiting. In view of the considerable danger of confusion when special meanings are applied to rate-determining and rate-limiting, it is recommended that they be regarded as synonymous, with the meaning explained under the entry rate-controlling step.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:R05140 "rate-limiting step")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05140 goldbook:M03892)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05140 goldbook:R05139)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:R05140 doi:10.1351/pac199466051077)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:R05140 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:R05141))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:R05141 "rate law")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:R05141 "An expression for the rate of reaction of a particular reaction in terms of concentrations of chemical species and constant parameters (normally rate coefficients and partial orders of reaction) only. For examples of rate laws see equations (1)-(3) under kinetic equivalence, and (1) under steady state.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:R05141 "empirical differential rate equation")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05141 goldbook:CT01038)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05141 goldbook:K03403)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:R05141 goldbook:O04322)
