AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:S05652 doi:10.1351/pac199264010143)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:S05652 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:S05657))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:S05657 "siemens")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:S05657 "SI derived unit of electric conductance, \\(\\pu{S} = \\pu{\\Omega^{-1}} = \\pu{m-2 kg-1 s3 A2}\\).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S05657 goldbook:E01925)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:S05657 doi:10.1351/pac199668040957)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:S05657 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:S05658))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:S05658 "sievert")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:S05658 "SI derived unit of dose equivalent (the mean specific energy imparted to an element of matter corrected by a quality factor and a modifying factor to take into account the properties of irradiated matter) equal to one joule per kilogram and admitted for reasons of safeguarding human health.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S05658 goldbook:D01841)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S05658 goldbook:J03363)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S05658 goldbook:K03391)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:S05658 doi:10.1351/pac199668040957)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:S05658 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:S05660))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:S05660 "sigmatropic rearrangement")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:S05660 "A molecular rearrangement that involves both the creation of a new $\\ce{\\upsigma\\!\\mbox{-}bond}$ between atoms previously not directly linked and the breaking of an existing $\\ce{\\upsigma\\!\\mbox{-}bond}$. There is normally a concurrent relocation of $\\ce{\\uppi\\!\\mbox{-}bonds}$ in the molecule concerned, but the total number of $\\ce{\\uppi\\!\\mbox{-}}$ and $\\ce{\\upsigma\\!\\mbox{-}bonds}$ does not change. The term was originally restricted to intramolecular pericyclic reactions, and many authors use it with this connotation. It is, however, also applied in a more general, purely structural, sense. If such reactions are intramolecular, their transition state may be visualized as an association of two fragments connected at their termini by two partial $\\ce{\\upsigma\\!\\mbox{-}bonds}$, one being broken and the other being formed as, for example, the two allyl fragments in ($\\ce{a'}$). Considering only atoms within the (real or hypothetical) cyclic array undergoing reorganization, if the numbers of these in the two fragments are designated \\(i\\) and \\(j\\), then the rearrangement is said to be a sigmatropic change of order [\\(i\\), \\(j\\)] (conventionally \\(\\rm{[}i\\rm{]}\\leq \\rm{[}j\\rm{]}\\)). Thus the rearrangement (a) is of order, whilst reaction (b) is asigmatropic shift of hydrogen. (N.B. By convention square brackets here refer to numbers of atoms, in contrast with current usage in the context of cycloaddition.)   The descriptors a and s (antarafacial and antarafacial) may also be annexed to the numbers \\(i\\) and \\(j\\); (b) is then described as a [1s,5s] sigmatropic rearrangement, since it is suprafacial with respect both to the hydrogen atom and to the pentadienyl system:  The prefix 'homo' (meaning one extra atom, interrupting conjugation — cf. 'homoaromaticity') has frequently been applied to sigmatropic rearrangements, but is misleading.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S05660 goldbook:A00472)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S05660 goldbook:C01267)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S05660 goldbook:C01496)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S05660 goldbook:H02838)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S05660 goldbook:H02839)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S05660 goldbook:I03130)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S05660 goldbook:M03997)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S05660 goldbook:R05194)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S05660 goldbook:A00377)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S05660 goldbook:T06252)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S05660 goldbook:T06468)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:S05660 doi:10.1351/pac199466051077)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:S05660 "current"^^xsd:string)
