Declaration(Class(goldbook:S05695))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:S05695 "singlet molecular oxygen")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:S05695 "Oxygen molecule (dioxygen), $\\ce{O2}$, in an excited singlet state. The ground state of $\\ce{O2}$ is a triplet (\\(^{3}\\Sigma_{\\rm{g}}^{-}\\)). The two metastable singlet states derived from the ground-state configuration are \\(^{1}\\Delta_{\\rm{g}}\\) and \\(^{1}\\Sigma_{\\rm{g}}^{+}\\) (the latter with the higher energy).")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:S05695 "singlet molecular dioxygen")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:S05695 "Use of the term singlet oxygen alone, without mention of the chemical species is discouraged since it can also refer to an oxygen atom in a \\(^{1}\\rm{S}\\) or \\(^{1}\\rm{D}\\) excited state. The oxygen atom ground state is a triplet \\(^{3}\\rm{P}\\) state and the \\(^{1}\\rm{S}\\) and \\(^{1}\\rm{D}\\) states are also derived from the ground-state configuration."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:S05695 "Triplet state quenching by triplet dioxygen (i.e., a process of photosensitization) is the most common procedure for the production of singlet molecular dioxygen in solution. For many chemical species, the efficiency with which the triplet state is quenched by triplet dioxygen and, independently, the efficiency with singlet molecular dioxygen is produced, is controlled by the spin-statistical factor."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S05695 goldbook:E02257)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S05695 goldbook:G02704)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S05695 goldbook:M03872)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S05695 goldbook:P04652)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S05695 goldbook:Q05007)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S05695 goldbook:S05699)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S05695 goldbook:R05175)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S05695 goldbook:T06503)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:S05695 doi:10.1351/pac200779030293)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:S05695 "current"^^xsd:string)
