AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:S05945 "static pressure")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:S05945 "The pressure of a fluid at rest or in motion exerted perpendicularly to the direction of flow.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:S05945 doi:10.1351/pac199062112167)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:S05945 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:S05947))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:S05947 "static stability")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:S05947 "In meteorology, the stability of the atmosphere in the vertical direction to vertical displacements. If \\(\\mathit{\\Gamma}\\) is the dry adiabatic lapse rate, dry air is stable if the lapse rate \\(-\\frac{{\\rm{d}}T}{{\\rm{d}}z} \\lt \\Gamma\\), unstable if \\(-\\frac{{\\rm{d}}T}{{\\rm{d}}z} \\gt \\Gamma\\) and neutral \\(-\\frac{{\\rm{d}}T}{{\\rm{d}}z} = \\Gamma\\).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S05947 goldbook:A00141)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S05947 goldbook:I03146)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S05947 goldbook:L03455)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S05947 goldbook:S05900)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S05947 goldbook:U06569)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:S05947 doi:10.1351/pac199062112167)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:S05947 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:S05948))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:S05948 "stationary phase")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:S05948 "The phase of a culture of microorganisms or animal and plant cells cultured in vitro that follows the exponential growth phase and in which there is little or no growth. In some cases it is a phase of product formation, e.g. formation of secondary metabolites.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S05948 goldbook:I03153)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S05948 goldbook:S05526)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:S05948 doi:10.1351/pac199264010143)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:S05948 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:S05949))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:S05949 "stationary phase")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:S05949 "One of the two phases forming a chromatographic system. It may be a solid, a gel or a liquid. If a liquid, it may be distributed on a solid. This solid may or may not contribute to the separation process. The liquid may also be chemically bonded to the solid (bonded phase) or immobilized onto it (immobilized phase). The expression chromatographic bed or sorbent may be used as a general term to denote any of the different forms in which the stationary phase is used. Particularly in gas chromatography where the stationary phase is most often a liquid, the term liquid phase is used for it as compared to the gas phase, i.e. the mobile phase. However, particularly in the early development of liquid chromatography, the term 'liquid phase' had also been used to characterize the mobile phase as compared to the 'solid phase' i.e. the stationary phase. Due to this ambiguity, the use of the term 'liquid phase' is discouraged. If the physical state of the stationary phase is to be expressed, the use of the adjective forms such as liquid stationary phase and solid stationary phase, bonded phase or immobilized phase is proposed.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S05949 goldbook:C01075)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S05949 goldbook:G02600)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:S05949 doi:10.1351/pac199365040819)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:S05949 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:S05952))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:S05952 "stationary phase volume")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:S05952 "The volume of the liquid stationary phase or the active solid in the column. The volume of any solid support is not included. In the case of partition chromatography with a liquid stationary phase, it is identical to the liquid phase volume.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S05952 goldbook:A00109)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S05952 goldbook:P04436)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:S05952 doi:10.1351/pac199365040819)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:S05952 "current"^^xsd:string)
