Declaration(Class(goldbook:S06021))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:S06021 "stoichiometric")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:S06021 "Involving chemical combination in simple integral ratios. Characterized by having no excess of reactants or products over that required to satisfy the balanced chemical equation representing the given chemical reaction.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:S06021 doi:10.1351/pac199062112167)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:S06021 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:S06023))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:S06023 "stoichiometric concentration")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:S06023 "The stoichiometric concentration, \\(c_{\\rm{B}}\\), of a component B in a system is given by the expression: \\[c_{\\rm{B}}=\\frac{n_{\\rm{B}}}{V}\\] where \\(n_{\\rm{B}}\\) is the stoichiometric amount of substance of component B in the system and \\(V\\) is the volume of the system. The component added to the system may dissociate or react with other components to form a series of derived components and only a fraction of the original component may actually exist in a free form in the system. It is therefore essential to distinguish between the stoichiometric concentration and the amount-of-substance concentration of the free form of the component in the system. Sometimes stoichiometric quantities are indicated by a subscript (\\(_{\\circ}\\)), e.g. \\(n_{\\rm{o,B}}\\), \\(c_{\\rm{o,B}}\\). In clinical chemistry, the term stoichiometric concentration is rarely employed. Instead, the name of the component is modified to indicate inclusion of the various derived forms, e.g. mixtures of a defined chemical component and its derivatives may be denoted by the plural form of the name of the pure unchanged substance, or to indicate the sum of components specified in individual quantities the specification 'total' may be employed.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06023 goldbook:A00297)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06023 goldbook:A00298)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06023 goldbook:S06021)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:S06023 doi:10.1351/pac198456050567)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:S06023 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:S06024))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:S06024 "stoichiometric mean molal")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:S06024 "The practical activity coefficient of electrolyte B is given by \\[\\gamma _{\\pm }=\\frac{a_{\\pm }}{\\sqrt{ u _{\\rm{+}}^{ u _{\\rm{+}}}\\  u _{\\rm{-}}^{ u _{\\rm{-}}}}\\ \\frac{m_{\\rm{B}}}{m^{\\rm{+}}}}\\] where \\(a_{\\pm }\\) is the mean activity of B in solution, \\(m_{\\rm{B}}\\) is the molality of B, \\(m^{+} = \\pu{1 mol kg-1}\\), \\( u _{\\rm{+}}\\) is the number of cations and \\( u _{\\unicode{x2013}}\\) the number of anions in the chosen group B which is taken as the electrolyte. \\[ u =  u _{\\rm{+}}+ u _{\\rm{-}}\\]")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:S06024 "practical activity coefficient")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06024 goldbook:C01124)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06024 goldbook:M03970)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:S06024 doi:10.1351/pac197437040499)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:S06024 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:S06025))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:S06025 "stoichiometric number")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:S06025 "A chemical reaction of known stoichiometry can be written in general as: \\[a\\rm{A}\\,+\\,b\\rm{B}\\,+\\,...\\rightarrow\\,...\\,+y\\rm{Y}\\,+\\,z\\rm{Z}\\] For the reaction products Y and Z the numbers \\(y\\) and \\(z\\) are known as the stoichiometric numbers, \\( u _{\\rm{Y}}\\) and \\( u _{\\rm{Z}}\\), for Y and Z respectively. For the reactants the stoichiometric numbers are the negatives of the numbers appearing in the equation; for example the stoichiometric number \\( u _{\\rm{A}}\\) for the reactant A is \\(-a\\). In other words, the stoichiometric numbers are positive for products and negative for reactants.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06025 goldbook:S06021)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06025 goldbook:S06026)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:S06025 doi:10.1351/pac199668010149)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:S06025 doi:10.1351/pac199668040957)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:S06025 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:S06026))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:S06026 "stoichiometry")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:S06026 "The term refers to the relationship between the amounts of substances that react together in a particular chemical reaction, and the amounts of products that are formed. The general stoichiometric equation: \\[a\\rm{A}\\,+\\,b\\rm{B}\\,+\\,...\\,\\rightarrow\\,...\\,+\\,y\\rm{Y}\\,+\\,z\\rm{Z}\\] provides the information that a moles of A reacts with b moles of B to produce y moles of Y and z moles of Z. The stoichiometry of a reaction may be unknown, or may be very complex. For example, the thermal decomposition of acetaldehyde yields mainly methane and carbon monoxide, but also a variety of minor products such as ethane, acetone and diacetyl. The stoichiometric equation:  is therefore only an approximate one. Even when the overall stoichiometry of a reaction is well defined, it may be time-dependent in that it varies during the course of a reaction. Thus if a reaction occurs by the mechanism \\(\\rm{A}\\rightarrow \\rm{X}\\rightarrow \\rm{Y}\\), and X is formed in substantial amounts during the course of the process, the relationship between the amounts of A, X and Y will vary with time, and no one stoichiometric equation can represent the reaction at all times.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06026 goldbook:D01547)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06026 goldbook:S06021)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:S06026 doi:10.1351/pac199668010149)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:S06026 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:S06027))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:S06027 "stokes")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:S06027 "cgs unit of kinematic viscosity, \\(\\rm{St} = 10^{-4}\\ \\rm{m}^{2}\\ \\rm{s}^{-1}\\).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06027 goldbook:K03395)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:S06027 doi:10.1351/pac199668040957)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:S06027 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:S06028))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:S06028 "Stokes law")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:S06028 "\\(F=6\\ \\pi \\ \\eta \\ r\\  u\\), where \\(F\\) is the force exerted on a sphere of radius \\(r\\) which is moving through a fluid of viscosity \\(\\eta \\) with a relative velocity \\( u\\); this equation holds at low velocities which are free from turbulence (called the stokes region).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06028 goldbook:S06027)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06028 goldbook:V06627)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:S06028 doi:10.1351/pac199062112167)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:S06028 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:S06029))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:S06029 "Stokes number")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:S06029 "Sometimes referred to as the inertial parameter; it is an index of the impactability of an aerosol particle. It is defined by the equation: \\(St = 2\\ \\tau \\ (V_{\\rm{t}}-  u_{\\rm{t}})\\ D_{\\rm{p}}\\) where \\(D_{\\rm{p}}\\) is the diameter of a small drop, \\(V_{\\rm{t}}-  u_{\\rm{t}}\\) is the difference in fall velocities of the drop and aerosol particles and \\(\\tau \\) is the characteristic relaxation time of a particle.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06029 goldbook:A00176)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06029 goldbook:R05287)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:S06029 doi:10.1351/pac199062112167)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:S06029 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:S06030))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:S06030 "Stokes parameters")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:S06030 "Of elliptically polarized incident radiation, these are given by \\[s_{0}^{0}=E_{1}^{0}+E_{2}^{0}\\] \\[s_{1}^{0}=E_{1}^{0}- E_{2}^{0}\\] \\[s_{2}^{0}=2\\ \\sqrt{E_{1}^{0}\\ E_{2}^{0}}\\ \\cos   \\delta ^{0}\\] \\[s_{3}^{0}=2\\ \\sqrt{E_{1}^{0}\\ E_{2}^{0}}\\ \\sin   \\delta ^{0}\\] where \\(E_{1}^{0}\\) and \\(E_{2}^{0}\\) specify the irradiances of the incident light polarized with their electric vectors vibrating perpendicular and parallel to the scattering, respectively and \\(\\delta ^{0}\\) is the phase difference between these electric vectors.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06030 goldbook:I03254)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06030 goldbook:R05048)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06030 goldbook:S05493)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06030 goldbook:S05492)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:S06030 doi:10.1351/pac198355060931)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:S06030 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:S06031))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:S06031 "Stokes shift")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:S06031 "The difference (usually in frequency units) between the spectral positions of the band maxima (or the band origin) of the absorption and luminescence arising from the same electronic transition. Generally, the luminescence occurring at a longer wavelength than the absorption is stronger than the opposite. The latter may be called an anti-Stokes shift.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06031 goldbook:C01130)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06031 goldbook:L03641)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06031 goldbook:W06659)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:S06031 doi:10.1351/pac199668122223)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:S06031 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:S06032))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:S06032 "Stokes type radiation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:S06032 "Fluorescence radiation occurring at wavelengths longer than absorption, i.e. the normal case, is said to be of the Stokes type.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06032 goldbook:F02453)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06032 goldbook:S06027)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:S06032 doi:10.1351/pac198456020231)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:S06032 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:S06033))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:S06033 "stopped flow")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:S06033 "A technique for following the kinetics of reactions in solution (usually in the millisecond time range) in which two reactant solutions are rapidly mixed by being forced through a mixing chamber. The flow of the mixed solution along a uniform tube is then suddenly arrested. At a fixed position along the tube the solution is monitored (as a function of time following the stoppage of the flow) by some method with a rapid response (e.g. photometry).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06033 goldbook:M03946)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06033 goldbook:P04625)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:S06033 doi:10.1351/pac199365102291)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:S06033 doi:10.1351/pac199466051077)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:S06033 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:S06034))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:S06034 "stopped-flow cell")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:S06034 "A small-volume absorption cell connected to a rapid mixing chamber.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:S06034 doi:10.1351/pac198860091449)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:S06034 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:S06035))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:S06035 "stopping power")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:S06035 "Of a substance, for charged particles of specified energy, the average energy loss in passing through a thin layer of that substance, divided by the thickness of that layer.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:S06035 doi:10.1351/pac198254081533)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:S06035 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:S06036))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:S06036 "STP")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:S06036 "Abbreviation for standard temperature (\\(273.15\\ \\rm{K}\\) or \\(0\\ ^{\\,\\unicode{x26ac}}\\rm{C}\\)) and pressure (\\(10^{5}\\ \\rm{Pa}\\)); usually employed in reporting gas volumes. Note that flow meters calibrated in standard gas volumes per unit time often refer to volumes at \\(25\\ ^{\\,\\unicode{x26ac}}\\rm{C}\\), not \\(0\\ ^{\\,\\unicode{x26ac}}\\rm{C}\\).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:S06036 "STP")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06036 goldbook:S05910)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:S06036 doi:10.1351/pac199062112167)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:S06036 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:S06037))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:S06037 "strain")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:S06037 "Strain is present in a molecular entity or transition structure if the energy is enhanced because of unfavourable bond lengths, bond angles or dihedral angles ('torsional strain') relative to a standard. It is quantitatively defined as the standard enthalpy of a structure relative to a strainless structure (real or hypothetical) made up from the same atoms with the same types of bonding. (The enthalpy of formation of cyclopropane is \\(\\pu{53.6 kJ mol-1}\\), whereas the enthalpy of formation based on three 'normal' methylene groups, from acyclic models, is \\(\\pu{-62 kJ mol-1}\\). On this basis cyclopropane is destabilized by ca. \\(\\pu{115 kJ mol-1}\\) of strain energy.)")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:S06037 "steric strain")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06037 goldbook:A00349)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06037 goldbook:E01886)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06037 goldbook:E02141)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06037 goldbook:M03881)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06037 goldbook:M03986)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06037 goldbook:M03993)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06037 goldbook:ST07108)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06037 goldbook:T06434)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06037 goldbook:T06471)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:S06037 doi:10.1351/pac199466051077)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:S06037 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:S06038))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:S06038 "strain-induced transition")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:S06038 "A transition in a solid that is initiated by plastic strain.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06038 goldbook:S06037)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:S06038 doi:10.1351/pac199466030577)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:S06038 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:S06039))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:S06039 "stratified film")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:S06039 "A film in which more than two thicknesses coexist in a fixed configuration over significant periods of time.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06039 goldbook:F02366)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:S06039 doi:10.1351/pac197231040577)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:S06039 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:S06040))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:S06040 "stratified sample")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:S06040 "A sample consisting of portions obtained from identified subparts (strata) of the parent population. Within each stratum, the samples are taken randomly. The objective of taking stratified samples is to obtain a more representative sample than that which might otherwise be obtained by random sampling.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06040 goldbook:R05303)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:S06040 doi:10.1351/pac199062061193)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:S06040 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:S06041))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:S06041 "stratocumulus cloud")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:S06041 "A layer of patches composed of laminae or globular masses arranged in groups, lines or waves and having a soft, grey appearance; very often the rolls are so close together that their edges join and give the undersurface a wavy character; the process of formation (cumulogenesis) involves the spreading out of the tops of cumulus clouds, the latter having disappeared; \\(")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:S06041 doi:10.1351/pac199062112167)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:S06041 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:S06042))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:S06042 "stratopause")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:S06042 "That region of the atmosphere which lies between the stratosphere and the mesosphere and in which a maximum in the temperature occurs.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06042 goldbook:M03855)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06042 goldbook:S06043)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:S06042 doi:10.1351/pac199062112167)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:S06042 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:S06043))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:S06043 "stratosphere")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:S06043 "The atmospheric shell lying just above the troposphere which is characterized by an increasing temperature with altitude. The stratosphere begins at the tropopause (about \\(10{-}15\\ \\rm{km}\\) height) and extends to a height of about \\(50\\ \\rm{km}\\), where the lapse rate changes sign at the stratopause and the beginning of the mesosphere.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06043 goldbook:M03855)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06043 goldbook:S06042)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06043 goldbook:T06521)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06043 goldbook:T06522)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:S06043 doi:10.1351/pac199062112167)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:S06043 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:S06044))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:S06044 "stratus cloud")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:S06044 "A uniform, featureless layer of cloud resembling fog but not resting on the ground; when this very low layer is broken up into irregular shreds, it is designated as fractostratus; \\(300{-}600\\ \\rm{m}\\); widespread irregular stirring and lifting of the shallow layer of cool, damp air near the ground.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06044 goldbook:F02470)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:S06044 doi:10.1351/pac199062112167)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:S06044 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:S06045))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:S06045 "stray radiation error")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:S06045 "A spectrometer set to pass radiation of a particular wavelength band always has a small amount of stray radiation of other wavelengths. Since the sample may absorb more (or less) of this stray radiation than of the radiation at the selected wavelength an error can occur. This error is called a stray radiation error.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06045 goldbook:S05837)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06045 goldbook:W06659)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:S06045 doi:10.1351/pac198860091449)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:S06045 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:S06047))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:S06047 "streak tube")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:S06047 "An image converter adapted to provide scanning or time-resolved images. If the image is recorded the whole device is an example of a streak camera.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06047 goldbook:I02942)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:S06047 doi:10.1351/pac199567101745)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:S06047 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:S06049))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:S06049 "streaming current")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:S06049 "The electric current \\(I\\) flowing in a streaming cell if the electrodes, which are supposed to be ideally depolarized, are short-circuited. \\(I\\) is positive if the current in the membrane, plug, etc., is from high to low pressure side (and in the outside lead from low to high pressure side).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06049 goldbook:E01927)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06049 goldbook:MT06878)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:S06049 doi:10.1351/pac197231040577)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:S06049 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:S06050))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:S06050 "streaming potential difference")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:S06050 "The potential difference \\(E_{\\mathrm{st}}\\) or \\(E\\) at zero current caused by the flow of liquid under a pressure gradient through a membrane, plug or capillary. Identical electrodes must be used on both sides of the membrane, plug, etc. \\(E\\) is positive if the higher potential is on the high pressure side.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:S06050 "streaming potential")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06050 goldbook:G02669)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06050 goldbook:MT06878)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:S06050 doi:10.1351/pac197231040577)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:S06050 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:S06051))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:S06051 "stress-assisted transition")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:S06051 "A transition that takes place when an applied stress assists the transition to the new phase.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:S06051 doi:10.1351/pac199466030577)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:S06051 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:S06052))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:S06052 "stress graphitization")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:S06052 "The solid-state transformation of non-graphitic carbon into graphite by heat treatment combined with application of mechanical stress, resulting in a defined degree of graphitization being obtained at a lower temperature and/or after a shorter time of heat treatment than in the absence of applied stress.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:S06052 "Stress graphitization may also occur in volume elements of a carbon body in the process of heat treatment as a result of the action of internal residual or thermal stresses."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06052 goldbook:G02684)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06052 goldbook:G02691)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06052 goldbook:N04193)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06052 goldbook:T06446)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:S06052 doi:10.1351/pac199567030473)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:S06052 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:S06054))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:S06054 "stripping")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:S06054 "The process of removing solute(s) from a loaded solvent or extract. Generally this refers to the main solute(s) present.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:S06054 "back extraction")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:S06054 "Where appropriate, e.g. when liquid-liquid distribution is used for stripping, the term back-extraction can be used. The terms back-washing and re-extraction are not recommended."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:S06054 "The recent application of selective stripping of solutes as a separation method leads to some confusion between the terms stripping and scrubbing. It is recommended that the term scrubbing be reserved for the operation of removing contaminants (impurities) from an extract (where the scrub raffinate is often recycled to the loading step) and the term selective stripping be used where two or more main solutes are stripped successively from an extract, usually with different stripping agents, with a view to their subsequent separate recovery from solution for analysis."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06054 goldbook:E02301)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06054 goldbook:R05122)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06054 goldbook:R05225)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06054 goldbook:R05206)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06054 goldbook:S05511)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:S06054 doi:10.1351/pac199365112373)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:S06054 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:S06057))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:S06057 "stripping reaction")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:S06057 "A chemical process, studied in a molecular beam, in which the reaction products are scattered forward with respect to the moving centre of mass of the system.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06057 goldbook:M03982)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:S06057 doi:10.1351/pac199668010149)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:S06057 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:S06059))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:S06059 "strong collision")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:S06059 "A collision between two molecules in which the amount of energy transferred from one to the other is large compared with \\(k_{\\rm{B}}\\ T\\), where \\(k_{\\rm{B}}\\) is the Boltzmann constant and \\(T\\) the absolute temperature.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06059 goldbook:B00695)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:S06059 doi:10.1351/pac199668010149)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:S06059 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:S06061))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:S06061 "structural formula")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:S06061 "A formula which gives information about the way the atoms in a molecule are connected and arranged in space.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:S06061 doi:10.1515/pac-2014-0718)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:S06061 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:S06062))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:S06062 "structural transition")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:S06062 "A reversible or irreversible transition that involves a change of the crystal structure. Example: The transition of $\\ce{NH4Cl}$ at $\\pu{469 K}$ from a $\\ce{CsCl}$-type structure to a $\\ce{NaCl}$-type structure.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06062 goldbook:I03258)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06062 goldbook:R05379)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:S06062 doi:10.1351/pac199466030577)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:S06062 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:S06063))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:S06063 "structure")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:S06063 "The distribution in space of the atoms or ions in the material part of the catalyst and, in particular, the distribution at the surface.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:S06063 goldbook:C00876)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:S06063 doi:10.1351/pac197646010071)
