AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:ST07476 "Schenck reaction")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:ST07476 "The diastereoselective ene reaction of singlet molecular dioxygen with alkenes. An example is:")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:ST07476 goldbook:A00224)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:ST07476 goldbook:E02099)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:ST07476 doi:10.1351/pac200779030293)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:ST07476 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:ST07477))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:ST07477 "singlet–triplet crossing")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:ST07477 "Point of intersection between the potential energy surfaces of states of different multiplicity.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:ST07477 "The intersection belongs to a (\\(3\\ N-7\\))-dimensional subspace of the (\\(3\\ N-6\\))-dimensional nuclear coordinate space and therefore appears as a line on a two-dimensional energy surface (\\(N\\) is the number of nuclei). In this case the branching plane is one-dimensional and is defined by the gradient difference vector \\(x_{1}\\)."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:ST07477 goldbook:BT07335)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:ST07477 goldbook:G02669)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:ST07477 doi:10.1351/pac200779030293)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:ST07477 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:ST07478))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:ST07478 "solvent-induced symmetry breaking")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:ST07478 "Breaking of symmetry of a molecular species by interactions with the solvent that can modify the molecular charge distribution, to favour asymmetrical configurations.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:ST07478 "An example is the stabilization by a polar solvent of a light-induced charge transfer state in a symmetric donor–acceptor–donor system."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:ST07478 goldbook:P04717)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:ST07478 doi:10.1351/pac200779030293)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:ST07478 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:ST07479))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:ST07479 "spectral fluence rate")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:ST07479 "Derivative of fluence rate, \\(E_{\\rm{o}}\\), with respect to wavelength, \\(\\lambda\\). SI unit is \\(\\rm{W m}^{-3}\\); common unit is \\(\\rm{W m}^{-2}\\ \\rm{nm}^{-1}\\).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:ST07479 "All spectral terms may also be defined as derivatives with respect to frequency, \\(\\nu\\), or wavenumber, \\(\\tilde{\\nu}\\), and are referred to, when necessary, as in terms of wavelength, or frequency or wavenumber, respectively."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:ST07479 goldbook:FT07376)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:ST07479 goldbook:W06659)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:ST07479 doi:10.1351/pac200779030293)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:ST07479 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:ST07480))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:ST07480 "spectral radiant energy")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:ST07480 "Derivative of radiant energy, \\(Q\\), with respect to wavelength \\(\\lambda \\). SI unit is \\(\\pu{J m-1}\\); common unit is \\(\\pu{J nm-1}\\).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:ST07480 goldbook:R05039)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:ST07480 goldbook:W06659)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:ST07480 doi:10.1351/pac200779030293)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:ST07480 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:ST07481))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:ST07481 "spin-flip method")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:ST07481 "Quantum mechanical method for the calculation of open-shell excited states. The method accurately describes low-lying multi-configurational electronic states of diradicals and triradicals in an efficient and robust single-reference scheme. The target low-spin states (e.g., S = 0 or S = 1/2) are described as spin-flipping excitations (S = −1) from a well-behaved high-spin reference state (e.g., S = 1 or S = 3/4). By employing theoretical models of increasing complexity for the reference (e.g., SCF, MP2, CCSD), the accuracy in the target states’ description can be systematically improved. The SF methods result in multistate single-step computational schemes, e.g., several low-lying states can be computed in a single calculation that includes both dynamical and non-dynamical correlation effects.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:ST07481 "SF method")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:ST07481 goldbook:D01765)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:ST07481 goldbook:LT06788)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:ST07481 doi:10.1351/pac200779030293)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:ST07481 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:ST07482))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:ST07482 "spin-statistical factor")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:ST07482 "From the possible encounter pairs between states of different spin multiplicity, only those conserving multiplicity in going to products are expected to react.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment goldbook:ST07482 "This factor determines the efficiency of diffusion-controlled reactions, which have an encounter-controlled rate. Typical examples are quenching of fluorescence of aromatic hydrocarbons by $\\ce{O2}$, quenching of triplet states by $\\ce{O2}$, and triplet–triplet annihilation."^^xsd:string)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:ST07482 goldbook:A00366)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:ST07482 goldbook:D01716)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:ST07482 goldbook:E02086)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:ST07482 goldbook:E02089)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:ST07482 goldbook:F02453)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:ST07482 goldbook:H02889)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:ST07482 goldbook:Q05007)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:ST07482 doi:10.1351/pac200779030293)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:ST07482 "current"^^xsd:string)
