Declaration(Class(goldbook:T06472))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:T06472 "transition time")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:T06472 "In chronopotentiometry and related techniques, the time that elapses between the instant at which current is applied and the instant at which the concentration of an electroactive substance B at the electrode-solution interface becomes indistinguishable from zero. In experimental practice the latter time is often taken to be the instant at which the rate of variation of the potential of the indicator electrode attains a maximum value.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:T06472 goldbook:E01940)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:T06472 goldbook:I03006)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:T06472 goldbook:I03082)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:T06472 doi:10.1351/pac198557101491)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:T06472 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:T06474))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:T06474 "transit time")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:T06474 "The time needed for the component to pass through the observation space (in \\(\\mathrm{s}\\)). It depends on the geometry of the observation space, the flame temperature and the solute nebulized.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:T06474 doi:10.1351/pac198658121737)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:T06474 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:T06475))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:T06475 "translation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:T06475 "The unidirectional process that takes place on the ribosomes whereby the genetic information present in an mRNA is converted into a corresponding sequence of amino acids in a protein.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:T06475 goldbook:M03857)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:T06475 goldbook:R05389)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:T06475 goldbook:ST06775)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:T06475 doi:10.1351/pac199264010143)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:T06475 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:T06476))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:T06476 "translational spectroscopy")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:T06476 "A technique to investigate the distribution of the velocity of product ions from reactions of ions and neutral species.")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:T06476 doi:10.1351/pac199163101541)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:T06476 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:T06478))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:T06478 "transmission")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:T06478 "The ratio of the number of ions leaving a region of a mass spectrometer to the number entering that region.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:T06478 goldbook:M03732)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:T06478 doi:10.1351/pac199163101541)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:T06478 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:T06480))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:T06480 "transmission electron energy loss spectroscopy")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:T06480 "Any technique in which an electron transparent specimen is bombarded with a finely focused electron beam and the energy distribution of the transmitted electrons is measured. This energy spectrum contains features corresponding to discrete losses of energy of the transmitted electrons due to excitation of electronic or plasmon states and provides information on the identity (and in some cases) chemical bonding of the elements in the sample.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003012) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:T06480 "TEELS")
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:T06480 doi:10.1351/pac198355122023)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:T06480 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:T06481))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:T06481 "transmission electron microscopy")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:T06481 "Any technique in which an electron transparent sample is bombarded with an electron beam and the intensity of the transmitted electrons which is determined by scattering phenomena (electron absorption phenomena) in the interior of the sample is recorded. TEM essentially provides a high resolution image of the microstructure of a thin sample. This technique is often just called 'electron microscopy'. The term transmission electron microscopy is however recommended for the sake of a clear distinction from other electron microscopic techniques.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType OMO:0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:T06481 "TEM")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:T06481 "electron microscopy")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:T06481 goldbook:S05487)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:T06481 doi:10.1351/pac198355122023)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:T06481 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:T06484))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:T06484 "transmittance")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:T06484 "The ratio of the transmitted radiant power (\\(P_{\\lambda }\\)) to that incident on the sample (\\(P_{\\lambda }^{0}\\)): \\[T=\\frac{P_{\\lambda }}{P_{\\lambda }^{0}}\\] Internal transmittance refers to energy loss by absorption, whereas the total transmittance is that due to absorption, reflection, scatter, etc.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:T06484 "transmission factor")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:T06484 goldbook:B00626)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:T06484 goldbook:A00028)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:T06484 goldbook:A00513)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:T06484 goldbook:R05046)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:T06484 doi:10.1351/pac199668122223)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:T06484 doi:10.1351/pac199668040957)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:T06484 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:T06486))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:T06486 "transport")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:T06486 "The action of moving materials within the analytical instrument. Transport can involve any of several means including pressure flow, where the materials are moved by fluid pressure, either continuously or discontinuously; centrifugal flow, where the materials are moved by centrifugal force; spontaneous motion, where the materials are moved due to their intrinsic properties, e.g. diffusion, capillarity; and discrete transport, where materials are enclosed within a moving container.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:T06486 goldbook:A00333)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:T06486 goldbook:C00936)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:seeAlso goldbook:T06486 goldbook:D01716)
AnnotationAssertion(mito:isMentionedBy goldbook:T06486 doi:10.1351/pac198961091657)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:goldbook#hasStatus goldbook:T06486 "current"^^xsd:string)
Declaration(Class(goldbook:T06490))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:T06490 "transposon")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:T06490 "A movable DNA element that can be inserted at new sites into plasmids or chromosomes independently of the host cell recombination system. Prokaryotic transposons can carry genes that confer new phenotypic properties, such as resistance to antibiotics on the host.")
